TURATH_CHUNK(50,[{"num":10000,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنِ ابْنِ عُمَرَ رَضِيَ اللَّهُ عَنْهُمَا قَالَ: كُنَّا فِي زَمَنِ النَّبِيِّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ لاَ نَعْدِلُ بِأَبِي بَكْرٍ أَحَدًا، ثُمَّ عُمَرَ، ثُمَّ عُثْمَانَ، ثُمَّ نَتْرُكُ أَصْحَابَ النَّبِيِّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ لاَ نُفَاضِلُ بَيْنَهُمْ."],"takhrij":"صحيح: رواه البخاري في فضائل الصحابة (3697) عن محمد بن حاتم، ثنا شاذان، ثناعبد العزيز بن أبي سلمة الماجشون ، عن عبيدالله، عن نافع، عن ابن عمر قال: فذكره.","grade":"صحيح","chapter_ar":"باب ما جاء في فضل الخلفاء الثلاثة: أبي بكر، وعمر، وعثمان","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب فضائل الصحابة وأخبارهم","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Authentic: Narrated by al-Bukhārī (3697).","chapter_en":"Reports Concerning the Virtues of the Three Caliphs: Abū Bakr, ʿUmar, and ʿUthmān","part_en":"The Book of the Virtues and Accounts of the Companions","group_ar":"مجموع ما جاء في فضل جماعات الصحابة","group_en":"Collected Reports Concerning the Virtues of Groups of the Companions","part_no":49,"group_no":12,"chapter_no":4,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Ibn ʿUmar narrated: During the lifetime of the Prophet ﷺ, we regarded no one as equal to Abū Bakr, then came ʿUmar, then ʿUthmān. After them, we would leave the Companions of the Prophet ﷺ without ranking one above another."]}},"tuhfa":{},"voc":["fazail",198],"full":1,"dr":1,"tks":"صحيح: رواه البخاري (3697)."},{"num":10001,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ أنس أَنَّ النَّبِيَّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ صَعِدَ أُحُدًا وَأَبُو بَكْرٍ، وَعُمَرُ، وَعُثْمَانُ، فَرَجَفَ بِهِمْ فَقَالَ: اثْبُتْ أُحُدُ، فَإِنَّمَا عَلَيْكَ نَبِيٌّ وَصِدِّيقٌ وَشَهِيدَانِ."],"takhrij":"صحيح: رواه البخاري في فضائل الصحابة (3675) عن محمد ابن بشار، ثنا يحيى، عن سعيد، عن قتادة، أن أنس بن مالك، فذكره.","grade":"صحيح","chapter_ar":"باب ما جاء في فضل الخلفاء الثلاثة: أبي بكر، وعمر، وعثمان","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب فضائل الصحابة وأخبارهم","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Authentic: Narrated by al-Bukhārī (3675).","chapter_en":"Reports Concerning the Virtues of the Three Caliphs: Abū Bakr, ʿUmar, and ʿUthmān","part_en":"The Book of the Virtues and Accounts of the Companions","group_ar":"مجموع ما جاء في فضل جماعات الصحابة","group_en":"Collected Reports Concerning the Virtues of Groups of the Companions","part_no":49,"group_no":12,"chapter_no":4,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Anas narrated that the Prophet ﷺ ascended Mount Uḥud accompanied by Abū Bakr, ʿUmar, and ʿUthmān. The mountain shook beneath them, so the Prophet ﷺ said: “Be firm, Uḥud, for upon you are only a prophet, a truthful one, and two martyrs.”"]},"buhuth":{"en":["Another wording recorded by al-Bukhārī states:","“It shook beneath them, so he struck it with his foot and said: ‘Be firm, Uḥud…’”","Recorded by al-Bukhārī (3686)."]}},"tuhfa":{},"voc":["fazail",199],"full":1,"dr":1,"tks":"صحيح: رواه البخاري (3675)."},{"num":10002,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ أَبِي مُوسَى: أَنَّهُ تَوَضَّأَ فِي بَيْتِهِ ثُمَّ خَرَجَ، فَقُلْتُ: لَأَلْزَمَنَّ رَسُولَ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ، ، وَلَأَكُونَنَّ مَعَهُ يَوْمِي هَذَا، قَالَ: فَجَاءَ الْمَسْجِدَ فَسَأَلَ عَنِ النَّبِيِّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ، ، فَقَالُوا: خَرَجَ ووَجَّه هَاهُنَا، فَخَرَجْتُ عَلَى إثره، أَسْأَلُ عَنْهُ حَتَّى دَخَلَ بِئْرَ أَرِيسٍ، فَجَلَسْتُ عن الْبَابِ وَبَابُهَا مِنْ جَرِيدٍ، حَتَّى قَضَى رَسُولُ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ حَاجَتَهُ فَتَوَضَّأَ، فَقُمْتُ إِلَيْهِ، فَإِذَا هُوَ جَالِسٌ عَلَى بِئْرِ أَرِيسٍ وَتَوَسَّطَ قُفَّها، وَكَشَفَ عَنْ سَاقَيْهِ وَدَلَّاهُمَا فِي الْبِئْرِ، فَسَلَّمْتُ عَلَيْهِ، ثُمَّ انْصَرَفْتُ فَجَلَسْتُ عِنْدَ الْبَابِ، فَقُلْتُ: لأكونَنَّ بَوَّابَ رَسُولِ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ الْيَوْمَ، فَجَاءَ أَبُو بَكْرٍ فَدَفَعَ الْبَابَ، فَقُلْتُ مَنْ هَذَا؟ فَقَالَ أَبُو بَكْرٍ، فَقُلْتُ: عَلَى رِسْلِكَ، ثُمَّ ذَهَبْتُ، فَقُلْتُ: يارسول اللهِ هَذَا أَبُو بَكْرٍ يَسْتَأْذِنُ؟ فَقَالَ: ائْذَنْ لَهُ وَبَشِّرْهُ بِالْجَنَّةِ، فَأَقْبَلْتُ حَتَّى قُلْتُ لِأَبِي بَكْرٍ: ادْخُلْ، وَرَسُولُ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ يُبَشِّرُكَ بِالْجَنَّةِ، فَدَخَلَ أبوبكر فَجَلَسَ عَنْ يَمِينِ رَسُولِ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ مَعَهُ فِي القُفِّ، وَدَلَّى رِجْلَيْهِ فِي الْبِئْرِ كَمَا صَنَعَ النَّبِيُّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ وَكَشَفَ عَنْ سَاقَيْهِ، ثُمَّ رَجَعْتُ فَجَلَسْتُ، وَقَدْ تَرَكْتُ أَخِي يتوضأويلحقني، فَقُلْتُ: إِنْ يُرِدِ اللَّهُ بِفُلَانٍ خَيْرًا- يُرِيدُ أَخَاهُ - يَأْتِ بِهِ، فَإِذَا إِنْسَانٌ يُحَرِّكُ الْبَابَ، فَقُلْتُ: مَنْ هَذَا؟ فَقَالَ: عُمَرُ بْنُ الْخَطَّابِ، فَقُلْتُ: عَلَى رِسْلِكَ، ثُمَّ جِئْتُ رَسُولِ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ فَسَلَّمْتُ عَلَيْهِ، فَقُلْتُ: هَذَا عُمَرُ بن الْخَطَّابِ يَسْتَأْذِنُ؟ فَقَالَ: ائْذَنْ لَهُ وَبَشِّرْهُ بِالْجَنَّةِ.فَجِئْتُ فَقُلْتُ: ادْخُلْ وبشرك رَسُولُ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ بِالْجَنَّةِ، فَدَخَلَ فَجَلَسَ مَعَ رَسُولِ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ فِي القُفِّ عَنْ يَسَارِهِ، وَدَلَّى رِجْلَيْهِ فِي الْبِئْرِ، ثُمَّ رَجَعْتُ فَجَلَسْتُ، فَقُلْتُ: إِنْ يردالله بِفُلَانٍ خَيْرًا يَأْتِ بِهِ، فَجَاءَ انسان يُحَرِّكُ الْبَابَ، فَقُلْتُ مَنْ هَذَا؟ فَقَالَ: عُثْمَانُ بْنُ عَفَّانَ، فَقُلْتُ: عَلَى رِسْلِكَ، فَجِئْتُ إِلَى رَسُولِ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ فَأَخْبَرْتُهُ، فَقَالَ: ائْذَنْ لَهُ وَبَشِّرْهُ بِالْجَنَّةِ، عَلَى بَلْوَى تُصِيبُهُ.فجئته فَقُلْتُ لَهُ:ادْخُلِ، وبشرك رَسُولُ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ بِالْجَنَّةِ، عَلَى بَلْوَى تُصِيبُكَ، فَدَخَلَ فَوَجَدَ الْقُفَّ قَدْ مليء، فَجَلَسَ وجاهه مِنَ الشِّقِّ الْآخَرِ، قَالَ شَرِيكٌ: قَالَ سَعِيدُ بْنُ الْمُسَيَِّبِ: فَأَوَّلْتُهَا قُبُورَهُمْ."],"takhrij":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاري في فضائل الصحابة (3647)، ومسلم في فضائل الصحابة (2403-9) كلاهم عن محمد بن مسكين أبي الحسين، ثنا يحيى بن حسان، ثنا سليمان بن بلال، عن شريك بن أبي نمر، عن سعيد ابن المسيب، أخبرني أبو موسى الأشعري قال: فذكره.","grade":"متفق عليه","chapter_ar":"باب ما جاء في فضل الخلفاء الثلاثة: أبي بكر، وعمر، وعثمان","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب فضائل الصحابة وأخبارهم","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Agreed upon: Narrated by al-Bukhārī (3647) and Muslim (2403, no. 29).","chapter_en":"Reports Concerning the Virtues of the Three Caliphs: Abū Bakr, ʿUmar, and ʿUthmān","part_en":"The Book of the Virtues and Accounts of the Companions","group_ar":"مجموع ما جاء في فضل جماعات الصحابة","group_en":"Collected Reports Concerning the Virtues of Groups of the Companions","part_no":49,"group_no":12,"chapter_no":4,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Abū Mūsā narrated: I performed ablution in my house and then went out, saying to myself: “I will remain close to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and spend this entire day with him.” I went to the mosque and asked where the Prophet ﷺ was. The people said: “He went out and headed in that direction.” I followed his path, asking about him, until he entered the garden containing the Well of Arīs. I sat at its gate, which was made of palm branches, until the Messenger of Allah ﷺ relieved himself and performed ablution. I then went to him and found him sitting upon the stone ledge surrounding the Well of Arīs. He sat in the middle of it, uncovered his lower legs, and let them hang into the well. I greeted him and then returned to sit at the gate, saying: “Today I will serve as the gatekeeper of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ.” Abū Bakr came and pushed the gate. I asked: “Who is it?” He replied: “Abū Bakr.” I said: “Wait there.” I went to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and said: “O Messenger of Allah, Abū Bakr is requesting permission to enter.” He said: “Admit him and give him the glad tidings of Paradise.” I returned and said to Abū Bakr: “Enter, for the Messenger of Allah ﷺ gives you the glad tidings of Paradise.” Abū Bakr entered and sat to the Prophet’s right upon the stone ledge. He uncovered his lower legs and let them hang into the well, just as the Prophet ﷺ had done. I then returned to my place. I had left my brother performing ablution, intending to join me, so I thought: “Should Allah intend good for him, He will bring him here.” Then someone moved the gate. I asked: “Who is it?” He replied: “ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb.” I said: “Wait there.” I went to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, greeted him, and said: “ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb is requesting permission to enter.” He said: “Admit him and give him the glad tidings of Paradise.” I returned and said: “Enter, for the Messenger of Allah ﷺ gives you the glad tidings of Paradise.” He entered and sat to the Prophet’s left upon the stone ledge, and he let his legs hang into the well. I returned to the gate and again thought: “Should Allah intend good for my brother, He will bring him here.” Then someone came and moved the gate. I asked: “Who is it?” He replied: “ʿUthmān ibn ʿAffān.” I said: “Wait there.” I went to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and informed him. He said: “Admit him and give him the glad tidings of Paradise, along with a trial that will afflict him.” I returned and said: “Enter, for the Messenger of Allah ﷺ gives you the glad tidings of Paradise, along with a trial that will afflict you.” He entered and found that the stone ledge was full, so he sat facing them on the opposite side. Sharīk said that Saʿīd ibn al-Musayyib stated: “I interpreted this as referring to their graves.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"voc":["fazail",200],"full":1,"tks":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (3647)، ومسلم (2403-29)."},{"num":10003,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ أَبِي مُوسَى رَضِيَ اللَّهُ عَنْهُ قَالَ: كُنْتُ مَعَ النَّبِيِّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ فِي حَائِطٍ مِنْ حِيطَانِ الْمَدِينَةِ، فَجَاءَ رَجُلٌ فَاسْتَفْتَحَ، فَقَالَ النَّبِيُّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ: افْتَحْ لَهُ وَبَشِّرْهُ بِالْجَنَّةِ. فَفَتَحْتُ لَهُ، فَإِذَا أَبُو بَكْرٍ، فَبَشَّرْتُهُ بِمَا قَالَ النَّبِيُّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ، فَحَمِدَ اللَّهَ، ثُمَّ جَاءَ رَجُلٌ فَاسْتَفْتَحَ، فَقَالَ النَّبِيُّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ: افْتَحْ لَهُ وَبَشِّرْهُ بِالْجَنَّةِ. فَفَتَحْتُ لَهُ، فَإِذَا هُوَ عُمَرُ، فَأَخْبَرْتُهُ بِمَا قَالَ النَّبِيُّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ، فَحَمِدَ اللَّهَ، ثُمَّ اسْتَفْتَحَ رَجُلٌ، فَقَالَ لِي: افْتَحْ لَهُ وَبَشِّرْهُ بِالْجَنَّةِ عَلَى بَلْوَى تُصِيبُهُ. فَإِذَا عُثْمَانُ، فَأَخْبَرْتُهُ بِمَا قَالَ رَسُولُ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ، فَحَمِدَ اللَّهَ ثُمَّ قَالَ: اللَّهُ الْمُسْتَعَانُ."],"takhrij":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاري في فضائل الصحابة (3693)، ومسلم في فضائل الصحابة (2403-28) كلاهما من طريق عثمان بن غياث، ثنا أبو عثمان النهدي، عن أبي موسى الأشعري، فذكره.","grade":"متفق عليه","chapter_ar":"باب ما جاء في فضل الخلفاء الثلاثة: أبي بكر، وعمر، وعثمان","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب فضائل الصحابة وأخبارهم","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Authentic: Narrated by al-Bukhārī (3693) and Muslim (2403, no. 28).","chapter_en":"Reports Concerning the Virtues of the Three Caliphs: Abū Bakr, ʿUmar, and ʿUthmān","part_en":"The Book of the Virtues and Accounts of the Companions","group_ar":"مجموع ما جاء في فضل جماعات الصحابة","group_en":"Collected Reports Concerning the Virtues of Groups of the Companions","part_no":49,"group_no":12,"chapter_no":4,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Abū Mūsā narrated: I was with the Prophet ﷺ in one of the gardens of Madinah when a man came seeking permission to enter. The Prophet ﷺ said: “Open the gate for him and give him the glad tidings of Paradise.” I opened it, and it was Abū Bakr. I informed him of what the Prophet ﷺ had said, and he praised Allah. Then another man came requesting permission to enter. The Prophet ﷺ said: “Open the gate for him and give him the glad tidings of Paradise.” I opened it, and it was ʿUmar. I informed him of what the Prophet ﷺ had said, and he praised Allah. Then another man requested permission to enter. The Prophet ﷺ said to me: “Open the gate for him and give him the glad tidings of Paradise, along with a trial that will befall him.” It was ʿUthmān. I informed him of what the Messenger of Allah ﷺ had said. He praised Allah and then said: “Allah is the One whose help is sought.”"]},"buhuth":{"en":["Another wording recorded by Muslim states that ʿUthmān said:","“O Allah, grant me patience,”","or","“Allah is the One whose help is sought.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"voc":["fazail",201],"full":1,"dr":1,"tks":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (3693)، ومسلم (2403/28)."},{"num":10004,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ أَبِي مُوسَى رَضِيَ اللَّهُ عَنْهُ أَنَّ النَّبِيَّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ دَخَلَ حَائِطًا وَأَمَرَنِي بِحِفْظِ باب الْحَائِطِ، فَجَاءَ رَجُلٌ يَسْتَأْذِنُ، فَقَالَ: ائْذَنْ لَهُ وَبَشِّرْهُ بِالْجَنَّةِ. فَإِذَا أَبُو بَكْرٍ، ثُمَّ جَاءَ آخَرُ يَسْتَأْذِنُ، فَقَالَ: ائْذَنْ لَهُ وَبَشِّرْهُ بِالْجَنَّةِ. فَإِذَا عُمَرُ، ثُمَّ جَاءَ آخَرُ يَسْتَأْذِنُ، فَسَكَتَ هُنَيْهَةً، ثُمَّ قَالَ: ائْذَنْ لَهُ وَبَشِّرْهُ بِالْجَنَّةِ عَلَى بَلْوَى سَتُصِيبُهُ. فَإِذَا عُثْمَانُ بْنُ عَفَّانَ.","قَالَ حَمَّادٌ: وَحَدَّثَنَا عَاصِمٌ الْأَحْوَلُ وَعَلِيُّ بْنُ الْحَكَمِ سَمِعَا أَبَا عُثْمَانَ يُحَدِّثُ عَنْ أَبِي مو سى بِنَحْوِهِ، وَزَادَ فِيهِ عَاصِمٌ: \"أَنَّ النَّبِيَّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ كَانَ قَاعِدًا فِي مَكَانٍ فِيهِ مَاءٌ، قَدِ انْكَشَفَ عَنْ رُكْبَتَيْهِ أَوْ رُكْبَتِهِ فَلَمَّا دَخَلَ عُثْمَانُ غَطَّاهَا\"."],"takhrij":"صحيح: رواه البخاري في فضائل الصحابة (3695) عن سليمان بن حرب، ثنا حماد، عن أيوب، عن أبي عثمان، عن أبي موسى، أن النبي صلى الله عليه وسلم دخل حائطاً فذكره.","grade":"صحيح","chapter_ar":"باب ما جاء في فضل الخلفاء الثلاثة: أبي بكر، وعمر، وعثمان","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب فضائل الصحابة وأخبارهم","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Authentic: Narrated by al-Bukhārī (3695).","chapter_en":"Reports Concerning the Virtues of the Three Caliphs: Abū Bakr, ʿUmar, and ʿUthmān","part_en":"The Book of the Virtues and Accounts of the Companions","group_ar":"مجموع ما جاء في فضل جماعات الصحابة","group_en":"Collected Reports Concerning the Virtues of Groups of the Companions","part_no":49,"group_no":12,"chapter_no":4,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Abū Mūsā narrated: The Prophet ﷺ entered a garden and instructed me to guard its gate. A man came requesting permission to enter. The Prophet ﷺ said: “Let him enter and give him the glad tidings of Paradise.” It was Abū Bakr. Then another man came requesting permission. The Prophet ﷺ said: “Let him enter and give him the glad tidings of Paradise.” It was ʿUmar. Then another man came requesting permission. The Prophet ﷺ remained silent for a short while before saying: “Let him enter and give him the glad tidings of Paradise together with a trial that will befall him.”","It was ʿUthmān ibn ʿAffān. Ḥammād said: ʿĀṣim al-Aḥwal and ʿAlī ibn al-Ḥakam narrated to us that they heard Abū ʿUthmān narrating from Abū Mūsā a similar report. ʿĀṣim added: “The Prophet ﷺ was sitting in a place containing water, and his knees—or one of his knees—were uncovered. When ʿUthmān entered, he covered them.”"]},"buhuth":{"en":["Another wording recorded by al-Bukhārī states:","The Prophet ﷺ was in one of the gardens of Madinah holding a small stick with which he was striking the water and mud when a man came requesting permission to enter.","At the end of the narration it states:","“Then another man requested permission to enter. The Prophet ﷺ had been reclining, but he sat upright and said: ‘Open the gate for him and give him the glad tidings of Paradise together with a trial that will befall him.’”","Recorded by al-Bukhārī (6216)."]}},"tuhfa":{},"voc":["fazail",202],"full":1,"dr":1,"tks":"صحيح: رواه البخاري (3695)."},{"num":10005,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ أَبِي مُوسَى الأَشْعَرِيِّ، قَالَ: خَرَجَ النَّبِيُّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ إِلَى حَائِطٍ مِنْ حَوَائِطِ الْمَدِينَةِ، لِحَاجَتِهِ، وَخَرَجْتُ فِي إِثْرِهِ، فَلَمَّا دَخَلَ الْحَائِطَ جَلَسْتُ عَلَى بَابِهِ، وَقُلْتُ: لأَكُونَنَّ الْيَوْمَ بَوَّابَ النَّبِيِّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ وَلَمْ يَأْمُرْنِي، فَذَهَبَ النَّبِيُّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ، وَقَضَى حَاجَتَهُ، وَجَلَسَ عَلَى قُفِّ الْبِئْرِ، فَكَشَفَ عَنْ سَاقَيْهِ وَدَلاَّهُمَا فِي الْبِئْرِ، فَجَاءَ أَبُو بَكْرٍ، يَسْتَأْذِنُ عَلَيْهِ لِيَدْخُلَ فَقُلْتُ كَمَا أَنْتَ، حَتَّى أَسْتَأْذِنَ لَكَ، فَوَقَفَ فَجِئْتُ إِلَى النَّبِيِّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ فَقُلْتُ: يَا نَبِيَّ اللَّهِ، أَبُو بَكْرٍ يَسْتَأْذِنُ عَلَيْكَ. قَالَ: ائْذَنْ لَهُ، وَبَشِّرْهُ بِالْجَنَّةِ. فَدَخَلَ فَجَاءَ عَنْ يَمِينِ النَّبِيِّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ، فَكَشَفَ عَنْ سَاقَيْهِ وَدَلاَّهُمَا فِي الْبِئْرِ، فَجَاءَ عُمَرُ فَقُلْتُ: كَمَا أَنْتَ حَتَّى أَسْتَأْذِنَ لَكَ. فَقَالَ النَّبِيُّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ ائْذَنْ لَهُ، وَبَشِّرْهُ بِالْجَنَّةِ. فَجَاءَ عَنْ يَسَارِ النَّبِيِّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ فَكَشَفَ عَنْ سَاقَيْهِ فَدَلاَّهُمَا فِي الْبِئْرِ، فَامْتَلأَ الْقُفُّ فَلَمْ يَكُنْ فِيهِ مَجْلِسٌ، ثُمَّ جَاءَ عُثْمَانُ فَقُلْتُ كَمَا أَنْتَ حَتَّى أَسْتَأْذِنَ لَكَ. فَقَالَ النَّبِيُّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ ائْذَنْ لَهُ، وَبَشِّرْهُ بِالْجَنَّةِ، مَعَهَا بَلاَءٌ يُصِيبُهُ. فَدَخَلَ فَلَمْ يَجِدْ مَعَهُمْ مَجْلِسًا، فَتَحَوَّلَ حَتَّى جَاءَ مُقَابِلَهُمْ عَلَى شَفَةِ الْبِئْرِ، فَكَشَفَ عَنْ سَاقَيْهِ ثُمَّ دَلاَّهُمَا فِي الْبِئْرِ. فَجَعَلْتُ أَتَمَنَّى أَخًا لِي وَأَدْعُو اللَّهَ أَنْ يَأْتِيَ.","قَالَ ابْنُ الْمُسَيِّبِ فَتَأَوَّلْتُ ذَلِكَ قُبُورَهُمُ اجْتَمَعَتْ هَا ههنا، وَانْفَرَدَ عُثْمَانُ."],"takhrij":"صحيح: رواه البخاري في الفتن (7097) عن سعيد بن أبي مريم، أنا محمد بن جعفر، عن شريك بن عبدالله، عن سعيد بن المسيب، عن أبي موسى الأشعري قال: فذكره.","grade":"صحيح","chapter_ar":"باب ما جاء في فضل الخلفاء الثلاثة: أبي بكر، وعمر، وعثمان","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب فضائل الصحابة وأخبارهم","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Authentic: Narrated by al-Bukhārī (7097).","chapter_en":"Reports Concerning the Virtues of the Three Caliphs: Abū Bakr, ʿUmar, and ʿUthmān","part_en":"The Book of the Virtues and Accounts of the Companions","group_ar":"مجموع ما جاء في فضل جماعات الصحابة","group_en":"Collected Reports Concerning the Virtues of Groups of the Companions","part_no":49,"group_no":12,"chapter_no":4,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Abū Mūsā al-Ashʿarī narrated: One day the Prophet ﷺ went out to one of the gardens of Madinah to relieve himself, and I followed him. When he entered the garden, I sat at its gate and said to myself: “Today I will serve as the gatekeeper of the Prophet ﷺ,” even though he had not instructed me to do so. The Prophet ﷺ relieved himself and then sat upon the stone ledge surrounding the well. He uncovered his lower legs and let them hang into the well. Abū Bakr then came seeking permission to enter. I said: “Please wait until I ask permission for you.” He waited. I went to the Prophet ﷺ and said: “O Prophet of Allah, Abū Bakr is asking permission to enter.” He replied: “Let him enter and give him the glad tidings of Paradise.” Abū Bakr entered and sat on the Prophet’s right. He uncovered his lower legs and let them hang into the well. Then ʿUmar came. I said: “Please wait until I ask permission for you.” The Prophet ﷺ said: “Let him enter and give him the glad tidings of Paradise.” He entered, sat on the Prophet’s left, uncovered his lower legs, and let them hang into the well until the stone ledge became completely occupied. Then ʿUthmān came. I said: “Please wait until I ask permission for you.” The Prophet ﷺ said: “Let him enter and give him the glad tidings of Paradise together with a trial that will befall him.” He entered but found no place to sit with them, so he moved to the opposite edge of the well, uncovered his lower legs, and let them hang into the well. Meanwhile, I continued hoping that my brother would arrive and kept praying to Allah that he would come. Saʿīd ibn al-Musayyib said: “I interpreted this as symbolizing their graves: Abū Bakr, ʿUmar, and the Prophet ﷺ would be buried together, while ʿUthmān would be buried separately.”"]},"buhuth":{"en":["The author’s statement regarding Abū Mūsā’s words:","“I will serve today as the Prophet’s gatekeeper, although he had not instructed me.”","may be understood to mean that Abū Mūsā initially volunteered to guard the entrance without being instructed by the Prophet ﷺ. Later, the Prophet ﷺ formally directed him to guard the gate."]}},"tuhfa":{},"voc":["fazail",203],"full":1,"dr":1,"tks":"صحيح: رواه البخاري (7097)."},{"num":10006,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عن عَائِشَةَ قَالَتْ:  كَانَ رَسُولُ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ مُضْطَجِعًا فِي بَيْتِي، كَاشِفًا عَنْ فَخِذَيْهِ، أَوْ سَاقَيْهِ، فَاسْتَأْذَنَ أَبُو بَكْرٍ، فَأَذِنَ لَهُ، وَهُوَ عَلَى تِلْكَ الْحَالِ، فَتَحَدَّثَ، ثُمَّ اسْتَأْذَنَ عُمَرُ فَأَذِنَ لَهُ، وَهُوَ كَذَلِكَ فَتَحَدَّثَ، ثُمَّ اسْتَأْذَنَ عُثْمَانُ، فَجَلَسَ رَسُولُ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ وَسَوَّى ثِيَابَهُ - قَالَ مُحَمَّدٌ: وَلَا أَقُولُ ذَلِكَ فِي يَوْمٍ وَاحِدٍ - فَدَخَلَ فَتَحَدَّثَ، فَلَمَّا خَرَجَ قَالَتْ عَائِشَةُ: دَخَلَ أَبُو بَكْرٍ فَلَمْ تَهْتَشَّ لَهُ، وَلَمْ تُبَالِهِ، ثُمَّ دَخَلَ عُمَرُ فَلَمْ تَهْتَشَّ لَهُ وَلَمْ تُبَالِهِ، ثُمَّ دَخَلَ عُثْمَانُ فَجَلَسْتَ وَسَوَّيْتَ ثِيَابَكَ! فَقَالَ: أَلَا أَسْتَحْيِي مِنْ رَجُلٍ تَسْتَحْيِي مِنْهُ الْمَلَائِكَةُ."],"takhrij":"صحيح: رواه مسلم في فضائل الصحابة (2401) من طرق عن إسماعيل بن جعفر، عن محمد بن أبي حرملة، عن عطاء وسليمان ابني يسار وأبي سلمة بن عبد الرحمن أن عائشة قالت: فذكرته.","grade":"صحيح","chapter_ar":"باب ما جاء في فضل الخلفاء الثلاثة: أبي بكر، وعمر، وعثمان","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب فضائل الصحابة وأخبارهم","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Authentic: Narrated by Muslim (2401).","chapter_en":"Reports Concerning the Virtues of the Three Caliphs: Abū Bakr, ʿUmar, and ʿUthmān","part_en":"The Book of the Virtues and Accounts of the Companions","group_ar":"مجموع ما جاء في فضل جماعات الصحابة","group_en":"Collected Reports Concerning the Virtues of Groups of the Companions","part_no":49,"group_no":12,"chapter_no":4,"content":{"translation":{"en":["ʿĀ’ishah narrated: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was reclining in my house with his thighs—or his lower legs—uncovered. Abū Bakr sought permission to enter, and the Prophet ﷺ admitted him while remaining in that state. They spoke together. Then ʿUmar sought permission to enter, and the Prophet ﷺ admitted him while remaining in the same state. They spoke together. Then ʿUthmān sought permission to enter. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ sat upright and adjusted his clothing. Muḥammad said: “I do not say that all of this occurred on the same day.” ʿUthmān entered and spoke with him. After he left, ʿĀ’ishah said: “Abū Bakr entered, yet you did not become particularly animated or concerned by his entrance. Then ʿUmar entered, and you did not become particularly animated or concerned by his entrance. But when ʿUthmān entered, you sat upright and adjusted your clothing.” The Prophet ﷺ replied: “Should I not feel modest before a man before whom the angels feel modest?”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"voc":["fazail",204],"full":1,"rep":[15380],"tks":"صحيح: رواه مسلم (2401)."},{"num":10007,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ عَائِشَةَ زوج النَّبِيِّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ وعثمان حَدَّثَاهُ أَنَّ أَبَا بَكْرٍ اسْتَأْذَنَ عَلَى رَسُولِ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ وَهُوَ مُضْطَجِعٌ عَلَى فِرَاشِهِ، لَابِسٌ مِرْط عَائِشَةَ، فَأَذِنَ لِأَبِي بَكْرٍ وَهُوَ كَذَلِكَ، فَقَضَى إِلَيْهِ حَاجَتَهُ ثُمَّ انْصَرَفَ، ثُمَّ اسْتَأْذَنَ عُمَرُ، فَأَذِنَ لَهُ وهوعلى تِلْكَ الْحَالِ فَقَضَى إِلَيْهِ حَاجَتَهُ، ثُمَّ انْصَرَفَ، قَالَ عُثْمَانُ: ثُمَّ اسْتَأْذَنْتُ عَلَيْهِ فَجَلَسَ، وَقَالَ لِعَائِشَةَ: اجْمَعِي عَلَيْكِ ثِيَابَكِ.فَقَضَيْتُ إِلَيْهِ حَاجَتِي ثُمَّ انْصَرَفْتُ، فَقَالَتْ عَائِشَةُ: يَا رَسُولَ اللَّهِ مَالِي لَمْ أَرَكَ فَزِعْتَ لِأَبِي بكروعمر رَضِيَ اللَّهُ عَنْهُمَا، كَمَا فَزِعْتَ لِعُثْمَانَ؟ قَالَ رَسُولُ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ: إِنَّ عُثْمَانَ رَجُلٌ حييّ، وَإِنِّي خَشِيتُ، إنْ أَذِنْتُ لَهُ عَلَى تِلْكَ الْحَالِ، أَنْ لَا يَبْلُغَ إليَّ فِي حَاجَتِهِ."],"takhrij":"صحيح: رواه مسلم في فضائل الصحابة (2402) عن عبدالملك بن شعيب بن الليث بن سعد، ثني أبي، عن جدي، ثني عقيل بن خالد، عن ابن شهاب، عن يحيى بن سعيد بن العاص، أن سعيد بن العاص أخبره أن عائشة زوج النبي صلى الله عليه وسلم وعثمان حدثاه فذكراه.","grade":"صحيح","chapter_ar":"باب ما جاء في فضل الخلفاء الثلاثة: أبي بكر، وعمر، وعثمان","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب فضائل الصحابة وأخبارهم","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Authentic: Narrated by Muslim (2402).","chapter_en":"Reports Concerning the Virtues of the Three Caliphs: Abū Bakr, ʿUmar, and ʿUthmān","part_en":"The Book of the Virtues and Accounts of the Companions","group_ar":"مجموع ما جاء في فضل جماعات الصحابة","group_en":"Collected Reports Concerning the Virtues of Groups of the Companions","part_no":49,"group_no":12,"chapter_no":4,"content":{"translation":{"en":["ʿĀ’ishah, the wife of the Prophet ﷺ, and ʿUthmān narrated: Abū Bakr sought permission to enter upon the Messenger of Allah ﷺ while he was reclining upon his bed and wearing ʿĀ’ishah’s woolen garment. The Prophet ﷺ permitted Abū Bakr to enter while remaining in that state. Abū Bakr presented his need and then departed. Then ʿUmar sought permission to enter. The Prophet ﷺ admitted him while remaining in the same state. ʿUmar presented his need and then departed. ʿUthmān said: Then I sought permission to enter. The Prophet ﷺ sat upright and said to ʿĀ’ishah: “Gather your garments around yourself.” I presented my need to him and then departed. ʿĀ’ishah asked: “O Messenger of Allah, why did I not see you become concerned about Abū Bakr and ʿUmar, may Allah be pleased with them both, as you became concerned about ʿUthmān?” The Messenger of Allah ﷺ replied: “ʿUthmān is an exceedingly modest man, and I feared that if I admitted him while I was in that state, he would not fully express his need to me.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"voc":["fazail",205],"full":1,"tks":"صحيح: رواه مسلم (2402)."},{"num":10008,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ مُحَمَّدِ بْنِ سِيرِينَ، أَنَّ رَجُلًا، بِالْكُوفَةِ، شَهِدَ أَنَّ عُثْمَانَ رَضِيَ اللَّهُ، عَنْهُ قُتِلَ شَهِيدًا، فَأَخَذَتْهُ الزَّبَانِيَةُ فَرَفَعُوهُ إِلَى عَلِيٍّ رَضِيَ اللَّهُ، عَنْهُ، وَقَالُوا: لَوْلَا أَنْ تَنْهَانَا - أَوْ نَهَيْتَنَا - أَنْ لَا نَقْتُلَ أَحَدًا لَقَتَلْنَاهُ. هَذَا زَعَمَ أَنَّهُ يَشْهَدُ أَنَّ عُثْمَانَ رَضِيَ اللَّهُ عَنْهُ قُتِلَ شَهِيدًا، فَقَالَ الرَّجُلُ لِعَلِيٍّ، رَضِيَ اللَّهُ عَنْهُ: وَأَنْتَ تَشْهَدُ. أَتَذْكُرُ أَنِّي أَتَيْتُ رَسُولَ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ فَسَأَلْتُهُ فَأَعْطَانِي، وَأَتَيْتُ أَبَا بَكْرٍ رَضِيَ اللَّهُ عَنْهُ فَسَأَلْتُهُ فَأَعْطَانِي. وَأَتَيْتُ عُمَرَ رَضِيَ اللَّهُ عَنْهُ فَسَأَلْتُهُ فَأَعْطَانِي، وَأَتَيْتُ عُثْمَانَ رَضِيَ اللَّهُ عَنْهُ فَسَأَلْتُهُ فَأَعْطَانِي، قَالَ: فَأَتَيْتُ رَسُولَ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ فَقُلْتُ: يَا رَسُولَ اللَّهِ، ادْعُ اللَّهَ أَنْ يُبَارِكَ لِي، فَقَالَ النَّبِيُّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ: كَيْفَ لَا يُبَارَكُ لَكَ وَأَعْطَاكَ نَبِيٌّ وَصِدِّيقٌ، وَشَهِيدَانِ، وَأَعْطَاكَ نَبِيٌّ وَصِدِّيقٌ وَشَهِيدَانِ، وَأَعْطَاكَ نَبِيٌّ وَصِدِّيقٌ وَشَهِيدَانِ؟"],"takhrij":"صحيح: رواه أبو يعلى (1601) عن هدبة، حدثنا همام، عن قتادة، عن محمد بن سيرين قال: فذكره.","grade":"صحيح","chapter_ar":"باب ما جاء في فضل الخلفاء الثلاثة: أبي بكر، وعمر، وعثمان","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب فضائل الصحابة وأخبارهم","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Authentic: Narrated by Abū Yaʿlā (1601).","chapter_en":"Reports Concerning the Virtues of the Three Caliphs: Abū Bakr, ʿUmar, and ʿUthmān","part_en":"The Book of the Virtues and Accounts of the Companions","group_ar":"مجموع ما جاء في فضل جماعات الصحابة","group_en":"Collected Reports Concerning the Virtues of Groups of the Companions","part_no":49,"group_no":12,"chapter_no":4,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Muḥammad ibn Sīrīn narrated: A man in Kūfah testified that ʿUthmān, may Allah be pleased with him, had been killed as a martyr. Some harsh guards seized him and brought him before ʿAlī, may Allah be pleased with him. They said: “Were it not that you have forbidden us—or had forbidden us—from killing anyone, we would have killed him. He claims to testify that ʿUthmān was killed as a martyr.” The man said to ʿAlī: “You also bear witness to this. Do you remember that I came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and asked him, and he gave to me; then I came to Abū Bakr and asked him, and he gave to me; then I came to ʿUmar and asked him, and he gave to me; and then I came to ʿUthmān, may Allah be pleased with him, and asked him, and he gave to me?” He continued: I came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and said: “O Messenger of Allah, supplicate to Allah to bless me.” The Prophet ﷺ replied: “How could you not be blessed when a prophet, a truthful one, and two martyrs have given to you? A prophet, a truthful one, and two martyrs have given to you. A prophet, a truthful one, and two martyrs have given to you.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"voc":["fazail",206],"full":1,"dr":1,"tks":"صحيح: رواه أبو يعلى (1601)."},{"num":10009,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنِ الْأَسْوَدِ بْنِ هِلَالٍ، عَنْ رَجُلٍ، مِنْ قَوْمِهِ قَالَ: كَانَ يَقُولُ فِي خِلَافَةِ عُمَرَ بْنِ الْخَطَّابِ: لَا يَمُوتُ عُثْمَانُ حَتَّى يُسْتَخْلَفَ، قُلْنَا: مِنْ أَيْنَ تَعْلَمُ ذَلِكَ؟ قَالَ: سَمِعْتُ رَسُولَ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ يَقُولُ: رَأَيْتُ اللَّيْلَةَ فِي الْمَنَامِ كَأَنَّهُ ثَلَاثَةٌ مِنْ أَصْحَابِي وُزِنُوا، فَوُزِنَ أَبُو بَكْرٍ، فَوَزَنَ، ثُمَّ وُزِنَ عُمَرُ، فَوَزَنَ، ثُمَّ وُزِنَ عُثْمَانُ، فَنَقَصَ صَاحِبُنَا، وَهُوَ صَالِحٌ."],"takhrij":"صحيح: رواه أحمد (16604) عن أبي النضر قال: ثنا شيبان، عن أشعث، عن الأسود بن هلال ، عن رجل من قومه قال: فذكره.","grade":"صحيح","chapter_ar":"باب ما جاء في فضل الخلفاء الثلاثة: أبي بكر، وعمر، وعثمان","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب فضائل الصحابة وأخبارهم","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Authentic: Narrated by Aḥmad (16604).","chapter_en":"Reports Concerning the Virtues of the Three Caliphs: Abū Bakr, ʿUmar, and ʿUthmān","part_en":"The Book of the Virtues and Accounts of the Companions","group_ar":"مجموع ما جاء في فضل جماعات الصحابة","group_en":"Collected Reports Concerning the Virtues of Groups of the Companions","part_no":49,"group_no":12,"chapter_no":4,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Al-Aswad ibn Hilāl narrated from a man of his people who used to say during the caliphate of ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb: “ʿUthmān will not die until he becomes caliph.” We asked him: “How do you know that?” He replied: I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: “Last night, I saw in a dream that three of my Companions were weighed. Abū Bakr was weighed and proved weighty. Then ʿUmar was weighed and proved weighty. Then ʿUthmān was weighed, and our companion fell short, though he is righteous.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"voc":["fazail",207],"full":1,"dr":1,"tks":"صحيح: رواه أحمد (16604)."},{"num":10010,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ عبدالله بن عمرو قَالَ: كُنْتُ مَعَ رَسُولِ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ فَجَاءَ أَبُو بَكْرٍ فَاسْتَأْذَنَ، فَقَالَ: ائْذَنْ لَهُ، وَبَشِّرْهُ بِالْجَنَّةِ.ثُمَّ جَاءَ عُمَرُ فَاسْتَأْذَنَ، فَقَالَ: ائْذَنْ لَهُ، وَبَشِّرْهُ بِالْجَنَّةِ.ثُمَّ جَاءَ عُثْمَانُ فَاسْتَأْذَنَ، فَقَالَ: ائْذَنْ لَهُ، وَبَشِّرْهُ بِالْجَنَّةِ.قَالَ: قُلْتُ فَأَيْنَ أَنَا؟ قَالَ: أَنْتَ مَعَ أَبِيكَ."],"takhrij":"صحيح: رواه أحمد (6548)، والطبراني في الكبير (13/615-616) كلاهما من طريق همام، عن قتادة، عن ابن سريرن ومحمد بن عبيد، عن عبدالله بن عمرو قال: فذكره.","grade":"صحيح","chapter_ar":"باب ما جاء في فضل الخلفاء الثلاثة: أبي بكر، وعمر، وعثمان","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب فضائل الصحابة وأخبارهم","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Authentic: Narrated by Aḥmad (6548) and al-Ṭabarānī in al-Muʿjam al-Kabīr (13/615–616).","chapter_en":"Reports Concerning the Virtues of the Three Caliphs: Abū Bakr, ʿUmar, and ʿUthmān","part_en":"The Book of the Virtues and Accounts of the Companions","group_ar":"مجموع ما جاء في فضل جماعات الصحابة","group_en":"Collected Reports Concerning the Virtues of Groups of the Companions","part_no":49,"group_no":12,"chapter_no":4,"content":{"translation":{"en":["ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿAmr narrated: I was with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ when Abū Bakr came and sought permission to enter. The Prophet ﷺ said: “Admit him and give him the glad tidings of Paradise.” Then ʿUmar came and sought permission to enter. The Prophet ﷺ said: “Admit him and give him the glad tidings of Paradise.” Then ʿUthmān came and sought permission to enter. The Prophet ﷺ said: “Admit him and give him the glad tidings of Paradise.” I asked: “Then where will I be?” He replied: “You will be with your father.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"voc":["fazail",208],"full":1,"dr":1,"tks":"صحيح: رواه أحمد (6548)، والطبراني في الكبير (13/615-616)."},{"num":10011,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ أَبِيهِ، أَنَّ رَسُولَ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ كَانَ جَالِسًا عَلَى حِرَاءٍ، وَمَعَهُ أَبُو بَكْرٍ، وَعُمَرُ، وَعُثْمَانُ فَتَحَرَّكَ الْجَبَلُ، فَقَالَ رَسُولُ اللَّهِ: صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ: اثْبُتْ حِرَاءُ؛ فَإِنَّهُ لَيْسَ عَلَيْكَ إِلَّا نَبِيٌّ أَوْ صِدِّيقٌ، أَوْ شَهِيدٌ."],"takhrij":"حسن: رواه أحمد (22939)، وابن أبي عاصم في السنة (1443) كلاهما من طريق علي بن الحسن بن شقيق، أخبرنا الحسين بن واقد، عن عبدالله بن بريدة، عن أبيه فذكره.","grade":"حسن","chapter_ar":"باب ما جاء في فضل الخلفاء الثلاثة: أبي بكر، وعمر، وعثمان","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب فضائل الصحابة وأخبارهم","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Hasan: Narrated by Aḥmad (22939) and Ibn Abī ʿĀṣim in al-Sunnah (1443).","chapter_en":"Reports Concerning the Virtues of the Three Caliphs: Abū Bakr, ʿUmar, and ʿUthmān","part_en":"The Book of the Virtues and Accounts of the Companions","group_ar":"مجموع ما جاء في فضل جماعات الصحابة","group_en":"Collected Reports Concerning the Virtues of Groups of the Companions","part_no":49,"group_no":12,"chapter_no":4,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Buraydah ibn al-Ḥuṣayb narrated: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was sitting upon Mount Ḥirāʾ with Abū Bakr, ʿUmar, and ʿUthmān when the mountain moved. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Be firm, Ḥirāʾ, for upon you there is only a prophet, a truthful one, or a martyr.”"]},"buhuth":{"en":["The wording “Ḥirāʾ” is incorrect. The correct wording is “Uḥud,” as established in the authentic narrations."]}},"tuhfa":{},"voc":["fazail",209],"full":1,"dr":1,"tks":"حسن: رواه أحمد (22939)، وابن أبي عاصم في السنة (1443)، وقوله: “حراء” غير صحيح، والصواب: “أحد” كما في الأحاديث الصحيحة."},{"num":10012,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ سَهْلِ بْنِ سَعْدٍ: ارْتَجَّ أُحُدٌ، وَعَلَيْهِ النَّبِيُّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ وَأَبُو بَكْرٍ وَعُمَرُ وَعُثْمَانُ، فَقَالَ النَّبِيُّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ: اثْبُتْ أُحُدُ، مَا عَلَيْكَ إِلَّا نَبِيٌّ وَصِدِّيقٌ وَشَهِيدَانِ."],"takhrij":"صحيح: رواه أحمد (22811)، وعبيد بن حميد (449)، وابن أبي عاصم في السنة (1444)، وابن حبان (6492)، والبيهقي في الدلائل (2401) كلهم من طريق عبدالرزاق، أخبرنا معمر، عن أبي حازم، عن سهل بن سعد قال: فذكره.","grade":"صحيح","chapter_ar":"باب ما جاء في فضل الخلفاء الثلاثة: أبي بكر، وعمر، وعثمان","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب فضائل الصحابة وأخبارهم","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Authentic: Narrated by Aḥmad (22811), Ibn Abī ʿĀṣim in al-Sunnah (1444), and Ibn Ḥibbān (6492).","chapter_en":"Reports Concerning the Virtues of the Three Caliphs: Abū Bakr, ʿUmar, and ʿUthmān","part_en":"The Book of the Virtues and Accounts of the Companions","group_ar":"مجموع ما جاء في فضل جماعات الصحابة","group_en":"Collected Reports Concerning the Virtues of Groups of the Companions","part_no":49,"group_no":12,"chapter_no":4,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Sahl ibn Saʿd narrated: Mount Uḥud shook while the Prophet ﷺ, Abū Bakr, ʿUmar, and ʿUthmān were upon it. The Prophet ﷺ said: “Be firm, Uḥud. Upon you are only a prophet, a truthful one, and two martyrs.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"voc":["fazail",210],"full":1,"dr":1,"tks":"صحيح: رواه أحمد (22811)، وابن أبي عاصم في السنة (1444)، وابن حبان (6492)."},{"num":10013,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ أَبِي بَكْرَةَ، أَنَّ النَّبِيَّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ قَالَ ذَاتَ يَوْمٍ: مَنْ رَأَى مِنْكُمْ رُؤْيَا. فَقَالَ رَجُلٌ: أَنَا رَأَيْتُ كَأَنَّ مِيزَانًا نَزَلَ مِنَ السَّمَاءِ، فَوُزِنْتَ أَنْتَ وَأَبُو بَكْرٍ، فَرُجِحْتَ أَنْتَ بِأَبِي بَكْرٍ، وَوُزِنَ عُمَرُ وَأَبُو بَكْرٍ فَرُجِحَ أَبُو بَكْرٍ، وَوُزِنَ عُمَرُ وَعُثْمَانُ، فَرُجِحَ عُمَرُ، ثُمَّ رُفِعَ الْمِيزَانُ، فَرَأَيْنَا الْكَرَاهِيَةَ فِي وَجْهِ رَسُولِ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ."],"takhrij":"حسن: رواه أبو داود (4634)، والترمذي (2287)، والنسائي في الكبرى (8080)، والحاكم (4437)،(4/393-394) كلهم من طريق محمد بن عبدالله الأنصاري، حدثنا أشعث بن عبدالملك الحمراني، عن الحسن، عن أبي بكرة فذكره.","grade":"حسن","chapter_ar":"باب ما جاء في فضل الخلفاء الثلاثة: أبي بكر، وعمر، وعثمان","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب فضائل الصحابة وأخبارهم","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Hasan: Narrated by Abū Dāwūd (4634), al-Tirmidhī (2287), al-Nasā’ī in al-Sunan al-Kubrā (8080), and al-Ḥākim (4437).","chapter_en":"Reports Concerning the Virtues of the Three Caliphs: Abū Bakr, ʿUmar, and ʿUthmān","part_en":"The Book of the Virtues and Accounts of the Companions","group_ar":"مجموع ما جاء في فضل جماعات الصحابة","group_en":"Collected Reports Concerning the Virtues of Groups of the Companions","part_no":49,"group_no":12,"chapter_no":4,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Abū Bakrah narrated: One day, the Prophet ﷺ asked: “Who among you has seen a dream?” A man replied: “I have. I saw as though a scale descended from heaven. You and Abū Bakr were weighed, and you outweighed Abū Bakr. Then Abū Bakr and ʿUmar were weighed, and Abū Bakr outweighed ʿUmar. Then ʿUmar and ʿUthmān were weighed, and ʿUmar outweighed ʿUthmān. Then the scale was raised.” We then saw displeasure upon the face of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ."]}},"tuhfa":{},"voc":["fazail",211],"full":1,"dr":1,"rep":[11729],"tks":"حسن: رواه أبو داود (4634)، والترمذي (2287)، والنسائي في الكبرى (8080)، والحاكم (4437)."},{"num":10014,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ سَمُرَةَ بْنِ جُنْدُبٍ، أَنَّ رَجُلاً، قَالَ: يَا رَسُولَ اللَّهِ إِنِّي رَأَيْتُ كَأَنَّ دَلْوًا دُلِّيَ مِنَ السَّمَاءِ فَجَاءَ أَبُو بَكْرٍ، فَأَخَذَ بِعَرَاقِيهَا فَشَرِبَ شُرْبًا ضَعِيفًا، ثُمَّ جَاءَ عُمَرُ فَأَخَذَ بِعَرَاقِيهَا فَشَرِبَ حَتَّى تَضَلَّعَ، ثُمَّ جَاءَ عُثْمَانُ فَأَخَذَ بِعَرَاقِيهَا فَشَرِبَ حَتَّى تَضَلَّعَ، ثُمَّ جَاءَ عَلِيٌّ فَأَخَذَ بِعَرَاقِيهَا فَانْتَشَطَتْ وَانْتَضَحَ عَلَيْهِ مِنْهَا شَىْءٌ."],"takhrij":"حسن: رواه أبو داود (4637)، وأحمد (20242) كلاهما من طريق حماد بن سلمة، عن أشعث بن عبد الرحمن، عن أبيه، عن سمرة بن جندب قال: فذكره.","grade":"حسن","chapter_ar":"باب ما جاء في فضل الخلفاء الأربعة","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب فضائل الصحابة وأخبارهم","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Hasan: Narrated by Abū Dāwūd (4637) and Aḥmad (20242).","chapter_en":"Reports Concerning the Virtues of the Four Caliphs","part_en":"The Book of the Virtues and Accounts of the Companions","group_ar":"مجموع ما جاء في فضل جماعات الصحابة","group_en":"Collected Reports Concerning the Virtues of Groups of the Companions","part_no":49,"group_no":12,"chapter_no":5,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Samurah ibn Jundub narrated that a man said: “O Messenger of Allah, I saw in a dream that a bucket was lowered from the sky. Abū Bakr came, took hold of its crosspieces, and drank a small amount. Then ʿUmar came, took hold of its crosspieces, and drank until he was fully satisfied. Then ʿUthmān came, took hold of its crosspieces, and drank until he was fully satisfied. Then ʿAlī came and took hold of its crosspieces, but the bucket was suddenly pulled upward, and some of its water splashed upon him.”"]},"buhuth":{"en":["The word “دُلِّي” means that it was lowered.","The expression “بعراقيها” refers to the wooden crosspieces of the bucket to which the rope is attached.","The word “فانتُشِطت” means that it was suddenly pulled toward the sky and swiftly raised.","The word “انتضح” refers to drops or splashes of water falling upon a garment or something similar."]}},"tuhfa":{},"voc":["fazail",212],"full":1,"dr":1,"tks":"حسن: رواه أبو داود (4637)، وأحمد (20242)."},{"num":10015,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ أَبِي هُرَيْرَةَ  أَنَّ رَسُولَ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ كَانَ عَلَى حِرَاءٍ هُوَ وَأَبُو بَكْرٍ، وَعُمَرُ، وَعُثْمَانُ، وَعَلِيٌّ، وَطَلْحَةُ، وَالزُّبَيْرُ، فَتَحَرَّكَتِ الصَّخْرَةُ، فَقَالَ رَسُولُ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ: اهْدَأْ، فَمَا عَلَيْكَ إِلَّا نَبِيٌّ، أَوْ صِدِّيقٌ، أَوْ شَهِيدٌ."],"takhrij":"صحيح: رواه مسلم في فضائل الصحابة (2417-50) عن قتيبة بن سعيد، ثنا عبدالعزيز بن محمد، عن سهيل، عن أبيه، عن أبي هريرة فذكره.","grade":"صحيح","chapter_ar":"باب في فضل الخلفاء الأربعة وطلحة والزبير","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب فضائل الصحابة وأخبارهم","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Authentic: Narrated by Muslim (2417, no. 50).","chapter_en":"The Virtues of the Four Caliphs, Ṭalḥah, and al-Zubayr","part_en":"The Book of the Virtues and Accounts of the Companions","group_ar":"مجموع ما جاء في فضل جماعات الصحابة","group_en":"Collected Reports Concerning the Virtues of Groups of the Companions","part_no":49,"group_no":12,"chapter_no":6,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Abū Hurayrah narrated: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was upon Mount Ḥirāʾ together with Abū Bakr, ʿUmar, ʿUthmān, ʿAlī, Ṭalḥah, and al-Zubayr. The rock moved beneath them, so the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Be still, for upon you there is only a prophet, a truthful one, or a martyr.”"]},"buhuth":{"en":["As for the mention of Ḥirāʾ in this narration, the correct name is Uḥud, as established in the other authentic narrations."]}},"tuhfa":{},"voc":["fazail",213],"full":1,"dr":1,"tks":"صحيح: رواه مسلم (2417-50)."},{"num":10016,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عن سَعِيدِ بْنِ زَيْدٍ قَالَ: فَأَنَا أَشْهَدُ عَلَى رَسُولِ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ، بِمَا سَمِعَتِ أذُنَايَ وَوَعَاهُ قَلْبِي مِنْ رَسُولِ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ، فَإِنِّي لَمْ أَكُنِ أرْوِي عَنْهُ كَذِبًا يَسْأَلُنِي عَنْهُ إِذَا لَقِيتُهُ، أَنَّهُ قَالَ: أَبُو بَكْرٍ فِي الْجَنَّةِ، وَعُمَرُ فِي الْجَنَّةِ، وَعَلِيٌّ فِي الْجَنَّةِ، وَعُثْمَانُ فِي الْجَنَّةِ، وَطَلْحَةُ فِي الْجَنَّةِ، وَالزُّبَيْرُ فِي الْجَنَّةِ، وَعَبْدُ الرَّحْمَنِ فِي الْجَنَّةِ، وَسَعْدُ بْنُ مَالِكٍ فِي الْجَنَّةِ، وَتَاسِعُ الْمُؤْمِنِينَ فِي الْجَنَّةِ لَوْ شِئْتُ أَنْ أُسَمِّيَهُ لَسَمَّيْتُهُ، قَالَ: فَضَجَّ أَهْلُ الْمَسْجِدِ يُنَاشِدُونَهُ يَا صَاحِبَ رَسُولِ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ مَنِ التَّاسِعُ؟ قَالَ: نَاشَدْتُمُونِي بِاللهِ، وَاللهِ عَظِيمِ أَنَا تَاسِعُ الْمُؤْمِنِينَ، وَرَسُولُ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ، الْعَاشِرُ، ثُمَّ أَتْبَعَ ذَلِكَ يَمِينًا، قَالَ: وَاللهِ لَمَشْهَدٌ شَهِدَهُ رَجُلٌ يُغَبِّرُ فِيهِ وَجْهَهُ مَعَ رَسُولِ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ، أَفْضَلُ مِنْ عَمَلِ أَحَدِكُمْ. وَلَوْ عُمِّرَ عُمُرَ نُوحٍ عَلَيْهِ السلام."],"takhrij":"صحيح: رواه أحمد (1629) – واللفظ له -، وأبو داود (4650)، وابن ماجه (133) كلهم من حديث صدقة بن المثنى النخعي، حدثني جدي رياح بن الحارث أن المغيرة بن شعبة كان في المسجد الأكبر، وعنده أهل الكوفة عن يمينه، وعن يساره، فجائه رجل يدعى سعيد بن زيد، فحياه المغيرة وأجلسه عند رجليه عالسرير.فجاء رجل من أهل المغيرة فاستقبل المغيرة، فسب وسب، فقال: من يسب هذا يا مغيرة؟ قال: يسب علي بن أبي طالب، قال: يا مغير بن شعب، يا مغير بن شعب- ثلاثا- ألا أسمع أصحاب رسول الله صلى الله عليه وسلم يسبون عندك؟ لا تنكر ولا تغير، فذكر الحديث.وإسناده صحيح.","grade":"صحيح","chapter_ar":"باب ما جاء في فضل العشرة المبشرين بالجنة","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب فضائل الصحابة وأخبارهم","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Authentic: Narrated by Aḥmad (1629), whose wording is cited here, Abū Dāwūd (4650), and Ibn Mājah (133).","chapter_en":"Reports Concerning the Virtues of the Ten Who Were Given the Glad Tidings of Paradise","part_en":"The Book of the Virtues and Accounts of the Companions","group_ar":"مجموع ما جاء في فضل جماعات الصحابة","group_en":"Collected Reports Concerning the Virtues of Groups of the Companions","part_no":49,"group_no":12,"chapter_no":7,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Saʿīd ibn Zayd said: I bear witness concerning the Messenger of Allah ﷺ to that which my ears heard and my heart retained from him. I would never narrate a lie concerning him for which he might question me when I meet him. He said: “Abū Bakr is in Paradise, ʿUmar is in Paradise, ʿAlī is in Paradise, ʿUthmān is in Paradise, Ṭalḥah is in Paradise, al-Zubayr is in Paradise, ʿAbd al-Raḥmān is in Paradise, Saʿd ibn Mālik is in Paradise, and the ninth believer is in Paradise.” Saʿīd added: “Were I to wish to name him, I could do so.” The people in the mosque raised their voices and implored him: “O Companion of the Messenger of Allah, who is the ninth?” He replied: “You have adjured me by Allah—and Allah is Most Great—I am the ninth believer, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ is the tenth.” He then followed this with an oath, saying: “By Allah, a single battle attended by a man, in which his face became covered with dust alongside the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, is better than the lifetime deeds of any one of you, even were he granted the lifespan of Nūḥ, peace be upon him.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"voc":["fazail",214],"full":1,"dr":1,"tks":"صحيح: رواه أحمد (1629) - واللفظ له -، وأبو داود (4650)، وابن ماجه (133)."},{"num":10017,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عن عَبْدِ اللَّهِ بن عُمَرَ قَالَ: قَالَ: قَالَ رَسُولُ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ: عَشَرَةٌ مِنْ قُرَيْشٍ فِي الْجَنَّةِ: أَبُو بَكْرٍ وَعُمَرُ فِي الْجَنَّةِ، وَعُثْمَانُ فِي الْجَنَّةِ، وَعَلِيٌّ فِي الْجَنَّةِ، وَطَلْحَةُ فِي الْجَنَّةِ، وَالزُّبَيْرُ فِي الْجَنَّةِ، وَسَعْدٌ فِي الْجَنَّةِ، وَسَعِيدٌ فِي الْجَنَّةِ، وَعَبْدُ الرَحْمَنِ بْنُ عَوْفٍ فِي الْجَنَّةِ، وَأَبُو عُبَيْدَةَ بْنُ الْجَرَّاحِ فِي الْجَنَّةِ."],"takhrij":"حسن: رواه الطبراني في الكبير (13823) وفي الأوسط (2222) وفي الصغير sh13068(62) من طرق عن حامد بن يحيي البلخي، عن سُعير بن الخِمس، عن حبيب بن أبي ثابت، عن ابن عمر فذكره.","grade":"حسن","chapter_ar":"باب ما جاء في فضل العشرة المبشرين بالجنة","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب فضائل الصحابة وأخبارهم","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Hasan: Narrated by al-Ṭabarānī in al-Muʿjam al-Kabīr (13823), al-Muʿjam al-Awsaṭ (2222), and al-Muʿjam al-Ṣaghīr (62).","chapter_en":"Reports Concerning the Virtues of the Ten Who Were Given the Glad Tidings of Paradise","part_en":"The Book of the Virtues and Accounts of the Companions","group_ar":"مجموع ما جاء في فضل جماعات الصحابة","group_en":"Collected Reports Concerning the Virtues of Groups of the Companions","part_no":49,"group_no":12,"chapter_no":7,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Ibn ʿUmar narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Ten men from Quraysh are in Paradise: Abū Bakr is in Paradise, ʿUmar is in Paradise, ʿUthmān is in Paradise, ʿAlī is in Paradise, Ṭalḥah is in Paradise, al-Zubayr is in Paradise, Saʿd and Saʿīd are in Paradise, ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn ʿAwf is in Paradise, and Abū ʿUbaydah ibn al-Jarrāḥ is in Paradise.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"voc":["fazail",215],"full":1,"dr":1,"tks":"حسن: رواه الطبراني في الكبير (13823)، وفي الأوسط (2222)، وفي الصغير sh13068(62)."},{"num":10018,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عن عَائِشَةَ، وَسُئِلَتْ: مَنْ كَانَ رَسُولُ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ مُسْتَخْلِفًا لَوِ اسْتَخْلَفَهُ؟ قَالَتْ: أَبُو بَكْرٍ، فَقِيلَ لَهَا: ثُمَّ مَنْ بَعْدَ أَبِي بَكْرٍ؟ قَالَتْ: عُمَرُ، ثُمَّ قِيلَ لَهَا: مَنْ بَعْدَ عُمَرَ؟ قَالَتْ: أَبُو عُبَيْدَةَ بْنُ الْجَرَّاحِ - ثُمَّ انْتَهَتْ إِلَى هَذَا."],"takhrij":"حسن: رواه مسلم في فضائل الصحابة (2385) من حديث جعفر بن عوف، أخبرنا أبو عميس، عن ابن أبي مليكة، سمعت عائشة فذكرته.","grade":"حسن","chapter_ar":"باب ما جاء في فضل أبي بكر وعمر وأبي عبيدة بن الجراح","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب فضائل الصحابة وأخبارهم","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Hasan: Narrated by Muslim (2385).","chapter_en":"Reports Concerning the Virtues of Abū Bakr, ʿUmar, and Abū ʿUbaydah ibn al-Jarrāḥ","part_en":"The Book of the Virtues and Accounts of the Companions","group_ar":"مجموع ما جاء في فضل جماعات الصحابة","group_en":"Collected Reports Concerning the Virtues of Groups of the Companions","part_no":49,"group_no":12,"chapter_no":8,"content":{"translation":{"en":["ʿĀ’ishah was asked: “Whom would the Messenger of Allah ﷺ have appointed as his successor, had he appointed one?” She replied: “Abū Bakr.” She was asked: “Then who after Abū Bakr?” She replied: “ʿUmar.” She was then asked: “Who after ʿUmar?” She replied: “Abū ʿUbaydah ibn al-Jarrāḥ.” She went no further than that."]}},"tuhfa":{},"voc":["fazail",216],"full":1,"tks":"حسن: رواه مسلم (2385)."},{"num":10019,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ عبدالله بن شَقِيقٍ قَالَ: قُلْتُ لِعَائِشَةَ: أي أَصْحَابِ رَسُولِ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ كَانَ أَحَبَّ إِلَى رَسُولِ اللَّهِ؟ قَالَتْ: أَبُو بَكْرٍ، قُلْتُ: ثُمَّ مَنْ؟ قَالَتْ: عُمَرُ، قُلْتُ: ثُمَّ مَنْ؟ قَالَتْ: ثُمَّ أَبُو عُبَيْدَةَ بْنُ الْجَرَّاحِ، قُلْتُ ثُمَّ مَنْ؟ قَالَ: فَسَكَتَتْ."],"takhrij":"صحيح: رواه الترمذي (3657)، وابن ماجه (102)، وأبو يعلى (4732) كلهم من طرق عن الجريري-هو سعيد بن إياس-، عن عبدالله بن شقيق فذكره.","grade":"صحيح","chapter_ar":"باب ما جاء في فضل أبي بكر وعمر وأبي عبيدة بن الجراح","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب فضائل الصحابة وأخبارهم","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Authentic: Narrated by al-Tirmidhī (3657), Ibn Mājah (102), and Abū Yaʿlā (4732). Al-Tirmidhī said: “good authentic hadith.”","chapter_en":"Reports Concerning the Virtues of Abū Bakr, ʿUmar, and Abū ʿUbaydah ibn al-Jarrāḥ","part_en":"The Book of the Virtues and Accounts of the Companions","group_ar":"مجموع ما جاء في فضل جماعات الصحابة","group_en":"Collected Reports Concerning the Virtues of Groups of the Companions","part_no":49,"group_no":12,"chapter_no":8,"content":{"translation":{"en":["ʿAbdullāh ibn Shaqīq narrated: I asked ʿĀ’ishah: “Which of the Companions of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was most beloved to him?” She replied: “Abū Bakr.” I asked: “Then who?” She replied: “ʿUmar.” I asked: “Then who?” She replied: “Then Abū ʿUbaydah ibn al-Jarrāḥ.” I asked: “Then who?” The narrator said: She remained silent."]}},"tuhfa":{},"voc":["fazail",217],"full":1,"dr":1,"rep":[9978],"tks":"صحيح: رواه الترمذي (3657)، وابن ماجه (102)، وأبو يعلى (4732)، وقال الترمذي: “حسن صحيح”."},{"num":10020,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عن عَمْرِو بْنِ الْعَاصِ رَضِيَ اللَّهُ عَنْهُ أَنَّ النَّبِيَّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ بَعَثَهُ عَلَى جَيْشِ ذَاتِ السَّلاَسِلِ، فَأَتَيْتُهُ فَقُلْتُ: أَىُّ النَّاسِ أَحَبُّ إِلَيْكَ؟ قَالَ: عَائِشَةُ. فَقُلْتُ: مِنَ الرِّجَالِ؟ فَقَالَ: أَبُوهَا. قُلْتُ: ثُمَّ مَنْ؟ قَالَ: ثُمَّ عُمَرُ بْنُ الْخَطَّابِ. فَعَدَّ رِجَالاً."],"takhrij":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاري في فضائل الصحابة (3662)، ومسلم في فضائل الصحابة (2348-8) كلاهما من طريق خالد بن عبدالله الحذاء، عن أبي عثمان، ثني عمرو بن العاص، فذكره.","grade":"متفق عليه","chapter_ar":"باب ما جاء في فضل أبي بكر وعمر وعائشة","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب فضائل الصحابة وأخبارهم","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Agreed upon: Narrated by al-Bukhārī (3662) and Muslim (2384, no. 8).","chapter_en":"Reports Concerning the Virtues of Abū Bakr, ʿUmar, and ʿĀ’ishah","part_en":"The Book of the Virtues and Accounts of the Companions","group_ar":"مجموع ما جاء في فضل جماعات الصحابة","group_en":"Collected Reports Concerning the Virtues of Groups of the Companions","part_no":49,"group_no":12,"chapter_no":9,"content":{"translation":{"en":["ʿAmr ibn al-ʿĀṣ narrated: The Prophet ﷺ appointed me commander of the army sent on the expedition of Dhāt al-Salāsil. I came to him and asked: “Who among the people is most beloved to you?” He replied: “ʿĀ’ishah.” I asked: “Among the men?” He replied: “Her father.” I asked: “Then who?” He replied: “Then ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb.” He then named a number of other men."]}},"tuhfa":{},"voc":["fazail",218],"full":1,"dr":1,"tks":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (3662)، ومسلم (2384-8)."},{"num":10021,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ بُرَيْدَةَ بْنِ الحصيب قَالَ: كَانَ أَحَبُّ النِّسَاءِ إِلَى رَسُولِ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ فَاطِمَةَ، وَمِنَ الرِّجَالِ عَلِيٌّ."],"takhrij":"حسن: رواه الترمذي (3868)، والطبراني في الأوسط (7258)، والحاكم (4735) كلهم من طريق الأسود بن عامر شاذان، عن جعفر بن زياد الأحمر، عن عبدالله بن عطاء، عن عبدالله بن بريدة، عن أبيه قال: فذكره.","grade":"حسن","chapter_ar":"باب في فضل فاطمة وعلي","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب فضائل الصحابة وأخبارهم","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Hasan: Narrated by al-Tirmidhī (3868), al-Ṭabarānī in al-Muʿjam al-Awsaṭ (7258), and al-Ḥākim (4735).","chapter_en":"The Virtue of Fāṭimah and ʿAlī","part_en":"The Book of the Virtues and Accounts of the Companions","group_ar":"مجموع ما جاء في فضل جماعات الصحابة","group_en":"Collected Reports Concerning the Virtues of Groups of the Companions","part_no":49,"group_no":12,"chapter_no":10,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Buraydah ibn al-Ḥuṣayb narrated: The most beloved of women to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was Fāṭimah, and the most beloved of men was ʿAlī."]},"buhuth":{"en":["This hadith is understood as referring specifically to the members of the Prophet’s household and his blood relatives, as al-Tirmidhī related from his teacher Ibrāhīm ibn Saʿīd al-Jawharī.","Accordingly, there is no contradiction between this hadith and the narration stating that the most beloved person to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was ʿĀ’ishah, and among the men, her father."]}},"tuhfa":{},"voc":["fazail",219],"full":1,"dr":1,"tks":"حسن: رواه الترمذي (3868)، والطبراني في الأوسط (7258)، والحاكم (4735)."},{"num":10022,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["قَالَتْ عَائِشَةُ:  خَرَجَ النَّبِيُّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ غَدَاةً وَعَلَيْهِ مِرْطٌ مُرَحَّلٌ، مِنْ شَعَْرٍ أَسْوَدَ، فَجَاءَ الْحَسَنُ بْنُ عَلِيٍّ فَأَدْخَلَهُ، ثُمَّ جَاءَ الْحُسَيْنُ فَدَخَلَ مَعَهُ، ثُمَّ جَاءَتْ فَاطِمَةُ فَأَدْخَلَهَا، ثُمَّ جَاءَ عَلِيٌّ فَأَدْخَلَهُ، ثُمَّ قَالَ: ﴿إِنَّمَا يُرِيدُ اللَّهُ لِيُذْهِبَ عَنْكُمُ الرِّجْسَ أَهْلَ الْبَيْتِ وَيُطَهِّرَكُمْ تَطْهِيرًا ﴾."],"takhrij":"صحيح: رواه مسلم في فضائل الصحابة (2424) من طرق عن محمد بن بشر، عن زكريا، عن مصعب بن شيبة، عن صفية بنت شيبة قالت: قالت عائشة: فذكرته.","grade":"صحيح","chapter_ar":"باب في فضل علي والحسن والحسين وفاطمة","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب فضائل الصحابة وأخبارهم","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Authentic: Narrated by Muslim (2424).","chapter_en":"The Virtue of ʿAlī, al-Ḥasan, al-Ḥusayn, and Fāṭimah","part_en":"The Book of the Virtues and Accounts of the Companions","group_ar":"مجموع ما جاء في فضل جماعات الصحابة","group_en":"Collected Reports Concerning the Virtues of Groups of the Companions","part_no":49,"group_no":12,"chapter_no":11,"content":{"translation":{"en":["ʿĀ’ishah, the wife of the Prophet ﷺ, narrated: The Prophet ﷺ went out one morning wearing a striped cloak made of black hair. Al-Ḥasan ibn ʿAlī came, and the Prophet ﷺ brought him beneath it. Then al-Ḥusayn came and entered beneath it with him. Then Fāṭimah came, and he brought her beneath it. Then ʿAlī came, and he brought him beneath it. He then recited: “Allah only intends to remove impurity from you, O People of the Household, and to purify you completely.” [Al-Aḥzāb 33:33]"]}},"tuhfa":{},"full":1,"rep":[13062],"tks":"صحيح: رواه مسلم (2424)."},{"num":10023,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عن أُمِّ سَلَمَةَ تَذْكُرُ أَنَّ النَّبِيَّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ كَانَ فِي بَيْتِهَا، فَأَتَتْهُ فَاطِمَةُ بِبُرْمَةٍ، فِيهَا خَزِيرَةٌ، فَدَخَلَتْ بِهَا عَلَيْهِ، فَقَالَ لَهَا: ادْعِي زَوْجَكِ وَابْنَيْكِ قَالَتْ: فَجَاءَ عَلِيٌّ، وَالْحُسَيْنُ، وَالْحَسَنُ، فَدَخَلُوا عَلَيْهِ، فَجَلَسُوا يَأْكُلُونَ مِنْ تِلْكَ الْخَزِيرَةِ، وَهُوَ عَلَى مَنَامَةٍ لَهُ عَلَى دُكَّانٍ تَحْتَهُ كِسَاءٌ خَيْبَرِيٌّ. قَالَتْ: وَأَنَا أُصَلِّي فِي الْحُجْرَةِ، فَأَنْزَلَ اللَّهُ عَزَّ وَجَلَّ هَذِهِ الْآيَةَ: ﴿إِنَّمَا يُرِيدُ اللَّهُ لِيُذْهِبَ عَنْكُمُ الرِّجْسَ أَهْلَ الْبَيْتِ وَيُطَهِّرَكُمْ تَطْهِيرًا﴾ [الأحزاب: ٣٣] قَالَتْ: فَأَخَذَ فَضْلَ الْكِسَاءِ، فَغَشَّاهُمْ بِهِ، ثُمَّ أَخْرَجَ يَدَهُ، فَأَلْوَى بِهَا إِلَى السَّمَاءِ، ثُمَّ قَالَ: اللهُمَّ هَؤُلَاءِ أَهْلُ بَيْتِي وَخَاصَّتِي، فَأَذْهِبْ عَنْهُمُ الرِّجْسَ، وَطَهِّرْهُمْ تَطْهِيرًا، اللهُمَّ هَؤُلَاءِ أَهْلُ بَيْتِي وَخَاصَّتِي، فَأَذْهِبْ عَنْهُمُ الرِّجْسَ، وَطَهِّرْهُمْ تَطْهِيرًا قَالَتْ: فَأَدْخَلْتُ رَأْسِي الْبَيْتَ، فَقُلْتُ: وَأَنَا مَعَكُمْ يَا رَسُولَ اللَّهِ، قَالَ: إِنَّكِ إِلَى خَيْرٍ، إِنَّكِ إِلَى خَيْرٍ."],"takhrij":"حسن: رواه أحمد (26508) عن عبداله بن نمير، حدثنا عبدالملك – يعني ابن أبي سليمان -، عن عطاء ابن أبي رباح قال: حدثني من سمع أم سلمة قالت: فذكرت الحديث.","grade":"حسن","chapter_ar":"باب في فضل علي والحسن والحسين وفاطمة","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب فضائل الصحابة وأخبارهم","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Hasan: Narrated by Aḥmad (26508).","chapter_en":"The Virtue of ʿAlī, al-Ḥasan, al-Ḥusayn, and Fāṭimah","part_en":"The Book of the Virtues and Accounts of the Companions","group_ar":"مجموع ما جاء في فضل جماعات الصحابة","group_en":"Collected Reports Concerning the Virtues of Groups of the Companions","part_no":49,"group_no":12,"chapter_no":11,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Umm Salamah narrated: The Prophet ﷺ was in her house when Fāṭimah brought him a cooking pot containing a dish of meat and flour. She entered with it, and he said to her: “Call your husband and your two sons.” She said: ʿAlī, al-Ḥusayn, and al-Ḥasan came and entered upon him. They sat and ate from that dish while the Prophet ﷺ was upon a sleeping mat placed on a raised platform, beneath which was a Khaybarī cloak. She continued: I was praying in the room when Allah, Mighty and Majestic, revealed this verse: “Allah only intends to remove impurity from you, O People of the Household, and to purify you completely.” The Prophet ﷺ took the remaining part of the cloak and covered them with it. He then extended his hand and raised it toward the sky, saying: “O Allah, these are the members of my household and my closest ones. Remove impurity from them and purify them completely. O Allah, these are the members of my household and my closest ones. Remove impurity from them and purify them completely.” She said: I placed my head inside the room and asked: “Am I with you, O Messenger of Allah?” He replied: “You are upon goodness. You are upon goodness.”"]},"buhuth":{"en":["The expression “the People of the Household” here refers to those related to the Prophet ﷺ by blood. As for the purification of the household from impurity, it includes both blood relatives and those related through marriage."]}},"tuhfa":{},"voc":["fazail",221],"full":1,"dr":1,"rep":[13066],"tks":"حسن: رواه أحمد (26508)."},{"num":10024,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ عُمَرَ بْنِ أَبِي سَلَمَةَ رَبِيبِ النَّبِيِّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ قَالَ: نَزَلَتْ هَذِهِ الآيَةُ عَلَى النَّبِيِّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ: ﴿إِنَّمَا يُرِيدُ اللَّهُ لِيُذْهِبَ عَنْكُمُ الرِّجْسَ أَهْلَ الْبَيْتِ وَيُطَهِّرَكُمْ تَطْهِيرًا﴾ [سورة الأحزاب: 33] بَيْتِ أُمِّ سَلَمَةَ فَدَعَا النَّبِيِّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ فَاطِمَةَ وَحَسَنًا وَحُسَيْنًا فَجَلَّلَهُمْ بِكِسَاءٍ وعليٌّ خَلْفَ ظَهْرِهِ فجلّله بِكِسَاءٍ، ثُمَّ قَالَ: اللَّهُمَّ هَؤُلاَءِ أَهْلُ بَيْتِي فاذهب عَنْهُمُ الرِّجْسَ وَطَهِّرْهُمْ تَطْهِيرًا قَالَتْ أُمُّ سَلَمَةَ: وَأَنَا مَعَهُمْ يَا رَسُولَ اللَّهِ؟ قَالَ:أَنْتِ عَلَى مَكَانِكِ وَأَنْتِ إِلَى خَيْرٍ."],"takhrij":"حسن: رواه الترمذي (3205،3787)، والطبري في تفسيره (6176)، والطبراني في الكبير (8295) كلهم من طريق محمد بن سليمان بن الأصبهاني، عن يحيى بن عبيد، عن عطاء بن أبي رباح، عن عمر بن أبي سلمة قال: فذكره.","grade":"حسن","chapter_ar":"باب في فضل علي والحسن والحسين وفاطمة","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب فضائل الصحابة وأخبارهم","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Hasan: Narrated by al-Tirmidhī (3205, 3787), al-Ṭabarī in his Tafsīr (19/106), and al-Ṭabarānī in al-Muʿjam al-Kabīr (8295).","chapter_en":"The Virtue of ʿAlī, al-Ḥasan, al-Ḥusayn, and Fāṭimah","part_en":"The Book of the Virtues and Accounts of the Companions","group_ar":"مجموع ما جاء في فضل جماعات الصحابة","group_en":"Collected Reports Concerning the Virtues of Groups of the Companions","part_no":49,"group_no":12,"chapter_no":11,"content":{"translation":{"en":["ʿUmar ibn Abī Salamah, the stepson of the Prophet ﷺ, narrated: This verse was revealed to the Prophet ﷺ in the house of Umm Salamah: “Allah only intends to remove impurity from you, O People of the Household, and to purify you completely.” The Prophet ﷺ called Fāṭimah, al-Ḥasan, and al-Ḥusayn and covered them with a cloak. ʿAlī was behind him, so he covered him with the cloak as well. Then he said: “O Allah, these are the members of my household. Remove impurity from them and purify them completely.” Umm Salamah asked: “Am I with them, O Messenger of Allah?” He replied: “You shall remain in your place, and you are upon goodness.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"full":1,"dr":1,"tks":"حسن: رواه الترمذي (3205، 3787)، والطبري في تفسيره (6176)، والطبراني في الكبير (8295)."},{"num":10025,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ شَدَّادٍ أَبِي عَمَّارٍ، قَالَ: دَخَلْتُ عَلَى وَاثِلَةَ بْنِ الْأَسْقَعِ، وَعِنْدَهُ قَوْمٌ، فَذَكَرُوا عَلِيًّا، فَلَمَّا قَامُوا قَالَ لِي: أَلَا أُخْبِرُكَ بِمَا رَأَيْتُ مِنْ رَسُولِ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ؟ قُلْتُ: بَلَى، قَالَ: أَتَيْتُ فَاطِمَةَ رَضِيَ اللَّهُ تَعَالَى عَنْهَا أَسْأَلُهَا عَنْ عَلِيٍّ، قَالَتْ: تَوَجَّهَ إِلَى رَسُولِ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ. فَجَلَسْتُ أَنْتَظِرُهُ حَتَّى جَاءَ رَسُولُ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ وَمَعَهُ عَلِيٌّ وَحَسَنٌ وَحُسَيْنٌ رَضِيَ اللَّهُ تَعَالَى عَنْهُمْ، آخِذٌ كُلَّ وَاحِدٍ مِنْهُمَا بِيَدِهِ، حَتَّى دَخَلَ فَأَدْنَى عَلِيًّا وَفَاطِمَةَ، فَأَجْلَسَهُمَا بَيْنَ يَدَيْهِ، وَأَجْلَسَ حَسَنًا، وَحُسَيْنًا كُلَّ وَاحِدٍ مِنْهُمَا عَلَى فَخِذِهِ، ثُمَّ لَفَّ عَلَيْهِمْ ثَوْبَهُ، - أَوْ قَالَ: كِسَاءً، - ثُمَّ تَلَا هَذِهِ الْآيَةَ: ﴿إِنَّمَا يُرِيدُ اللَّهُ لِيُذْهِبَ عَنْكُمُ الرِّجْسَ أَهْلَ الْبَيْتِ وَيُطَهِّرَكُمْ تَطْهِيرًا﴾ [الأحزاب: ٣٣] وَقَالَ: اللهُمَّ هَؤُلَاءِ أَهْلُ بَيْتِي، وَأَهْلُ بَيْتِي أَحَقُّ."],"takhrij":"صحيح: رواه أحمد (16988)، وصحّحه ابن حبان (6976)، والحاكم (2/3،416/174)، والبيهقي في الكبرى (2/152) كلهم من طرق عن الأوزاعي، عن شداد أبي عمار قال: فذكره.وإسناده صحيح.","grade":"صحيح","chapter_ar":"باب في فضل علي والحسن والحسين وفاطمة","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب فضائل الصحابة وأخبارهم","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Authentic: Narrated by Aḥmad (16988), authenticated by Ibn Ḥibbān (6976), and recorded by al-Ḥākim (2/416, 3/147).","chapter_en":"The Virtue of ʿAlī, al-Ḥasan, al-Ḥusayn, and Fāṭimah","part_en":"The Book of the Virtues and Accounts of the Companions","group_ar":"مجموع ما جاء في فضل جماعات الصحابة","group_en":"Collected Reports Concerning the Virtues of Groups of the Companions","part_no":49,"group_no":12,"chapter_no":11,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Shaddād Abū ʿAmmār narrated: I entered upon Wāthilah ibn al-Asqaʿ while a group of people were with him. They mentioned ʿAlī. After they had left, he said to me: “Shall I tell you what I witnessed from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ?” I replied: “Yes.” He said: I went to Fāṭimah, may Allah be pleased with her, to ask about ʿAlī. She said: “He has gone to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ.” I sat and waited for him until the Messenger of Allah ﷺ arrived accompanied by ʿAlī, al-Ḥasan, and al-Ḥusayn, holding each of the two boys by the hand. When he entered, he drew ʿAlī and Fāṭimah close and seated them before him. He seated al-Ḥasan and al-Ḥusayn, one upon each thigh. He then wrapped his garment—or he said, a cloak—around them and recited: “Allah only intends to remove impurity from you, O People of the Household, and to purify you completely.” He then said: “O Allah, these are the members of my household, and the members of my household are the most entitled.”"]},"buhuth":{"en":["Ibn Ḥibbān and al-Bayhaqī added at the end of the hadith:","Wāthilah, who was standing at one side of the house, said:","“Am I also among your family, O Messenger of Allah?”","He replied:","“You are among my family.”","Wāthilah said:","“This is among the things for which I have the greatest hope.”","That is, he was among the Prophet’s family in the sense of belonging to the people of Islam, not through blood relationship."]}},"tuhfa":{},"full":1,"dr":1,"rep":[13064],"tks":"صحيح: رواه أحمد (16988)، وصححه ابن حبان (6976)، والحاكم (2/416، 3/147)."},{"num":10026,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ عَلِيٍّ، أَنَّهُ دَخَلَ عَلَى النَّبِيِّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ وَقَدْ بَسَطَ شَمْلَةً، فَجَلَسَ عَلَيْهَا هُوَ وَفَاطِمَةُ وَعَلِيٌّ وَالْحَسَنُ وَالْحُسَيْنُ، ثُمَّ أَخَذَ النَّبِيُّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ بِمَجَامِعِهِ، فَعَقَدَ عَلَيْهِمْ، ثُمَّ قَالَ: اللَّهُمَّ ارْضَ عَنْهُمْ كَمَا أَنَا عَنْهُمْ رَاضٍ."],"takhrij":"حسن: رواه الطبراني في الأوسط (5510) عن محمد بن عثمان بن أبي شيبة، حدثنا منجاب بن الحارث، حدثنا يحيى بن عبد الملك بن أبي غنيّة، حدثنا عبيد بن طفيل أبو سيدان، عن ربعي بن حراش، عن علي فذكره.","grade":"حسن","chapter_ar":"باب في فضل علي والحسن والحسين وفاطمة","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب فضائل الصحابة وأخبارهم","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Hasan: Narrated by al-Ṭabarānī in al-Muʿjam al-Awsaṭ (5510).","chapter_en":"The Virtue of ʿAlī, al-Ḥasan, al-Ḥusayn, and Fāṭimah","part_en":"The Book of the Virtues and Accounts of the Companions","group_ar":"مجموع ما جاء في فضل جماعات الصحابة","group_en":"Collected Reports Concerning the Virtues of Groups of the Companions","part_no":49,"group_no":12,"chapter_no":11,"content":{"translation":{"en":["ʿAlī narrated: The Prophet ﷺ went to a cloak that had been folded, and he sat upon it together with Fāṭimah, ʿAlī, al-Ḥasan, and al-Ḥusayn. The Prophet ﷺ then gathered its edges and wrapped it around them, saying: “O Allah, be pleased with them just as I am pleased with them.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"voc":["fazail",224],"full":1,"dr":1,"tks":"حسن: رواه الطبراني في الأوسط (5510)."},{"num":10027,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ عَطَاءٍ، أَنَّ رَجُلًا أَخْبَرَهُ: أَنَّهُ رَأَى النَّبِيَّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ يَضُمُّ إِلَيْهِ حَسَنًا وَحُسَيْنًا يَقُولُ: اللهُمَّ إِنِّي أُحِبُّهُمَا فَأَحِبَّهُمَا."],"takhrij":"صحيح: رواه أحمد (23133) عن سليمان بن داود (هو الهاشمي)، حدثنا إسماعيل –يعني ابن جعفر- ، أخبرني محمد – يعني ابن أبي حرملة -، عن عطاء (هو ابن يسار) قال: فذكره.وإسناده صحيح.","grade":"صحيح","chapter_ar":"باب في حب النبي ﷺ للحسن والحسين","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب فضائل الصحابة وأخبارهم","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Authentic: Narrated by Aḥmad (23133).","chapter_en":"The Prophet’s ﷺ Love for al-Ḥasan and al-Ḥusayn","part_en":"The Book of the Virtues and Accounts of the Companions","group_ar":"مجموع ما جاء في فضل جماعات الصحابة","group_en":"Collected Reports Concerning the Virtues of Groups of the Companions","part_no":49,"group_no":12,"chapter_no":12,"content":{"translation":{"en":["ʿAṭāʾ ibn Yasār narrated that a man informed him that he saw the Prophet ﷺ embracing al-Ḥasan and al-Ḥusayn and saying: “O Allah, I love them both, so love them both.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"voc":["fazail",225],"full":1,"dr":1,"tks":"صحيح: رواه أحمد (23133)."},{"num":10028,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ أَبِي هُرَيْرَةَ، قَالَ: قَالَ رَسُولُ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ لِلْحَسَنِ وَالْحُسَيْنِ: اللَّهُمَّ إِنِّي أُحِبُّهُمَا، فَأَحِبَّهُمَا."],"takhrij":"صحيح: رواه أحمد (9759)، والبزار (9736)، والطبراني في الكبير (3/42) كلهم من طرق عن أبي حازم ( اسمه: سلمان الأشجعي)، عن أبي هريرة قال: فذكره.وزاد الطبراني في آخر الحديث: وأبغض من أبغضهما.","grade":"صحيح","chapter_ar":"باب في حب النبي ﷺ للحسن والحسين","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب فضائل الصحابة وأخبارهم","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Authentic: Narrated by Aḥmad (9759), al-Bazzār (9736), and al-Ṭabarānī in al-Muʿjam al-Kabīr (3/42).","chapter_en":"The Prophet’s ﷺ Love for al-Ḥasan and al-Ḥusayn","part_en":"The Book of the Virtues and Accounts of the Companions","group_ar":"مجموع ما جاء في فضل جماعات الصحابة","group_en":"Collected Reports Concerning the Virtues of Groups of the Companions","part_no":49,"group_no":12,"chapter_no":12,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Abū Hurayrah narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said concerning al-Ḥasan and al-Ḥusayn: “O Allah, I love them both, so love them both.”"]},"buhuth":{"en":["Al-Ṭabarānī added at the end of the hadith:","“And hate whoever hates them both.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"voc":["fazail",226],"full":1,"dr":1,"tks":"صحيح: رواه أحمد (9759)، والبزار (9736)، والطبراني في الكبير (3/42). وزاد الطبراني في آخر الحديث: ((وأبغض من أبغضهما))."},{"num":10029,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["أَنَّ النَّبِيَّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ قَالَ لِلْحَسَنِ وَالْحُسَيْنِ: اللَّهُمَّ إِنِّي أُحِبُّهُمَا فَأَحِبَّهُمَا، وَمَنْ أَحَبَّهُمَا فَقَدْ أَحَبَّنِي."],"takhrij":"حسن: رواه البزار (1820) عن يوسف بن موسى، حدثنا أبو بكر بن عياش، عن عاصم (هو ابن بهدلة)، عن زيد (هو ابن حبيش)، عن عبدالله فذكره.","grade":"حسن","chapter_ar":"باب في حب النبي ﷺ للحسن والحسين","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب فضائل الصحابة وأخبارهم","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Hasan: Narrated by al-Bazzār (1820).","chapter_en":"The Prophet’s ﷺ Love for al-Ḥasan and al-Ḥusayn","part_en":"The Book of the Virtues and Accounts of the Companions","group_ar":"مجموع ما جاء في فضل جماعات الصحابة","group_en":"Collected Reports Concerning the Virtues of Groups of the Companions","part_no":49,"group_no":12,"chapter_no":12,"content":{"translation":{"en":["ʿAbdullāh ibn Masʿūd narrated that the Prophet ﷺ said concerning al-Ḥasan and al-Ḥusayn: “O Allah, I love them both, so love them both. Whoever loves them has indeed loved me.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"voc":["fazail",227],"full":1,"dr":1,"tks":"حسن: رواه البزار (1820)."},{"num":10030,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ أَبِي هُرَيْرَةَ، قَالَ: قَالَ رَسُولُ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ مَنْ أَحَبَّ الْحَسَنَ وَالْحُسَيْنَ فَقَدْ أَحَبَّنِي، وَمَنْ أَبْغَضَهُمَا فَقَدْ أَبْغَضَنِي."],"takhrij":"حسن: رواه النسائي في الكبرى (8112)، وابن ماجه (143)، وأحمد (7876) كلهم من طريق سفيان الثوري، عن أبي الجحاف داود بن أبي عوف، عن أبي حازم، عن أبي هريرة فذكره.","grade":"حسن","chapter_ar":"باب في حب النبي ﷺ للحسن والحسين","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب فضائل الصحابة وأخبارهم","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Hasan: Narrated by al-Nasā’ī in al-Sunan al-Kubrā (8112), Ibn Mājah (143), and Aḥmad (7876).","chapter_en":"The Prophet’s ﷺ Love for al-Ḥasan and al-Ḥusayn","part_en":"The Book of the Virtues and Accounts of the Companions","group_ar":"مجموع ما جاء في فضل جماعات الصحابة","group_en":"Collected Reports Concerning the Virtues of Groups of the Companions","part_no":49,"group_no":12,"chapter_no":12,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Abū Hurayrah narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Whoever loves al-Ḥasan and al-Ḥusayn has loved me, and whoever hates them has hated me.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"voc":["fazail",228],"full":1,"dr":1,"tks":"حسن: رواه النسائي في الكبرى (8112)، وابن ماجه (143)، وأحمد (7876)."},{"num":10031,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ عبدالله بن مَسْعُودٍ قَالَ: كَانَ رَسُولُ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ يُصَلِّي، فَإِذَا سَجَدَ وَثَبَ الْحَسَنُ وَالْحُسَيْنُ عَلَى ظَهْرِهِ، فَإِذَا مَنَعُوهُمَا أَشَارَ إِلَيْهِمْ أَنْ دَعُوهُمَا، فَلَمَّا قَضَى الصَّلَاةَ وَضَعَهُمَا فِي حِجْرِهِ فَقَالَ: مَنْ أَحَبَّنِي فَلْيُحِبَّ هَذَيْنِ."],"takhrij":"حسن: رواه النسائي في الكبرى (8114)، وصحّحه ابن خزيمة (887) –والسياق له- وابن حبان (6970)، والطبراني في الكبير (3/40) كلهم من طرق عن عاصم (هو ابن بهدلة)، عن زر (هو ابن حبيش)، عن عبدالله فذكره.","grade":"حسن","chapter_ar":"باب في حب النبي ﷺ للحسن والحسين","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب فضائل الصحابة وأخبارهم","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Hasan: Narrated by al-Nasā’ī in al-Sunan al-Kubrā (8114), authenticated by Ibn Khuzaymah (887), whose wording is cited here, and recorded by Ibn Ḥibbān (6970).","chapter_en":"The Prophet’s ﷺ Love for al-Ḥasan and al-Ḥusayn","part_en":"The Book of the Virtues and Accounts of the Companions","group_ar":"مجموع ما جاء في فضل جماعات الصحابة","group_en":"Collected Reports Concerning the Virtues of Groups of the Companions","part_no":49,"group_no":12,"chapter_no":12,"content":{"translation":{"en":["ʿAbdullāh ibn Masʿūd narrated: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was praying, and whenever he prostrated, al-Ḥasan and al-Ḥusayn would leap upon his back. When the people attempted to prevent them, he gestured to them to leave the two boys alone. When he completed the prayer, he placed them in his lap and said: “Whoever loves me should love these two.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"voc":["fazail",229],"full":1,"dr":1,"tks":"حسن: رواه النسائي في الكبرى (8114)، وصححه ابن خزيمة (887) - والسياق له -، وابن حبان (6970)."},{"num":10032,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ بُرَيْدَةَ بْنِ الحصيب قَالَ: كَانَ رَسُولُ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ يَخْطُبُنَا إِذْ جَاءَ الْحَسَنُ وَالْحُسَيْنُ عَلَيْهِمَا قَمِيصَانِ أَحْمَرَانِ يَمْشِيَانِ وَيَعْثُرَانِ، فَنَزَلَ رَسُولُ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ مِنَ الْمِنْبَرِ فَحَمَلَهُمَا وَوَضَعَهُمَا بَيْنَ يَدَيْهِ، ثُمَّ قَالَ: صَدَقَ اللَّهُ إِنَّمَا أَمْوَالُكُمْ وَأَوْلَادُكُمْ فِتْنَةٌ نَظَرْتُ إِلَى هَذَيْنِ الصَّبِيَّيْنِ يَمْشِيَانِ وَيَعْثُرَانِ فَلَمْ أَصْبِرْ حَتَّى قَطَعْتُ حَدِيثِي وَرَفَعْتُهُمَا."],"takhrij":"حسن: رواه أبو داود (1109)، والترمذي (3774)، والنسائي (1413،1585)، وابن ماجه (3600)، وابن خزيمة (1456)، وابن حبان (6039)، والحاكم (1/287) كلهم من طرق عن حسين بن واقد، حدثني عبدالله بن بريدة، سمعت أبي بريدة يقول:فذكره.","grade":"حسن","chapter_ar":"باب في حب النبي ﷺ للحسن والحسين","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب فضائل الصحابة وأخبارهم","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Hasan: Narrated by Abū Dāwūd (1109), al-Tirmidhī (3774), who graded it good, and al-Nasā’ī (1413, 1585).","chapter_en":"The Prophet’s ﷺ Love for al-Ḥasan and al-Ḥusayn","part_en":"The Book of the Virtues and Accounts of the Companions","group_ar":"مجموع ما جاء في فضل جماعات الصحابة","group_en":"Collected Reports Concerning the Virtues of Groups of the Companions","part_no":49,"group_no":12,"chapter_no":12,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Buraydah ibn al-Ḥuṣayb narrated: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was delivering a sermon to us when al-Ḥasan and al-Ḥusayn came wearing two red shirts, walking and stumbling. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ descended from the pulpit, carried them, and placed them before him. He then said: “Allah has spoken the truth: ‘Your wealth and your children are only a trial.’ I looked at these two boys walking and stumbling, and I could not remain patient until I interrupted my speech and lifted them up.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"voc":["fazail",230],"full":1,"dr":1,"rep":[13571],"tks":"حسن: رواه أبو داود (1109)، والترمذي (3774) وحسنه، والنسائي (1413، 1585)."},{"num":10033,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ خَالِدٍ، قَالَ: وَفَدَ الْمِقْدَامُ بْنُ مَعْدِيكَرِبَ وَعَمْرُو بْنُ الأَسْوَدِ وَرَجُلٌ مِنْ بَنِي أَسَدٍ مِنْ أَهْلِ قِنَّسْرِينَ إِلَى مُعَاوِيَةَ بْنِ أَبِي سُفْيَانَ، فَقَالَ مُعَاوِيَةُ لِلْمِقْدَامِ: أَعَلِمْتَ أَنَّ الْحَسَنَ بْنَ عَلِيٍّ تُوُفِّيَ؟ فَرَجَّعَ الْمِقْدَامُ، فَقَالَ لَهُ رَجُلٌ: أَتَرَاهَا مُصِيبَةً؟ قَالَ لَهُ: وَلِمَ لاَ أَرَاهَا مُصِيبَةً وَقَدْ وَضَعَهُ رَسُولُ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ فِي حِجْرِهِ فَقَالَ: هَذَا مِنِّي وَحُسَيْنٌ مِنْ عَلِيٍّ."],"takhrij":"حسن: رواه أبو داود (4131)، وأحمد (17189)، والطبراني في الكبير (20/269) كلهم من طرق عن بقية بن الوليد، حدثنا بحير بن سعد، عن خالد بن معدان قال: فذكره.","grade":"حسن","chapter_ar":"باب في حب النبي ﷺ للحسن والحسين","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب فضائل الصحابة وأخبارهم","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Hasan: Narrated by Abū Dāwūd (4131), Aḥmad (17189), and al-Ṭabarānī in al-Muʿjam al-Kabīr (20/269).","chapter_en":"The Prophet’s ﷺ Love for al-Ḥasan and al-Ḥusayn","part_en":"The Book of the Virtues and Accounts of the Companions","group_ar":"مجموع ما جاء في فضل جماعات الصحابة","group_en":"Collected Reports Concerning the Virtues of Groups of the Companions","part_no":49,"group_no":12,"chapter_no":12,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Khālid ibn Maʿdān narrated: Al-Miqdām ibn Maʿdīkarib, ʿAmr ibn al-Aswad, and a man from Banū Asad who lived in Qinnasrīn came as a delegation to Muʿāwiyah ibn Abī Sufyān. Muʿāwiyah said to al-Miqdām: “Have you learned that al-Ḥasan ibn ʿAlī has died?” Al-Miqdām began reciting the words said when a calamity occurs. A man asked him: “Do you regard it as a calamity?” He replied: “Why should I not regard it as a calamity when the Messenger of Allah ﷺ placed him in his lap and said: ‘This one is from me, and Ḥusayn is from ʿAlī’?”"]},"buhuth":{"en":["The Prophet’s statement in this hadith, “This one is from me,” refers to al-Ḥasan ibn ʿAlī. It was an expression of special affection, because al-Ḥasan was older than al-Ḥusayn and because the Prophet ﷺ said concerning him:","“Allah will bring reconciliation through him between two great groups.”","Therefore, the statement “This one is from me” indicates an additional distinction."]}},"tuhfa":{},"voc":["fazail",231],"full":1,"dr":1,"tks":"حسن: رواه أبو داود (4131)، وأحمد (17189)، والطبراني في الكبير (20/269)."},{"num":10034,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ عبدالله بن عُمَرَ- وَسَأَلَهُ عَنِ الْمُحْرِمِ، قَالَ شُعْبَةُ: أَحْسِبُهُ، يَقْتُلُ الذُّبَابَ؟- فَقَالَ: أَهْلُ الْعِرَاقِ يَسْأَلُونَ عَنِ الذُّبَابِ وَقَدْ قَتَلُوا ابْنَ ابْنَةِ رَسُولِ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ، ، وَقَالَ النَّبِيُّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ : هُمَا ريحانتاي مِنَ الدُّنْيَا ."],"takhrij":"صحيح: رواه البخاري في فضائل الصحابة (3753) عن محمد بن بشار، حدثنا غندر، ثنا شعبة، عن محمد بن أبي يعقوب، سمعت أبي نُعْم، سمعت عبدالله بن عمر فذكره.","grade":"صحيح","chapter_ar":"باب ما جاء أن الحسن والحسين هما ريحانتا رسول الله ﷺ","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب فضائل الصحابة وأخبارهم","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Authentic: Narrated by al-Bukhārī (3753).","chapter_en":"Al-Ḥasan and al-Ḥusayn Are the Two Fragrant Flowers of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ","part_en":"The Book of the Virtues and Accounts of the Companions","group_ar":"مجموع ما جاء في فضل جماعات الصحابة","group_en":"Collected Reports Concerning the Virtues of Groups of the Companions","part_no":49,"group_no":12,"chapter_no":13,"content":{"translation":{"en":["ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿUmar was asked about a person in the state of iḥrām. Shuʿbah said: “I think he was asked whether such a person could kill flies.” Ibn ʿUmar replied: “The people of Iraq ask about flies, although they killed the son of the daughter of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ!” The Prophet ﷺ said: “They are my two fragrant flowers in this world.”"]},"buhuth":{"en":["In another wording recorded by al-Bukhārī (5994), Ibn Abī Nuʿm said:","I was present with Ibn ʿUmar when a man asked him about the blood of a mosquito.","He asked:","“Where are you from?”","The man replied:","“From Iraq.”","Ibn ʿUmar said:","“Look at this man! He asks me about the blood of a mosquito, although they killed the grandson of the Prophet ﷺ…”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"voc":["fazail",232],"full":1,"dr":1,"tks":"صحيح: رواه البخاري (3753)."},{"num":10035,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ سَعْدِ بن أَبِي وَقَّاصٍ قَالَ: دَخَلْتُ عَلَى رَسُولِ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ وَالْحَسَنُ وَالْحُسَيْنُ يَلْعَبَانِ عَلَى بَطْنِهِ فَقُلْتُ: يَا رَسُولَ اللَّهِ أَتُحِبُّهُمَا؟ قَالَ: ومالي لَا أُحِبُّهُمَا، رَيْحَانَتَايَ."],"takhrij":"حسن: رواه البزار (1078) عن عباد بن يعقوب، حدثنا علي بن هاشم بن البريد، ثنا عبدالرحمن بن عبدالله بن دينار، عن أبي سهيل بن مالك( واسمه: نافع)، عن سعيد بن المسيب، عن سعد بن أبي وقاص فذكره.","grade":"حسن","chapter_ar":"باب ما جاء أن الحسن والحسين هما ريحانتا رسول الله ﷺ","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب فضائل الصحابة وأخبارهم","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Hasan: Narrated by al-Bazzār (1078).","chapter_en":"Al-Ḥasan and al-Ḥusayn Are the Two Fragrant Flowers of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ","part_en":"The Book of the Virtues and Accounts of the Companions","group_ar":"مجموع ما جاء في فضل جماعات الصحابة","group_en":"Collected Reports Concerning the Virtues of Groups of the Companions","part_no":49,"group_no":12,"chapter_no":13,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Saʿd ibn Abī Waqqāṣ narrated: I entered upon the Messenger of Allah ﷺ while al-Ḥasan and al-Ḥusayn were playing upon his stomach. I asked: “O Messenger of Allah, do you love them?” He replied: “Why should I not love them? They are my two fragrant flowers.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"voc":["fazail",233],"full":1,"dr":1,"tks":"حسن: رواه البزار (1078)."},{"num":10036,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ أَبِي سَعِيدٍ الْخُدْرِيِّ، رَضِيَ اللَّهُ عَنْهُ قَالَ: قَالَ رَسُولُ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ الْحَسَنُ وَالْحُسَيْنُ سَيِّدَا شَبَابِ أَهْلِ الْجَنَّةِ."],"takhrij":"حسن: رواه الترمذي (3768)، وأحمد (10999)، والنسائي في الكبرى (8474،8473،8472) كلهم من طرق عن عبدالرحمن بن أبي نُعم (هو البجلي الكوفي)، عن أبي سعيد الخدري قال: فذكره.","grade":"حسن","chapter_ar":"باب أن الحسن والحسين سيدا شباب أهل الجنة","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب فضائل الصحابة وأخبارهم","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Hasan: Narrated by al-Tirmidhī (3768), Aḥmad (10999), and al-Nasā’ī in al-Sunan al-Kubrā (8472, 8473, 8474).","chapter_en":"Al-Ḥasan and al-Ḥusayn Are the Leaders of the Youth of Paradise","part_en":"The Book of the Virtues and Accounts of the Companions","group_ar":"مجموع ما جاء في فضل جماعات الصحابة","group_en":"Collected Reports Concerning the Virtues of Groups of the Companions","part_no":49,"group_no":12,"chapter_no":14,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Abū Saʿīd al-Khudrī narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Al-Ḥasan and al-Ḥusayn are the leaders of the youth of Paradise.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"voc":["fazail",234],"full":1,"dr":1,"tks":"حسن: رواه الترمذي (3768)، وأحمد (10999)، والنسائي في الكبرى (8472، 8473، 8474)."},{"num":10037,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ حُذَيْفَةَ قَالَ: سَأَلَتْنِي أُمِّي: مَتَى عَهْدُكَ؟ تَعْنِي بِالنَّبِيِّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ فَقُلْتُ: مَالِي بِهِ عَهْدٌ مُنْذُ كَذَا كَذَا، فَنَالَتْ مِنِّي ، فَقُلْتُ لَهَا: دَعِينِي آتِي النَّبِيَّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ فَأُصَلِّيَ مَعَهُ الْمَغْرِبَ واسأله أَنْ يَسْتَغْفِرَ لِي وَلَكِ، فَأَتَيْتُ النَّبِيَّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ فَصَلَّيْتُ مَعَهُ الْمَغْرِبَ، فَصَلَّى حَتَّى صَلَّى الْعِشَاءَ ثُمَّ انْفَتَلَ فَتَبِعْتُهُ، فَسَمِعَ صَوْتِي فَقَالَ: مَنْ هَذَا؟ حُذَيْفَةُ؟.قُلْتُ: نَعَمْ، قَالَ: ماحاجتك، غفرالله لَكَ وَلأُمِّكَ؟.قَالَ: إِنَّ هَذَا مَلَكٌ لَمْ يَنْزِلِ الأَرْضَ قَطُّ قَبْلَ هَذِهِ اللَّيْلَةِ، اسْتَأْذَنَ رَبَّهُ أَنْ يُسَلِّمَ علي وَيُبَشِّرَنِي بِأَنَّ فَاطِمَةَ سَيِّدَةُ نِسَاءِ أَهْلِ الْجَنَّةِ، وَأَنَّ الْحَسَنَ وَالْحُسَيْنَ سَيِّدَا شَبَابِ أَهْلِ الْجَنَّةِ."],"takhrij":"حسن: رواه الترمذي (3781) عن عبد الله بن عبد الرحمن وإسحاق بن منصور قالا: أخبرنا محمد بن يوسف، عن إسرائيل، عن ميسرة بن حبيب، عن المنهال بن عمرو، عن زر بن حبيش، عن حذيفة فذكره.","grade":"حسن","chapter_ar":"باب أن الحسن والحسين سيدا شباب أهل الجنة","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب فضائل الصحابة وأخبارهم","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Hasan: Narrated by al-Tirmidhī (3781), Ibn Khuzaymah (1194), Ibn Ḥibbān (6960), and al-Ḥākim (3/381).","chapter_en":"Al-Ḥasan and al-Ḥusayn Are the Leaders of the Youth of Paradise","part_en":"The Book of the Virtues and Accounts of the Companions","group_ar":"مجموع ما جاء في فضل جماعات الصحابة","group_en":"Collected Reports Concerning the Virtues of Groups of the Companions","part_no":49,"group_no":12,"chapter_no":14,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Ḥudhayfah narrated: My mother asked me: “When was the last time you met him?” She meant the Prophet ﷺ. I replied: “I have not met him for such-and-such a period.” She reproached me, so I said to her: “Let me go to the Prophet ﷺ, pray Maghrib with him, and ask him to seek forgiveness for you and me.” I went to the Prophet ﷺ and prayed Maghrib with him. He continued praying until he prayed ʿIshāʾ. Then he departed, and I followed him. He heard my footsteps and said: “Who is this? Is it Ḥudhayfah?” I replied: “Yes.” He asked: “What do you need? May Allah forgive you and your mother.” He then said: “This is an angel who had never descended to the earth before this night. He sought permission from his Lord to greet me and give me the glad tidings that Fāṭimah is the leader of the women of Paradise, and that al-Ḥasan and al-Ḥusayn are the leaders of the youth of Paradise.”"]},"buhuth":{"en":["Aḥmad (23330) also recorded it through another chain from Isrāʾīl, from Abū al-Safar, from al-Shaʿbī, from Ḥudhayfah, who said:","I came to the Prophet ﷺ and prayed Ẓuhr, ʿAṣr, Maghrib, and ʿIshāʾ with him. Then I followed him as he intended to enter one of his rooms. He stopped while I stood behind him, and it appeared that he was speaking to someone.","He then asked:","“Who is this?”","I replied:","“Ḥudhayfah.”","He asked:","“Do you know who was with me?”","I replied:","“No.”","He said:","“Jibrīl came to give me the glad tidings that al-Ḥasan and al-Ḥusayn are the leaders of the youth of Paradise.”","Ḥudhayfah said:","“Then seek forgiveness for me and my mother.”","He replied:","“May Allah forgive you, O Ḥudhayfah, and your mother.”","The narrators in its chain are trustworthy. Ibn Abī al-Safar is ʿAbdullāh ibn Abī al-Safar al-Thawrī al-Kūfī, one of the narrators relied upon by the major hadith compilers.","However, al-Shaʿbī—ʿĀmir ibn Sharāḥīl Abū ʿAmr al-Kūfī—lived during the time of Ḥudhayfah while still young. If Ibn al-Samʿānī’s statement that he was born in the year 20 AH is correct, he would have been sixteen years old when Ḥudhayfah died, because Ḥudhayfah died at the beginning of ʿAlī’s caliphate in the year 36 AH. Therefore, I have not found anyone who conclusively stated that al-Shaʿbī did not hear from him."]}},"tuhfa":{},"voc":["fazail",235],"full":1,"dr":1,"tks":"حسن: رواه الترمذي (3781)، وابن خزيمة (1194)، وابن حبان (6960)، والحاكم (3/381)."},{"num":10038,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ أَبِي سَعِيدٍ قَالَ: قَالَ رَسُولُ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ: الْحَسَنُ وَالْحُسَيْنُ سَيِّدَا شَبَابِ أَهْلِ الْجَنَّةِ، وَفَاطِمَةُ سَيِّدَةُ نِسَاءِ أَهْلِ الْجَنَّةِ، إِلَّا مَا كَانَ مِنْ مَرْيَمَ ابْنَةِ عِمْرَانَ."],"takhrij":"حسن: رواه النسائي في الكبرى (8416)، وأحمد في مسنده (11618، 11756) وفي فضائل الصحابة (1331)، وأبو يعلى (1169) كلهم من حديث يزيد بن أبي زياد، عن عبدالرحمن بن أبي نعم، عن أبي سعيد الخدري فذكره.","grade":"حسن","chapter_ar":"باب أن الحسن والحسين سيدا شباب أهل الجنة","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب فضائل الصحابة وأخبارهم","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Hasan: Narrated by al-Nasā’ī in al-Sunan al-Kubrā (8416), Aḥmad in his Musnad (11618, 11756), and al-Ḥākim (4733).","chapter_en":"Al-Ḥasan and al-Ḥusayn Are the Leaders of the Youth of Paradise","part_en":"The Book of the Virtues and Accounts of the Companions","group_ar":"مجموع ما جاء في فضل جماعات الصحابة","group_en":"Collected Reports Concerning the Virtues of Groups of the Companions","part_no":49,"group_no":12,"chapter_no":14,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Abū Saʿīd al-Khudrī narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Al-Ḥasan and al-Ḥusayn are the leaders of the youth of Paradise, and Fāṭimah is the leader of the women of Paradise, except for Maryam, the daughter of ʿImrān.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"voc":["fazail",236],"full":1,"dr":1,"tks":"حسن: رواه النسائي في الكبرى (8416)، وأحمد في مسنده (11618، 11756)، والحاكم (4733)."},{"num":10039,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ أَبِي مُوسَى رَضِيَ اللَّهُ عَنْهُ قَالَ: كُنْتُ عِنْدَ النَّبِيِّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ وَهْوَ نَازِلٌ بِالْجِعْرَانَةِ بَيْنَ مَكَّةَ وَالْمَدِينَةِ، وَمَعَهُ بِلاَلٌ، فَأَتَى النَّبِيَّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ أَعْرَابِيٌّ فَقَالَ: أَلاَ تُنْجِزُ لِي مَا وَعَدْتَنِي. فَقَالَ لَهُ: أَبْشِرْ. فَقَالَ: قَدْ أَكْثَرْتَ عَلَىَّ مِنْ أَبْشِرْ. فَأَقْبَلَ عَلَى أَبِي مُوسَى وَبِلاَلٍ كَهَيْئَةِ الْغَضْبَانِ، فَقَالَ: رَدَّ الْبُشْرَى فَاقْبَلاَ أَنْتُمَا. قَالاَ: قَبِلْنَا. ثُمَّ دَعَا بِقَدَحٍ فِيهِ مَاءٌ فَغَسَلَ يَدَيْهِ وَوَجْهَهُ فِيهِ، وَمَجَّ فِيهِ، ثُمَّ قَالَ: اشْرَبَا مِنْهُ، وَأَفْرِغَا عَلَى وُجُوهِكُمَا وَنُحُورِكُمَا، وَأَبْشِرَا. فَأَخَذَا الْقَدَحَ فَفَعَلاَ، فَنَادَتْ أُمُّ سَلَمَةَ مِنْ وَرَاءِ السِّتْرِ: أَنْ أَفْضِلاَ لأُمِّكُمَا. فَأَفْضَلاَ لَهَا مِنْهُ طَائِفَةً."],"takhrij":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاري في المغازي (4328)، ومسلم في فضائل الصحابة (2497) كلاهما عن أبي كريب محمد بن العلاء، حدثنا أبو أسامة، عن بريد بن عبدالله، عن أبي بردة، عن أبي موسى قال: فذكره.","grade":"متفق عليه","chapter_ar":"باب في فضل أبي موسى الأشعري وبلال","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب فضائل الصحابة وأخبارهم","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Agreed upon: Narrated by al-Bukhārī (4328) and Muslim (2497).","chapter_en":"The Virtues of Abū Mūsā al-Ashʿarī and Bilāl","part_en":"The Book of the Virtues and Accounts of the Companions","group_ar":"مجموع ما جاء في فضل جماعات الصحابة","group_en":"Collected Reports Concerning the Virtues of Groups of the Companions","part_no":49,"group_no":12,"chapter_no":15,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Abū Mūsā narrated: I was with the Prophet ﷺ while he was staying at al-Jiʿrānah, between Makkah and Madinah, and Bilāl was with him. A Bedouin came to the Prophet ﷺ and said: “Will you not fulfill what you promised me?” The Prophet ﷺ replied: “Receive glad tidings.” The man said: “You have given me ‘glad tidings’ too many times.” The Prophet ﷺ then turned toward Abū Mūsā and Bilāl, appearing somewhat displeased, and said: “He has rejected the glad tidings, so you two accept them.” They both replied: “We accept them.” The Prophet ﷺ then called for a vessel containing water. He washed his hands and face in it, rinsed his mouth into it, and then said: “Drink from it, pour some of it over your faces and chests, and receive glad tidings.” They took the vessel and did as they were instructed. Umm Salamah then called out from behind the curtain: “Leave some for your mother.” So they left a portion of it for her."]}},"tuhfa":{},"voc":["fazail",237],"full":1,"rep":[1338,9250,14647],"tks":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (4328)، ومسلم (2497)."},{"num":10040,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ أَنَسٍ رَضِيَ اللَّهُ عَنْهُ أَنَّ رَجُلَيْنِ، خَرَجَا مِنْ عِنْدِ النَّبِيِّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ فِي لَيْلَةٍ مُظْلِمَةٍ، وَإِذَا نُورٌ بَيْنَ أَيْدِيهِمَا حَتَّى تَفَرَّقَا، فَتَفَرَّقَ النُّورُ مَعَهُمَا."],"takhrij":"صحيح: رواه البخاري في مناقب الأنصار (3805) عن علي بن مسلم، ثنا حبان، ثنا همام، أنا قتادة، عن أنس أن رجلين فذكره.","grade":"صحيح","chapter_ar":"باب في فضل أسيد بن حضير وعباد بن بشر","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب فضائل الصحابة وأخبارهم","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Authentic: Narrated by al-Bukhārī (3805).","chapter_en":"The Virtues of Usayd ibn Ḥuḍayr and ʿAbbād ibn Bishr","part_en":"The Book of the Virtues and Accounts of the Companions","group_ar":"مجموع ما جاء في فضل جماعات الصحابة","group_en":"Collected Reports Concerning the Virtues of Groups of the Companions","part_no":49,"group_no":12,"chapter_no":16,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Anas narrated: Two men departed from the Prophet ﷺ on a very dark night, and a light appeared before them. When they separated, the light also separated with them. Maʿmar narrated from Thābit, from Anas, that they were Usayd ibn Ḥuḍayr and another man from the Anṣār. Ḥammād narrated from Thābit, from Anas, that the two men were Usayd ibn Ḥuḍayr and ʿAbbād ibn Bishr."]}},"tuhfa":{},"voc":["fazail",238],"full":1,"dr":1,"rep":[10102],"tks":"صحيح: رواه البخاري (3805)."},{"num":10041,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ عَائِذِ بْنِ عَمْرٍو  أَنَّ أَبَا سُفْيَانَ أَتَى عَلَى سَلْمَانَ وَصُهَيْبٍ وَبِلَالٍ فِي نَفَرٍ فَقَالُوا: وَاللهِ مَا أَخَذَتْ سُيُوفُ اللَّهِ مِنْ عُنُقِ عَدُوِّ اللَّهِ مَأْخَذَهَا! قَالَ: فَقَالَ أَبُو بَكْرٍ: أَتَقُولُونَ هَذَا لِشَيْخِ قُرَيْشٍ وَسَيِّدِهِمْ! فَأَتَى النَّبِيَّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ فَأَخْبَرَهُ، فَقَالَ: يَا أَبَا بَكْرٍ، لَعَلَّكَ أَغْضَبْتَهُمْ، لَئِنْ كُنْتَ أَغْضَبْتَهُمْ لَقَدْ أَغْضَبْتَ رَبَّكَ. فَأَتَاهُمْ أَبُو بَكْرٍ فَقَالَ: يَا إِخْوَتَاهْ، أَغْضَبْتُكُمْ؟ قَالُوا: لَا، يَغْفِرُ اللَّهُ لَكَ يَا أَخِي."],"takhrij":"صحيح: رواه مسلم في فضائل الصحابة (2504) عن محمد بن حاتم، ثنا بهز، ثنا حماد بن سلمة، عن ثابت، عن معاوية بن قرة، عن عائذ بن عمرو، فذكره.","grade":"صحيح","chapter_ar":"باب ما جاء في فضل سلمان وصهيب وبلال","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب فضائل الصحابة وأخبارهم","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Authentic: Narrated by Muslim (2504).","chapter_en":"Reports Concerning the Virtues of Salmān, Ṣuhayb, and Bilāl","part_en":"The Book of the Virtues and Accounts of the Companions","group_ar":"مجموع ما جاء في فضل جماعات الصحابة","group_en":"Collected Reports Concerning the Virtues of Groups of the Companions","part_no":49,"group_no":12,"chapter_no":17,"content":{"translation":{"en":["ʿĀʾidh ibn ʿAmr narrated: Abū Sufyān passed by Salmān, Ṣuhayb, Bilāl, and a group of others. They said: “By Allah, the swords of Allah have not yet taken their full due from the neck of the enemy of Allah.” Abū Bakr said to them: “Do you say this to the elder of Quraysh and their chief?” He then went to the Prophet ﷺ and informed him. The Prophet ﷺ said: “O Abū Bakr, perhaps you have offended them. If you have indeed offended them, then you have offended your Lord.” Abū Bakr went back to them and said: “My brothers, have I offended you?” They replied: “No. May Allah forgive you, our brother.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"voc":["fazail",239],"full":1,"tks":"صحيح: رواه مسلم (2504)."},{"num":10042,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ الْبَرَاءِ قَالَ: اعْتَمَرَ النَّبِيُّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ فِي ذِي الْقَعْدَةِ الحديث...وَفِيهِ: قصة ابْنَةُ حَمْزَةَ وأنها تبعتهم حِينَ الخروج مِنْ مَكَّةَ، فَتَنَاوَلَهَا عَلِيٌّ فَأَخَذَ بِيَدِهَا، وَقَالَ لِفَاطِمَةَ: دُونَكِ ابْنَةَ عَمِّكِ، احْمِلِيهَا، فَاخْتَصَمَ فِيهَا عَلِيٌّ، وَزَيْدٌ، وَجَعْفَرٌ، فَقَالَ عَلِيٌّ: أَنَا أَحَقُّ بِهَا، وهي ابْنَةُ عَمِّي، وَقَالَ جَعْفَرٌ: ابْنَةُ عَمِّي وَخَالَتُهَا تَحْتِي، وَقَالَ زَيْدٌ: ابْنَةُ أَخِي، فَقَضَى بِهَا النَّبِيُّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ لِخَالَتِهَا وَقَالَ:الْخَالَةُ بِمَنْزِلَةِ الأُمِّ، وَقَالَ لِعَلِيٍّ: أَنْتَ مِنِّي وَأَنَا مِنْكَ، وَقَالَ لِجَعْفَرٍ: أَشْبَهْتَ خَلْقِي وَخُلُقِي، وَقَالَ لِزَيْدٍ: أَنْتَ أَخُونَا وَمَوْلاَنَا."],"takhrij":"صحيح: رواه البخاري في الصلح (2699) عن عبيدالله بن موسى، عن إسرئيل، عن أبي إسحاق، عن البراء قال: فذكره.","grade":"صحيح","chapter_ar":"باب في فضائل علي بن أبي طالب، وجعفر بن أبي طالب، وزيد بن حارثة","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب فضائل الصحابة وأخبارهم","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Authentic: Narrated by al-Bukhārī (2699).","chapter_en":"The Virtues of ʿAlī ibn Abī Ṭālib, Jaʿfar ibn Abī Ṭālib, and Zayd ibn Ḥārithah","part_en":"The Book of the Virtues and Accounts of the Companions","group_ar":"مجموع ما جاء في فضل جماعات الصحابة","group_en":"Collected Reports Concerning the Virtues of Groups of the Companions","part_no":49,"group_no":12,"chapter_no":18,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Al-Barāʾ narrated: The Prophet ﷺ performed ʿUmrah during the month of Dhū al-Qaʿdah… The narration includes the story of the daughter of Ḥamzah, who followed them as they were leaving Makkah. ʿAlī took her by the hand and said to Fāṭimah: “Take charge of your cousin.” Fāṭimah carried her. Then ʿAlī, Zayd, and Jaʿfar disputed over who had the greater right to care for her. ʿAlī said: “I have the greatest right to her, for she is my cousin.” Jaʿfar said: “She is my cousin, and her maternal aunt is my wife.” Zayd said: “She is the daughter of my brother.” The Prophet ﷺ awarded custody to her maternal aunt and said: “The maternal aunt is in the position of the mother.” He then said to ʿAlī: “You are from me, and I am from you.” He said to Jaʿfar: “You resemble me in both appearance and character.” And he said to Zayd: “You are our brother and our freedman.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"voc":["fazail",240],"full":1,"rep":[6588],"tks":"صحيح: رواه البخاري (2699)."},{"num":10043,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ عَلِيٍّ، قَالَ: لَمَّا خَرَجْنَا مِنْ مَكَّةَ اتَّبَعَتْنَا ابْنَةُ حَمْزَةَ تُنَادِي: يَا عَمِّ، يَا عَمِّ. قَالَ: فَتَنَاوَلْتُهَا بِيَدِهَا، فَدَفَعْتُهَا إِلَى فَاطِمَةَ، فَقُلْتُ: دُونَكِ ابْنَةَ عَمِّكِ. قَالَ: فَلَمَّا قَدِمْنَا الْمَدِينَةَ اخْتَصَمْنَا فِيهَا أَنَا وَجَعْفَرٌ وَزَيْدُ بْنُ حَارِثَةَ، فَقَالَ جَعْفَرٌ: ابْنَةُ عَمِّي، وَخَالَتُهَا عِنْدِي، - يَعْنِي أَسْمَاءَ بِنْتَ عُمَيْسٍ، - وَقَالَ زَيْدٌ: ابْنَةُ أَخِي. وَقُلْتُ: أَنَا أَخَذْتُهَا وَهِيَ ابْنَةُ عَمِّي. فَقَالَ رَسُولُ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ: أَمَّا أَنْتَ يَا جَعْفَرُ، فَأَشْبَهْتَ خَلْقِي وَخُلُقِي، وَأَمَّا أَنْتَ يَا عَلِيُّ، فَمِنِّي وَأَنَا مِنْكَ، وَأَمَّا أَنْتَ يَا زَيْدُ، فَأَخُونَا وَمَوْلَانَا، وَالْجَارِيَةُ عِنْدَ خَالَتِهَا، فَإِنَّ الْخَالَةَ وَالِدَةٌ قُلْتُ: يَا رَسُولَ اللَّهِ، أَلَا تَزَوَّجُهَا؟ قَالَ: إِنَّهَا ابْنَةُ أَخِي مِنَ الرَّضَاعَةِ."],"takhrij":"حسن: رواه أبو داود (2280)، وأحمد (770) واللفظ له، وصحّحه الحاكم (4614) كلهم من طريق أبي إسحاق، عن هانئ بن هانئ وهبيرة بن يريم، عن علي بن أبي طالب فذكره.","grade":"حسن","chapter_ar":"باب في فضائل علي بن أبي طالب، وجعفر بن أبي طالب، وزيد بن حارثة","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب فضائل الصحابة وأخبارهم","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Hasan: Narrated by Abū Dāwūd (2280), Aḥmad (770), whose wording is cited here, and authenticated by al-Ḥākim (4614).","chapter_en":"The Virtues of ʿAlī ibn Abī Ṭālib, Jaʿfar ibn Abī Ṭālib, and Zayd ibn Ḥārithah","part_en":"The Book of the Virtues and Accounts of the Companions","group_ar":"مجموع ما جاء في فضل جماعات الصحابة","group_en":"Collected Reports Concerning the Virtues of Groups of the Companions","part_no":49,"group_no":12,"chapter_no":18,"content":{"translation":{"en":["ʿAlī ibn Abī Ṭālib narrated: When we departed from Makkah, the daughter of Ḥamzah followed us, calling out: “O my uncle! O my uncle!” I took her by the hand and entrusted her to Fāṭimah, saying: “Take charge of your cousin.” When we arrived in Madinah, Jaʿfar, Zayd ibn Ḥārithah, and I disputed over her custody. Jaʿfar said: “She is my cousin, and her maternal aunt—Asmāʾ bint ʿUmays—is with me.” Zayd said: “She is the daughter of my brother.” I said: “I took responsibility for her, and she is my cousin.” The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “As for you, Jaʿfar, you resemble me in both appearance and character. As for you, ʿAlī, you are from me, and I am from you. As for you, Zayd, you are our brother and our freedman. The girl shall remain with her maternal aunt, for the maternal aunt is like a mother.” I then asked: “O Messenger of Allah, will you not marry her?” He replied: “She is the daughter of my foster brother.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"voc":["fazail",241],"full":1,"dr":1,"rep":[6589],"tks":"حسن: رواه أبو داود (2280)، وأحمد (770) واللفظ له، وصححه الحاكم (4614)."},{"num":10044,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ أُسَامَةَ بن زَيْدٍ قَالَ: اجْتَمَعَ جَعْفَرٌ وَعَلِيٌّ وَزَيْدُ بْنُ حَارِثَةَ، فَقَالَ جَعْفَرٌ: أَنَا أَحَبُّكُمْ إِلَى رَسُولِ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ، ، وَقَالَ عَلِيٌّ: أَنَا أَحَبُّكُمْ إِلَى رَسُولِ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ، ، وَقَالَ زَيْدٌ: أَنَا أَحَبُّكُمْ إِلَى رَسُولِ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ فَقَالُوا: انْطَلِقُوا بِنَا إِلَى رَسُولِ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ حَتَّى نَسْأَلَهُ، فَقَالَ أُسَامَةُ بْنُ زَيْدٍ: فجاؤوا يَسْتَأْذِنُونَهُ فَقَالَ: اخْرُجْ فَانْظُرْ مَنْ هَؤُلَاءِ؟ فَقُلْتُ هَذَا جَعْفَرٌ وَعَلِيٌّ وَزَيْدٌ - مَا أَقُولُ: أَبِي- قَالَ: ائْذَنْ لَهُمْ.وَدَخَلُوا فَقَالُوا: مَنْ أَحَبُّ إِلَيْكَ؟ قَالَ: فَاطِمَةُ.قَالُوا:نَسْأَلُكَ عَنِ الرِّجَالِ، قَالَ: أَمَّا أَنْتَ يَا جَعْفَرُ فَأَشْبَهَ خُلُقك خُلُقي، وَأَشْبَهَ خَلْقي خَلْقك، وَأَنْتَ مِنِّي وَشَجَرَتِي، وَأَمَّا أَنْتَ يَا عليُّ فَخَتني وَأَبُو وَلَدِي، وَأَنَا مِنْكَ وَأَنْتَ مِنِّي، وَأَمَّا أَنْتَ يَا زَيْدُ فَمَوْلَايَ وَمِنِّي وإليَّ وَأَحَبُّ الْقَوْمِ إليَّ."],"takhrij":"حسن: رواه أحمد (21777)، والنسائي في خصائص علي (138)، والحاكم (4957) كلهم من طريق محمد بن سلمة، عن محمد بن إسحاق، عن يزيد بن عبدالله بن قسيط، عن محمد بن أسامة، عن أبيه قال: فذكره.","grade":"حسن","chapter_ar":"باب في فضائل علي بن أبي طالب، وجعفر بن أبي طالب، وزيد بن حارثة","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب فضائل الصحابة وأخبارهم","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Hasan: Narrated by Aḥmad (21777), al-Nasā’ī in Khaṣāʾiṣ ʿAlī (138), and al-Ḥākim (4957).","chapter_en":"The Virtues of ʿAlī ibn Abī Ṭālib, Jaʿfar ibn Abī Ṭālib, and Zayd ibn Ḥārithah","part_en":"The Book of the Virtues and Accounts of the Companions","group_ar":"مجموع ما جاء في فضل جماعات الصحابة","group_en":"Collected Reports Concerning the Virtues of Groups of the Companions","part_no":49,"group_no":12,"chapter_no":18,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Usāmah ibn Zayd narrated: Jaʿfar, ʿAlī, and Zayd ibn Ḥārithah gathered together. Jaʿfar said: “I am the most beloved of you to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ.” ʿAlī said: “I am the most beloved of you to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ.” Zayd said: “I am the most beloved of you to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ.” They then said: “Let us go to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and ask him.” Usāmah ibn Zayd said: They came seeking permission to enter. The Prophet ﷺ said to me: “Go out and see who they are.” I replied: “They are Jaʿfar, ʿAlī, and Zayd”—I did not say, “my father.” He said: “Permit them to enter.” They entered and asked: “Who is most beloved to you?” He replied: “Fāṭimah.” They said: “We are asking you about the men.” He said: “As for you, Jaʿfar, your character resembles my character, and your appearance resembles my appearance. You are from me and from my family tree. As for you, ʿAlī, you are my son-in-law and the father of my children. I am from you, and you are from me. As for you, Zayd, you are my freedman, from me and close to me, and the most beloved of these men to me.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"voc":["fazail",242],"full":1,"dr":1,"tks":"حسن: رواه أحمد (21777)، والنسائي في خصائص علي (138)، والحاكم (4957)."},{"num":10045,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ خَالِدِ بْنِ سُمَيْرٍ قَالَ: قَدِمَ عَلَيْنَا عَبْدُ اللَّهِ بْنُ رَبَاحٍ فَوَجَدْتُهُ قَدْ اجْتَمَعَ إِلَيْهِ نَاسٌ مِنَ النَّاسِ، قَالَ: حَدَّثَنَا أَبُو قَتَادَةَ فَارِسُ رَسُولِ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ قَالَ: بَعَثَ رَسُولُ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ جَيْشَ الْأُمَرَاءِ وَقَالَ: عَلَيْكُمْ زَيْدُ بْنُ حَارِثَةَ، فَإِنْ أُصِيبَ زَيْدٌ، فجَعْفَرٌ، فَإِنْ أُصِيبَ جَعْفَرٌ، فعَبْدُ اللهِ بْنُ رَوَاحَةَ الْأَنْصَارِيُّ فَوَثَبَ جَعْفَرٌ فَقَالَ: بِأَبِي أَنْتَ يَا نَبِيَّ اللَّهِ وَأُمِّي مَا كُنْتُ أَرْهَبُ أَنْ تَسْتَعْمِلَ عَلَيَّ زَيْدًا، قَالَ: امْضُوا، فَإِنَّكَ لَا تَدْرِي أَيُّ ذَلِكَ خَيْرٌ. قَالَ: فَانْطَلَقَ الْجَيْشُ فَلَبِثُوا مَا شَاءَ اللَّهُ، ثُمَّ إِنَّ رَسُولَ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ صَعِدَ الْمِنْبَرَ، وَأَمَرَ أَنْ يُنَادَى: الصَّلَاةُ جَامِعَةٌ، فَقَالَ رَسُولُ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ: نَابَ خَبرٌ، أَوْ ثَابَ خَبَرٌ، شَكَّ عَبْدُ الرَّحْمَنِ، أَلَا أُخْبِرُكُمْ عَنْ جَيْشِكُمْ هَذَا الْغَازِي، إِنَّهُمْ انْطَلَقُوا حَتَّى لَقُوا الْعَدُوَّ، فَأُصِيبَ زَيْدٌ شَهِيدًا، فَاسْتَغْفِرُوا لَهُ. فَاسْتَغْفَرَ لَهُ النَّاسُ، ثُمَّ أَخَذَ اللِّوَاءَ جَعْفَرُ بْنُ أَبِي طَالِبٍ فَشَدَّ عَلَى الْقَوْمِ حَتَّى قُتِلَ شَهِيدًا، أَشْهَدُ لَهُ بِالشَّهَادَةِ، فَاسْتَغْفِرُوا لَهُ، ثُمَّ أَخَذَ اللِّوَاءَ عَبْدُ اللَّهِ بْنُ رَوَاحَةَ، فَأَثْبَتَ قَدَمَيْهِ حَتَّى أُصِيبَ شَهِيدًا، فَاسْتَغْفِرُوا لَهُ، ثُمَّ أَخَذَ اللِّوَاءَ خَالِدُ بْنُ الْوَلِيدِ وَلَمْ يَكُنْ مِنَ الْأُمَرَاءِ، هُوَ أَمَّرَ نَفْسَهُ. فَرَفَعَ رَسُولُ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ أُصْبُعَيْهِ وَقَالَ: اللهُمَّ هُوَ سَيْفٌ مِنْ سُيُوفِكَ فَانْصُرْهُ، وَقَالَ عَبْدُ الرَّحْمَنِ مَرَّةً: فَانْتَصِرْ بِهِ. فَيَوْمَئِذٍ سُمِّيَ خَالِدٌ سَيْفَ اللهِ، ثُمَّ قَالَ النَّبِيُّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ: انْفِرُوا، فَأَمِدُّوا إِخْوَانَكُمْ، وَلَا يَتَخَلَّفَنَّ أَحَدٌ فَنَفَرَ النَّاسُ فِي حَرٍّ شَدِيدٍ مُشَاةً وَرُكْبَانًا."],"takhrij":"حسن: رواه النسائي في الكبرى (8159)، وأحمد (22551)-والسياق له-، وابن حبان (7048) كلهم من طرق عن الأسود بن شيبان، عن خالد بن سمير فذكره.","grade":"حسن","chapter_ar":"باب ما جاء في فضائل زيد بن حارثة، وجعفر، وعبد الله بن رواحة، وخالد بن الوليد","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب فضائل الصحابة وأخبارهم","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Hasan: Narrated by al-Nasā’ī in al-Sunan al-Kubrā (8159), Aḥmad (22551), whose wording is cited here, and authenticated by Ibn Ḥibbān (7048).","chapter_en":"Reports Concerning the Virtues of Zayd ibn Ḥārithah, Jaʿfar, ʿAbdullāh ibn Rawāḥah, and Khālid ibn al-Walīd","part_en":"The Book of the Virtues and Accounts of the Companions","group_ar":"مجموع ما جاء في فضل جماعات الصحابة","group_en":"Collected Reports Concerning the Virtues of Groups of the Companions","part_no":49,"group_no":12,"chapter_no":19,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Khālid ibn Sumayr narrated: ʿAbdullāh ibn Rabāḥ came to us, and I found a group of people gathered around him. He said: Abū Qatādah, the horseman of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, narrated to us: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ dispatched the army of commanders and said: “Zayd ibn Ḥārithah shall be in command over you. If Zayd is struck down, then Jaʿfar shall take command. If Jaʿfar is struck down, then ʿAbdullāh ibn Rawāḥah al-Anṣārī shall take command.” Jaʿfar sprang up and said: “May my father and mother be sacrificed for you, O Prophet of Allah. I never expected that you would appoint Zayd over me.” He replied: “Proceed, for you do not know which of the two situations is better.” The army departed and remained away for as long as Allah willed. Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ ascended the pulpit and ordered that the call be made: “Gather for prayer.” The Messenger of Allah ﷺ then said: “News has come—or good news has returned; ʿAbd al-Raḥmān was uncertain—which I shall tell you concerning this army of yours that went out to fight. They proceeded until they met the enemy. Zayd was struck down as a martyr, so seek forgiveness for him.” The people sought forgiveness for him. He continued: “Then Jaʿfar ibn Abī Ṭālib took the banner and charged against the enemy until he was killed as a martyr. I bear witness that he is a martyr, so seek forgiveness for him. Then ʿAbdullāh ibn Rawāḥah took the banner and stood his ground until he was struck down as a martyr, so seek forgiveness for him. Then Khālid ibn al-Walīd took the banner. He had not been one of the appointed commanders, but he assumed command himself.” The Messenger of Allah ﷺ raised two of his fingers and said: “O Allah, he is a sword from among Your swords, so grant him victory.” On another occasion, ʿAbd al-Raḥmān narrated the wording: “So grant victory through him.” From that day onward, Khālid was called the Sword of Allah. The Prophet ﷺ then said: “Go forth and reinforce your brothers, and let no one remain behind.” The people set out in intense heat, some on foot and others mounted."]}},"tuhfa":{},"voc":["fazail",243],"full":1,"dr":1,"rep":[3540],"tks":"حسن: رواه النسائي في الكبرى (8159)، وأحمد (22551) - والسياق له -، وصححه ابن حبان (7048)."},{"num":10046,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ أَنَسٍ قَالَ: جَمَعَ الْقُرْآنَ عَلَى عَهْدِ رَسُولِ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ أَرْبَعَةٌ كُلُّهُمْ مِنَ الأَنْصَارِ: معاذ بْنُ جَبَلٍ، وأبي بْنُ كَعْبٍ، وَزَيْدُ بْنُ ثَابِتٍ، وَأَبُو زَيْدٍ.","قَالَ قَتَادَةُ: \" قُلْتُ لِأَنَسٍ : مَنْ أَبُو زَيْدٍ؟ قَالَ: أَحَدُ عُمُومَتِي\"."],"takhrij":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاري في مناقب الأنصار (3810)، ومسلم في فضائل الصحابة (2465-119) كلاهما من طريق شعبة عن قتادة قال: سمعت أنسا يقول فذكره.","grade":"متفق عليه","chapter_ar":"باب ما جاء في فضائل أربعة من الأنصار جمعوا القرآن على عهد رسول الله ﷺ","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب فضائل الصحابة وأخبارهم","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Agreed upon: Narrated by al-Bukhārī (3810) and Muslim (2465, no. 119).","chapter_en":"Reports Concerning the Virtues of Four Men from the Anṣār Who Collected the Qur’an during the Lifetime of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ","part_en":"The Book of the Virtues and Accounts of the Companions","group_ar":"مجموع ما جاء في فضل جماعات الصحابة","group_en":"Collected Reports Concerning the Virtues of Groups of the Companions","part_no":49,"group_no":12,"chapter_no":20,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Anas narrated: Four men collected the Qur’an during the lifetime of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, all of whom were from the Anṣār: Muʿādh ibn Jabal, Ubayy ibn Kaʿb, Zayd ibn Thābit, and Abū Zayd. Qatādah said: I asked Anas: “Who was Abū Zayd?” He replied: “One of my paternal uncles.”"]},"buhuth":{"en":["In another wording:","I asked Anas ibn Mālik:","“Who collected the Qur’an during the lifetime of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ?”","He replied:","“Four men, all of whom were from the Anṣār…”","He then mentioned the same narration.","Recorded by al-Bukhārī (5003) and Muslim (2465, no. 120)."]}},"tuhfa":{},"voc":["fazail",244],"full":1,"dr":1,"tks":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (3810)، ومسلم (2465-119)."},{"num":10047,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ مَسْرُوقٍ قَالَ:  ذَكَرُوا ابْنَ مَسْعُودٍ عِنْدَ عَبْدِ اللَّهِ بْنِ عَمْرٍو فَقَالَ: ذَاكَ رَجُلٌ لَا أَزَالُ أُحِبُّهُ بَعْدَمَا سَمِعْتُ مِنْ رَسُولِ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ يَقُولُ: اسْتَقْرِئُوا الْقُرْآنَ مِنْ أَرْبَعَةٍ؛ مِنِ ابْنِ مَسْعُودٍ، وَسَالِمٍ مَوْلَى أَبِي حُذَيْفَةَ، وَأُبَيِّ بْنِ كَعْبٍ، وَمُعَاذِ بْنِ جَبَلٍ."],"takhrij":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاري في فضائل الصحابة (3758)، ومسلم في فضائل الصحابة (2464-118) كلاهما من طريق شعبة عن عمرو بن مرة، عن إبراهيم، عن مسروق قال: فذكره.وهذا لفظ مسلم، وزاد البخاري في آ خره: \"قال: لا أدري بدأ بأُبي أو بمعاذ\".","grade":"متفق عليه","chapter_ar":"باب في بيان أربعة من الصحابة يؤخذ عنهم القرآن","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب فضائل الصحابة وأخبارهم","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Authentic: Narrated by al-Bukhārī (3758) and Muslim (2464, no. 118).","chapter_en":"Identifying Four Companions from Whom the Qur’an Should Be Learned","part_en":"The Book of the Virtues and Accounts of the Companions","group_ar":"مجموع ما جاء في فضل جماعات الصحابة","group_en":"Collected Reports Concerning the Virtues of Groups of the Companions","part_no":49,"group_no":12,"chapter_no":21,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Masrūq narrated: Ibn Masʿūd was mentioned in the presence of ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿAmr, and he said: “He is a man whom I shall always continue to love after hearing the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: ‘Learn the Qur’an from four: Ibn Masʿūd, Sālim the freedman of Abū Ḥudhayfah, Ubayy ibn Kaʿb, and Muʿādh ibn Jabal.’”"]},"buhuth":{"en":["In one wording:","“Learn the Qur’an from four men.”","In another wording:","“Take the Qur’an from four.”","He then named them.","Recorded by Muslim (2464, nos. 116–117)."]}},"tuhfa":{},"voc":["fazail",245],"full":1,"dr":1,"tks":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (3758)، ومسلم (2464-118)."},{"num":10048,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ أَبِي هُرَيْرَةَ أَنَّ رَسُولَ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ قَالَ: نِعْمَ الرَّجُلُ أَبُو بَكْرٍ، نِعْمَ الرَّجُلُ عُمَرُ، نِعْمَ الرَّجُلُ أَبُو عُبَيْدَةَ بْنُ الْجَرَّاحِ، نِعْمَ الرَّجُلُ أُسَيْدُ بْنُ حُضَيْرٍ، نِعْمَ الرَّجُلُ ثَابِتُ بْنُ قَيْسِ بْنِ شَمَّاسٍ، نِعْمَ الرَّجُلُ مُعَاذُ بْنُ جَبَلٍ، نِعْمَ الرَّجُلُ مُعَاذُ بن عَمْرِو بْنِ الْجَمُوحِ."],"takhrij":"حسن: رواه أحمد (9431)، والنسائي في الكبرى (8186)، وصحّحه ابن حبان (7129،6997)، والحاكم (3/233، 3/268) كلهم من طرق عن سهيل بن أبي صالح، عن أبيه، عن أبي هريرة فذكره.","grade":"حسن","chapter_ar":"باب ما جاء في فضل أبي بكر، وعمر، وأبي عبيدة، وأسيد بن حضير، وثابت بن قيس، ومعاذ بن جبل، ومعاذ بن عمرو بن الجموح","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب فضائل الصحابة وأخبارهم","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Hasan: Narrated by Aḥmad (9431), al-Nasā’ī in al-Sunan al-Kubrā (8186), and authenticated by Ibn Ḥibbān (6997, 7129).","chapter_en":"Reports Concerning the Virtues of Abū Bakr, ʿUmar, Abū ʿUbaydah, Usayd ibn Ḥuḍayr, Thābit ibn Qays, Muʿādh ibn Jabal, and Muʿādh ibn ʿAmr ibn al-Jamūḥ","part_en":"The Book of the Virtues and Accounts of the Companions","group_ar":"مجموع ما جاء في فضل جماعات الصحابة","group_en":"Collected Reports Concerning the Virtues of Groups of the Companions","part_no":49,"group_no":12,"chapter_no":22,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Abū Hurayrah narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “What an excellent man Abū Bakr is. What an excellent man ʿUmar is. What an excellent man Abū ʿUbaydah ibn al-Jarrāḥ is. What an excellent man Usayd ibn Ḥuḍayr is. What an excellent man Thābit ibn Qays ibn Shammās is. What an excellent man Muʿādh ibn Jabal is. What an excellent man Muʿādh ibn ʿAmr ibn al-Jamūḥ is.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"voc":["fazail",246],"full":1,"dr":1,"tks":"حسن: رواه أحمد (9431)، والنسائي في الكبرى (8186)، وصححه ابن حبان (6997، 7129)."},{"num":10049,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ أَبِي مُوسَى رَضِيَ اللَّهُ عَنْهُ قَالَ: لَمَّا فَرَغَ النَّبِيُّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ مِنْ حُنَيْنٍ بَعَثَ أَبَا عَامِرٍ عَلَى جَيْشٍ إِلَى أَوْطَاسٍ، فَلَقِيَ دُرَيْدَ بْنَ الصِّمَّةِ، فَقُتِلَ دُرَيْدٌ وَهَزَمَ اللَّهُ أَصْحَابَهُ. قَالَ أَبُو مُوسَى: وَبَعَثَنِي مَعَ أَبِي عَامِرٍ، فَرُمِيَ أَبُو عَامِرٍ فِي رُكْبَتِهِ، رَمَاهُ جُشَمِيٌّ بِسَهْمٍ فَأَثْبَتَهُ فِي رُكْبَتِهِ، فَانْتَهَيْتُ إِلَيْهِ فَقُلْتُ: يَا عَمِّ مَنْ رَمَاكَ؟ فَأَشَارَ إِلَى أَبِي مُوسَى فَقَالَ: ذَاكَ قَاتِلِي الَّذِي رَمَانِي. فَقَصَدْتُ لَهُ فَلَحِقْتُهُ، فَلَمَّا رَآنِي وَلَّى فَاتَّبَعْتُهُ وَجَعَلْتُ أَقُولُ لَهُ: أَلاَ تَسْتَحِي، أَلاَ تَثْبُتُ. فَكَفَّ، فَاخْتَلَفْنَا ضَرْبَتَيْنِ بِالسَّيْفِ فَقَتَلْتُهُ، ثُمَّ قُلْتُ لأَبِي عَامِرٍ قَتَلَ اللَّهُ صَاحِبَكَ. قَالَ: فَانْزِع هَذَا السَّهْمَ، فَنَزَعْتُهُ فَنَزَا مِنْهُ الْمَاءُ. قَالَ: يَا ابْنَ أَخِي أَقْرِئِ النَّبِيَّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ السَّلاَمَ، وَقُلْ لَهُ: اسْتَغْفِرْ لِي. وَاسْتَخْلَفَنِي أَبُو عَامِرٍ عَلَى النَّاسِ، فَمَكَثَ يَسِيرًا ثُمَّ مَاتَ، فَرَجَعْتُ فَدَخَلْتُ عَلَى النَّبِيِّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ فِي بَيْتِهِ عَلَى سَرِيرٍ مُرْمَلٍ وَعَلَيْهِ فِرَاشٌ، قَدْ أَثَّرَ رِمَالُ السَّرِيرِ بِظَهْرِهِ وَجَنْبَيْهِ، فَأَخْبَرْتُهُ بِخَبَرِنَا وَخَبَرِ أَبِي عَامِرٍ، وَقَالَ: قُلْ لَهُ: اسْتَغْفِرْ لِي، فَدَعَا بِمَاءٍ فَتَوَضَّأَ، ثُمَّ رَفَعَ يَدَيْهِ فَقَالَ: اللَّهُمَّ اغْفِرْ لِعُبَيْدٍ أَبِي عَامِرٍ. وَرَأَيْتُ بَيَاضَ إِبْطَيْهِ، ثُمَّ قَالَ: اللَّهُمَّ اجْعَلْهُ يَوْمَ الْقِيَامَةِ فَوْقَ كَثِيرٍ مِنْ خَلْقِكَ مِنَ النَّاسِ. فَقُلْتُ وَلِي فَاسْتَغْفِرْ. فَقَالَ: اللَّهُمَّ اغْفِرْ لِعَبْدِ اللَّهِ بْنِ قَيْسٍ ذَنْبَهُ، وَأَدْخِلْهُ يَوْمَ الْقِيَامَةِ مُدْخَلاً كَرِيمًا. قَالَ أَبُو بُرْدَةَ: إِحْدَاهُمَا لأَبِي عَامِرٍ، وَالأُخْرَى لأَبِي مُوسَى."],"takhrij":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاري في المغازي (4323)، ومسلم في فضائل الصحابة (2498) كلاهما عن أبي كريب محمد بن العلاء، ثنا أبو أسامة، عن بريد بن عبدالله، عن أبي بردة، عن أبيه أبي موسى الأشعري قال: فذكره.","grade":"متفق عليه","chapter_ar":"باب في فضل أبي موسى، وأبي عامر الأشعريين","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب فضائل الصحابة وأخبارهم","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Agreed upon: Narrated by al-Bukhārī (4323) and Muslim (2498).","chapter_en":"The Virtues of Abū Mūsā and Abū ʿĀmir al-Ashʿarī","part_en":"The Book of the Virtues and Accounts of the Companions","group_ar":"مجموع ما جاء في فضل جماعات الصحابة","group_en":"Collected Reports Concerning the Virtues of Groups of the Companions","part_no":49,"group_no":12,"chapter_no":23,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Abū Mūsā narrated: When the Prophet ﷺ had finished with the Battle of Ḥunayn, he sent Abū ʿĀmir at the head of an army toward Awṭās. He encountered Durayd ibn al-Ṣimmah. Durayd was killed, and Allah defeated his companions. Abū Mūsā said: The Prophet ﷺ sent me with Abū ʿĀmir. Abū ʿĀmir was struck in the knee by an arrow shot by a man from Jusham, and the arrow lodged in his knee. I reached him and said: “O uncle, who shot you?” Abū ʿĀmir pointed and said: “That is the man who killed me, the one who shot me.” I went after him and caught up with him. When he saw me, he turned and fled. I pursued him, saying: “Are you not ashamed? Will you not stand your ground?” He stopped, and we exchanged two sword blows. I killed him. I then returned to Abū ʿĀmir and said: “Allah has killed your attacker.” He said: “Pull this arrow out.” I removed it, and water began to flow from the wound. He then said: “O son of my brother, convey my greetings of peace to the Prophet ﷺ and ask him to seek forgiveness for me.” Abū ʿĀmir appointed me to lead the people after him. He remained alive for only a short time and then died. I returned and entered upon the Prophet ﷺ in his house. He was lying upon a woven bed with a mattress upon it, and the cords of the bed had left marks upon his back and sides. I informed him of what had happened to us and of what had happened to Abū ʿĀmir, and I told him that Abū ʿĀmir had asked him to seek forgiveness for him. The Prophet ﷺ called for water, performed ablution, then raised his hands and said: “O Allah, forgive ʿUbayd Abū ʿĀmir.” I could see the whiteness of his armpits. He then said: “O Allah, place him on the Day of Resurrection above many of the people You created.” I said: “And seek forgiveness for me as well.” He said: “O Allah, forgive the sin of ʿAbdullāh ibn Qays and admit him on the Day of Resurrection through an honorable entrance.” Abū Burdah said: One supplication was for Abū ʿĀmir, and the other was for Abū Mūsā."]},"buhuth":{"en":["The statement, “He pointed to Abū Mūsā and said: ‘That is my killer who shot me,’” means that Abū ʿĀmir spoke to Abū Mūsā while pointing toward the attacker, saying:","“That is the man who killed me, the one who shot me.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"voc":["fazail",247],"full":1,"dr":1,"tks":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (4323)، ومسلم (2498)."},{"num":10050,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ أُسَامَةَ بْنِ زَيْدٍ رَضِيَ اللَّهُ عَنْهُمَا حَدَّثَ عَنِ النَّبِيِّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ أَنَّهُ كَانَ يَأْخُذُهُ وَالْحَسَنَ، فَيَقُولُ: اللَّهُمَّ أَحِبَّهُمَا فَإِنِّي أُحِبُّهُمَا."],"takhrij":"صحيح: رواه البخاري في فضائل أصحاب النبي صلى الله عليه وسلم (3735) عن موسى بن إسماعيل، حدثنا معتمر قال: سمعت أبي، حدثنا أبو عثمان، عن أسامة بن زيد فذكره.","grade":"صحيح","chapter_ar":"باب حب النبي ﷺ لأسامة والحسن","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب فضائل الصحابة وأخبارهم","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Authentic: Narrated by al-Bukhārī (3735).","chapter_en":"The Prophet’s ﷺ Love for Usāmah and al-Ḥasan","part_en":"The Book of the Virtues and Accounts of the Companions","group_ar":"مجموع ما جاء في فضل جماعات الصحابة","group_en":"Collected Reports Concerning the Virtues of Groups of the Companions","part_no":49,"group_no":12,"chapter_no":24,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Usāmah ibn Zayd narrated that the Prophet ﷺ would take him and al-Ḥasan together and say: “O Allah, love them both, for I love them both.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"voc":["fazail",248],"full":1,"rep":[10095,10163],"tks":"صحيح: رواه البخاري (3735)."},{"num":10051,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عن عَمْرِو بْنِ الْعَاصِ يَقُولُ: فَزِعَ النَّاسُ بِالْمَدِينَةِ مَعَ النَّبِيِّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ فَتَفَرَّقُوا، فَرَأَيْتُ سَالِمًا مَوْلَى أَبِي حُذَيْفَةَ احْتَبَى بِسَيْفِهِ، وَجَلَسَ فِي الْمَسْجِدِ، فَلَمَّا رَأَيْتُ ذَلِكَ، فَعَلْتُ مِثْلَ الَّذِي فَعَلَ، فَخَرَجَ رَسُولُ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ فَرَآنِي وَسَالِمًا، وَأَتَى النَّاسُ، فَقَالَ رَسُولُ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ: يَا أَيُّهَا النَّاسُ، أَلَا كَانَ مَفْزَعُكُمْ إِلَى اللَّهِ وَرَسُولِهِ، هَلَّا فَعَلْتُمْ كَمَا فَعَلَ هَذَانِ الرَّجُلَانِ الْمُؤْمِنَانِ؟"],"takhrij":"صحيح: رواه أحمد (17810)، والنسائي في الكبرى (8243)، وصحّحه ابن حبان (7092) كلهم من طريق موسى بن علي بن رباح قال: سمعت أبي يقول: سمعت عمرو بن العاص يقول فذكره.وإسناده صحيح.","grade":"صحيح","chapter_ar":"باب فضل سالم مولى أبي حذيفة وعمرو بن العاص","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب فضائل الصحابة وأخبارهم","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Authentic: Narrated by Aḥmad (17810), al-Nasā’ī in al-Sunan al-Kubrā (8243), and authenticated by Ibn Ḥibbān (7092).","chapter_en":"The Virtue of Sālim, the Freedman of Abū Ḥudhayfah, and ʿAmr ibn al-ʿĀṣ","part_en":"The Book of the Virtues and Accounts of the Companions","group_ar":"مجموع ما جاء في فضل جماعات الصحابة","group_en":"Collected Reports Concerning the Virtues of Groups of the Companions","part_no":49,"group_no":12,"chapter_no":27,"content":{"translation":{"en":["ʿAmr ibn al-ʿĀṣ narrated: The people in Madinah were suddenly alarmed while the Prophet ﷺ was among them, and they scattered. I saw Sālim, the freedman of Abū Ḥudhayfah, sitting in the mosque with his knees drawn up, using the straps of his sword. When I saw him, I did the same as he had done. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ came out and saw Sālim and me, while the rest of the people were arriving. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “O people, should not your place of refuge be with Allah and His Messenger? Why did you not do as these two believing men did?”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"voc":["fazail",249],"full":1,"dr":1,"tks":"صحيح: رواه أحمد (17810)، والنسائي في الكبرى (8243)، وصححه ابن حبان (7092)."},{"num":10052,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ عَلْقَمَةَ،، قَالَ: قَدِمْتُ الشَّأْمَ فَصَلَّيْتُ رَكْعَتَيْنِ، ثُمَّ قُلْتُ: اللَّهُمَّ يَسِّرْ لِي جَلِيسًا صَالِحًا، فَأَتَيْتُ قَوْمًا فَجَلَسْتُ إِلَيْهِمْ، فَإِذَا شَيْخٌ قَدْ جَاءَ حَتَّى جَلَسَ إِلَى جَنْبِي، قُلْتُ مَنْ هَذَا؟ قَالُوا: أَبُو الدَّرْدَاءِ. فَقُلْتُ إِنِّي دَعَوْتُ اللَّهَ أَنْ يُيَسِّرَ لِي جَلِيسًا صَالِحًا فَيَسَّرَكَ لِي، قَالَ: مِمَّنْ أَنْتَ؟ قُلْتُ: مِنْ أَهْلِ الْكُوفَةِ. قَالَ: أَوَلَيْسَ عِنْدَكُمُ ابْنُ أُمِّ عَبْدٍ، صَاحِبُ النَّعْلَيْنِ وَالْوِسَادِ وَالْمِطْهَرَةِ؟ وَفِيكُمُ الَّذِي أَجَارَهُ اللَّهُ مِنَ الشَّيْطَانِ عَلَى لِسَانِ نَبِيِّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ أَوَلَيْسَ فِيكُمْ صَاحِبُ سِرِّ النَّبِيِّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ الَّذِي لاَ يَعْلَمُ أَحَدٌ غَيْرُهُ؟، ثُمَّ قَالَ: كَيْفَ يَقْرَأُ عَبْدُ اللَّهِ {وَاللَّيْلِ إِذَا يَغْشَى}، فَقَرَأْتُ عَلَيْهِ: {وَاللَّيْلِ إِذَا يَغْشَى * وَالنَّهَارِ إِذَا تَجَلَّى * وَالذَّكَرِ وَالأُنْثَى}. قَالَ: وَاللَّهِ لَقَدْ أَقْرَأَنِيهَا رَسُولُ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ مِنْ فِيهِ إِلَى فِيَّ."],"takhrij":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاري في فضائل الصحابة (3742)، ومسلم في صلاة المسافرين قصرها (283:823) كلاهما من طريق المغيرة، عن إبراهيم، عن علقمة قال: فذكره.واللفظ للبخاري ولفظ مسلم مختصر.","grade":"متفق عليه","chapter_ar":"باب فضل ابن مسعود، وعمار، وحذيفة","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب فضائل الصحابة وأخبارهم","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Authentic: Narrated by al-Bukhārī (3742) and Muslim (823, no. 283).","chapter_en":"The Virtues of Ibn Masʿūd, ʿAmmār, and Ḥudhayfah","part_en":"The Book of the Virtues and Accounts of the Companions","group_ar":"مجموع ما جاء في فضل جماعات الصحابة","group_en":"Collected Reports Concerning the Virtues of Groups of the Companions","part_no":49,"group_no":12,"chapter_no":28,"content":{"translation":{"en":["ʿAlqamah narrated: I came to Syria and prayed two rakʿahs. Then I said: “O Allah, make a righteous companion easy for me.” I went to a group of people and sat with them. An elderly man came and sat beside me. I asked: “Who is this?” They replied: “Abū al-Dardāʾ.” I said to him: “I asked Allah to make a righteous companion easy for me, and He has made you available to me.” He asked: “Where are you from?” I replied: “From Kūfah.” He said: “Do you not have among you Ibn Umm ʿAbd, the keeper of the sandals, the cushion, and the water vessel? Is there not among you the man whom Allah protected from Satan through the words of His Prophet ﷺ? And is there not among you the keeper of the Prophet’s ﷺ secret, which no one else knows?” He then asked: “How does ʿAbdullāh recite: ‘By the night when it covers’?” I recited to him: “By the night when it covers, and by the day when it appears, and by the male and the female.” He said: “By Allah, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ taught me this recitation directly from his mouth to mine.”"]},"buhuth":{"en":["Al-Bukhārī (3743) also recorded it through another chain from Ibrāhīm, who said:","ʿAlqamah traveled to Syria. When he entered the mosque, he said:","“O Allah, make a righteous companion easy for me.”","He then sat beside Abū al-Dardāʾ.","Abū al-Dardāʾ asked:","“Where are you from?”","He replied:","“From Kūfah.”","Abū al-Dardāʾ said:","“Is there not among you—or from among you—the keeper of the secret that no one else knows?”","He meant Ḥudhayfah.","ʿAlqamah replied:","“Yes.”","He said:","“Is there not among you—or from among you—the one whom Allah protected through the words of His Prophet ﷺ?”","He meant protection from Satan, referring to ʿAmmār.","ʿAlqamah replied:","“Yes.”","He said:","“Is there not among you—or from among you—the keeper of the tooth-stick or the private belongings?”","He replied:","“Yes.”","Abū al-Dardāʾ asked:","“How did ʿAbdullāh recite:","‘By the night when it covers, and by the day when it appears’?”","I replied:","“And by the male and the female.”","He said:","“These people continued pressuring me until they almost caused me to abandon something I heard directly from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"full":1,"dr":1,"tks":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (3742)، ومسلم (283:823)."},{"num":10053,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ خثيمة بن أَبِي سَبْرَةَ قَالَ: أَتَيْتُ الْمَدِينَةَ فَسَأَلْتُ اللَّهَ أَنْ يُيَسِّرَ لِي جَلِيسًا صَالِحًا ، فَيَسَّرَ لِي أَبَا هُرَيْرَةَ ، فَجَلَسْتُ إِلَيْهِ، فَقُلْتُ لَهُ: إِنِّي سَأَلْتُ اللَّهَ أَنْ يُيَسِّرَ لِي جَلِيسًا صَالِحًا فَوُفِّقْتَ لِي، فَقَالَ: مِنْ أَيْنَ أَنْتَ؟ قُلْتُ: مِنْ أَهْلِ الْكُوفَةِ، جِئْتُ أَلْتَمِسُ الْخَيْرَ وَأَطْلُبُهُ فَقَالَ: أَلَيْسَ فِيكُمْ سَعْدُ بْنُ مَالِكٍ مُجَابُ الدَّعْوَةِ، وَابْنُ مَسْعُودٍ صَاحِبُ طَهُورِ رَسُولِ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ وَنَعْلَيْهِ، وَحُذَيْفَةُ صَاحِبُ سِرِّ رَسُولِ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ، ، وَعَمَّارُ الَّذِي أَجَارَهُ اللَّهُ مِنَ الشَّيْطَانِ عَلَى لِسَانِ نَبِيِّهِ، وَسَلْمَانُ صَاحِبُ الْكِتَابَيْنِ؟ قَالَ قَتَادَةُ: وَالْكِتَابَانِ الإِنْجِيلُ وَالْقُرْآنُ."],"takhrij":"حسن: رواه الترمذي (3811) عن الجراح بن مخلد البصري، حدثنا معاذ بن هشام، حدثني أبي، عن قتادة( هو ابن دعامة)، عن خثيمة بن أبي سبرة قال: فذكره.وإسناده حسن من أجل معاذ بن هشان الدستوائي فإنه حسن الحديث.","grade":"حسن","chapter_ar":"باب ما جاء في أخبار أبي سعيد، وابن مسعود، وحذيفة، وسلمان","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب فضائل الصحابة وأخبارهم","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Hasan: Narrated by al-Tirmidhī (3811). Al-Tirmidhī said:","chapter_en":"Reports Concerning Abū Saʿīd, Ibn Masʿūd, Ḥudhayfah, and Salmān","part_en":"The Book of the Virtues and Accounts of the Companions","group_ar":"مجموع ما جاء في فضل جماعات الصحابة","group_en":"Collected Reports Concerning the Virtues of Groups of the Companions","part_no":49,"group_no":12,"chapter_no":29,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Khaythamah ibn Abī Sabrah narrated: I came to Madinah and asked Allah to make a righteous companion easy for me. He made Abū Hurayrah available to me, so I sat with him. I said: “I asked Allah to make a righteous companion easy for me, and I was guided to you.” He asked: “Where are you from?” I replied: “From Kūfah. I came seeking goodness and pursuing it.” He said: “Do you not have among you Saʿd ibn Mālik, whose supplications are answered; Ibn Masʿūd, the keeper of the Messenger of Allah’s ﷺ purification water and sandals; Ḥudhayfah, the keeper of the Messenger of Allah’s ﷺ secret; ʿAmmār, whom Allah protected from Satan through the words of His Prophet; and Salmān, the possessor of the two scriptures?” Qatādah said: The two scriptures were the Gospel and the Qur’an."]},"buhuth":{"en":["“This is a good, authentic, strange hadith.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"voc":["fazail",251],"full":1,"dr":1,"tks":"حسن: رواه الترمذي (3811). وقال الترمذي: “هذا حديث حسن صحيح غريب”."},{"num":10054,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ أَبِي مُوسَى قَالَ:  بَلَغَنَا مَخْرَجُ رَسُولِ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ وَنَحْنُ بِالْيَمَنِ، فَخَرَجْنَا مُهَاجِرِينَ إِلَيْهِ، أَنَا وَأَخَوَانِ لِي، أَنَا أَصْغَرُهُمَا، أَحَدُهُمَا أَبُو بُرْدَةَ، وَالْآخَرُ أَبُو رُهْمٍ - إِمَّا قَالَ بِضْعًا، وَإِمَّا قَالَ: ثَلَاثَةً وَخَمْسِينَ أَوِ اثْنَيْنِ وَخَمْسِينَ رَجُلًا مِنْ قَوْمِي، قَالَ: فَرَكِبْنَا سَفِينَةً، فَأَلْقَتْنَا سَفِينَتُنَا إِلَى النَّجَاشِيِّ بِالْحَبَشَةِ، فَوَافَقْنَا جَعْفَرَ بْنَ أَبِي طَالِبٍ وَأَصْحَابَهُ عِنْدَهُ. فَقَالَ جَعْفَرٌ: إِنَّ رَسُولَ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ بَعَثَنَا هَا هُنَا وَأَمَرَنَا بِالْإِقَامَةِ، فَأَقِيمُوا مَعَنَا. فَأَقَمْنَا مَعَهُ حَتَّى قَدِمْنَا جَمِيعًا، قَالَ: فَوَافَقْنَا رَسُولَ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ حِينَ افْتَتَحَ خَيْبَرَ، فَأَسْهَمَ لَنَا، - أَوْ قَالَ أَعْطَانَا مِنْهَا، - وَمَا قَسَمَ لِأَحَدٍ غَابَ عَنْ فَتْحِ خَيْبَرَ مِنْهَا شَيْئًا، إِلَّا لِمَنْ شَهِدَ مَعَهُ، إِلَّا لِأَصْحَابِ سَفِينَتِنَا مَعَ جَعْفَرٍ وَأَصْحَابِهِ، قَسَمَ لَهُمْ مَعَهُمْ. قَالَ: فَكَانَ نَاسٌ مِنَ النَّاسِ يَقُولُونَ لَنَا - يَعْنِي لِأَهْلِ السَّفِينَةِ: نَحْنُ سَبَقْنَاكُمْ بِالْهِجْرَةِ!","قَالَ: فَدَخَلْتُ أَسْمَاءُ بِنْتُ عُمَيْسٍ وَهِيَ مِمَّنْ قَدِمَ مَعَنَا، عَلَى حَفْصَةَ زَوْجِ النَّبِيِّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ زَائِرَةً وَقَدْ كَانَتْ هَاجَرَتُ إِلَى النَّجَاشِيِّ فِيمَنْ هَاجَرَ إِلَيْهِ، فَدَخَلَ عُمَرُ عَلَى حَفْصَةَ وَأَسْمَاءَ عِنْدَهَا، فَقَالَ عُمَرُ حِينَ رَأَى أَسْمَاءَ: مَنْ هَذِهِ؟ قَالَتْ: أَسْمَاءُ بِنْتُ عُمَيْسٍ، قَالَ عُمَرُ: الْحَبَشِيَّةُ هَذِهِ؟ الْبَحْرِيَّةُ هَذِهِ؟ فَقَالَتْ أَسْمَاءُ: نَعَمْ، فَقَالَ عُمَرُ: سَبَقْنَاكُمْ بالهجرة.فنحن أَحَقُّ بِرَسُولِ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ منكم.فغضبت وَقَالَتْ كَلِمَةُ: كَذَبْتَ يَا عُمَرُ! كَلا وَاللَّهِ! كُنْتُمْ مَعَ رَسُولِ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ يُطْعِمُ جَائِعَكُمْ، وَكُنَّا فِي دَارٍ، أَوْ فِي أَرْضٍ الْبُعَدَاءُ، الْبَغْضَاءُ فِي الْحَبَشَةِ، وَذَلِكَ فِي اللَّهِ وَفِي رَسُولِهِ وَايْمُ اللَّهِ! والله لا أُطْعِمُ طَعَامًا وَلا أَشْرَبُ شَرَابًا حَتَّى أَذْكُرَ مَا قُلْتُ لِرَسُولِ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ، وَنَحْنُ كُنَّا نُؤْذِى وَنَخَافُ، وَسَأَذْكُرُ ذَلِكَ لِرَسُولِ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ وَأَسْأَلُهُ، وَوَاللَّهِ لاَ أَكْذِبُ وَلا أَزِيغُ وَلاَ أَزِيدُ عَلَى ذَلِكَ، قَالَ: فَلَمَّا جَاءَ النَّبِيُّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ قَالَتْ: يَا نَبِيَّ اللَّهِ! إِنَّ عُمَرَ قَالَ كَذَا وَكَذَا، فَقَالَ رَسُولُ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ: لَيْسَ بِأَحَقَّ بِي مِنْكُمْ وَلَهُ وَلأَصْحَابِهِ هِجْرَةٌ وَاحِدَةٌ، ولكن أَنْتُمْ، أَهْلُ السَّفِينَةِ، هَجْرَتَانِ.","قَالَتْ: فَلَقَدْ رَأَيْتُ أَبَا مُوسَى وَأَصْحَابَ السَّفِينَةِ يَأْتُونِي أَرْسَالًا، يَسْأَلُونِي عَنْ هَذَا الْحَدِيثِ مَا مِنَ الدُّنْيَا شَيْءٌ هُمْ بِهِ أَفْرَحُ وَلَا أَعْظَمُ فِي أَنْفُسِهِمْ مِمَّا قَالَ لَهُمْ رَسُولُ اللهِ صلى الله عليه وسلم.","قَالَ أَبُو بُرْدَةَ: فَقَالَتْ أَسْمَاءُ: فَلَقَدْ رَأَيْتُ أَبَا مُوسَى، وَإِنَّهُ لَيَسْتَعِيدُ هَذَا الْحَدِيثَ مِنِّي."],"takhrij":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاري في المغازي (4230)، ومسلم في فضائل الصحابة (2502) كلاهما عن أبي كريب محمد بن العلاء، ثنا أبو أسامة، ثنا بريد بن عبدالله، عن أبي بردة ، عن أبي موسى قال: فذكره.","grade":"متفق عليه","chapter_ar":"باب ما جاء في فضل أهل السفينة ممن هاجروا إلى الحبشة وأن لهم أجر هجرتين","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب فضائل الصحابة وأخبارهم","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Authentic: Narrated by al-Bukhārī (4230) and Muslim (2502).","chapter_en":"Reports Concerning the Virtue of the People of the Ship Who Migrated to Abyssinia and Their Reward for Two Migrations","part_en":"The Book of the Virtues and Accounts of the Companions","group_ar":"مجموع ما جاء في فضل جماعات الصحابة","group_en":"Collected Reports Concerning the Virtues of Groups of the Companions","part_no":49,"group_no":12,"chapter_no":30,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Abū Mūsā narrated: News of the departure of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ reached us while we were in Yemen, so we set out as emigrants to join him. I was accompanied by two of my brothers, and I was the youngest of the three. One of them was Abū Burdah and the other was Abū Ruhm. There were either a little over fifty men from my people, or fifty-three, or fifty-two—the narrator was uncertain. We boarded a ship, but our ship carried us to al-Najāshī in Abyssinia. There we met Jaʿfar ibn Abī Ṭālib and his companions. Jaʿfar said: “The Messenger of Allah ﷺ sent us here and ordered us to remain, so stay with us.” We remained with him until we all arrived together. We reached the Messenger of Allah ﷺ at the time when he conquered Khaybar. He assigned us a share from its spoils—or the narrator said that he gave us some of it. He did not give any share from Khaybar to anyone who had been absent from its conquest except those who had actually been present with him, with the exception of the people of our ship who had come with Jaʿfar and his companions. He gave them shares along with the others. Some people would say to us—that is, to the people of the ship: “We preceded you in migration.” Asmāʾ bint ʿUmays, who was among those who had arrived with us, visited Ḥafṣah, the wife of the Prophet ﷺ. Asmāʾ had been among those who migrated to al-Najāshī. ʿUmar entered upon Ḥafṣah while Asmāʾ was with her. When he saw Asmāʾ, he asked: “Who is this?” Ḥafṣah replied: “Asmāʾ bint ʿUmays.” ʿUmar said: “Is this the Abyssinian woman? Is this the woman who came by sea?”","She replied: “Yes.” ʿUmar said: “We preceded you in migration, so we have a greater right to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ than you do.” Asmāʾ became angry and said: “You are mistaken, O ʿUmar! No, by Allah! You were with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ while he fed your hungry and instructed your ignorant. We, meanwhile, were in the land—or the territory—of distant and hostile people in Abyssinia, and that was for the sake of Allah and His Messenger. By Allah, I will neither eat food nor drink anything until I mention to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ what you have said. We used to suffer harm and live in fear. I will mention this to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and ask him about it. By Allah, I will neither lie, deviate from the truth, nor add anything to what you said.” When the Prophet ﷺ arrived, she said: “O Prophet of Allah, ʿUmar said such-and-such.” The Messenger of Allah ﷺ replied: “He and his companions have no greater right to me than you. He and his companions have one migration, while you, the people of the ship, have two migrations.” Asmāʾ said: I saw Abū Mūsā and the other people of the ship coming to me in successive groups and asking me about this hadith. Nothing in the world brought them greater happiness or held greater importance in their hearts than what the Messenger of Allah ﷺ had said to them.","Abū Burdah said: Asmāʾ said: “I saw Abū Mūsā repeatedly asking me to narrate this hadith to him again.”"]},"buhuth":{"en":["Abū Yaʿlā (3717), after citing the wording of al-Bukhārī and Muslim, added:","“He narrated it to us on another occasion and said:","‘You have the reward of two migrations: you migrated to al-Najāshī, and you migrated to me.’”","In another wording:","“You have the reward of two migrations: your migration to Madinah and your migration to Abyssinia.”","Recorded by Aḥmad (19524)."]}},"tuhfa":{},"voc":["fazail",252],"full":1,"dr":1,"tks":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (4230)، ومسلم (2502)."},{"num":10055,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عن أَبِي عبد الرَّحْمَنِ الحبلي قَالَ: سَمِعْتُ عَبْدَ اللَّهِ بْنَ عَمْرِو بْنِ الْعَاصِ، وَسَأَلَهُ رَجُلٌ، فَقَالَ: أَلَسْنَا مِنْ فُقَرَاءِ الْمُهَاجِرِينَ؟ فَقَالَ لَهُ عَبْدُ اللَّهِ: أَلَكَ امْرَأَةٌ تَأْوِي إِلَيْهَا؟ قَالَ: نَعَمْ. قَالَ: أَلَكَ مَسْكَنٌ تَسْكُنُهُ؟ قَالَ: نَعَمْ. قَالَ: فَأَنْتَ مِنَ الْأَغْنِيَاءِ. قَالَ: فَإِنَّ لِي خَادِمًا. قَالَ: فَأَنْتَ مِنَ الْمُلُوكِ.","قَالَ أَبُو عَبْدِ الرَّحْمَنِ: وَجَاءَ ثَلَاثَةُ نَفَرٍ إِلَى عَبْدِ اللهِ بْنِ عَمْرِو بْنِ الْعَاصِ، وَأَنَا عِنْدَهُ، فَقَالُوا: يَا أَبَا مُحَمَّدٍ، إِنَّا وَاللهِ! مَا نَقْدِرُ عَلَى شَيْءٍ: لَا نَفَقَةٍ، وَلَا دَابَّةٍ، وَلَا مَتَاعٍ، فَقَالَ لَهُمْ: مَا شِئْتُمْ، إِنْ شِئْتُمْ رَجَعْتُمْ إِلَيْنَا، فَأَعْطَيْنَاكُمْ مَا يَسَّرَ اللهُ لَكُمْ، وَإِنْ شِئْتُمْ ذَكَرْنَا أَمْرَكُمْ لِلسُّلْطَانِ، وَإِنْ شِئْتُمْ صَبَرْتُمْ، فَإِنِّي سَمِعْتُ رَسُولَ اللهِ صلى الله عليه وسلم يَقُولُ: إِنَّ فُقَرَاءَ الْمُهَاجِرِينَ يَسْبِقُونَ الْأَغْنِيَاءَ يَوْمَ الْقِيَامَةِ إِلَى الْجَنَّةِ بِأَرْبَعِينَ خريفا.قالوا: فَإِنَّا نَصْبِرُ، لَا نَسْأَلُ شَيْئًا .."],"takhrij":"صحيح: رواه مسلم في الزهد والرقائق (73:2797) عن أبي الطاهر أحمد بن عمرو بن سرح، أخبرنا ابن وهب، أخبرني أبو هانيء سمع أبا عبد الرحمن الجبلي يقول: فذكره","grade":"صحيح","chapter_ar":"باب ما جاء في فضل فقراء المهاجرين","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب فضائل الصحابة وأخبارهم","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Authentic: Narrated by Muslim (2979, no. 73).","chapter_en":"Reports Concerning the Virtue of the Poor Emigrants","part_en":"The Book of the Virtues and Accounts of the Companions","group_ar":"مجموع ما جاء في فضل جماعات الصحابة","group_en":"Collected Reports Concerning the Virtues of Groups of the Companions","part_no":49,"group_no":12,"chapter_no":31,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Abū ʿAbd al-Raḥmān al-Ḥubulī narrated: I heard ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿAmr ibn al-ʿĀṣ when a man asked him: “Are we not among the poor Emigrants?” ʿAbdullāh asked him: “Do you have a wife with whom you find shelter?” He replied: “Yes.” He asked: “Do you have a house in which you live?” He replied: “Yes.” ʿAbdullāh said: “Then you are among the wealthy.” The man said: “I also have a servant.” He replied: “Then you are among kings.” Abū ʿAbd al-Raḥmān continued: Three men came to ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿAmr ibn al-ʿĀṣ while I was with him and said: “O Abū Muḥammad, by Allah, we possess nothing—no provisions, no riding animal, and no belongings.”","He said to them: “You may choose as you wish. If you wish, return to us and we will give you whatever Allah makes easy for us to provide. If you wish, we will present your situation to the ruler. And if you wish, remain patient, for I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: ‘The poor Emigrants will enter Paradise forty years before the wealthy on the Day of Resurrection.’” They replied: “We will remain patient and ask no one for anything.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"voc":["fazail",253],"full":1,"tks":"صحيح: رواه مسلم (2979/73)."},{"num":10056,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ ثَوْبَانَ مَوْلَى رَسُولِ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ قَالَ: كُنْتُ قَائِمًا عِنْدَ رَسُولِ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ فَجَاءَ حَبْر مِنْ أَحْبَارِ الْيَهُودِ فَقَالَ: السَّلَامُ عَلَيْكَ يَا مُحَمَّدُ!، فَدَفَعْتُهُ دَفْعَةً كَادَ يُصْرَعُ مِنْهَا، فَقَالَ: لِمَ تَدْفَعُنِي؟ فَقُلْتُ: أَلَا تَقُولُ يَا رَسُولَ اللَّهِ؟ فَقَالَ الْيَهُودِيُّ: إِنَّمَا نَدْعُوهُ بِاسْمِهِ الَّذِي سَمَّاهُ بِهِ أَهْلُهُ، فَقَالَ رَسُولُ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ: إِنَّ اسْمِي مُحَمَّدٌ الَّذِي سَمَّانِي بِهِ أَهْلِي).فَقَالَ الْيَهُودِيُّ: جِئْتُ أَسْأَلُكَ، فَقَالَ لَهُ رَسُولُ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ: أَيَنْفَعُكَ شَيْءٌ إِنْ حَدَّثْتُكَ؟.قَالَ: أَسْمَعُ بِأُذُنَيَّ، فَنَكَتَ رَسُولُ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ بِعُودٍ مَعَهُ فَقَالَ: سَلْ.فَقَالَ الْيَهُودِيُّ: أَيْنَ يَكُونُ النَّاسُ يَوْمَ تُبَدّل الْأَرْضُ غَيْرَ الْأَرْضِ والسموات؟ فَقَالَ رَسُولُ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ: هُمْ فِي الظُّلْمَةِ دُونَ الْجِسْرِ.قَالَ: فَمَنْ أوَّل النَّاسِ إِجَازَةً؟ قَالَ: فُقَرَاءُ الْمُهَاجِرِينَ.قَالَ الْيَهُودِيُّ: فَمَا تُحْفَتُهُمْ حِينَ يَدْخُلُونَ الْجَنَّةَ؟ قَالَ: زِيَادَةُ كَبِدِ النُّونِ.قَالَ: فَمَا غِذَاؤُهُمْ عَلَى إِثْرِهَا؟ قَالَ: يُنْحر لَهُمْ ثَوْرُ الْجَنَّةِ الَّذِي كَانَ يَأْكُلُ مِنْ أَطْرَافِهَا.قَالَ: فَمَا شَرَابُهُمْ عَلَيْهِ؟ قَالَ: مِنْ عَيْنٍ فِيهَا تُسَمَّى سَلْسَبِيلًا.فَقَالَ: صَدَقْتَ، قَالَ: وَجِئْتُ أَسْأَلُكَ عَنْ شىء لَا يَعْلَمُهُ أَحَدٌ مِنْ أَهْلِ الْأَرْضِ إِلَّا نبيّ، أَوْ رَجُلٌ أَوْ رَجُلَانِ، قَالَ: يَنْفَعُكَ إِنْ حَدَّثْتُكَ؟.قَالَ: أَسْمَعُ بِأُذُنَيَّ، قَالَ: جِئْتُ أَسْأَلُكَ عَنِ الْوَلَدِ؟ قَالَ: مَاءُ الرَّجُلِ أَبْيَضُ وَمَاءُ الْمَرْأَةِ أَصْفَرُ، فَإِذَا اجْتَمَعَا، فَعَلَا منيّ الرَّجُلِ منيّ الْمَرْأَةِ أَذْكَرَا بِإِذْنِ اللَّهِ، وَإِذَا عَلَا منيّ الْمَرْأَةِ منيّ الرَّجُلِ آنَثَا بِإِذْنِ اللَّهِ.قَالَ الْيَهُودِيُّ: لَقَدْ صَدَقْتَ، وَإِنَّكَ لَنَبِيٌّ، ثُمَّ انْصَرَفَ فَذَهَبَ، فَقَالَ رَسُولُ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ: لَقَدْ سَأَلَنِي هَذَا عَنِ الَّذِي سَأَلَنِي عَنْهُ، وَمَا لِي عِلْمٌ بِشَيْءٍ مِنْهُ، حَتَّى أَتَانِيَ اللهُ بِهِ."],"takhrij":"صحيح: رواه مسلم في الحيض (34:315) عن الحسن بن علي الحلواني، حدثنا أبو توبة (هو الربيع بن نافع)، حدثنا معاوية (يعني ابن سلام)، عن زيد (يعني أخاه)، أنه سمع أبا سلام قال: حدثني أبو أسماء الرحيبي، عن ثوبان فذكره.","grade":"صحيح","chapter_ar":"باب ما جاء في فضل فقراء المهاجرين","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب فضائل الصحابة وأخبارهم","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Authentic: Narrated by Muslim (315, no. 34).","chapter_en":"Reports Concerning the Virtue of the Poor Emigrants","part_en":"The Book of the Virtues and Accounts of the Companions","group_ar":"مجموع ما جاء في فضل جماعات الصحابة","group_en":"Collected Reports Concerning the Virtues of Groups of the Companions","part_no":49,"group_no":12,"chapter_no":31,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Thawbān, the freedman of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, narrated: I was standing beside the Messenger of Allah ﷺ when a Jewish rabbi came and said: “Peace be upon you, O Muḥammad.” I pushed him with such force that he nearly fell. He asked: “Why did you push me?” I replied: “Why did you not say, ‘O Messenger of Allah’?” The Jew answered: “We call him only by the name given to him by his family.” The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “My name is indeed Muḥammad, the name given to me by my family.” The Jew said: “I have come to ask you some questions.” The Messenger of Allah ﷺ asked: “Will it benefit you if I answer you?” He replied: “I shall listen with my own ears.” The Messenger of Allah ﷺ scratched the ground with a stick he was holding and said: “Ask.” The Jew asked: “Where will the people be when the earth is changed into another earth and the heavens as well?” The Messenger of Allah ﷺ replied: “They will be in darkness before the Bridge.” He asked: “Who will be the first people permitted to cross?” He replied: “The poor Emigrants.” He asked: “What will be their first hospitality when they enter Paradise?” He replied: “The extra lobe of the fish’s liver.” He asked: “What will they eat after that?” He replied: “The bull of Paradise, which used to graze along its edges, will be slaughtered for them.” He asked: “What will they drink with it?” He replied: “From a spring in Paradise called Salsabīl.” The Jew said: “You have spoken the truth.” He then said: “I have also come to ask you about something that no one on earth knows except a prophet, or perhaps one or two men.” The Prophet ﷺ asked: “Will it benefit you if I tell you?” He replied: “I shall listen with my own ears.” He said: “I have come to ask you about the child.” The Prophet ﷺ replied: “The fluid of the man is white, and the fluid of the woman is yellow. When they come together, if the man’s fluid prevails over the woman’s fluid, the child will be male by Allah’s permission. If the woman’s fluid prevails over the man’s fluid, the child will be female by Allah’s permission.” The Jew said: “You have spoken the truth. Indeed, you are a prophet.” He then departed. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “He asked me about matters of which I had no knowledge until Allah revealed them to me.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"voc":["fazail",254],"full":1,"tks":"صحيح: رواه مسلم (34:315)."},{"num":10057,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ عَبْدِ اللَّهِ بْنِ عَمْرِو بْنِ الْعَاصِي، عَنْ رَسُولِ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ أَنَّهُ قَالَ: هَلْ تَدْرُونَ أَوَّلَ مَنْ يَدْخُلُ الْجَنَّةَ مِنْ خَلْقِ اللهِ؟ قَالُوا: اللَّهُ وَرَسُولُهُ أَعْلَمُ، قَالَ: أَوَّلُ مَنْ يَدْخُلُ الْجَنَّةَ مِنْ خَلْقِ اللهِ الْفُقَرَاءُ الْمُهَاجِرُونَ، الَّذِينَ تُسَدُّ بِهِمُ الثُّغُورُ، وَيُتَّقَى بِهِمُ الْمَكَارِهُ، وَيَمُوتُ أَحَدُهُمْ وَحَاجَتُهُ فِي صَدْرِهِ، لَا يَسْتَطِيعُ لَهَا قَضَاءً، فَيَقُولُ اللَّهُ عَزَّ وَجَلَّ لِمَنْ يَشَاءُ مِنْ مَلَائِكَتِهِ: ائْتُوهُمْ فَحَيُّوهُمْ، فَتَقُولُ الْمَلَائِكَةُ: نَحْنُ سُكَّانُ سَمَائِكَ، وَخِيرَتُكَ مِنْ خَلْقِكَ، أَفَتَأْمُرُنَا أَنْ نَأْتِيَ هَؤُلَاءِ فَنُسَلِّمَ عَلَيْهِمْ؟ قَالَ: إِنَّهُمْ كَانُوا عِبَادًا يَعْبُدُونِي، لَا يُشْرِكُونَ بِي شَيْئًا، وَتُسَدُّ بِهِمُ الثُّغُورُ، وَيُتَّقَى بِهِمُ الْمَكَارِهُ، وَيَمُوتُ أَحَدُهُمْ، وَحَاجَتُهُ فِي صَدْرِهِ، لَا يَسْتَطِيعُ لَهَا قَضَاءً، قَالَ: فَتَأْتِيهِمُ الْمَلَائِكَةُ عِنْدَ ذَلِكَ، فَيَدْخُلُونَ عَلَيْهِمْ مِنْ كُلِّ بَابٍ: ﴿سَلَامٌ عَلَيْكُمْ بِمَا صَبَرْتُمْ فَنِعْمَ عُقْبَى الدَّارِ﴾ [الرعد:"],"takhrij":"صحيح: رواه أحمد (6570،6571)، والبزار (2457)، وصحّحه ابن حبان (7421)، والحاكم (2/71-72) كلهم من طرق عن أبي عُشَّانة المعافري حي بن يؤمن، عن عبدالله بن عمرو قال: فذكره.","grade":"صحيح","chapter_ar":"باب ما جاء في فضل فقراء المهاجرين","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب فضائل الصحابة وأخبارهم","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Authentic: Narrated by Aḥmad (6570, 6571), al-Bazzār (2457), authenticated by Ibn Ḥibbān (7421), and al-Ḥākim (2/71).","chapter_en":"Reports Concerning the Virtue of the Poor Emigrants","part_en":"The Book of the Virtues and Accounts of the Companions","group_ar":"مجموع ما جاء في فضل جماعات الصحابة","group_en":"Collected Reports Concerning the Virtues of Groups of the Companions","part_no":49,"group_no":12,"chapter_no":31,"content":{"translation":{"en":["ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿAmr ibn al-ʿĀṣ narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Do you know who will be the first of Allah’s creation to enter Paradise?” They replied: “Allah and His Messenger know best.” He said: “The first of Allah’s creation to enter Paradise will be the poor Emigrants, through whom the frontiers are guarded and by whom hardships are warded off. One of them dies while still carrying an unfulfilled need in his heart that he was unable to satisfy. Then Allah, the Mighty and Majestic, will say to whichever of His angels He wills: ‘Go to them and greet them.’ The angels will say: ‘We are the inhabitants of Your heavens and the chosen among Your creation. Do You command us to go and greet these people?’ Allah will say: ‘They were servants who worshipped Me and associated nothing with Me. Through them the frontiers were guarded, by them hardships were repelled, and one of them died while carrying an unfulfilled need in his heart which he was unable to fulfill.’ Then the angels will come to them and enter upon them through every gate, saying: ‘Peace be upon you for what you patiently endured. How excellent is the final home!’” (Qur’an 13:24)"]}},"tuhfa":{},"voc":["fazail",255],"full":1,"dr":1,"rep":[16370],"tks":"صحيح: رواه أحمد (6570، 6571)، والبزار (2457)، وصححه ابن حبان (7421)، والحاكم (2/71)."},{"num":10058,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عن وَاثِلَةَ بْنِ الأسقع كنت قَالَ: كُنْتُ فِي أَصْحَابِ الصُّفَّةِ، فَلَقَدْ رَأَيْتُنَا، وَمَا مِنَّا إِنْسَانٌ عَلَيْهِ ثَوْبٌ تَامٌّ، وَأَخَذَ الْعَرَقُ فِي جُلُودِنَا طُرُقًا مِنَ الْغُبَارِ وَالْوَسَخِ، إِذْ خَرَجَ عَلَيْنَا رَسُولُ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ فَقَالَ: لِتُبَشَّرْ فُقَرَاءُ الْمُهَاجِرِينَ. إِذْ أَقْبَلَ رَجُلٌ عَلَيْهِ شَارَةٌ حَسَنَةٌ، فَجَعَلَ النَّبِيُّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ لَا يَتَكَلَّمُ بِكَلَامٍ إِلَّا كَلَّفَتْهُ نَفْسُهُ أَنْ يَأْتِيَ بِكَلَامٍ يَعْلُو كَلَامَ النَّبِيِّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ، فَلَمَّا انْصَرَفَ قَالَ: إِنَّ اللَّهَ لَا يُحِبُّ هَذَا وَضَرَبَهُ، يَلْوُونَ أَلْسِنَتَهُمْ كَلَيِّ الْبَقَرِ بِلِسَانِهَا الْمَرْعَى، كَذَلِكَ يَلْوِي اللَّهُ تَعَالَى أَلْسِنَتَهُمْ وَوُجُوهَهُمْ فِي النَّارِ."],"takhrij":"صحيح: رواه الطبراني في الكبير (22/ح 170) عن أبي زرعة عبدالرحمن بن عمرو الدمشقي، ثنا أبو مسهر (هو عبدالأعلى بن مسهر)، ثنا صدقة بن خالد، قال: حدثني زيد بن واقد، عن بسر بن عبيد الله، عن واثلة بن الأسقع قال: فذكره.وإسناده صحيح.","grade":"صحيح","chapter_ar":"باب ما جاء في فضل فقراء المهاجرين","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب فضائل الصحابة وأخبارهم","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Authentic: Narrated by al-Ṭabarānī in al-Muʿjam al-Kabīr (22/170).","chapter_en":"Reports Concerning the Virtue of the Poor Emigrants","part_en":"The Book of the Virtues and Accounts of the Companions","group_ar":"مجموع ما جاء في فضل جماعات الصحابة","group_en":"Collected Reports Concerning the Virtues of Groups of the Companions","part_no":49,"group_no":12,"chapter_no":31,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Wāthilah ibn al-Asqaʿ narrated: I was among the People of the Ṣuffah. I remember that not one of us possessed a complete garment. Sweat had mixed with the dust and dirt upon our skin. Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ came out to us and said: “Glad tidings to the poor Emigrants.” A man wearing fine clothing then approached. Whenever the Prophet ﷺ spoke, the man would deliberately try to speak in a manner that rose above the Prophet’s words. When he departed, the Prophet ﷺ said: “Indeed, Allah does not love this type of person. They twist their tongues before people just as a cow twists its tongue around pasture. Likewise, Allah will twist their tongues and their faces in the Fire.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"voc":["fazail",256],"full":1,"dr":1,"tks":"صحيح: رواه الطبراني في الكبير (22/ح 170)."},{"num":10059,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عن جابر بْنِ عَبْدِ اللَّهِ أَنَّ رَسُولَ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ لَبِثَ عَشْرَ سِنِينَ يَتَّبِعُ الْحَاجَّ فِي مَنَازِلِهِمْ، فِي الْمَوْسِمِ وَبِمَجَنَّةٍ وَبِعُكَاظٍ، وَبِمَنَازِلِهِمْ بِمِنًى يَقُولُ: مَنْ يُؤْوِينِي، مَنْ يَنْصُرُنِي، حَتَّى أُبَلِّغَ رِسَالَاتِ رَبِّي، وَلَهُ الْجَنَّةُ؟، فَلَا يَجِدُ أَحَدًا يَنْصُرُهُ وَيُؤْوِيهِ، حَتَّى إِنَّ الرَّجُلَ يَرْحَلُ مِنْ مُضَرَ، أَوْ مِنَ الْيَمَنِ، إِلَى ذِي رَحِمِهِ، فَيَأْتِيهِ قَوْمُهُ، فَيَقُولُونَ: احْذَرْ غُلَامَ قُرَيْشٍ لَا يَفْتِنُكَ، وَيَمْشِي بَيْنَ رِحَالِهِمْ يَدْعُوهُمْ إِلَى اللَّهِ عَزَّ وَجَلَّ يُشِيرُونَ إِلَيْهِ بِالْأَصَابِعِ، حَتَّى بَعَثَنَا اللهُ عَزَّ وَجَلَّ لَهُ مِنْ يَثْرِبَ، فَيَأْتِيهِ الرَّجُلُ فَيُؤْمِنُ بِهِ، فَيُقْرِئُهُ الْقُرْآنَ، فَيَنْقَلِبُ إِلَى أَهْلِهِ، فَيُسْلِمُونَ بِإِسْلَامِهِ، حَتَّى لَمْ يَبْقَ دَارٌ مِنْ دُورِ يَثْرِبَ إِلَّا فِيهَا رَهْطٌ مِنَ الْمُسْلِمِينَ يُظْهِرُونَ الْإِسْلَامَ، ثُمَّ بَعَثَنَا اللهُ عَزَّ وَجَلَّ، فَأْتَمَرْنَا، وَاجْتَمَعْنَا سَبْعُونَ رَجُلًا مِنَّا، فَقُلْنَا: حَتَّى مَتَى نَذَرُ رَسُولَ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ يُطْرَدُ فِي جِبَالِ مَكَّةَ، وَيَخَافُ، فَرَحَلْنَا حَتَّى قَدِمْنَا عَلَيْهِ فِي الْمَوْسِمِ، فَوَاعَدْنَاهُ شِعْبَ الْعَقَبَةِ، فَقَالَ عَمُّهُ الْعَبَّاسُ: يَا ابْنَ أَخِي، إِنِّي لَا أَدْرِي مَا هَؤُلَاءِ الْقَوْمُ الَّذِينَ جَاءُوكَ؟ إِنِّي ذُو مَعْرِفَةٍ بِأَهْلِ يَثْرِبَ، فَاجْتَمَعْنَا عِنْدَهُ مِنْ رَجُلٍ وَرَجُلَيْنِ، فَلَمَّا نَظَرَ الْعَبَّاسُ فِي وُجُوهِنَا، قَالَ: هَؤُلَاءِ قَوْمٌ لَا أَعْرِفُهُمْ، هَؤُلَاءِ أَحْدَاثٌ، فَقُلْنَا: يَا رَسُولَ اللَّهِ، عَلَامَ نُبَايِعُكَ؟ قَالَ: تُبَايِعُونِي عَلَى السَّمْعِ وَالطَّاعَةِ فِي النَّشَاطِ وَالْكَسَلِ، وَعَلَى النَّفَقَةِ فِي الْعُسْرِ وَالْيُسْرِ، وَعَلَى الْأَمْرِ بِالْمَعْرُوفِ، وَالنَّهْيِ عَنِ الْمُنْكَرِ، وَعَلَى أَنْ تَقُولُوا فِي اللَّهِ لَا تَأْخُذُكُمْ فِيهِ لَوْمَةُ لَائِمٍ، وَعَلَى أَنْ تَنْصُرُونِي إِذَا قَدِمْتُ يَثْرِبَ، فَتَمْنَعُونِي مِمَّا تَمْنَعُونَ مِنْهُ أَنْفُسَكُمْ وَأَزْوَاجَكُمْ وَأَبْنَاءَكُمْ وَلَكُمُ الْجَنَّةُ، فَقُمْنَا نُبَايِعُهُ، فَأَخَذَ بِيَدِهِ أَسْعَدُ بْنُ زُرَارَةَ وَهُوَ أَصْغَرُ السَّبْعِينَ، فَقَالَ: رُوَيْدًا يَا أَهْلَ يَثْرِبَ، إِنَّا لَمْ نَضْرِبْ إِلَيْهِ أَكْبَادَ الْمَطِيِّ إِلَّا وَنَحْنُ نَعْلَمُ أَنَّهُ رَسُولُ اللَّهِ، إِنَّ إِخْرَاجَهُ الْيَوْمَ مُفَارَقَةُ الْعَرَبِ كَافَّةً، وَقَتْلُ خِيَارِكُمْ، وَأَنْ تَعَضَّكُمُ السُّيُوفُ، فَإِمَّا أَنْتُمْ قَوْمٌ تَصْبِرُونَ عَلَى السُّيُوفِ إِذَا مَسَّتْكُمْ، وَعَلَى قَتْلِ خِيَارِكُمْ، وَعَلَى مُفَارَقَةِ الْعَرَبِ كَافَّةً، فَخُذُوهُ وَأَجْرُكُمْ عَلَى اللَّهِ، وَإِمَّا أَنْتُمْ قَوْمٌ تَخَافُونَ مِنْ أَنْفُسِكُمْ خِيفَةً فَذَرُوهُ، فَهُوَ أَعْذَرُ عِنْدَ اللَّهِ، قَالَوا: يَا أَسْعَدُ بْنَ زُرَارَةَ أَمِطْ عَنَّا يَدَكَ، فَوَاللهِ لَا نَذَرُ هَذِهِ الْبَيْعَةَ، وَلَا نَسْتَقِيلُهَا، فَقُمْنَا إِلَيْهِ رَجُلًا رَجُلًا يَأْخُذُ عَلَيْنَا بِشُرْطَةِ الْعَبَّاسِ،، وَيُعْطِينَا عَلَى ذَلِكَ الْجَنَّةَ."],"takhrij":"حسن: رواه أحمد (14653)، وصحّحه ابن حبان (7012)، والحاكم (4251) كلهم من حديث يحيى بن سليم، عن عبدالله بن عثمان بن خثيم، عن أبي الزبير أنه حدثه جابر بن عبدالله فذكره.","grade":"حسن","chapter_ar":"باب ما جاء في فضل أهل بيعة العقبة الثانية","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب فضائل الصحابة وأخبارهم","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Hasan: Narrated by Aḥmad (14653), authenticated by Ibn Ḥibbān (7012), and al-Ḥākim (4251).","chapter_en":"Reports Concerning the Virtue of Those Who Took Part in the Second Pledge of al-ʿAqabah","part_en":"The Book of the Virtues and Accounts of the Companions","group_ar":"مجموع ما جاء في فضل جماعات الصحابة","group_en":"Collected Reports Concerning the Virtues of Groups of the Companions","part_no":49,"group_no":12,"chapter_no":32,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Jābir ibn ʿAbdullāh (may Allah be pleased with them both) narrated: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ spent ten years visiting the camps of the pilgrims during the pilgrimage season, at Majannah, at ʿUkāẓ, and at their encampments in Minā, saying: “Who will give me shelter? Who will support me so that I may convey the messages of my Lord? Paradise shall be his.” Yet he found no one who would support or shelter him. A man would travel from Muḍar or from Yemen to visit his relatives, and his people would warn him: “Beware of the young man of Quraysh lest he lead you astray.” Meanwhile, the Prophet ﷺ walked among their camps calling them to Allah, while they pointed at him with their fingers. Then Allah sent supporters for him from Yathrib. A man would come to him, embrace Islam, learn the Qur’an from him, and return to his family, who would accept Islam through him, until there remained no household in Yathrib except that it contained Muslims openly practicing their faith. Then Allah sent us forth, and we conferred together. Seventy of us gathered and said: “How long shall we leave the Messenger of Allah ﷺ being driven through the mountains of Makkah and living in fear?” We traveled until we met him during the pilgrimage season at the valley of al-ʿAqabah. His uncle al-ʿAbbās said: “O son of my brother, I do not know these people who have come to you. I know the people of Yathrib well.” We approached him one or two at a time. When al-ʿAbbās looked at our faces, he said: “These are people I do not recognize. They are young men.” We asked: “O Messenger of Allah, upon what shall we pledge allegiance to you?” He replied: “You pledge to hear and obey whether energetic or weary; to spend in ease and hardship; to enjoin what is right and forbid what is wrong; to speak the truth for Allah without fearing the blame of any critic; and to support me when I come to Yathrib, protecting me as you protect yourselves, your wives, and your children. In return, Paradise will be yours.” We stood to pledge our allegiance. Asʿad ibn Zurārah, the youngest of the seventy, took hold of the Prophet’s hand and said: “Take your time, O people of Yathrib. We have not exhausted our riding camels in coming here except because we know that he is truly the Messenger of Allah. Taking him away today means declaring yourselves against all the Arabs, the killing of your finest men, and that swords will strike you. If you are prepared to endure that patiently, then take him, and your reward is with Allah. But if you fear that you will fail, then leave him now, for that will be a better excuse before Allah.” They replied: “O Asʿad ibn Zurārah, remove your hand. By Allah, we will never abandon this pledge nor seek release from it.” Then we pledged allegiance to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ one by one. He accepted our pledge upon the conditions mentioned by al-ʿAbbās and promised us Paradise in return."]}},"tuhfa":{},"voc":["fazail",257],"full":1,"dr":1,"rep":[8645],"tks":"حسن: رواه أحمد (14653)، وصححه ابن حبان (7012)، والحاكم (4251)."},{"num":10060,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ عَلِيٍّ، أَنَّ رَسُولَ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ لَمَّا زَوَّجَهُ فَاطِمَةَ بَعَثَ مَعَهُ بِخَمِيلَةٍ، وَوِسَادَةٍ، مِنْ أَدَمٍ حَشْوُهَا لِيفٌ، وَرَحَيَيْنِ وَسِقَاءٍ وَجَرَّتَيْنِ، فَقَالَ عَلِيٌّ لِفَاطِمَةَ ذَاتَ يَوْمٍ: وَاللهِ لَقَدْ سَنَوْتُ حَتَّى لَقَدِ اشْتَكَيْتُ صَدْرِي، قَالَ: وَقَدْ جَاءَ اللَّهُ أَبَاكِ بِسَبْيٍ، فَاذْهَبِي فَاسْتَخْدِمِيهِ، فَقَالَتْ: وَأَنَا وَاللهِ قَدْ طَحَنْتُ حَتَّى مَجَلَتْ يَدَايَ، فَأَتَتِ النَّبِيَّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ، فَقَالَ: مَا جَاءَ بِكِ أَيْ بُنَيَّةُ؟ قَالَتْ: جِئْتُ لِأُسَلِّمَ عَلَيْكَ، وَاسْتَحْيَتْ أَنْ تَسْأَلَهُ وَرَجَعَتْ، فَقَالَ: مَا فَعَلْتِ؟ قَالَتْ: اسْتَحْيَيْتُ أَنْ أَسْأَلَهُ، فَأَتَيْنَاهُ جَمِيعًا، فَقَالَ عَلِيٌّ: يَا رَسُولَ اللَّهِ، وَاللهِ لَقَدْ سَنَوْتُ حَتَّى اشْتَكَيْتُ صَدْرِي، وَقَالَتْ فَاطِمَةُ: قَدْ طَحَنْتُ حَتَّى مَجَلَتْ يَدَايَ، وَقَدْ جَاءَكَ اللهُ بِسَبْيٍ وَسَعَةٍ فَأَخْدِمْنَا، فَقَالَ رَسُولُ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ: وَاللهِ لَا أُعْطِيكُمَا وَأَدَعُ أَهْلَ الصُّفَّةِ تَطْوَى بُطُونُهُمْ، لَا أَجِدُ مَا أُنْفِقُ عَلَيْهِمْ، وَلَكِنِّي أَبِيعُهُمْ وَأُنْفِقُ عَلَيْهِمْ أَثْمَانَهُمْ فَرَجَعَا، فَأَتَاهُمَا النَّبِيُّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ وَقَدْ دَخَلَا فِي قَطِيفَتِهِمَا، إِذَا غَطَّتْ رُءُوسَهُمَا تَكَشَّفَتْ أَقْدَامُهُمَا، وَإِذَا غَطَّيَا أَقْدَامَهُمَا تَكَشَّفَتْ رُءُوسُهُمَا، فَثَارَا، فَقَالَ: مَكَانَكُمَا ثُمَّ قَالَ: أَلَا أُخْبِرُكُمَا بِخَيْرٍ مِمَّا سَأَلْتُمَانِي؟ قَالَا: بَلَى. فَقَالَ: كَلِمَاتٌ عَلَّمَنِيهِنَّ جِبْرِيلُ، فَقَالَ: تُسَبِّحَانِ فِي دُبُرِ كُلِّ صَلَاةٍ عَشْرًا، وَتَحْمَدَانِ عَشْرًا، وَتُكَبِّرَانِ عَشْرًا، وَإِذَا أَوَيْتُمَا إِلَى فِرَاشِكُمَا فَسَبِّحَا ثَلَاثًا وَثَلَاثِينَ، وَاحْمَدَا ثَلَاثًا وَثَلَاثِينَ، وَكَبِّرَا أَرْبَعًا وَثَلَاثِينَ قَالَ: فَوَ اللهِ مَا تَرَكْتُهُنَّ مُنْذُ عَلَّمَنِيهِنَّ رَسُولُ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ، قَالَ: فَقَالَ لَهُ ابْنُ الْكَوَّاءِ: وَلَا لَيْلَةَ صِفِّينَ؟ فَقَالَ: قَاتَلَكُمِ اللهُ يَا أَهْلَ الْعِرَاقِ، نَعَمْ، وَلَا لَيْلَةَ صِفِّينَ."],"takhrij":"صحيح: رواه أحمد (838،596)، وابن سعد (6897)، والبزار (757)، كلهم من طرق عن حماد بن سلمة، عن عطاء بن السائب، عن أبيه، عن علي قال: فذكره.","grade":"صحيح","chapter_ar":"باب ما جاء في فضل أهل الصفة","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب فضائل الصحابة وأخبارهم","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Authentic: Narrated by Aḥmad (596, 838), Ibn Saʿd (8/25), and al-Bazzār (757).","chapter_en":"Reports Concerning the Virtue of the People of the Ṣuffah","part_en":"The Book of the Virtues and Accounts of the Companions","group_ar":"مجموع ما جاء في فضل جماعات الصحابة","group_en":"Collected Reports Concerning the Virtues of Groups of the Companions","part_no":49,"group_no":12,"chapter_no":33,"content":{"translation":{"en":["ʿAlī ibn Abī Ṭālib narrated: When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ married Fāṭimah to me, he sent with her a velvet covering, a leather pillow stuffed with palm fiber, two hand mills, a waterskin, and two earthenware jars. One day I said to Fāṭimah: “By Allah, I have drawn water until my chest has become sore. Allah has brought your father captives, so go and ask him for a servant.” She replied: “By Allah, I have ground grain until my hands have become blistered.” She went to the Prophet ﷺ, who asked: “What has brought you here, my dear daughter?” She replied: “I came to greet you.” She felt too shy to ask him and returned. I asked her: “What happened?” She replied: “I was too shy to ask him.” So we both went to him together. I said: “O Messenger of Allah, by Allah, I have drawn water until my chest has become sore.” Fāṭimah said: “I have ground grain until my hands have become blistered. Allah has granted you captives and abundance, so provide us with a servant.” The Messenger of Allah ﷺ replied: “By Allah, I will not give you a servant while leaving the People of the Ṣuffah with their stomachs empty. I have nothing else to spend on them. Rather, I will sell these captives and spend their price on them.” They returned home. Later, the Prophet ﷺ came to them after they had wrapped themselves in a blanket. Whenever they covered their heads, their feet became uncovered, and whenever they covered their feet, their heads became exposed. They rose, but he said: “Stay where you are.” Then he said: “Shall I not tell you something better than what you asked for?” They replied: “Yes.” He said: “These are words Jibrīl taught me: after every prayer, glorify Allah ten times, praise Him ten times, and proclaim His greatness ten times. When you go to bed, glorify Allah thirty-three times, praise Him thirty-three times, and proclaim His greatness thirty-four times.” ʿAlī said: “By Allah, I have never abandoned these words since the Messenger of Allah ﷺ taught them to me.” Ibn al-Kawwāʾ asked him: “Not even on the night of Ṣiffīn?” He replied: “May Allah fight you, O people of Iraq! No—not even on the night of Ṣiffīn.”"]},"buhuth":{"en":["The Ṣuffah—with a ḍammah on the letter ṣād and a doubled fāʾ—was a shaded shelter at the rear of the Prophet’s Mosque. It served as a refuge for poor Muslims who had neither a home nor family to care for them. Their numbers increased and decreased according to changing circumstances, and it has been reported that, at various times, they numbered around six hundred people."]}},"tuhfa":{},"voc":["fazail",258],"full":1,"dr":1,"rep":[11251],"tks":"صحيح: رواه أحمد (596، 838)، وابن سعد (6897)، والبزار (757)."},{"num":10061,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عن عُبَيْدِ اللَّهِ بن أَبِي رَافِعٍ، وَهُوَ كَاتِبُ عَلِيٍّ قَالَ: سَمِعْتُ عَلِيًّا رَضِيَ اللَّهُ عَنْهُ وَهُوَ يَقُولُ:  بَعَثَنَا رَسُولُ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ أَنَا وَالزُّبَيْرَ وَالْمِقْدَادَ، فَقَالَ: ائْتُوا رَوْضَةَ خَاخٍ، فَإِنَّ بِهَا ظَعِينَةً مَعَهَا كِتَابٌ، فَخُذُوهُ مِنْهَا. فَانْطَلَقْنَا تَعَادَى بِنَا خَيْلُنَا، فَإِذَا نَحْنُ بِالْمَرْأَةِ، فَقُلْنَا: أَخْرِجِي الْكِتَابَ! فَقَالَتْ: مَا مَعِي كِتَابٌ. فَقُلْنَا: لَتُخْرِجِنَّ الْكِتَابَ أَوْ لَتُلْقِيَنَّ الثِّيَابَ! فَأَخْرَجَتْهُ مِنْ عِقَاصِهَا، فَأَتَيْنَا بِهِ رَسُولَ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ، فَإِذَا فِيهِ: مِنْ حَاطِبِ بْنِ أَبِي بَلْتَعَةَ إِلَى نَاسٍ مِنَ الْمُشْرِكِينَ مِنْ أَهْلِ مَكَّةَ، يُخْبِرُهُمْ بِبَعْضِ أَمْرِ رَسُولِ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ، فَقَالَ رَسُولُ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ: يَا حَاطِبُ، مَا هَذَا؟ قَالَ: لَا تَعْجَلْ عَلَيَّ يَا رَسُولَ اللَّهِ، إِنِّي كُنْتُ امْرَأً مُلْصَقًا فِي قُرَيْشٍ، - قَالَ سُفْيَانُ: كَانَ حَلِيفًا لَهُمْ، وَلَمْ يَكُنْ مِنْ أَنْفُسِهَا - وَكَانَ مِمَّنْ كَانَ مَعَكَ مِنَ الْمُهَاجِرِينَ لَهُمْ قَرَابَاتٌ يَحْمُونَ بِهَا أَهْلِيهِمْ، فَأَحْبَبْتُ إِذْ فَاتَنِي ذَلِكَ مِنَ النَّسَبِ فِيهِمْ، أَنْ أَتَّخِذَ فِيهِمْ يَدًا يَحْمُونَ بِهَا قَرَابَتِي، وَلَمْ أَفْعَلْهُ كُفْرًا وَلَا ارْتِدَادًا عَنْ دِينِي، وَلَا رِضًا بِالْكُفْرِ بَعْدَ الْإِسْلَامِ. فَقَالَ النَّبِيُّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ: صَدَقَ. فَقَالَ عُمَرُ: دَعْنِي يَا رَسُولَ اللَّهِ أَضْرِبْ عُنُقَ هَذَا الْمُنَافِقِ! فَقَالَ: إِنَّهُ قَدْ شَهِدَ بَدْرًا، وَمَا يُدْرِيكَ لَعَلَّ اللَّهَ اطَّلَعَ عَلَى أَهْلِ بَدْرٍ فَقَالَ: اعْمَلُوا مَا شِئْتُمْ فَقَدْ غَفَرْتُ لَكُمْ. فَأَنْزَلَ اللَّهُ عَزَّ وَجَلَّ: ﴿يَا أَيُّهَا الَّذِينَ آمَنُوا لا تَتَّخِذُوا عَدُوِّي وَعَدُوَّكُمْ أَوْلِيَاءَ﴾. وَلَيْسَ فِي حَدِيثِ أَبِي بَكْرٍ وَزُهَيْرٍ ذِكْرُ الْآيَةِ، وَجَعَلَهَا إِسْحَاقُ فِي رِوَايَتِهِ مِنْ تِلَاوَةِ سُفْيَانَ."],"takhrij":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاري في الجهاد (3007)، ومسلم في فضائل الصحابة (2494-161) كلاهما من طريق سفيان بن عيينة، عن عمرو، عن الحسن بن محمد، أخبرني عبيدالله بن أبي رافع – وهو كاتب علي- قال: سمعت علي وهو يقول: فذكره.","grade":"متفق عليه","chapter_ar":"باب ما جاء في فضائل أهل بدر","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب فضائل الصحابة وأخبارهم","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Authentic: Narrated by al-Bukhārī (3007) and Muslim (2494, no. 161).","chapter_en":"Reports Concerning the Virtues of the People of Badr","part_en":"The Book of the Virtues and Accounts of the Companions","group_ar":"مجموع ما جاء في فضل جماعات الصحابة","group_en":"Collected Reports Concerning the Virtues of Groups of the Companions","part_no":49,"group_no":12,"chapter_no":34,"content":{"translation":{"en":["ʿUbaydullāh ibn Abī Rāfiʿ, the scribe of ʿAlī, narrated: I heard ʿAlī (may Allah be pleased with him) say: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ sent me, al-Zubayr, and al-Miqdād, saying: “Go to Rawḍat Khākh. There you will find a woman carrying a letter. Take it from her.” We rode swiftly until we found the woman. We said: “Produce the letter.” She replied: “I do not have any letter.” We said: “You will either produce the letter or remove your clothing.” She then took the letter out from the braids of her hair. We brought it to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and it was found to be from Ḥāṭib ibn Abī Baltaʿah to some of the idolaters of Makkah, informing them about part of the Prophet’s plans. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ asked: “O Ḥāṭib, what is this?” Ḥāṭib replied: “O Messenger of Allah, do not be hasty in judging me. I was a man attached to Quraysh”—Sufyān explained that he was their ally but not one of them by lineage—“while the other Emigrants had relatives there who protected their families. Since I had no such relatives, I wished to establish a favor with them so they would protect my family. I did not do this out of disbelief, apostasy, or approval of disbelief after embracing Islam.” The Prophet ﷺ said: “He has spoken the truth.” ʿUmar said: “O Messenger of Allah, allow me to strike the neck of this hypocrite.” The Prophet ﷺ replied: “He participated in Badr. And what makes you know? Perhaps Allah looked upon the people of Badr and said: ‘Do whatever you wish, for I have forgiven you.’” Then Allah revealed: “O you who believe! Do not take My enemies and your enemies as allies…” (Qur’an 60:1)"]},"buhuth":{"en":["In another narration, the Prophet ﷺ sent me, Abū Marthad, and al-Zubayr, all of us mounted on horseback, and said:","“Proceed until you reach Rawḍat Khākh. There you will find a woman from among the polytheists carrying a letter from Ḥāṭib to the polytheists…”","At the end of the narration, the Prophet ﷺ said:","“Is he not one of the people of Badr?”","He then said:","“Perhaps Allah looked upon the people of Badr and said: ‘Do whatever you wish, for Paradise has become obligatory for you,’ or, ‘I have forgiven you.’”","At this, ʿUmar’s eyes filled with tears, and he said:","“Allah and His Messenger know best.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"voc":["fazail",259],"full":1,"dr":1,"tks":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (3007)، ومسلم (2494/161)."},{"num":10062,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ أَبِي هُرَيْرَةَ عَنْ رَسُولُ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ: اطَّلَعَ اللَّهُ عَلَى أَهْلِ بَدْرٍ فَقَالَ: اعْمَلُوا مَا شأتم فَقَدْ غَفَرْتُ لَكُمْ."],"takhrij":"حسن: رواه أبو داود (4654)، وأحمد (7940)، والحاكم (4/77،78) كلهم من طريق يزيد بن هارون، أنا حماد بن سلمة، عن عاصم، عن أبي صالح، عن أبي هريرة قال: فذكره.","grade":"حسن","chapter_ar":"باب ما جاء في فضائل أهل بدر","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب فضائل الصحابة وأخبارهم","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Hasan: Narrated by Abū Dāwūd (4654), Aḥmad (7940), and al-Ḥākim (6968).","chapter_en":"Reports Concerning the Virtues of the People of Badr","part_en":"The Book of the Virtues and Accounts of the Companions","group_ar":"مجموع ما جاء في فضل جماعات الصحابة","group_en":"Collected Reports Concerning the Virtues of Groups of the Companions","part_no":49,"group_no":12,"chapter_no":34,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Abū Hurayrah narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Allah looked upon the people of Badr and said: ‘Do whatever you wish, for I have forgiven you.’”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"voc":["fazail",260],"full":1,"dr":1,"tks":"حسن: رواه أبو داود (4654)، وأحمد (7940)، والحاكم (6968)."},{"num":10063,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ مُعَاذِ بْنِ رِفَاعَةَ بْنِ رَافِعٍ الزُّرَقِيِّ، عَنْ أَبِيهِ ـ وَكَانَ أَبُوهُ مِنْ أَهْلِ بَدْرٍ ـ قَالَ: جَاءَ جِبْرِيلُ إِلَى النَّبِيِّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ فَقَالَ: مَا تَعُدُّونَ أَهْلَ بَدْرٍ فِيكُمْ؟ قَالَ: مِنْ أَفْضَلِ الْمُسْلِمِينَ ـ أَوْ كَلِمَةً نَحْوَهَا، ـ قَالَ: وَكَذَلِكَ مَنْ شَهِدَ بَدْرًا مِنَ الْمَلاَئِكَةِ."],"takhrij":"صحيح: رواه البخاري في المغازي (3992) عن إسحاق بن إبراهيم، أنا جرير، عن يحيىى بن سعيد، عن معاذ بن رفاعة، عن أبيه قال: فذكره.","grade":"صحيح","chapter_ar":"باب ما جاء في فضائل أهل بدر","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب فضائل الصحابة وأخبارهم","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Authentic: Narrated by al-Bukhārī (3992).","chapter_en":"Reports Concerning the Virtues of the People of Badr","part_en":"The Book of the Virtues and Accounts of the Companions","group_ar":"مجموع ما جاء في فضل جماعات الصحابة","group_en":"Collected Reports Concerning the Virtues of Groups of the Companions","part_no":49,"group_no":12,"chapter_no":34,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Muʿādh ibn Rifāʿah ibn Rāfiʿ al-Zuraqī narrated from his father—who was one of the participants of Badr—that Jibrīl (Gabriel) came to the Prophet ﷺ and asked: “How do you regard those among you who took part in the Battle of Badr?” The Prophet ﷺ replied: “They are among the best of the Muslims,” or words to that effect. Jibrīl then said: “And likewise, among us, those angels who witnessed Badr are the best.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"voc":["fazail",261],"full":1,"rep":[635],"tks":"صحيح: رواه البخاري (3992)."},{"num":10064,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عن رَافِعِ بن خَدِيجٍ قَالَ: إِنَّ جِبْرِيلَ - أَوْ مَلَكًا - جَاءَ إِلَى النَّبِيِّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ، فَقَالَ: مَا تَعُدُّونَ مَنْ شَهِدَ بَدْرًا فِيكُمْ؟ قَالُوا: خِيَارُنَا، قَالَ: كَذَلِكَ هُمْ عِنْدَنَا خِيَارُنَا مِنَ الْمَلَائِكَةِ."],"takhrij":"صحيح: رواه ابن ماجه (106)، وأحمد (15820)، وعبد بن حميد (425)، وصحّحه ابن حبان (7224) كلهم من طريق سفيان (هو الثوري)، عن يحيىى بن سعيد (هو التيمي أبو حيان)، عن عباية بن رفاعة، عن جده رافع بن خديج فذكره.وإسناده صحيح.","grade":"صحيح","chapter_ar":"باب ما جاء في فضائل أهل بدر","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب فضائل الصحابة وأخبارهم","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Authentic: Narrated by Ibn Mājah (106), Aḥmad (15820), ʿAbd ibn Ḥumayd (425), and authenticated by Ibn Ḥibbān (7224).","chapter_en":"Reports Concerning the Virtues of the People of Badr","part_en":"The Book of the Virtues and Accounts of the Companions","group_ar":"مجموع ما جاء في فضل جماعات الصحابة","group_en":"Collected Reports Concerning the Virtues of Groups of the Companions","part_no":49,"group_no":12,"chapter_no":34,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Rāfiʿ ibn Khadīj narrated: Jibrīl—or an angel—came to the Prophet ﷺ and asked: “How do you regard those among you who participated in Badr?” They replied: “They are the best among us.” He said: “In the same way, among us, those angels who took part in Badr are our best.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"voc":["fazail",262],"full":1,"tks":"صحيح: رواه ابن ماجه (106)، وأحمد (15820)، وعبد بن حميد (425)، وصححه ابن حبان (7224)."},{"num":10065,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنِ ابْنِ عَبَّاسٍ، أَنَّ النَّبِيَّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ قَالَ وَهْوَ فِي قُبَّةٍ لَهُ يَوْمَ بَدْرٍ: أَنْشُدُكَ عَهْدَكَ وَوَعْدَكَ، اللَّهُمَّ إِنْ شِئْتَ لَمْ تُعْبَدْ بَعْدَ الْيَوْمِ أَبَدًا. فَأَخَذَ أَبُو بَكْرٍ بِيَدِهِ وَقَالَ: حَسْبُكَ يَا رَسُولَ اللَّهِ، فَقَدْ أَلْحَحْتَ عَلَى رَبِّكَ. وَهْوَ فِي الدِّرْعِ، فَخَرَجَ وَهْوَ يَقُولُ: {سَيُهْزَمُ الْجَمْعُ وَيُوَلُّونَ الدُّبُرَ * بَلِ السَّاعَةُ مَوْعِدُهُمْ وَالسَّاعَةُ أَدْهَى وَأَمَرُّ}."],"takhrij":"صحيح: رواه البخاري في التفسير (4877) عن إسحاق، ثنا خالد، عن خالد، عن عكرمة، عن ابن عباس فذكره.","grade":"صحيح","chapter_ar":"باب ما جاء في فضائل أهل بدر","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب فضائل الصحابة وأخبارهم","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Authentic: Narrated by al-Bukhārī (4877).","chapter_en":"Reports Concerning the Virtues of the People of Badr","part_en":"The Book of the Virtues and Accounts of the Companions","group_ar":"مجموع ما جاء في فضل جماعات الصحابة","group_en":"Collected Reports Concerning the Virtues of Groups of the Companions","part_no":49,"group_no":12,"chapter_no":34,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Ibn ʿAbbās narrated: On the Day of Badr, while the Prophet ﷺ was inside a small tent, he supplicated: “O Allah, I implore You by Your covenant and Your promise. O Allah, if You will, You will not be worshipped after today.” Abū Bakr took hold of his hand and said: “That is enough, O Messenger of Allah. You have earnestly and repeatedly called upon your Lord.” The Prophet ﷺ then emerged wearing his coat of armor while reciting: “Their assembly will be defeated, and they will turn their backs in flight. Rather, the Hour is their appointed time, and the Hour is more disastrous and more bitter.” (Qur’an 54:45–46)"]}},"tuhfa":{},"full":1,"rep":[8749,13454],"tks":"صحيح: رواه البخاري (4877)."},{"num":10066,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ عُمَرَ بن الْخَطَّابِ قَالَ: لَمَّا كَانَ يَوْمُ بَدْرٍ نَظَرَ رَسُولُ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ إِلَى الْمُشْرِكِينَ وَهُمْ أَلْفٌ، وَأَصْحَابُهُ ثلاثمئة وَتِسْعَةَ عَشَرَ رَجُلًا، فَاسْتَقْبَلَ نَبِيُّ اللَّهِ الْقِبْلَةَ، ثُمَّ مَدَّ يَدَيْهِ فَجَعَلَ يَهْتِفُ بِرَبِّهِ: اللَّهُمَّ أَنْجِزْ لِي مَا وَعَدْتَنِي، اللَّهُمَّ آتِ مَا وَعَدْتَنِي، اللَّهُمَّ إِنْ تَُهْلِكْ هَذِهِ الْعِصَابَةَُ مِنْ أَهْلِ الْإِسْلَامِ لَا تُعْبَدْ فِي الْأَرْضِ...فَأَمَدَّهُ الله بِالْمَلَائِكَةِ.الحديث."],"takhrij":"صحيح: رواه مسلم في الجهاد (1763) عن هنّاد بن السري، ثنا ابن المبارك، عن عكرمة بن عمار، ثني سماك الحنفي قال: سمعت ابن عباس يقول: حدثني عمر بن الخطاب قال: فذكره.","grade":"صحيح","chapter_ar":"باب ما جاء في فضائل أهل بدر","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب فضائل الصحابة وأخبارهم","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Authentic: Narrated by Muslim (1763).","chapter_en":"Reports Concerning the Virtues of the People of Badr","part_en":"The Book of the Virtues and Accounts of the Companions","group_ar":"مجموع ما جاء في فضل جماعات الصحابة","group_en":"Collected Reports Concerning the Virtues of Groups of the Companions","part_no":49,"group_no":12,"chapter_no":34,"content":{"translation":{"en":["ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb narrated: On the Day of Badr, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ looked at the army of the polytheists, who numbered one thousand, while his own companions numbered only three hundred and nineteen men. The Prophet ﷺ then faced the qiblah, raised his hands, and continuously called upon his Lord, saying: “O Allah, fulfill for me what You have promised me. O Allah, grant me what You have promised me. O Allah, if this small group of the people of Islam is destroyed today, You will not be worshipped on earth.” Thereupon Allah reinforced him with the angels. (The remainder of the narration follows in the original source.)"]}},"tuhfa":{},"voc":["fazail",264],"full":1,"tks":"صحيح: رواه مسلم (1763)."},{"num":10067,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ علي قَالَ: بَاتَ رَسُولُ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ يَدْعُو رَبَّهُ عَزَّ وَجَلَّ وَيَقُولُ: اللهُمَّ إِنْ تُهْلِكْ هَذِهِ الْفِئَةَ لَا تُعْبَدْ."],"takhrij":"صحيح: رواه أحمد (948)، والبزار (719) كلاهما من حديث إسرائيل، عن أبي إسحاق، عن حارثة بن مضرب، عن علي قال: فذكره.وإسناده صحيح.","grade":"صحيح","chapter_ar":"باب ما جاء في فضائل أهل بدر","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب فضائل الصحابة وأخبارهم","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Authentic: Narrated by Aḥmad (948) and al-Bazzār (719).","chapter_en":"Reports Concerning the Virtues of the People of Badr","part_en":"The Book of the Virtues and Accounts of the Companions","group_ar":"مجموع ما جاء في فضل جماعات الصحابة","group_en":"Collected Reports Concerning the Virtues of Groups of the Companions","part_no":49,"group_no":12,"chapter_no":34,"content":{"translation":{"en":["ʿAlī narrated: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ spent the night supplicating to his Lord, the Mighty and Majestic, saying: “O Allah, if this group is destroyed, You will not be worshipped.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"voc":["fazail",265],"full":1,"dr":1,"tks":"صحيح: رواه أحمد (948)، والبزار (719)."},{"num":10068,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ أَنَسٍ ـ رَضِيَ اللَّهُ عَنْهُ أَنَّ النَّبِيَّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ أَتَاهُ رِعْلٌ وَذَكْوَانُ وَعُصَيَّةُ، وَبَنُو لِحْيَانَ، فَزَعَمُوا أَنَّهُمْ قَدْ أَسْلَمُوا، وَاسْتَمَدُّوهُ عَلَى قَوْمِهِمْ، فَأَمَدَّهُمُ النَّبِيُّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ بِسَبْعِينَ مِنَ الأَنْصَارِ.","قَالَ أَنَسٌ: كُنَّا نُسَمِّيهِمُ الْقُرَّاءَ، يَحْطِبُونَ بِالنَّهَارِ وَيُصَلُّونَ بِاللَّيْلِ، فَانْطَلَقُوا بِهِمْ حَتَّى بَلَغُوا بِئْرَ مَعُونَةَ غَدَرُوا بِهِمْ وَقَتَلُوهُمْ، فَقَنَتَ شَهْرًا يدعوا عَلَى رِعْلٍ وَذَكْوَانَ وَبَنِي لِحْيَانَ.","قال قتادة: وحدثنا أنس أنهم قرؤوا بهم قرآنا: ألا بلغوا عنا قومنا بأنا قد لقينا ربنا، فرضي عنا وأرضانا، ثم رفع ذلك بعد."],"takhrij":"صحيح: رواه البخاري في الجهاد والسير (3046) عن محمد بن بشار، ثنا ابن أبي عدي وسهل بن يوسف، عن سعيد، عن قتادة، عن أنس: فذكره.","grade":"صحيح","chapter_ar":"باب ما جاء في فضل أهل بئر معونة","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب فضائل الصحابة وأخبارهم","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Authentic: Narrated by al-Bukhārī (3064).","chapter_en":"Reports Concerning the Virtue of the People of Bi’r Maʿūnah","part_en":"The Book of the Virtues and Accounts of the Companions","group_ar":"مجموع ما جاء في فضل جماعات الصحابة","group_en":"Collected Reports Concerning the Virtues of Groups of the Companions","part_no":49,"group_no":12,"chapter_no":35,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Anas ibn Mālik narrated: Representatives of Riʿl, Dhakwān, ʿUṣayyah, and Banū Liḥyān came to the Prophet ﷺ claiming that they had accepted Islam and asked him to send assistance against their own people. The Prophet ﷺ sent with them seventy men from the Anṣār. Anas said: “We used to call them the Reciters (al-Qurrāʾ). During the day they gathered firewood, and during the night they devoted themselves to prayer.” When they reached Bi’r Maʿūnah, those tribes betrayed them and massacred them.","The Prophet ﷺ then supplicated against Riʿl, Dhakwān, and Banū Liḥyān during the qunūt prayer for an entire month. Qatādah narrated from Anas that a Qur’anic passage was revealed concerning them which the Muslims recited: “Convey to our people that we have met our Lord, and He is pleased with us and has made us pleased.” Later, the recitation of this verse was abrogated."]},"buhuth":{"en":["His statement, “They recited regarding them a Qur’anic passage…”, means that verses were revealed concerning those who were martyred at Bi’r Maʿūnah and were recited as part of the Qur’an before their recitation was later abrogated.","Another narration from Anas states:","“A Qur’anic passage was revealed concerning those who were killed at Bi’r Maʿūnah, which we recited, and then its recitation was abrogated: ‘Convey to our people that we have met our Lord…’”","Recorded by al-Bukhārī (2814) and Muslim (677, no. 297)."]}},"tuhfa":{},"voc":["fazail",266],"full":1,"dr":1,"tks":"صحيح: رواه البخاري (3046). وقوله: «قرؤوا فيهم قرآنا…» أي نزل فيهم قرآن يتلى ثم نسخ بعد ذلك، كما ورد في رواية أخرى عن أنس بلفظ: «أنزل في الذين قتلوا ببئر معونة قرآن قرأناه، ثم نسخ بعد: بلغوا قومنا أنه قد…» فذكره. رواه البخاري (3046)، ومسلم (677/297)."},{"num":10069,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ أَنَسٍ  أَنَّ رَسُولَ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ كَانَ يَقُولُ يَوْمَ أُحُدٍ: اللَّهُمَّ إِنَّكَ إِنْ تَشَأْ لَا تُعْبَدْ فِي الْأَرْضِ."],"takhrij":"صحيح: رواه مسلم في الجهاد (1743) عن حجاج بن الشاعر، ثنا عبدالصمد، ثنا حماد، عن ثابت، عن أنس قال: فذكره.","grade":"صحيح","chapter_ar":"باب ما جاء في فضائل أهل أحد","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب فضائل الصحابة وأخبارهم","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Authentic: Narrated by Muslim (1743).","chapter_en":"Reports Concerning the Virtues of the People of Uḥud","part_en":"The Book of the Virtues and Accounts of the Companions","group_ar":"مجموع ما جاء في فضل جماعات الصحابة","group_en":"Collected Reports Concerning the Virtues of Groups of the Companions","part_no":49,"group_no":12,"chapter_no":36,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Anas ibn Mālik al-Anṣārī narrated: On the Day of Uḥud, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to supplicate: “O Allah, if You will, You will not be worshipped on earth.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"voc":["fazail",267],"full":1,"rep":[7878,8822],"tks":"صحيح: رواه مسلم (1743)."},{"num":10070,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنِ ابْنِ عَبَّاسٍ، قَالَ: قَالَ رَسُولُ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ: لَمَّا أُصِيبَ إِخْوَانُكُمْ بِأُحُدٍ جَعَلَ اللَّهُ أَرْوَاحَهُمْ فِي جَوْفِ طَيْرٍ خُضْرٍ تَرِدُ أَنْهَارَ الْجَنَّةِ، تَأْكُلُ مِنْ ثِمَارِهَا، وَتَأْوِي إِلَى قَنَادِيلَ مِنْ ذَهَبٍ مُعَلَّقَةٍ فِي ظِلِّ الْعَرْشِ، فَلَمَّا وَجَدُوا طِيبَ مَأْكَلِهِمْ وَمَشْرَبِهِمْ وَمَقِيلِهِمْ قَالُوا: مَنْ يُبَلِّغُ إِخْوَانَنَا عَنَّا أَنَّا أَحْيَاءٌ فِي الْجَنَّةِ نُرْزَقُ لِئَلاَّ يَزْهَدُوا فِي الْجِهَادِ، وَلاَ يَنْكُلُوا عِنْدَ الْحَرْبِ؟ فَقَالَ اللَّهُ سُبْحَانَهُ: أَنَا أُبَلِّغُهُمْ عَنْكُمْ. قَالَ: فَأَنْزَلَ اللَّهُ: ﴿وَلاَ تَحْسَبَنَّ الَّذِينَ قُتِلُوا فِي سَبِيلِ اللَّهِ أَمْوَاتًا﴾ [سورة آل عمران: 169] }. إِلَى آخِرِ الآيَةِ."],"takhrij":"حسن: رواه أبو داود (2520) عن عثمان بن أبي شيبة، حدثنا عبد الله بن إدريس، عن محمد بن إسحاق، عن إسماعيل بن أمية، عن أبي الزبير، عن سعيد بن جبير، عن ابن عباس قال: فذكره.","grade":"حسن","chapter_ar":"باب ما جاء في فضل شهداء أحد","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب فضائل الصحابة وأخبارهم","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Hasan: Narrated by Abū Dāwūd (2520) and Aḥmad (2389).","chapter_en":"Reports Concerning the Virtue of the Martyrs of Uḥud","part_en":"The Book of the Virtues and Accounts of the Companions","group_ar":"مجموع ما جاء في فضل جماعات الصحابة","group_en":"Collected Reports Concerning the Virtues of Groups of the Companions","part_no":49,"group_no":12,"chapter_no":37,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Ibn ʿAbbās narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “When your brothers were martyred at Uḥud, Allah placed their souls inside green birds. They roam through the rivers of Paradise, eat from its fruits, and take refuge in lanterns of gold suspended beneath the Shade of the Throne. When they experienced the excellence of their food, drink, and resting place, they said: ‘Who will convey to our brothers that we are alive in Paradise, receiving provision, so that they will not lose interest in striving in Allah’s cause nor become reluctant in battle?’ Allah, the Exalted, said: ‘I shall convey it to them on your behalf.’ Then Allah revealed: ‘And never think of those who have been killed in the way of Allah as dead…’ (Qur’an 3:169), continuing to the end of the passage."]}},"tuhfa":{},"voc":["fazail",268],"full":1,"dr":1,"rep":[8098,12101],"tks":"حسن: رواه أبو داود (2520)، وأحمد (2389)."},{"num":10071,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عن جابر بْنِ عبدالله يَقُولُ: أَخْبَرَتْنِي أُمُّ مُبَشِّرٍ  أَنَّهَا سَمِعَتِ النَّبِيَّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ يَقُولُ عِنْدَ حَفْصَةَ: لَا يَدْخُلُ النَّارَ إِنْ شَاءَ اللَّهُ مِنْ أَصْحَابِ الشَّجَرَةِ أَحَدٌ الَّذِينَ بَايَعُوا تَحْتَهَا. قَالَتْ: بَلَى يَا رَسُولَ اللَّهِ! فَانْتَهَرَهَا، فَقَالَتْ حَفْصَةُ: ﴿وَإِنْ مِنْكُمْ إِلا وَارِدُهَا﴾ فَقَالَ النَّبِيُّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ: قَدْ قَالَ اللَّهُ عَزَّ وَجَلَّ: ﴿ثُمَّ نُنَجِّي الَّذِينَ اتَّقَوْا وَنَذَرُ الظَّالِمِينَ فِيهَا جِثِيًّا."],"takhrij":"صحيح: رواه مسلم في فضائل الصحابة (2496) عن هارون بن عبد الله، ثنا حجاج بن محمد قال: قال ابن جريج: أخبرني أبو الزبير، أنه سمع جابر بن عبدالله يقول: فذكره.","grade":"صحيح","chapter_ar":"باب ما جاء في فضائل أصحاب الشجرة","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب فضائل الصحابة وأخبارهم","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Authentic: Narrated by Muslim (2496).","chapter_en":"Reports Concerning the Virtues of the Companions of the Tree","part_en":"The Book of the Virtues and Accounts of the Companions","group_ar":"مجموع ما جاء في فضل جماعات الصحابة","group_en":"Collected Reports Concerning the Virtues of Groups of the Companions","part_no":49,"group_no":12,"chapter_no":38,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Jābir ibn ʿAbdullāh narrated: Umm Mubashshir informed me that she heard the Prophet ﷺ say in the presence of Ḥafṣah: “None of those who pledged allegiance beneath the Tree will enter the Fire, Allah willing.” Ḥafṣah said: “Yes, O Messenger of Allah, they will.” He rebuked her, so she recited: “There is none among you except that he will come to it.” (Qur’an 19:71) The Prophet ﷺ replied: “Allah, the Mighty and Majestic, has also said: ‘Then We will save those who were mindful of Allah and leave the wrongdoers therein on their knees.’” (Qur’an 19:72)"]}},"tuhfa":{},"full":1,"dr":1,"rep":[12717,13325],"tks":"صحيح: رواه مسلم (2496)."},{"num":10072,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ جَابِرٍ، عَنْ رَسُولِ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ أَنَّهُ قَالَ: لاَ يَدْخُلُ النَّارَ أَحَدٌ مِمَّنْ بَايَعَ تَحْتَ الشَّجَرَةِ."],"takhrij":"حسن: رواه أبو داود (4653)، وأحمد (14778)، والترمذي (3860)، والنسائي في الكبرى (11444)، وابن حبان (4802) كلهم من طرق عن الليث ابن سعد، عن أبي الزبير، عن جابر فذكره.وإسناده حسن من أجل أبي الزبير.","grade":"حسن","chapter_ar":"باب ما جاء في فضائل أصحاب الشجرة","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب فضائل الصحابة وأخبارهم","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Hasan: Narrated by Abū Dāwūd (4653), Aḥmad (14778), al-Tirmidhī (3860), and al-Nasā’ī in al-Sunan al-Kubrā (11444).","chapter_en":"Reports Concerning the Virtues of the Companions of the Tree","part_en":"The Book of the Virtues and Accounts of the Companions","group_ar":"مجموع ما جاء في فضل جماعات الصحابة","group_en":"Collected Reports Concerning the Virtues of Groups of the Companions","part_no":49,"group_no":12,"chapter_no":38,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Jābir narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “No one who pledged allegiance beneath the Tree will enter the Fire.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"voc":["fazail",270],"full":1,"dr":1,"tks":"حسن: رواه أبو داود (4653)، وأحمد (14778)، والترمذي (3860)، والنسائي في الكبرى (11444)."},{"num":10073,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ جَابِرٍ قَالَ:  كُنَّا يَوْمَ الْحُدَيْبِيَةِ أَلْفًا وَأَرْبَعَمِائَةٍ، فَقَالَ لَنَا النَّبِيُّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ: أَنْتُمُ الْيَوْمَ خَيْرُ أَهْلِ الْأَرْضِ. وَقَالَ جَابِرٌ: لَوْ كُنْتُ أُبْصِرُ لَأَرَيْتُكُمْ مَوْضِعَ الشَّجَرَةِ."],"takhrij":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاري في المغازي (4154)، ومسلم في الإمارة (1856-71) كلاهما من طريق سفيان، عن عمرو، عن جابر قال: فذكره.واللفظ لمسلم.","grade":"متفق عليه","chapter_ar":"باب ما جاء في فضائل أصحاب الشجرة","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب فضائل الصحابة وأخبارهم","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Agreed upon: Narrated by al-Bukhārī (4154) and Muslim (1856, no. 71). This is the wording of Muslim, while the wording of al-Bukhārī is similar.","chapter_en":"Reports Concerning the Virtues of the Companions of the Tree","part_en":"The Book of the Virtues and Accounts of the Companions","group_ar":"مجموع ما جاء في فضل جماعات الصحابة","group_en":"Collected Reports Concerning the Virtues of Groups of the Companions","part_no":49,"group_no":12,"chapter_no":38,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Jābir narrated: On the day of al-Ḥudaybiyah, we numbered fourteen hundred. The Prophet ﷺ said to us: “You are the best people on earth today.” Jābir also said: “Had I still been able to see, I would have shown you the location of the Tree.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"voc":["fazail",271],"full":1,"dr":1,"rep":[13321],"tks":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (4154)، ومسلم (1856/71). وهذا لفظ مسلم، ولفظ البخاري نحوه."},{"num":10074,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ أُمِّ مُبَشِّرٍ، امْرَأَةِ زَيْدِ بْنِ حَارِثَةَ، قَالَتْ: كَانَ رَسُولُ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ فِي بَيْتِ حَفْصَةَ، فَقَالَ: لَا يَدْخُلُ النَّارَ أَحَدٌ شَهِدَ بَدْرًا وَالْحُدَيْبِيَةَ.","قَالَتْ حَفْصَةُ: أَليسَ الله عَزَّ وَجَلَّ يَقُولُ: وَإِنْ مِنْكُمْ إِلَّا وَارِدُهَا قَالَ رَسُولُ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ: فمَهْ ثُمَّ نُنَجِّي الَّذِينَ اتَّقَوْا وَنَذَرُ الظَّالِمِينَ فِيهَا جِثِيًّا."],"takhrij":"صحيح: رواه أحمد (27042)، وابن ماجه (4281)، وابن أبي عاصم في السنة (887)، وصحّحه ابن حبان (4800) كلهم من طريق ابن إدريس، عن الأعمش، عن أبي سفيان، عن جابر، عن أم مبشر قالت: فذكرته.وإسناده صحيح.","grade":"صحيح","chapter_ar":"باب ما جاء في فضائل أصحاب الشجرة","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب فضائل الصحابة وأخبارهم","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Authentic: Narrated by Aḥmad (27042) and Ibn Mājah (4281), and authenticated by Ibn Ḥibbān (4800).","chapter_en":"Reports Concerning the Virtues of the Companions of the Tree","part_en":"The Book of the Virtues and Accounts of the Companions","group_ar":"مجموع ما جاء في فضل جماعات الصحابة","group_en":"Collected Reports Concerning the Virtues of Groups of the Companions","part_no":49,"group_no":12,"chapter_no":38,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Umm Mubashshir, the wife of Zayd ibn Ḥārithah, narrated: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was in the house of Ḥafṣah when he said: “No one who witnessed Badr and al-Ḥudaybiyah will enter the Fire.” Ḥafṣah asked: “Does Allah, the Mighty and Majestic, not say: ‘There is none among you except that he will come to it’?” (Qur’an 19:71) The Messenger of Allah ﷺ replied: “Stop there. Then Allah says: ‘Then We will save those who were mindful of Allah and leave the wrongdoers therein on their knees.’”","(Qur’an 19:72)"]}},"tuhfa":{},"full":1,"tks":"صحيح: رواه أحمد (27042)، وابن ماجه (4281)، وصححه ابن حبان (4800)."},{"num":10075,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ أُمِّ مُبَشِّرٍ، قَالَتْ: جَاءَ غُلَامُ حَاطِبٍ، فَقَالَ: وَاللهِ لَا يَدْخُلُ حَاطِبٌ الْجَنَّةَ، فَقَالَ رَسُولُ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ: كَذَبْتَ، قَدْ شَهِدَ بَدْرًا وَالْحُدَيْبِيَةَ."],"takhrij":"صحيح: رواه أحمد (27045)، وابن أبي عاصم في الآحاد والمثاني (334)، والطبراني في الكبير (25/ح 265) كلهم من طريق معاوية بن عمرو، ثنا زائدة، عن سليمان – هو الأعمش-، عن أبي سفيان، عن جابر، عن أم مبشر قالت: فذكرته.","grade":"صحيح","chapter_ar":"باب ما جاء في فضائل أصحاب الشجرة","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب فضائل الصحابة وأخبارهم","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Authentic: Narrated by Aḥmad (27045) and Ibn Abī ʿĀṣim in al-Āḥād wa-al-Mathānī (334).","chapter_en":"Reports Concerning the Virtues of the Companions of the Tree","part_en":"The Book of the Virtues and Accounts of the Companions","group_ar":"مجموع ما جاء في فضل جماعات الصحابة","group_en":"Collected Reports Concerning the Virtues of Groups of the Companions","part_no":49,"group_no":12,"chapter_no":38,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Umm Mubashshir narrated: A servant of Ḥāṭib came and said: “By Allah, Ḥāṭib will not enter Paradise.” The Messenger of Allah ﷺ replied: “You have lied. He witnessed Badr and al-Ḥudaybiyah.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"voc":["fazail",273],"full":1,"rep":[10147],"tks":"صحيح: رواه أحمد (27045)، وابن أبي عاصم في الآحاد والمثاني (334)."},{"num":10076,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ حَفْصَةَ، قَالَتْ: قَالَ رَسُولُ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ: إِنِّي لَأَرْجُو أَنْ لَا يَدْخُلَ النَّارَ، إِنْ شَاءَ اللَّهُ، أَحَدٌ شَهِدَ بَدْرًا، وَالْحُدَيْبِيَةَ قَالَتْ: فَقُلْتُ: أَلَيْسَ اللهُ عَزَّ وَجَلَّ يَقُولُ: ﴿وَإِنْ مِنْكُمْ إِلَّا وَارِدُهَا﴾ [مَرْيَمَ: ٧١]؟ قَالَتْ: فَسَمِعَتْهُ يَقُولُ: ﴿ثُمَّ نُنَجِّي الَّذِينَ اتَّقَوْا وَنَذَرُ الظَّالِمِينَ فِيهَا جِثِيًّا﴾"],"takhrij":"صحيح: رواه أحمد (26440)، وابن ماجه (4281)، وأبو يعلى (7044)، وابن أبي عاصم في السنة (886) كلهم من حديث أبي معاوية، ثنا الأعمش، عن أبي سفيان، عن جابر، عن أم مبشر، عن حفصة قالت: فذكرته.وإسناده صحيح.","grade":"صحيح","chapter_ar":"باب ما جاء في فضائل أصحاب الشجرة","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب فضائل الصحابة وأخبارهم","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Authentic: Narrated by Aḥmad (26440), Ibn Mājah (4281), and Abū Yaʿlā (7044).","chapter_en":"Reports Concerning the Virtues of the Companions of the Tree","part_en":"The Book of the Virtues and Accounts of the Companions","group_ar":"مجموع ما جاء في فضل جماعات الصحابة","group_en":"Collected Reports Concerning the Virtues of Groups of the Companions","part_no":49,"group_no":12,"chapter_no":38,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Ḥafṣah narrated: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “I truly hope that no one who witnessed Badr and al-Ḥudaybiyah will enter the Fire, Allah willing.” I said: “Does Allah, the Mighty and Majestic, not say: ‘There is none among you except that he will come to it’?” (Qur’an 19:71) She said: I then heard him recite: “Then We will save those who were mindful of Allah and leave the wrongdoers therein on their knees.” (Qur’an 19:72)"]}},"tuhfa":{},"full":1,"tks":"صحيح: رواه أحمد (26440)، وابن ماجه (4281)، وأبو يعلى (7044)."},{"num":10077,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ جَابِرٍ  أَنَّ عَبْدًا لِحَاطِبٍ جَاءَ رَسُولَ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ يَشْكُو حَاطِبًا، فَقَالَ: يَا رَسُولَ اللَّهِ، لَيَدْخُلَنَّ حَاطِبٌ النَّارَ! فَقَالَ رَسُولُ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ: كَذَبْتَ، لَا يَدْخُلُهَا؛ فَإِنَّهُ شَهِدَ بَدْرًا وَالْحُدَيْبِيَةَ."],"takhrij":"صحيح: رواه مسلم في فضائل الصحابة (2495) من طرق عن الليث، عن أبي الزبير، عن جابر قال: فذكره.","grade":"صحيح","chapter_ar":"باب ما جاء في فضائل أصحاب الشجرة","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب فضائل الصحابة وأخبارهم","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Authentic: Narrated by Muslim (2495).","chapter_en":"Reports Concerning the Virtues of the Companions of the Tree","part_en":"The Book of the Virtues and Accounts of the Companions","group_ar":"مجموع ما جاء في فضل جماعات الصحابة","group_en":"Collected Reports Concerning the Virtues of Groups of the Companions","part_no":49,"group_no":12,"chapter_no":38,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Jābir narrated: A servant of Ḥāṭib came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ complaining about Ḥāṭib and said: “O Messenger of Allah, Ḥāṭib will certainly enter the Fire.” The Messenger of Allah ﷺ replied: “You have lied. He will not enter it, for he witnessed Badr and al-Ḥudaybiyah.”"]},"buhuth":{"en":["In another wording, the Prophet ﷺ said:","“You have lied. He will never enter it.”","The word “never” is added in this narration. Recorded by Aḥmad (14484)."]}},"tuhfa":{},"voc":["fazail",275],"full":1,"dr":1,"rep":[10146,13326],"tks":"صحيح: رواه مسلم (2495)."},{"num":10078,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ جَابِرٍ قَالَ: قَالَ رَسُولُ الله صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ: لَنْ يَدْخُلَ النَّارَ رَجُلٌ شَهِدَ بَدْرًا وَالحُدَيْبِيَةَ."],"takhrij":"حسن: رواه الإمام أحمد (15262) عن سليمان بن داود (هو الهاشمي)، حدثنا أبوبكر بن عياش، حدثني الأعمشُ، عن أبي سفيان، عن جابر قال: فذكره.","grade":"حسن","chapter_ar":"باب ما جاء في فضائل أصحاب الشجرة","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب فضائل الصحابة وأخبارهم","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Hasan: Narrated by Imām Aḥmad (15262).","chapter_en":"Reports Concerning the Virtues of the Companions of the Tree","part_en":"The Book of the Virtues and Accounts of the Companions","group_ar":"مجموع ما جاء في فضل جماعات الصحابة","group_en":"Collected Reports Concerning the Virtues of Groups of the Companions","part_no":49,"group_no":12,"chapter_no":38,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Jābir narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “No man who witnessed Badr and al-Ḥudaybiyah will enter the Fire.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"voc":["fazail",276],"full":1,"dr":1,"tks":"حسن: رواه الإمام أحمد (15262)."},{"num":10079,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنِ ابْنِ أَبِي أَوْفَى، عَنِ النَّبِيِّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ قَالَ: لَنْ يَلِجَ النَّارَ أَحَدٌ شَهِدَ بَدْرًا وَالْحُدَيْبِيَةَ."],"takhrij":"صحيح: رواه البزار (3340) عن الفضل بن يعقوب الرخامي وهلال بن العلاء قالا: أنا عبدالله بن جعفر قال: أنا عيسى بن يونس، عن إسماعيل بن أبي خالد، عن ابن أبي أوفى قال: فذكره.","grade":"صحيح","chapter_ar":"باب ما جاء في فضائل أصحاب الشجرة","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب فضائل الصحابة وأخبارهم","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Authentic: Narrated by al-Bazzār (3340).","chapter_en":"Reports Concerning the Virtues of the Companions of the Tree","part_en":"The Book of the Virtues and Accounts of the Companions","group_ar":"مجموع ما جاء في فضل جماعات الصحابة","group_en":"Collected Reports Concerning the Virtues of Groups of the Companions","part_no":49,"group_no":12,"chapter_no":38,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Ibn Abī Awfā narrated that the Prophet ﷺ said: “No one who witnessed Badr and al-Ḥudaybiyah will enter the Fire.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"voc":["fazail",277],"full":1,"dr":1,"tks":"صحيح: رواه البزار (3340)."},{"num":10080,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ أَنَسٍ قَالَ: كَانَ مِنْ دُعَاءِ النَّبِيِّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ يَوْمَ حُنَيْنٍ: اللهُمَّ إِنْ تَشَأْ أَنْ لَا تُعْبَدَ بَعْدَ الْيَوْمِ."],"takhrij":"صحيح: رواه أحمد (12220)، وابن أبي شيبة (30200، 38140) كلاهما عن يزيد بن هارون، أخبرنا حميد عن أنس قال : فذكره.وهذا لفظ ابن أبي شيبة.","grade":"صحيح","chapter_ar":"باب ما جاء في فضائل أهل حنين","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب فضائل الصحابة وأخبارهم","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Authentic: Narrated by Aḥmad (12220) and Ibn Abī Shaybah (30200, 38140).","chapter_en":"Reports Concerning the Virtues of the People of Ḥunayn","part_en":"The Book of the Virtues and Accounts of the Companions","group_ar":"مجموع ما جاء في فضل جماعات الصحابة","group_en":"Collected Reports Concerning the Virtues of Groups of the Companions","part_no":49,"group_no":12,"chapter_no":39,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Anas ibn Mālik narrated: Among the supplications of the Prophet ﷺ on the day of Ḥunayn was: “O Allah, if You will, You will not be worshipped after this day.”"]},"buhuth":{"en":["The more widely known reports state that this supplication was made at Badr and Uḥud. However, there is nothing to prevent the Prophet ﷺ from having repeated it at Ḥunayn as well, because had the Muslims been defeated on the day of Ḥunayn, the Arab tribes might have apostatized, just as some of them later apostatized during the caliphate of Abū Bakr al-Ṣiddīq."]}},"tuhfa":{},"voc":["fazail",278],"full":1,"dr":1,"tks":"صحيح: رواه أحمد (12220)، وابن أبي شيبة (30200، 38140)."},{"num":10081,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عن أُمِّ حَرَامٍ أَنَّهَا سَمِعَتِ النَّبِيَّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ يَقُولُ: أَوَّلُ جَيْشٍ مِنْ أُمَّتِي يَغْزُونَ الْبَحْرَ قَدْ أَوْجَبُوا. قَالَتْ أُمُّ حَرَامٍ: قُلْتُ: يَا رَسُولَ اللَّهِ أَنَا فِيهِمْ. قَالَ: أَنْتِ فِيهِمْ. ثُمَّ قَالَ النَّبِيُّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ: أَوَّلُ جَيْشٍ مِنْ أُمَّتِي يَغْزُونَ مَدِينَةَ قَيْصَرَ مَغْفُورٌ لَهُمْ. فَقُلْتُ أَنَا فِيهِمْ يَا رَسُولَ اللَّهِ. قَالَ: لاَ."],"takhrij":"صحيح: رواه البخاري في الجهاد والسير (2924)، عن إسحاق بن يزيد الدمشقي، حدثنا يحيىى بن حمزة، ثني ثور بن يزيد، عن خالد بن معدان أن عمير بن الأسود العنسي حدثه أنه أتى عبادة بن الصامت وهو نازل في ساحة حمص، وهو في بناء له ومعه أم حرام، قال عمير: فحدثتنا أم حرام فذكرته.","grade":"صحيح","chapter_ar":"باب في فضل الجيش الذي يغزو مدينة قيصر","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب فضائل الصحابة وأخبارهم","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Authentic: Narrated by al-Bukhārī (2924).","chapter_en":"The Virtue of the Army That Would Invade the City of Caesar","part_en":"The Book of the Virtues and Accounts of the Companions","group_ar":"مجموع ما جاء في فضل جماعات الصحابة","group_en":"Collected Reports Concerning the Virtues of Groups of the Companions","part_no":49,"group_no":12,"chapter_no":40,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Umm Ḥarām narrated that she heard the Prophet ﷺ say: “The first army from my nation to undertake a naval expedition will have secured Paradise.” Umm Ḥarām said: I asked: “O Messenger of Allah, will I be among them?” He replied: “You will be among them.” Then the Prophet ﷺ said: “The first army from my nation to invade the city of Caesar will be forgiven.” I asked: “O Messenger of Allah, will I be among them?” He replied: “No.”"]},"buhuth":{"en":["The phrase “the city of Caesar” refers to Constantinople. The first expedition against it was led by Yazīd ibn Muʿāwiyah in the year 52 AH."]}},"tuhfa":{},"voc":["fazail",279],"full":1,"dr":1,"rep":[7795],"tks":"صحيح: رواه البخاري (2924)."},{"num":10082,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ ثَوْبَانَ مَوْلَى رَسُولِ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ، عَنِ النَّبِيِّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ قَالَ: عِصَابَتَانِ مِنْ أُمَّتِي أَحْرَزَهُمُ اللهُ مِنَ النَّارِ: عِصَابَةٌ تَغْزُو الْهِنْدَ، وَعِصَابَةٌ تَكُونُ مَعَ عِيسَى ابْنِ مَرْيَمَ."],"takhrij":"حسن: رواه النسائي (3175) عن محمد بن عبدالله بن عبد الرحيم قال: حدثنا أسد بن موسى قال: حدثنا بقية قال: حدثني أبو بكر الزبيدي، عن أخيه محمد بن الوليد، عن لقمان بن عامر، عن عبدالأعلى بن عدي البهراني، عن ثوبان فذكره.","grade":"حسن","chapter_ar":"باب في فضيلة العصابتين من أمة محمد ﷺ","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب فضائل الصحابة وأخبارهم","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Hasan: Narrated by al-Nasā’ī (3175) and Aḥmad (22396).","chapter_en":"The Virtue of Two Groups from the Nation of Muḥammad ﷺ","part_en":"The Book of the Virtues and Accounts of the Companions","group_ar":"مجموع ما جاء في فضل جماعات الصحابة","group_en":"Collected Reports Concerning the Virtues of Groups of the Companions","part_no":49,"group_no":12,"chapter_no":41,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Thawbān, the freedman of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Two groups from my nation have been protected by Allah from the Fire: a group that will campaign in India, and a group that will be with ʿĪsā ibn Maryam.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"voc":["fazail",280],"full":1,"dr":1,"rep":[7796],"tks":"حسن: رواه النسائي (3175)، وأحمد (22396)."},{"num":10083,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ أَنَسِ قَالَ: لَمَّا وَلَدَتْ أُمُّ إِبْرَاهِيمَ إِبْرَاهِيمَ، كَأَنَّهُ وَقَعَ فِي نَفْسِ النَّبِيِّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ مِنْهُ شيءٌ، حَتَّى جَاءَ جِبْرِيلُ فَقَالَ: السَّلَامُ عَلَيْكَ يَا أَبَا إِبْرَاهِيمَ."],"takhrij":"حسن: رواه ابن أبي عاصم في الآحاد والمثاني (3127)، وابن عبد الحكم في الفتوح ( ص 71) كلاهما من حديث دُحيم، عن عبد الرحمن بن إبراهيم، حدثنا ابن وهب، عن ابن لهيعة، عن يزيد بن أبي حبيب، عن الزهري، عن أنس فذكره.","grade":"حسن","chapter_ar":"باب تكنية النبي ﷺ بأبي إبراهيم","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب فضائل الصحابة وأخبارهم","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Hasan: Narrated by Ibn Abī ʿĀṣim in al-Āḥād wa-al-Mathānī (3127), and Ibn ʿAbd al-Ḥakam in al-Futūḥ (p. 71).","chapter_en":"The Prophet ﷺ Being Given the Kunyah Abū Ibrāhīm","part_en":"The Book of the Virtues and Accounts of the Companions","group_ar":"مجموع فضائل أفراد الصحابة وأخبارهم","group_en":"A Collection of the Virtues and Reports of Individual Companions","part_no":49,"group_no":13,"chapter_no":1,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Anas narrated: When the mother of Ibrāhīm gave birth to Ibrāhīm, it appeared that something concerning him entered the heart of the Prophet ﷺ, until Jibrīl came and said: “Peace be upon you, O Abū Ibrāhīm.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"voc":["fazail",281],"full":1,"dr":1,"tks":"حسن: رواه ابن أبي عاصم في الآحاد والمثاني (3127)، وابن عبد الحكم في الفتوح (ص: 71)."},{"num":10084,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ أَنَسِ بْنِ مَالِكٍ قَالَ:  مَا رَأَيْتُ أَحَدًا كَانَ أَرْحَمَ بِالْعِيَالِ مِنْ رَسُولِ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ. قَالَ: كَانَ إِبْرَاهِيمُ مُسْتَرْضِعًا لَهُ فِي عَوَالِي الْمَدِينَةِ، فَكَانَ يَنْطَلِقُ وَنَحْنُ مَعَهُ، فَيَدْخُلُ الْبَيْتَ، وَإِنَّهُ لَيُدَّخَنُ، وَكَانَ ظِئْرُهُ قَيْنًا، فَيَأْخُذُهُ فَيُقَبِّلُهُ، ثُمَّ يَرْجِعُ."],"takhrij":"صحيح: رواه مسلم في الفضائل (2316) من طريق إساعيل (هو ابن علية)، عن أيوب، عن عمرو بن سعيد، عن أنس فذكره.","grade":"صحيح","chapter_ar":"باب كان النبي ﷺ يقبل إبراهيم","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب فضائل الصحابة وأخبارهم","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Authentic: Narrated by Muslim (2316).","chapter_en":"The Prophet ﷺ Used to Kiss Ibrāhīm","part_en":"The Book of the Virtues and Accounts of the Companions","group_ar":"مجموع فضائل أفراد الصحابة وأخبارهم","group_en":"A Collection of the Virtues and Reports of Individual Companions","part_no":49,"group_no":13,"chapter_no":2,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Anas ibn Mālik narrated: I never saw anyone more merciful toward children than the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. Ibrāhīm was being nursed for him in the upper districts of Madinah. The Prophet ﷺ would go there while we accompanied him. He would enter the house, which was filled with smoke because Ibrāhīm’s foster father was a blacksmith. He would take Ibrāhīm, kiss him, and then return."]}},"tuhfa":{},"voc":["fazail",282],"full":1,"dr":1,"rep":[9422],"tks":"صحيح: رواه مسلم (2316)."},{"num":10085,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ الْبَرَاءِ بْنِ عَازِبٍ قَالَ: لَمَّا مَاتَ إِبْرَاهِيمُ قَالَ رَسُولُ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ: إِنَّ لَهُ مُرْضِعًا فِي الْجَنَّةِ."],"takhrij":"صحيح: رواه البخاري في الأدب (6195) عن سليمان بن حرب، أخبرنا شعبة، عن عدي بن ثابت، قال: سمعت البراء قال فذكره.","grade":"صحيح","chapter_ar":"باب إن الله جعل لإبراهيم ابن النبي ﷺ مرضعًا في الجنة","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب فضائل الصحابة وأخبارهم","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Authentic: Narrated by al-Bukhārī (6195).","chapter_en":"Allah Appointed a Wet Nurse in Paradise for Ibrāhīm, the Son of the Prophet ﷺ","part_en":"The Book of the Virtues and Accounts of the Companions","group_ar":"مجموع فضائل أفراد الصحابة وأخبارهم","group_en":"A Collection of the Virtues and Reports of Individual Companions","part_no":49,"group_no":13,"chapter_no":3,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Al-Barāʾ ibn ʿĀzib narrated: When Ibrāhīm died, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “He has a wet nurse in Paradise.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"voc":["fazail",283],"full":1,"dr":1,"tks":"صحيح: رواه البخاري (6195)."},{"num":10086,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عن إِسْمَاعِيلَ بن أَبِي أَوْفَى قَالَ: قُلْتُ: لاِبْنِ أَبِي أَوْفَى: رَأَيْتَ إِبْرَاهِيمَ ابْنَ النَّبِيِّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ، قَالَ: مَاتَ صَغِيرًا، وَلَوْ قُضِيَ أَنْ يَكُونَ بَعْدَ مُحَمَّدٍ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ نَبِيٌّ عَاشَ ابْنُهُ، وَلَكِنْ لاَ نَبِيَّ بَعْدَهُ."],"takhrij":"صحيح: رواه البخاري في الأدب (6194) عن ابن نمير، حدثنا محمد بن بشر، حدثنا إسماعيل فذكره.","grade":"صحيح","chapter_ar":"باب لو قُدِّرت النبوة بعد النبي ﷺ لكان إبراهيم","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب فضائل الصحابة وأخبارهم","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Authentic: Narrated by al-Bukhārī (6194).","chapter_en":"Had Prophethood Been Decreed After the Prophet ﷺ, Ibrāhīm Would Have Been a Prophet","part_en":"The Book of the Virtues and Accounts of the Companions","group_ar":"مجموع فضائل أفراد الصحابة وأخبارهم","group_en":"A Collection of the Virtues and Reports of Individual Companions","part_no":49,"group_no":13,"chapter_no":4,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Ismāʿīl ibn Abī Awfā narrated: I asked Ibn Abī Awfā: “Did you see Ibrāhīm, the son of the Prophet ﷺ?” He replied: “He died while still young. Had it been decreed that there would be a prophet after Muḥammad ﷺ, his son would have lived. However, there is no prophet after him.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"voc":["fazail",284],"full":1,"tks":"صحيح: رواه البخاري (6194)."},{"num":10087,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ أنس قَالَ: رَأَيْتُ إبراهيم وَهُوَ يَكِيدُ بِنَفْسِهِ بَيْنَ يَدَيْ رَسُولِ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ، ، فَدَمَعَتْ عَيْنَا رَسُولِ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ فَقَالَ: تَدْمَعُ الْعَيْنُ، وَيَحْزَنُ الْقَلْبُ، وَلَا نَقُولُ إِلَّا مَا يَرْضَى رَبُّنَا، وَاللهِ يَا إِبْرَاهِيمُ إِنَّا بِكَ لَمَحْزُونُونَ."],"takhrij":"متفق عليه: رواه مسلم في الفضائل (2315) من طريق سليمان بن المغيرة، عن ثابت، عن أنس فذكره، والسياق له.ورواه البخاري في الجنائز (1303) من طريق قريش بن حيان، عن ثابت، عن أنس فذكره نحوه.ثم قال: رواه موسى، عن سليمان بن المغيرة، عن ثابت، عن أنس، عن النبي صلى الله عليه وسلم.","grade":"متفق عليه","chapter_ar":"باب حزن النبي ﷺ بوفاة إبراهيم","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب فضائل الصحابة وأخبارهم","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Agreed upon: Narrated by al-Bukhārī (1303) and Muslim (2315).","chapter_en":"The Prophet’s ﷺ Grief over the Death of Ibrāhīm","part_en":"The Book of the Virtues and Accounts of the Companions","group_ar":"مجموع فضائل أفراد الصحابة وأخبارهم","group_en":"A Collection of the Virtues and Reports of Individual Companions","part_no":49,"group_no":13,"chapter_no":5,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Anas narrated: I saw Ibrāhīm struggling in the throes of death before the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. The eyes of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ filled with tears, and he said: “The eyes shed tears, the heart grieves, and we say only what pleases our Lord. By Allah, O Ibrāhīm, we are truly grieved by your departure.”"]},"buhuth":{"en":["The phrase “يكيد بنفسه” means that his soul was leaving his body; in other words, he was experiencing the final throes of death.","Ibrāhīm, the son of Muḥammad, the Prophet of Allah ﷺ, died in the year 10 AH at the age of eighteen months and was buried in al-Baqīʿ."]}},"tuhfa":{},"voc":["fazail",285],"full":1,"dr":1,"tks":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (1303)، ومسلم (2315)."},{"num":10088,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ أَنَسِ بْنِ مَالِكٍ رَضِيَ اللَّهُ عَنْهُ قَالَ النَّبِيُّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ لأُبَىٍّ: إِنَّ اللَّهَ أَمَرَنِي أَنْ أَقْرَأَ عَلَيْكَ {لَمْ يَكُنِ الَّذِينَ كَفَرُوا}. قَالَ: وَسَمَّانِي؟ قَالَ: نَعَمْ، فَبَكَى."],"takhrij":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاري في مناقب الأنصار (3809)، ومسلم في فضائل الصحابة (799-122) كلاهما عن محمد بن بشار، ثنا غندر قال: سمعت شعبة، سمعت قتادة، عن أنس بن مالك قال: فذكره.واللفظ للبخاري.","grade":"متفق عليه","chapter_ar":"باب فضائل أُبيّ بن كعب","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب فضائل الصحابة وأخبارهم","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Authentic: Narrated by al-Bukhārī (3809) and Muslim (799, no. 122). This is the wording of al-Bukhārī.","chapter_en":"The Virtues of Ubayy ibn Kaʿb","part_en":"The Book of the Virtues and Accounts of the Companions","group_ar":"مجموع فضائل أفراد الصحابة وأخبارهم","group_en":"A Collection of the Virtues and Reports of Individual Companions","part_no":49,"group_no":13,"chapter_no":6,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Anas ibn Mālik narrated: The Prophet ﷺ said to Ubayy: “Allah has commanded me to recite to you: ‘Those who disbelieved were not…’ (Qur’an 98:1)” Ubayy asked: “Did He mention me by name?” The Prophet ﷺ replied: “Yes.” Thereupon Ubayy wept."]},"buhuth":{"en":["In another wording, Ubayy asked:","“Did Allah name me to you?”","The Prophet ﷺ replied:","“Allah named you to me.”","Ubayy then began to weep.","Qatādah said:","I was informed that the Prophet ﷺ recited to him:","“Those who disbelieved among the People of the Book…”","(Qur’an 98:1)","Recorded by al-Bukhārī (4960) and Muslim (799, no. 121).","In another narration, the Prophet of Allah ﷺ said to Ubayy ibn Kaʿb:","“Allah has commanded me to recite the Qur’an to you.”","Ubayy asked:","“Did Allah name me to you?”","He replied:","“Yes.”","Ubayy asked:","“Was I mentioned before the Lord of all worlds?”","He replied:","“Yes.”","Then Ubayy’s eyes overflowed with tears.","Recorded by al-Bukhārī (4961)."]}},"tuhfa":{},"full":1,"dr":1,"tks":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (3809)، ومسلم (799/122)، واللفظ للبخاري."},{"num":10089,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ أُبَيِّ بْنِ كَعْبٍ، قَالَ: إِنَّ رَسُولَ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ قَالَ: إِنَّ اللَّهَ أَمَرَنِي أَنْ أَقْرَأَ عَلَيْكَ الْقُرْآنَ، قَالَ: فَقَرَأَ: ﴿لَمْ يَكُنِ الَّذِينَ كَفَرُوا مِنْ أَهْلِ الْكِتَابِ﴾ [البينة: ١] قَالَ: فَقَرَأَ فِيهَا: وَلَوْ أَنَّ ابْنَ آدَمَ سَأَلَ وَادِيًا مِنْ مَالٍ فَأُعْطِيَهُ، لَسَأَلَ ثَانِيًا، وَلَوْ سَأَلَ ثَانِيًا فَأُعْطِيَهُ، لَسَأَلَ ثَالِثًا، وَلَا يَمْلَأُ جَوْفَ ابْنِ آدَمَ إِلَّا التُّرَابُ، وَيَتُوبُ اللَّهُ عَلَى مَنْ تَابَ، وَإِنَّ ذَلِكَ الدِّينَ الْقَيِّمَ عِنْدَ اللَّهِ الْحَنِيفِيَّةُ، غَيْرُ الْمُشْرِكَةِ، وَلَا الْيَهُودِيَّةِ، وَلَا النَّصْرَانِيَّةِ، وَمَنْ يَفْعَلْ خَيْرًا، فَلَنْ يُكْفَرَهُ."],"takhrij":"حسن: رواه الترمذي (3898)، وأحمد (21202)، وصحّحه الحاكم (2889) كلهم من طريق شعبة، عن عاصم قال: سمعت زر بن حبيش يحدث عن أبي بن كعب قال: فذكره.","grade":"حسن","chapter_ar":"باب فضائل أُبيّ بن كعب","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب فضائل الصحابة وأخبارهم","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Hasan: Narrated by al-Tirmidhī (3898), Aḥmad (21202), and authenticated by al-Ḥākim (2/224 and 531).","chapter_en":"The Virtues of Ubayy ibn Kaʿb","part_en":"The Book of the Virtues and Accounts of the Companions","group_ar":"مجموع فضائل أفراد الصحابة وأخبارهم","group_en":"A Collection of the Virtues and Reports of Individual Companions","part_no":49,"group_no":13,"chapter_no":6,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Ubayy ibn Kaʿb narrated: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Allah has commanded me to recite the Qur’an to you.” He then recited: “Those who disbelieved among the People of the Book…” (Qur’an 98:1) And within the recitation he recited: “If the son of Adam were to ask for a valley filled with wealth and were given it, he would ask for a second. If he were given a second, he would ask for a third. Nothing fills the belly of the son of Adam except dust. Allah accepts the repentance of whoever repents. The religion with Allah is the upright religion, neither polytheism, Judaism, nor Christianity, and whoever does good will never have it denied.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"full":1,"dr":1,"rep":[13758,15262],"tks":"حسن: رواه الترمذي (3898)، وأحمد (21202)، وصححه الحاكم (2889)."},{"num":10090,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ أُبَيِّ بْنِ كَعْبٍ قَالَ: قَالَ رَسُولُ اللَّهِ: صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ:  يَا أَبَا الْمُنْذِرِ، أَتَدْرِي أَيُّ آيَةٍ مِنْ كِتَابِ اللَّهِ مَعَكَ أَعْظَمُ؟ قَالَ: قُلْتُ: اللَّهُ وَرَسُولُهُ أَعْلَمُ. قَالَ: يَا أَبَا الْمُنْذِرِ، أَتَدْرِي أَيُّ آيَةٍ مِنْ كِتَابِ اللَّهِ مَعَكَ أَعْظَمُ؟ قَالَ: قُلْتُ: ﴿اللَّهُ لا إِلَهَ إِلا هُوَ الْحَيُّ الْقَيُّومُ﴾ قَالَ: فَضَرَبَ فِي صَدْرِي، وَقَالَ: وَاللهِ لِيَهْنِكَ الْعِلْمُ، أَبَا الْمُنْذِرِ."],"takhrij":"صحيح: رواه مسلم في صلاة المسافرين (258:810) عن أبي بكر بن أبي شيبة، عن عبد الأعلى بن عبد الأعلى، عن الجريري، عن أبي السليل، عن عبد الله بن رباح الأنصاري، عن أبي بن كعب فذكره.","grade":"صحيح","chapter_ar":"باب دعاء النبي ﷺ لأُبيّ بن كعب بالعلم","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب فضائل الصحابة وأخبارهم","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Authentic: Narrated by Muslim (810, no. 258).","chapter_en":"The Prophet’s ﷺ Supplication for Ubayy ibn Kaʿb to Be Blessed in Knowledge","part_en":"The Book of the Virtues and Accounts of the Companions","group_ar":"مجموع فضائل أفراد الصحابة وأخبارهم","group_en":"A Collection of the Virtues and Reports of Individual Companions","part_no":49,"group_no":13,"chapter_no":7,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Ubayy ibn Kaʿb narrated: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ asked me: “O Abū al-Mundhir, do you know which verse of the Book of Allah that you possess is the greatest?” I replied: “Allah and His Messenger know best.” He again asked: “O Abū al-Mundhir, do you know which verse of the Book of Allah that you possess is the greatest?” I replied: “Allah—there is no deity except Him, the Ever-Living, the Sustainer of all.” (Qur’an 2:255) He struck me gently on the chest and said: “By Allah, may knowledge bring you joy, O Abū al-Mundhir.”"]},"buhuth":{"en":["His statement, “May knowledge bring you joy,” means:","“May you enjoy and be blessed with this knowledge.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"full":1,"dr":1,"rep":[11879],"tks":"صحيح: رواه مسلم (258:810)."},{"num":10091,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ عَائِشَةَ، رَضِيَ اللَّهُ عَنْهَا أَنَّ قُرَيْشًا، أَهَمَّهُمْ شَأْنُ الْمَخْزُومِيَّةِ، فَقَالُوا: مَنْ يَجْتَرِئُ عَلَيْهِ إِلاَّ أُسَامَةُ بْنُ زَيْدٍ، حِبُّ رَسُولِ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ."],"takhrij":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاري في فضائل الصحابة (3732)، ومسلم في الحدود (1688-8) كلاهما عن قتيبة، ثنا ليث، عن الزهري، عن عروة، عن عائشة فذكرته، وهذا لفظ البخاري.","grade":"متفق عليه","chapter_ar":"باب ما جاء في فضل أسامة بن زيد، وأنه حِبُّ رسول الله ﷺ","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب فضائل الصحابة وأخبارهم","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Agreed upon: Narrated by al-Bukhārī (3732) and Muslim (1688, no. 8).","chapter_en":"Reports Concerning the Virtue of Usāmah ibn Zayd and His Being the Beloved of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ","part_en":"The Book of the Virtues and Accounts of the Companions","group_ar":"مجموع فضائل أفراد الصحابة وأخبارهم","group_en":"A Collection of the Virtues and Reports of Individual Companions","part_no":49,"group_no":13,"chapter_no":8,"content":{"translation":{"en":["ʿĀ’ishah narrated: The affair of the Makhzūmī woman greatly concerned Quraysh, so they said: “Who would dare speak to him about her except Usāmah ibn Zayd, the beloved of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ?”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"voc":["fazail",289],"full":1,"tks":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (3732)، ومسلم (1688/8)."},{"num":10092,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ فَاطِمَةَ بنت قَيْسٍ –فِي سياق حديث الجساسة- قَالَتْ: فَلَمَّا تَأَيَّمْتُ خَطَبَنِي عَبْدُ الرَّحْمَنِ بْنُ عَوْفٍ فِي نَفَرٍ مِنْ أَصْحَابِ رَسُولِ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ، ، وَخَطَبَنِي رَسُولُ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ عَلَى مَوْلَاهُ أُسَامَةَ بْنِ زَيْدٍ، وَكُنْتُ قَدْ حُدِّثْتُ أَنَّ رَسُولَ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ قَالَ: مَنْ أَحَبَّنِي فَلْيُحِبَّ أُسَامَةَ."],"takhrij":"صحيح: رواه مسلم في الفتن (2942-119) من طرق عن عبد الصمد بن عبد الوارث، عن الوارث، عن الحسين بن ذكوان، حدثنا ابن بريدة، حدثني عامر بن شراحيل الشعبي، أنه سأل فاطمة بنت قيس فذكرته.","grade":"صحيح","chapter_ar":"باب ما جاء في فضل أسامة بن زيد، وأنه حِبُّ رسول الله ﷺ","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب فضائل الصحابة وأخبارهم","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Authentic: Narrated by Muslim (2942, no. 119).","chapter_en":"Reports Concerning the Virtue of Usāmah ibn Zayd and His Being the Beloved of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ","part_en":"The Book of the Virtues and Accounts of the Companions","group_ar":"مجموع فضائل أفراد الصحابة وأخبارهم","group_en":"A Collection of the Virtues and Reports of Individual Companions","part_no":49,"group_no":13,"chapter_no":8,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Fāṭimah bint Qays narrated, in the context of the ḥadīth of al-Jassāsah: After I became unmarried, ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn ʿAwf proposed to me along with several other Companions of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ proposed that I marry his freedman, Usāmah ibn Zayd. I had already been informed that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Whoever loves me should love Usāmah.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"voc":["fazail",290],"full":1,"dr":1,"tks":"صحيح: رواه مسلم (2942/119)."},{"num":10093,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ عَائِشَةَ قَالَتْ: أَرَادَ النَّبِيُّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ أَنْ ينحِّي مُخَاطَ أُسَامَةَ، قَالَتْ عَائِشَةُ: دَعْنِي حَتَّى أَنَا الَّذِي أَفْعَلُ.قَالَ: يَا عَائِشَةُ أحِبِّيه، فَإِنِّي أحبُّه."],"takhrij":"حسن: رواه الترمذي (3818)، وصحّحه ابن حبان (7058) كلاهما من طريق الحسين بن حريث أبي عمار، حدثنا الفضل بن موسى، عن طلحة بن يحيى، عن عائشة بنت طلحة، عن عائشة فذكرته.","grade":"حسن","chapter_ar":"باب ما جاء في فضل أسامة بن زيد، وأنه حِبُّ رسول الله ﷺ","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب فضائل الصحابة وأخبارهم","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Hasan: Narrated by al-Tirmidhī (3818) and authenticated by Ibn Ḥibbān (7058).","chapter_en":"Reports Concerning the Virtue of Usāmah ibn Zayd and His Being the Beloved of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ","part_en":"The Book of the Virtues and Accounts of the Companions","group_ar":"مجموع فضائل أفراد الصحابة وأخبارهم","group_en":"A Collection of the Virtues and Reports of Individual Companions","part_no":49,"group_no":13,"chapter_no":8,"content":{"translation":{"en":["ʿĀ’ishah narrated: The Prophet ﷺ intended to wipe mucus from Usāmah’s nose. I said: “Allow me to do it.” He replied: “O ʿĀ’ishah, love him, for indeed I love him.”"]},"buhuth":{"en":["Al-Tirmidhī said:","“This is a good authentic hadith.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"voc":["fazail",291],"full":1,"dr":1,"tks":"حسن: رواه الترمذي (3818)، وصححه ابن حبان (7058). قال الترمذي: هذا حديث حسن صحيح."},{"num":10094,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ عَبْدِ اللَّهِ بْنِ عُمَرَ رَضِيَ اللَّهُ عَنْهُمَا قَالَ: بَعَثَ النَّبِيُّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ بَعْثًا، وَأَمَّرَ عَلَيْهِمْ أُسَامَةَ بْنَ زَيْدٍ، فَطَعَنَ بَعْضُ النَّاسِ فِي إِمَارَتِهِ، فَقَالَ النَّبِيُّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ: إِنْ تَطْعُنُوا فِي إِمَارَتِهِ فَقَدْ كُنْتُمْ تَطْعُنُونَ فِي إِمَارَةِ أَبِيهِ مِنْ قَبْلُ، وَايْمُ اللَّهِ، إِنْ كَانَ لَخَلِيقًا لِلإِمَارَةِ، وَإِنْ كَانَ لَمِنْ أَحَبِّ النَّاسِ إِلَىَّ، وَإِنَّ هَذَا لَمِنْ أَحَبِّ النَّاسِ إِلَىَّ بَعْدَهُ."],"takhrij":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاري في فضائل الصحابة (3730)، ومسلم في فضائل الصحابة (2426-63) كلاهما من طريق عبد الله بن دينار، أنه سمع ابن عمر يقول: فذكره.","grade":"متفق عليه","chapter_ar":"باب أن أسامة من أحب الناس إلى النبي ﷺ","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب فضائل الصحابة وأخبارهم","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Authentic: Narrated by al-Bukhārī (3730) and Muslim (2426, no. 63).","chapter_en":"Usāmah Was Among the Most Beloved People to the Prophet ﷺ","part_en":"The Book of the Virtues and Accounts of the Companions","group_ar":"مجموع فضائل أفراد الصحابة وأخبارهم","group_en":"A Collection of the Virtues and Reports of Individual Companions","part_no":49,"group_no":13,"chapter_no":9,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Ibn ʿUmar narrated: The Prophet ﷺ dispatched an expedition and appointed Usāmah ibn Zayd as its commander. Some people criticized his appointment, so the Prophet ﷺ said: “If you criticize his leadership, you also criticized the leadership of his father before him. By Allah, his father was truly worthy of command and was among the most beloved people to me. And this son of his is among the most beloved people to me after him.”"]},"buhuth":{"en":["In another wording, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said while standing on the pulpit:","“If you criticize his leadership”—meaning Usāmah ibn Zayd—“you also criticized the leadership of his father before him. By Allah, his father was truly worthy of it. By Allah, he was among the most beloved people to me. By Allah, this son of his is also truly worthy of it. By Allah, he is among the most beloved people to me after his father. Therefore, I advise you to treat him well, for he is among the righteous among you.”","Recorded by Muslim (2426, no. 64)."]}},"tuhfa":{},"voc":["fazail",292],"full":1,"dr":1,"rep":[10196],"tks":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (3730)، ومسلم (2426/63)."},{"num":10095,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ أُسَامَةَ بْنِ زَيْدٍ رَضِيَ اللَّهُ عَنْهُمَا حَدَّثَ عَنِ النَّبِيِّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ أَنَّهُ كَانَ يَأْخُذُهُ وَالْحَسَنَ، فَيَقُولُ: اللَّهُمَّ أَحِبَّهُمَا فَإِنِّي أُحِبُّهُمَا."],"takhrij":"صحيح: رواه البخاري في فضائل الصحابة (3735) عن موسى بن إسماعيل، ثنا معتمر، قال: سمعت أبي، ثنا أبو عمثان، عن أسامة بن زيد فذكره.","grade":"صحيح","chapter_ar":"باب أن أسامة من أحب الناس إلى النبي ﷺ","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب فضائل الصحابة وأخبارهم","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Authentic: Narrated by al-Bukhārī (3735).","chapter_en":"Usāmah Was Among the Most Beloved People to the Prophet ﷺ","part_en":"The Book of the Virtues and Accounts of the Companions","group_ar":"مجموع فضائل أفراد الصحابة وأخبارهم","group_en":"A Collection of the Virtues and Reports of Individual Companions","part_no":49,"group_no":13,"chapter_no":9,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Usāmah ibn Zayd narrated that the Prophet ﷺ would take him and al-Ḥasan and say: “O Allah, love them both, for indeed I love them both.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"voc":["fazail",293],"full":1,"rep":[10050,10163],"tks":"صحيح: رواه البخاري (3735)."},{"num":10096,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عن حرملة مولى أسامة بن زَيْدٍ أَنَّهُ بَيْنَمَا هُوَ مَعَ عَبْدِ اللَّهِ بْنِ عُمَرَ إِذْ دَخَلَ الْحَجَّاجُ بْنُ أَيْمَنَ فَلَمْ يُتِمَّ رُكُوعَهُ وَلاَ سُجُودَهُ، فَقَالَ: أَعِدْ. فَلَمَّا وَلَّى قَالَ لِي ابْنُ عُمَرَ: مَنْ هَذَا؟ قُلْتُ: الْحَجَّاجُ بْنُ أَيْمَنَ ابْنِ أُمِّ أَيْمَنَ. فَقَالَ ابْنُ عُمَرَ: لَوْ رَأَى هَذَا رَسُولُ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ لأَحَبَّهُ، فَذَكَرَ حُبَّهُ، وَمَا وَلَدَتْهُ أُمُّ أَيْمَنَ."],"takhrij":"صحيح: رواه البخاري في فضائل الصحابة (3737) عن سليمان بن عبدالرحمن، ثنا الوليد، ثنا عبد الرحمن بن نمير، عن الزهري، ثني حرملة فذكره.","grade":"صحيح","chapter_ar":"باب أن أسامة من أحب الناس إلى النبي ﷺ","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب فضائل الصحابة وأخبارهم","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Authentic: Narrated by al-Bukhārī (3737).","chapter_en":"Usāmah Was Among the Most Beloved People to the Prophet ﷺ","part_en":"The Book of the Virtues and Accounts of the Companions","group_ar":"مجموع فضائل أفراد الصحابة وأخبارهم","group_en":"A Collection of the Virtues and Reports of Individual Companions","part_no":49,"group_no":13,"chapter_no":9,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Ḥarmalah, the freedman of Usāmah ibn Zayd, narrated: While I was with ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿUmar, al-Ḥajjāj ibn Ayman entered and performed a prayer in which he did not complete his bowing or prostration properly. Ibn ʿUmar said to him: “Repeat the prayer.” When he turned away, Ibn ʿUmar asked me: “Who is this?” I replied: “He is al-Ḥajjāj ibn Ayman, the son of Umm Ayman.” Ibn ʿUmar said: “Had the Messenger of Allah ﷺ seen him, he would have loved him.” He then mentioned the Prophet’s ﷺ love for Umm Ayman and for those to whom she gave birth."]}},"tuhfa":{},"voc":["fazail",294],"full":1,"tks":"صحيح: رواه البخاري (3737)."},{"num":10097,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عن عَبْدِ اللَّهِ بن دِينَارٍ قَالَ: نَظَرَ ابْنُ عُمَرَ يَوْمًا وَهْوَ فِي الْمَسْجِدِ إِلَى رَجُلٍ يَسْحَبُ ثِيَابَهُ فِي نَاحِيَةٍ مِنَ الْمَسْجِدِ، فَقَالَ: انْظُرْ مَنْ هَذَا؟ لَيْتَ هَذَا عِنْدِي. قَالَ لَهُ إِنْسَانٌ: أَمَا تَعْرِفُ هَذَا يَا أَبَا عَبْدِ الرَّحْمَنِ؟ هَذَا مُحَمَّدُ بْنُ أُسَامَةَ، قَالَ فَطَأْطَأَ ابْنُ عُمَرَ رَأْسَهُ، وَنَقَرَ بِيَدَيْهِ فِي الأَرْضِ، ثُمَّ قَالَ: لَوْ رَآهُ رَسُولُ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ لأَحَبَّهُ."],"takhrij":"صحيح: رواه البخاري في فضائل الصحابة (3734) عن الحسن بن محمد، ثنا أبو عباد يحيى بن عباد، ثنا الماجشون، أنا عبد الله بن دينار قال: فذكره.","grade":"صحيح","chapter_ar":"باب أن أسامة من أحب الناس إلى النبي ﷺ","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب فضائل الصحابة وأخبارهم","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Authentic: Narrated by al-Bukhārī (3734).","chapter_en":"Usāmah Was Among the Most Beloved People to the Prophet ﷺ","part_en":"The Book of the Virtues and Accounts of the Companions","group_ar":"مجموع فضائل أفراد الصحابة وأخبارهم","group_en":"A Collection of the Virtues and Reports of Individual Companions","part_no":49,"group_no":13,"chapter_no":9,"content":{"translation":{"en":["ʿAbdullāh ibn Dīnār narrated: One day, while Ibn ʿUmar was in the mosque, he saw a man dragging his garments in one corner of the mosque. He said: “Find out who this is. I wish he were here beside me.” A man said to him: “Do you not recognize him, O Abū ʿAbd al-Raḥmān? This is Muḥammad ibn Usāmah.” Ibn ʿUmar lowered his head and tapped the ground with his hands, then said: “Had the Messenger of Allah ﷺ seen him, he would have loved him.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"voc":["fazail",295],"full":1,"tks":"صحيح: رواه البخاري (3734)."},{"num":10098,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عن أُسَامَةَ بن زَيْدٍ عَنْ أَبِيهِ، قَالَ: لَمَّا ثَقُلَ رَسُولُ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ هَبَطْتُ وَهَبَطَ النَّاسُ الْمَدِينَةَ، فَدَخَلْتُ عَلَى رَسُولِ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ وَقَدْ أُصْمِتَ فَلَمْ يَتَكَلَّمْ، فَجَعَلَ رَسُولُ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ يَضَعُ يَدَيْهِ عَلَىَّ وَيَرْفَعُهُمَا فَأَعْرِفُ أَنَّهُ يَدْعُو لِي."],"takhrij":"حسن: رواه الترمذي (3817)، وأحمد (21755) كلاهما من طريق محمد بن إسحاق، حدثني سعيد بن عبيد بن السباق، عن محمد بن أسامة بن زيد، عن أبيه أسامة بن زيد فذكره.","grade":"حسن","chapter_ar":"باب أن أسامة من أحب الناس إلى النبي ﷺ","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب فضائل الصحابة وأخبارهم","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Hasan: Narrated by al-Tirmidhī (3817) and Aḥmad (21755).","chapter_en":"Usāmah Was Among the Most Beloved People to the Prophet ﷺ","part_en":"The Book of the Virtues and Accounts of the Companions","group_ar":"مجموع فضائل أفراد الصحابة وأخبارهم","group_en":"A Collection of the Virtues and Reports of Individual Companions","part_no":49,"group_no":13,"chapter_no":9,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Usāmah ibn Zayd narrated: When the illness of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ became severe, I came down to Madinah, and the people also came down to the city. I entered upon the Messenger of Allah ﷺ while he was silent and unable to speak. He began placing his hands upon me and then raising them, and I understood that he was supplicating for me."]},"buhuth":{"en":["Al-Tirmidhī said:","“This is a good, strange hadith.”","Among the reports concerning Usāmah ibn Zayd is that which al-Bukhārī recorded in The Book of Tribulations (7110), from ʿAlī ibn ʿAbdullāh, from Sufyān, who said:","ʿAmr said:","Muḥammad ibn ʿAlī informed me that Ḥarmalah, the freedman of Usāmah, informed him—and ʿAmr said, “I saw Ḥarmalah”—that Usāmah sent me to ʿAlī and said:","“He will ask you now, saying, ‘Why did your companion remain behind?’ Say to him: ‘He says to you: Had you been inside the jaws of a lion, I would have loved to be there with you. However, this is a matter whose correctness I did not recognize.’”","ʿAlī did not give me anything, so I went to al-Ḥasan, al-Ḥusayn, and Ibn Jaʿfar, and they loaded my riding animal with provisions."]}},"tuhfa":{},"voc":["fazail",296],"full":1,"dr":1,"tks":"حسن: رواه الترمذي (3817)، وأحمد (21755). قال الترمذي: هذا حديث حسن غريب."},{"num":10099,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ الْبَرَاءِ بْنِ عَازِبٍ قَالَ: قَرَأَ رَجُلٌ الْكَهْفَ وَفِي الدَّارِ دَابَّةٌ، فَجَعَلَتْ تَنْفِرُ، فَنَظَرَ فَإِذَا ضَبَابَةٌ أَوْ سَحَابَةٌ قَدْ غَشِيَتْهُ، قَالَ: فَذَكَرَ ذَلِكَ لِلنَّبِيِّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ فَقَالَ: اقْرَأْ فُلَانُ، فَإِنَّهَا السَّكِينَةُ تَنَزَّلَتْ عِنْدَ الْقُرْآنِ أَوْ تَنَزَّلَتْ لِلْقُرْآنِ."],"takhrij":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاري في المناقب (3614)، ومسلم في صلاة المسافرين (795-241) كلاهما عن محمد بن بشار، حدثنا غندر محمد بن جعفر، حدثنا شعبة، عن أبي أسحاق قال: سمعت البراء يقول: فذكره.","grade":"متفق عليه","chapter_ar":"باب ما جاء في فضل أسيد بن حضير","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب فضائل الصحابة وأخبارهم","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Agreed upon: Narrated by al-Bukhārī (3614) and Muslim (795, no. 241).","chapter_en":"Reports Concerning the Virtue of Usayd ibn Ḥuḍayr","part_en":"The Book of the Virtues and Accounts of the Companions","group_ar":"مجموع فضائل أفراد الصحابة وأخبارهم","group_en":"A Collection of the Virtues and Reports of Individual Companions","part_no":49,"group_no":13,"chapter_no":10,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Al-Barāʾ ibn ʿĀzib narrated: A man recited Sūrat al-Kahf while an animal was in the house, and the animal began to bolt and behave restlessly. He looked and saw something like a mist or cloud covering him. He later mentioned this to the Prophet ﷺ, who said: “Continue reciting, so-and-so, for that was the tranquility descending because of the Qur’an—or descending for the Qur’an.”"]},"buhuth":{"en":["It is stated in some chains of narration that the man was Usayd ibn Ḥuḍayr."]}},"tuhfa":{},"voc":["fazail",297],"full":1,"dr":1,"rep":[11840],"tks":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (3614)، ومسلم (795/241)."},{"num":10100,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عن أُسَيْدِ بن حُضَيْرٍ بَيْنَمَا هُوَ لَيْلَةً يَقْرَأُ فِي مِرْبَدِهِ إِذْ جَالَتْ فَرَسُهُ. فَقَرَأَ، ثُمَّ جَالَتْ أُخْرَى، فَقَرَأَ، ثُمَّ جَالَتْ أَيْضًا. قَالَ أُسَيْدٌ: فَخَشِيتُ أَنْ تَطَأَ يَحْيَى، فَقُمْتُ إِلَيْهَا، فَإِذَا مِثْلُ الظُّلَّةِ فَوْقَ رَأْسِي فِيهَا، أَمْثَالُ السُّرُجِ، عَرَجَتْ فِي الْجَوِّ حَتَّى مَا أَرَاهَا. قَالَ: فَغَدَوْتُ عَلَى رَسُولِ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ، فَقُلْتُ: يَا رَسُولَ اللَّهِ، بَيْنَمَا أَنَا الْبَارِحَةَ مِنْ جَوْفِ اللَّيْلِ أَقْرَأُ فِي مِرْبَدِي، إِذْ جَالَتْ فَرَسِي. فَقَالَ رَسُولُ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ: اقْرَأِ، ابْنَ حُضَيْرٍ قَالَ: فَقَرَأْتُ، ثُمَّ جَالَتْ أَيْضًا، فَقَالَ رَسُولُ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ: اقْرَأِ، ابْنَ حُضَيْرٍ. قَالَ: فَقَرَأْتُ، ثُمَّ جَالَتْ أَيْضًا، فَقَالَ رَسُولُ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ: اقْرَأِ، ابْنَ حُضَيْرٍ. قَالَ: فَانْصَرَفْتُ، وَكَانَ يَحْيَى قَرِيبًا مِنْهَا، خَشِيتُ أَنْ تَطَأَهُ، فَرَأَيْتُ مِثْلَ الظُّلَّةِ، فِيهَا أَمْثَالُ السُّرُجِ، عَرَجَتْ فِي الْجَوِّ حَتَّى مَا أَرَاهَا. فَقَالَ رَسُولُ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ: تِلْكَ الْمَلَائِكَةُ كَانَتْ تَسْتَمِعُ لَكَ، وَلَوْ قَرَأْتَ لَأَصْبَحَتْ يَرَاهَا النَّاسُ مَا تَسْتَتِرُ مِنْهُمْ."],"takhrij":"صحيح: رواه مسلم في صلاة المسافرين (796-242) من طرق عن يعقوب بن إبراهيم، حدثنا أبي، حدثنا يزيد بن الهاد، أن عبد الله بن خباب حدثه، أن أبا سعيد الخدري حدثه، أن أسيد بن حضير قال: فذكره.","grade":"صحيح","chapter_ar":"باب ما جاء في فضل أسيد بن حضير","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب فضائل الصحابة وأخبارهم","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Authentic: Narrated by Muslim (796, no. 242), and cited by al-Bukhārī in suspended form (5018).","chapter_en":"Reports Concerning the Virtue of Usayd ibn Ḥuḍayr","part_en":"The Book of the Virtues and Accounts of the Companions","group_ar":"مجموع فضائل أفراد الصحابة وأخبارهم","group_en":"A Collection of the Virtues and Reports of Individual Companions","part_no":49,"group_no":13,"chapter_no":10,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Usayd ibn Ḥuḍayr narrated: One night, while he was reciting in his threshing floor, his horse became agitated. He continued reciting, and it became agitated again. He recited once more, and the horse again moved restlessly. Usayd said: “I feared that it might trample Yaḥyā, so I went toward it. I then saw something resembling a canopy above my head, containing objects like lamps. It ascended into the sky until I could no longer see it.” The next morning, I went to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and said: “O Messenger of Allah, last night, in the middle of the night, while I was reciting in my threshing floor, my horse became agitated.” The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Continue reciting, O Ibn Ḥuḍayr.” I said: “I continued reciting, and it became agitated again.” He said: “Continue reciting, O Ibn Ḥuḍayr.” I said: “I recited again, and it became agitated once more.” He said: “Continue reciting, O Ibn Ḥuḍayr.” I said: “I then stopped, because Yaḥyā was close to the horse and I feared that it might trample him. I saw something resembling a canopy containing objects like lamps, which ascended into the sky until I could no longer see it.” The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Those were angels listening to your recitation. Had you continued reciting, the people would have seen them in the morning, and they would not have hidden themselves from them.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"voc":["fazail",298],"full":1,"dr":1,"rep":[11839],"tks":"صحيح: رواه مسلم (796/242)، وعلقه البخاري (5018)."},{"num":10101,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ كَعْبِ بْنِ مَالِكٍ قَالَ: كَانَ أسَيْدُ بْنُ حُضَيْرٍ حَسَنَ الصَّوْتِ بِالْقَرَآنِ، وَأنِهِ أتِي النَّبِيَّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ، فَقَالَ: بَيْنَا أنَا أقِرَا عَلَى ظَهْرِ بَيْتِي، وَالْمَرَأةُ فِي الْحُجْرَةِ، وَالْفَرَسُ مَرْبُوطٌ بِبَابِ الْحُجْرَةِ، إِذْ غَشَيْتَنِي مِثْلَ السَّحَابَةِ، فَخَشِيتُ أنَ يَبْقُرُ الْفَرَسَ فَتَفْزَعُ الْمَرَأةُ فَتَسْقُطُ، فَانْصَرَفَتْ، فَقِـالُ رَسُولِ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ: اقْرَا يَا أسَيدَ ذَلِكَ مَلَكٌ اسْتَمَعَ الْقَرَآنُ."],"takhrij":"صحيح: رواه البزار في مسنده (3209) والفريابي في فضائل القرآن (96) كلاهما من طرق عن الزهري، عن عبد الرحمن بن كعب بن مالك، عن أبيه فذكره.","grade":"صحيح","chapter_ar":"باب ما جاء في فضل أسيد بن حضير","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب فضائل الصحابة وأخبارهم","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Authentic: Narrated by al-Bazzār in his Musnad (3209), and al-Firyābī in Faḍāʾil al-Qurʾān (96).","chapter_en":"Reports Concerning the Virtue of Usayd ibn Ḥuḍayr","part_en":"The Book of the Virtues and Accounts of the Companions","group_ar":"مجموع فضائل أفراد الصحابة وأخبارهم","group_en":"A Collection of the Virtues and Reports of Individual Companions","part_no":49,"group_no":13,"chapter_no":10,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Kaʿb ibn Mālik narrated: Usayd ibn Ḥuḍayr had a beautiful voice when reciting the Qur’an. He came to the Prophet ﷺ and said: “While I was reciting on the roof of my house, with my wife inside the room and the horse tied at the room’s door, something resembling a cloud covered me. I feared that the horse might break loose, frightening my wife and causing her to fall, so I stopped reciting.” The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Continue reciting, O Usayd. That was an angel listening to the Qur’an.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"voc":["fazail",299],"full":1,"dr":1,"rep":[11843],"tks":"صحيح: رواه البزار في مسنده (3209)، والفريابي في فضائل القرآن (96)."},{"num":10102,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ أَنَسٍ رَضِيَ اللَّهُ عَنْهُ أَنَّ رَجُلَيْنِ، خَرَجَا مِنْ عِنْدِ النَّبِيِّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ فِي لَيْلَةٍ مُظْلِمَةٍ، وَإِذَا نُورٌ بَيْنَ أَيْدِيهِمَا حَتَّى تَفَرَّقَا، فَتَفَرَّقَ النُّورُ مَعَهُمَا."],"takhrij":"صحيح: رواه البخاري في مناقب الأنصار (3805) عن علي بن مسلم، حدثنا حبّان بن هلال، حدثنا همام، أخبرنا قتادة، عن أنس فذكره.","grade":"صحيح","chapter_ar":"باب ما جاء في فضل أسيد بن حضير","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب فضائل الصحابة وأخبارهم","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Authentic: Narrated by al-Bukhārī (3805).","chapter_en":"Reports Concerning the Virtue of Usayd ibn Ḥuḍayr","part_en":"The Book of the Virtues and Accounts of the Companions","group_ar":"مجموع فضائل أفراد الصحابة وأخبارهم","group_en":"A Collection of the Virtues and Reports of Individual Companions","part_no":49,"group_no":13,"chapter_no":10,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Anas narrated: Two men left the presence of the Prophet ﷺ on a dark night, and a light appeared before them. When they separated and each went his own way, the light also divided and accompanied each of them."]}},"tuhfa":{},"voc":["fazail",300],"full":1,"dr":1,"rep":[10040],"tks":"صحيح: رواه البخاري (3805)."},{"num":10103,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ أَنَسٍ، عَنْ أُمِّ سُلَيْمٍ، أَنَّهَا قَالَتْ: يَا رَسُولَ اللَّهِ، أَنَسٌ، خَادِمُكَ ادْعُ اللَّهَ لَهُ، قَالَ اللَّهُمَّ أَكْثِرْ مَالَهُ وَوَلَدَهُ، وَبَارِكْ لَهُ فِيمَا أَعْطَيْتَهُ."],"takhrij":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاري في الدعوات (6378، 6379) ومسلم في فضائل الصحابة (2480) كلاهما عن محمد بن بشار، ثنا غندر، ثنا شعبة، قال: سمعت قتادة، عن أنس، عن أم سليم فذكرته.وهذا لفظ مسلم، ولفظ البخاري نحوه.","grade":"متفق عليه","chapter_ar":"باب ما جاء في فضائل أنس","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب فضائل الصحابة وأخبارهم","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Agreed upon: Narrated by al-Bukhārī (6378, 6379) and Muslim (2480).","chapter_en":"Reports Concerning the Virtues of Anas","part_en":"The Book of the Virtues and Accounts of the Companions","group_ar":"مجموع فضائل أفراد الصحابة وأخبارهم","group_en":"A Collection of the Virtues and Reports of Individual Companions","part_no":49,"group_no":13,"chapter_no":11,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Anas narrated from Umm Sulaym that she said: “O Messenger of Allah, Anas is your servant, so supplicate to Allah for him.” The Prophet ﷺ said: “O Allah, increase his wealth and children, and bless him in what You have given him.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"voc":["fazail",301],"full":1,"rep":[10950],"tks":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (6378، 6379)، ومسلم (2480)."},{"num":10104,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ أَنَسٍ قَالَ:  دَخَلَ النَّبِيُّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ عَلَيْنَا، وَمَا هُوَ إِلَّا أَنَا وَأُمِّي وَأُمُّ حَرَامٍ خَالَتِي، فَقَالَتْ أُمِّي: يَا رَسُولَ اللَّهِ، خُوَيْدِمُكَ، ادْعُ اللَّهَ لَهُ! قَالَ: فَدَعَا لِي بِكُلِّ خَيْرٍ، وَكَانَ فِي آخِرِ مَا دَعَا لِي بِهِ أَنْ قَالَ: اللَّهُمَّ أَكْثِرْ مَالَهُ وَوَلَدَهُ، وَبَارِكْ لَهُ فِيهِ."],"takhrij":"صحيح: رواه مسلم في فضائل الصحابة (2481-142) عن زهير بن حرب، ثنا هاشم بن القاسم، ثنا سليمان، عن ثابت، عن أنس قال: فذكره.","grade":"صحيح","chapter_ar":"باب ما جاء في فضائل أنس","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب فضائل الصحابة وأخبارهم","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Authentic: Narrated by Muslim (2481, no. 142).","chapter_en":"Reports Concerning the Virtues of Anas","part_en":"The Book of the Virtues and Accounts of the Companions","group_ar":"مجموع فضائل أفراد الصحابة وأخبارهم","group_en":"A Collection of the Virtues and Reports of Individual Companions","part_no":49,"group_no":13,"chapter_no":11,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Anas narrated: The Prophet ﷺ entered upon us, and there was no one present except me, my mother, and my maternal aunt Umm Ḥarām. My mother said: “O Messenger of Allah, this is your little servant, so supplicate to Allah for him.” He supplicated for every form of goodness for me, and among the final things for which he supplicated was: “O Allah, increase his wealth and children, and bless him in them.”"]},"buhuth":{"en":["In another wording recorded by Muslim (2481, no. 143):","“My mother, Umm Anas, brought me to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. She had wrapped the lower half of her head covering around my waist and draped the other half over me. She said:","‘O Messenger of Allah, this is my little son Anas. I have brought him to you so that he may serve you.’”","The narration further states:","Anas said:","“By Allah, my wealth is abundant, and today my children and grandchildren number close to one hundred.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"voc":["fazail",302],"full":1,"dr":1,"tks":"صحيح: رواه مسلم (2481/142)."},{"num":10105,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عن أنس بْنِ مَالِكٍ قَالَ:  مَرَّ رَسُولُ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ، فَسَمِعَتْ أُمِّي أُمُّ سُلَيْمٍ صَوْتَهُ، فَقَالَتْ: بِأَبِي وَأُمِّي يَا رَسُولَ اللَّهِ، أُنَيْسٌ! فَدَعَا لِي رَسُولُ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ ثَلَاثَ دَعَوَاتٍ، قَدْ رَأَيْتُ مِنْهَا اثْنَتَيْنِ فِي الدُّنْيَا، وَأَنَا أَرْجُو الثَّالِثَةَ فِي الْآخِرَةِ."],"takhrij":"صحيح: رواه مسلم في فضائل الصحابة (2481-144) عن قتيبة بن سعيد، ثنا جعفر -يعني ابن سليمان-، عن الجعد أبي عثمان حدثنا أنس بن مالك فذكره.","grade":"صحيح","chapter_ar":"باب ما جاء في فضائل أنس","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب فضائل الصحابة وأخبارهم","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Authentic: Narrated by Muslim (2481, no. 144).","chapter_en":"Reports Concerning the Virtues of Anas","part_en":"The Book of the Virtues and Accounts of the Companions","group_ar":"مجموع فضائل أفراد الصحابة وأخبارهم","group_en":"A Collection of the Virtues and Reports of Individual Companions","part_no":49,"group_no":13,"chapter_no":11,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Anas ibn Mālik narrated: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ passed by, and my mother, Umm Sulaym, heard his voice. She said: “May my father and mother be sacrificed for you, O Messenger of Allah—here is little Anas.” The Messenger of Allah ﷺ then made three supplications for me. I have already seen two of them fulfilled in this world, and I hope for the third in the Hereafter."]}},"tuhfa":{},"voc":["fazail",303],"full":1,"tks":"صحيح: رواه مسلم (2481/144)."},{"num":10106,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ أَنَسٍ رَضِيَ اللَّهُ عَنْهُ دَخَلَ النَّبِيُّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ عَلَى أُمِّ سُلَيْمٍ، فَأَتَتْهُ بِتَمْرٍ وَسَمْنٍ، قَالَ: أَعِيدُوا سَمْنَكُمْ فِي سِقَائِهِ، وَتَمْرَكُمْ فِي وِعَائِهِ، فَإِنِّي صَائِمٌ. ثُمَّ قَامَ إِلَى نَاحِيَةٍ مِنَ الْبَيْتِ، فَصَلَّى غَيْرَ الْمَكْتُوبَةِ، فَدَعَا لأُمِّ سُلَيْمٍ، وَأَهْلِ بَيْتِهَا، فَقَالَتْ أُمُّ سُلَيْمٍ: يَا رَسُولَ اللَّهِ، إِنَّ لِي خُوَيْصَةً، قَالَ مَا هِيَ. قَالَتْ: خَادِمُكَ أَنَسٌ. فَمَا تَرَكَ خَيْرَ آخِرَةٍ وَلاَ دُنْيَا إِلاَّ دَعَا لِي بِهِ قَالَ اللَّهُمَّ ارْزُقْهُ مَالاً وَوَلَدًا، وَبَارِكْ لَهُ. فَإِنِّي لَمِنْ أَكْثَرِ الأَنْصَارِ مَالاً. وَحَدَّثَتْنِي ابْنَتِي أُمَيْنَةُ أَنَّهُ دُفِنَ لِصُلْبِي مَقْدَمَ حَجَّاجٍ الْبَصْرَةَ بِضْعٌ وَعِشْرُونَ وَمِائَةٌ."],"takhrij":"صحيح: رواه البخاري في الصوم (1982) عن محمد بن المثنى قال: ثني خالد هو ابن الحارث، ثنا حميد، عن أنس قال: فذكره.","grade":"صحيح","chapter_ar":"باب ما جاء في فضائل أنس","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب فضائل الصحابة وأخبارهم","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Authentic: Narrated by al-Bukhārī (1982).","chapter_en":"Reports Concerning the Virtues of Anas","part_en":"The Book of the Virtues and Accounts of the Companions","group_ar":"مجموع فضائل أفراد الصحابة وأخبارهم","group_en":"A Collection of the Virtues and Reports of Individual Companions","part_no":49,"group_no":13,"chapter_no":11,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Anas narrated: The Prophet ﷺ entered upon Umm Sulaym, and she brought him dates and clarified butter. He said: “Return your clarified butter to its waterskin and your dates to their container, for I am fasting.” He then stood in a corner of the house and performed a voluntary prayer. Afterward, he supplicated for Umm Sulaym and the members of her household. Umm Sulaym said: “O Messenger of Allah, I have a special request.” He asked: “What is it?” She replied: “Your servant Anas.” He did not leave any good of this world or the Hereafter without supplicating for me concerning it. Among his supplications was: “O Allah, grant him wealth and children, and bless him in them.” I became one of the wealthiest men among the Anṣār. My daughter Umaynah informed me that, by the time al-Ḥajjāj arrived in Baṣrah, more than one hundred and twenty of my direct descendants had been buried."]}},"tuhfa":{},"voc":["fazail",304],"full":1,"dr":1,"rep":[4418],"tks":"صحيح: رواه البخاري (1982)."},{"num":10107,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ أَنَسِ بْنِ مَالِكٍ قَالَ:  قَالَ لِي رَسُولُ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ: يَا بُنَيَّ."],"takhrij":"صحيح: رواه مسلم في الآداب (2151) عن محمد بن عبيد الغبري، ثنا أبو عوانة، عن أبي عثمان، عن أنس بن مالك قال: فذكره.","grade":"صحيح","chapter_ar":"باب ما جاء في فضائل أنس","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب فضائل الصحابة وأخبارهم","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Authentic: Narrated by Muslim (2151).","chapter_en":"Reports Concerning the Virtues of Anas","part_en":"The Book of the Virtues and Accounts of the Companions","group_ar":"مجموع فضائل أفراد الصحابة وأخبارهم","group_en":"A Collection of the Virtues and Reports of Individual Companions","part_no":49,"group_no":13,"chapter_no":11,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Anas ibn Mālik narrated: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to me: “My dear son.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"full":1,"rep":[13034,14546],"tks":"صحيح: رواه مسلم (2151)."},{"num":10108,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ أَنَسٍ رَضِيَ اللَّهُ عَنْهُ قَالَ: لَمْ يَبْقَ مِمَّنْ صَلَّى الْقِبْلَتَيْنِ غَيْرِي."],"takhrij":"صحيح: رواه البخاري في التفسير (4489) عن علي بن عبد الله، ثنا معتمر، عن أبيه، عن أنس قال: فذكره.","grade":"صحيح","chapter_ar":"باب من أخبار أنس بن مالك","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب فضائل الصحابة وأخبارهم","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Authentic: Narrated by al-Bukhārī (4489).","chapter_en":"Reports Concerning Anas ibn Mālik","part_en":"The Book of the Virtues and Accounts of the Companions","group_ar":"مجموع فضائل أفراد الصحابة وأخبارهم","group_en":"A Collection of the Virtues and Reports of Individual Companions","part_no":49,"group_no":13,"chapter_no":12,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Anas narrated: “No one remains among those who prayed toward both qiblahs except me.”"]},"buhuth":{"en":["Anas (may Allah be pleased with him) died in the year 92 AH, though it has also been said that he died in 93 AH. He had lived beyond one hundred years of age."]}},"tuhfa":{},"voc":["fazail",306],"full":1,"dr":1,"tks":"صحيح: رواه البخاري (4489). وتوفي أنس رضي الله عنه سنة اثنتين، وقيل: ثلاث وتسعين، وقد جاوز المائة."},{"num":10109,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عن أنس بْنِ مَالِكٍ أَسَرَّ إِلَىَّ النَّبِيُّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ سِرًّا، فَمَا أَخْبَرْتُ بِهِ أَحَدًا بَعْدَهُ، وَلَقَدْ سَأَلَتْنِي أُمُّ سُلَيْمٍ فَمَا أَخْبَرْتُهَا بِهِ."],"takhrij":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاري في الاستئذان (6289)، ومسلم في فضائل الصحابة (2482-146) كلاهما من طريق معتمر بن سليمان قال: سمعت أبي قال: سمعت أنس بن مالك قال: فذكره.وهذا لفظ البخاري ولفظ مسلم نحوه.","grade":"متفق عليه","chapter_ar":"باب كان أنس بن مالك موضع أسرار النبي ﷺ","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب فضائل الصحابة وأخبارهم","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Authentic: Narrated by al-Bukhārī (6289) and Muslim (2482, no. 146).","chapter_en":"Anas ibn Mālik Was Entrusted with the Secrets of the Prophet ﷺ","part_en":"The Book of the Virtues and Accounts of the Companions","group_ar":"مجموع فضائل أفراد الصحابة وأخبارهم","group_en":"A Collection of the Virtues and Reports of Individual Companions","part_no":49,"group_no":13,"chapter_no":13,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Anas narrated: The Prophet ﷺ entrusted me with a secret, and I never disclosed it to anyone after him. Even when Umm Sulaym asked me about it, I did not tell her."]},"buhuth":{"en":["In another wording recorded by Muslim:","“The Messenger of Allah ﷺ came upon me while I was playing with some boys. He greeted us and then sent me on an errand.","I was delayed in returning to my mother. When I arrived, she asked:","‘What delayed you?’","I replied:","‘The Messenger of Allah ﷺ sent me on an errand.’","She asked:","‘What was his errand?’","I replied:","‘It is a secret.’","She said:","‘Never disclose the secret of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ to anyone.’”","Anas then said:","“By Allah, had I ever disclosed it to anyone, I would have disclosed it to you, O Thābit.”","Among the reports concerning Anas is that which al-Tirmidhī narrated through his chain from Abū Khaldah, who said:","I asked Abū al-ʿĀliyah:","“Did Anas hear directly from the Prophet ﷺ?”","He replied:","“He served him for ten years, and the Prophet ﷺ supplicated for him. He had an orchard that produced fruit twice each year, and it contained sweet basil from which the fragrance of musk could be smelled.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"voc":["fazail",307],"full":1,"dr":1,"rep":[14606],"tks":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (6289)، ومسلم (2482/146)."},{"num":10110,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عن سهل بن الحنظلية أن رسول الله صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ قال يوم حنين في –– سياق طويل-: مَنْ يَحْرُسُنَا اللَّيْلَةَ؟ قَالَ أَنَسُ بْنُ أَبِي مَرْثَدٍ الْغَنَوِيُّ: أَنَا يَا رَسُولَ اللهِ، وفيه أن رسول الله صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ قال له: قَدْ أَوْجَبْتَ، فَلَا عَلَيْكَ أَنْ لَا تَعْمَلَ بَعْدَهَا."],"takhrij":"صحيح: رواه أبو داود (2501)، والنسائي في الكبرى (8819)، والحاكم (2433)، والبيهقي (18443) كلهم من طريق أبي توبة، حدثنا معاوية بن سلام، عن زيد بن سلام، أنه سمع أبا سلام قال: حدثني السلولي أبو كبشة، أنه حدثه سهل بن الحنظلية فذكره.","grade":"صحيح","chapter_ar":"باب فضل أنس بن مرثد الغنوي","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب فضائل الصحابة وأخبارهم","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Authentic: Narrated by Abū Dāwūd (2501), al-Nasā’ī in al-Sunan al-Kubrā (8819), al-Ḥākim (2433), and al-Bayhaqī (9/149).","chapter_en":"The Virtue of Anas ibn Abī Marthad al-Ghanawī","part_en":"The Book of the Virtues and Accounts of the Companions","group_ar":"مجموع فضائل أفراد الصحابة وأخبارهم","group_en":"A Collection of the Virtues and Reports of Individual Companions","part_no":49,"group_no":13,"chapter_no":14,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Sahl ibn al-Ḥanẓaliyyah narrated that, during a lengthy report concerning the day of Ḥunayn, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ asked: “Who will guard us tonight?” Anas ibn Abī Marthad al-Ghanawī replied: “I will, O Messenger of Allah.” The narration states that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ later said to him: “You have made Paradise obligatory for yourself, so there will be no blame upon you even if you perform no deed after this.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"voc":["fazail",308],"full":1,"dr":1,"tks":"صحيح: رواه أبو داود (2501)، والنسائي في الكبرى (8819)، والحاكم (2433)، والبيهقي (18443)."},{"num":10111,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ أنس بْنِ مَالِكٍ أَنَّ الرُّبيّع وهي ابْنَةُ النَّضْرِ كَسَرَتْ ثَنِيَّةَ جَارِيَةٍ، فَطَلَبُوا الأَرْشَ، وَطَلَبُوا الْعَفْوَ، فَأَبَوْا، فَأَتَوُا النَّبِيَّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ، ، فَأَمَرَهُمْ بِالْقِصَاصِ، فَقَالَ أَنَسُ بْنُ النَّضْرِ: أَتُكْسَرُ ثَنِيَّةُ الرُّبَيِّعِ يَا رَسُولَ اللَّهِ؟ لاَ وَالَّذِي بَعَثَكَ بِالْحَقِّ لاَ تُكْسَرُ ثَنِيَّتُهَا.فَقَالَ: يَا أَنَسُ، كِتَابُ اللَّهِ الْقِصَاصُ، فَرَضِيَ الْقَوْمُ وَعَفَوْا، فَقَالَ النَّبِيُّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ: إِنَّ مِنْ عِبَادِ اللَّهِ مَنْ لَوْ أَقْسَمَ عَلَى اللَّهِ لأَبَرَّهُ."],"takhrij":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاري في الصلح (2703) عن محمد بن عبد الله الأنصاري، قال: حدثني حميد أن أنسا حدثهم فذكره.","grade":"متفق عليه","chapter_ar":"باب فضل أنس بن النضر","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب فضائل الصحابة وأخبارهم","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Agreed upon: Narrated by al-Bukhārī (2703) and Muslim (1675).","chapter_en":"The Virtue of Anas ibn al-Naḍr","part_en":"The Book of the Virtues and Accounts of the Companions","group_ar":"مجموع فضائل أفراد الصحابة وأخبارهم","group_en":"A Collection of the Virtues and Reports of Individual Companions","part_no":49,"group_no":13,"chapter_no":15,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Anas narrated: Al-Rubayyiʿ, the daughter of al-Naḍr, broke the front tooth of a young woman. Her family requested monetary compensation and asked the injured party to pardon her, but they refused. They brought the matter before the Prophet ﷺ, and he ordered legal retaliation. Anas ibn al-Naḍr said: “O Messenger of Allah, will the front tooth of al-Rubayyiʿ be broken? No, by the One who sent you with the truth, her tooth will not be broken.” The Prophet ﷺ said: “O Anas, the ruling in the Book of Allah is legal retaliation.” The injured party then became satisfied and granted pardon. The Prophet ﷺ said: “Among the servants of Allah are those who, were they to swear by Allah that something would happen, Allah would fulfill their oath.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"voc":["fazail",309],"full":1,"dr":1,"tks":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (2703)، ومسلم (1675)."},{"num":10112,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ أَنَسِ بْنِ مَالِكٍ، قَالَ: قَالَ رَسُولُ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ: كَمْ مِنْ أَشْعَثَ أَغْبَرَ ذِي طِمْرَيْنِ لاَ يُؤْبَهُ لَهُ لَوْ أَقْسَمَ عَلَى اللَّهِ لأَبَرَّهُ، مِنْهُمُ الْبَرَاءُ بْنُ مَالِكٍ."],"takhrij":"حسن: رواه الترمذي (3854) عن عبد الله بن أبي زياد، حدثنا سيار، حدثنا جعفر بن سليمان، حدثنا ثابت وعلي بن زيد، عن أنس بن مالك فذكره.","grade":"حسن","chapter_ar":"باب فضل البراء بن مالك","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب فضائل الصحابة وأخبارهم","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Hasan: Narrated by al-Tirmidhī (3854).","chapter_en":"The Virtue of al-Barāʾ ibn Mālik","part_en":"The Book of the Virtues and Accounts of the Companions","group_ar":"مجموع فضائل أفراد الصحابة وأخبارهم","group_en":"A Collection of the Virtues and Reports of Individual Companions","part_no":49,"group_no":13,"chapter_no":16,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Anas narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “How many a person there is whose hair is disheveled, who is covered with dust, and who wears two worn-out garments, to whom people pay no attention, yet if he were to swear by Allah, Allah would fulfill his oath. Among them is al-Barāʾ ibn Mālik.”"]},"buhuth":{"en":["The word “الأشعث” refers to someone whose hair is disheveled and unkempt.","The phrase “ذي طمرين” means someone wearing two worn-out garments.","The phrase “لا يؤبه له” means that people neither pay attention to him nor accord him any importance."]}},"tuhfa":{},"voc":["fazail",310],"full":1,"dr":1,"tks":"حسن: رواه الترمذي (3854)."},{"num":10113,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عن بشر بن عقربة قال: اسْتُشْهِدَ أَبِي مَعَ النَّبِيِّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ في بَعْضِ غَزَوَاتِهِ، فَمَرَّ بِيَ النَّبِيُّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ، وَأَنَا أَبْكِي، فَقَالَ لِي: اسْكُتْ، أَمَا تَرْضَى أَنْ أَكونَ أَنَا أَبُوكَ، وَعَائِشَةُ أُمّكَ؟ قُلْتُ: بَلَى بِأَبِي أَنْتَ وَأُمِّي يَا رَسُولَ اللهِ."],"takhrij":"حسن: رواه البخاري في التاريخ الكبير (2/78)، -ومن طريقه البيهقي في الشعب (10533)- عن عبد الله بن عثمان بن عطاء، حدثنا حجر بن الحارث الغساني، قال: سمعت عبد الله بن عوف القاري قال: سمعت بشر بن عقربة يقول: فذكره.","grade":"حسن","chapter_ar":"باب ما جاء في بشر بن عقربة","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب فضائل الصحابة وأخبارهم","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Hasan: Narrated by al-Bukhārī in al-Tārīkh al-Kabīr (2/78), and through his route by al-Bayhaqī in Shuʿab al-Īmān (10533).","chapter_en":"Reports Concerning Bishr ibn ʿAqrabah","part_en":"The Book of the Virtues and Accounts of the Companions","group_ar":"مجموع فضائل أفراد الصحابة وأخبارهم","group_en":"A Collection of the Virtues and Reports of Individual Companions","part_no":49,"group_no":13,"chapter_no":17,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Bishr ibn ʿAqrabah narrated: My father was martyred alongside the Prophet ﷺ in one of his military expeditions. The Prophet ﷺ passed by me while I was crying and said: “Do not cry. Would you not be pleased for me to be your father and ʿĀ’ishah to be your mother?” I replied: “Yes indeed. May my father and mother be sacrificed for you, O Messenger of Allah.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"voc":["fazail",311],"full":1,"dr":1,"tks":"حسن: رواه البخاري في التاريخ الكبير (2/78)، ومن طريقه البيهقي في الشعب (10533)."},{"num":10114,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ أَبِي هُرَيْرَةَ رَضِيَ اللَّهُ عَنْهُ أَنَّ النَّبِيَّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ قَالَ لِبِلاَلٍ عِنْدَ صَلاَةِ الْفَجْرِ: يَا بِلاَلُ، حَدِّثْنِي بِأَرْجَى عَمَلٍ عَمِلْتَهُ فِي الإِسْلاَمِ، فَإِنِّي سَمِعْتُ دَفَّ نَعْلَيْكَ بَيْنَ يَدَىَّ فِي الْجَنَّةِ. قَالَ مَا عَمِلْتُ عَمَلاً أَرْجَى عِنْدِي أَنِّي لَمْ أَتَطَهَّرْ طُهُورًا فِي سَاعَةِ لَيْلٍ أَوْ نَهَارٍ إِلاَّ صَلَّيْتُ بِذَلِكَ الطُّهُورِ مَا كُتِبَ لِي أَنْ أُصَلِّيَ.","قَالَ أَبُو عَبْدِ اللهِ: دَفَّ نَعْلَيْكَ: يَعْنِي تَحْرِيكَ."],"takhrij":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاري في التهجد (1149)، ومسلم في فضائل الصحابة (2458) كلاهما من طريق أبي حيان التيمي يحيى بن سعيد، عن أبي زرعة، عن أبي هريرة فذكره.","grade":"متفق عليه","chapter_ar":"باب ما جاء في فضل بلال بن رباح","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب فضائل الصحابة وأخبارهم","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Agreed upon: Narrated by al-Bukhārī (1149) and Muslim (2458).","chapter_en":"Reports Concerning the Virtue of Bilāl ibn Rabāḥ","part_en":"The Book of the Virtues and Accounts of the Companions","group_ar":"مجموع فضائل أفراد الصحابة وأخبارهم","group_en":"A Collection of the Virtues and Reports of Individual Companions","part_no":49,"group_no":13,"chapter_no":18,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Abū Hurayrah narrated that, at the time of the dawn prayer, the Prophet ﷺ said to Bilāl: “O Bilāl, tell me about the deed you have performed in Islam for which you have the greatest hope, for I heard the sound of your sandals ahead of me in Paradise.” Bilāl replied: “I have not performed any deed for which I have greater hope than this: whenever I performed ablution at any hour of the night or day, I prayed with that ablution as much as had been decreed for me to pray.” Abū ʿAbdullāh said: The phrase “the sound of your sandals” means the sound of their movement."]},"intro":{"ar":["هو مؤذن رسول الله ﷺ، عُذِّب في الله وهو صابر يقول: أحد، أحد. اشتراه أبو بكر وأعتقه. كان آدم شديد الأدمة، نحيفًا طوالًا، خفيف العارضين.","وبعد وفاة رسول الله ﷺ خرج إلى الشام، ومات بها سنة عشرين بدمشق.","ورُوي أنه لم يؤذن لأحد بعد رسول الله ﷺ، وأراد الجهاد، فأراد أبو بكر منعه، فقال: إن كنت أعتقتني لله فخل سبيلي. فكان بالشام حتى قدم عمر الجابية، فسأل المسلمون عمر أن يسأل لهم بلالًا أن يؤذن لهم، فسأله، فأذن يومًا، فلم يُر يوم كان أكثر باكيًا من يومئذ، ذكرًا منهم للنبي ﷺ."],"en":["He was the caller to prayer of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. He was tortured for the sake of Allah, yet remained patient, repeatedly saying:","“Allah is One! Allah is One!”","Abū Bakr purchased him and set him free.","He was dark-skinned, very deeply complexioned, slender and tall, with sparse hair upon his cheeks.","After the death of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, he departed for al-Shām and died in Damascus in the year 20 AH.","It has been reported that he did not call the adhān for anyone after the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. He wished to participate in military campaigns, but Abū Bakr wanted to prevent him from leaving.","Bilāl said:","“If you freed me for the sake of Allah, then allow me to go.”","He remained in al-Shām until ʿUmar came to al-Jābiyah. The Muslims asked ʿUmar to request Bilāl to call the adhān for them. ʿUmar asked him, and Bilāl called the adhān on that day.","No day was seen in which more people wept than that day, because the adhān reminded them of the Prophet ﷺ."]}},"tuhfa":{},"voc":["fazail",312],"full":1,"tks":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (1149)، ومسلم (2458)."},{"num":10115,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ جَابِرِ بْنِ عَبْدِ اللَّهِ أَنَّ رَسُولَ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ قَالَ:  أُرِيتُ الْجَنَّةَ، فَرَأَيْتُ امْرَأَةَ أَبِي طَلْحَةَ، ثُمَّ سَمِعْتُ خَشْخَشَةً أَمَامِي، فَإِذَا بِلَالٌ."],"takhrij":"صحيح: رواه مسلم في فضائل الصحابة (2457) عن أبي جعفر محمد بن الفرج، ثنا زيد بن الحباب، أخبرني عبد العزيز بن أبي سلمة، أنا محمد بن المنكدر، عن جابر فذكره.","grade":"صحيح","chapter_ar":"باب ما جاء في فضل بلال بن رباح","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب فضائل الصحابة وأخبارهم","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Authentic: Narrated by Muslim (2457).","chapter_en":"Reports Concerning the Virtue of Bilāl ibn Rabāḥ","part_en":"The Book of the Virtues and Accounts of the Companions","group_ar":"مجموع فضائل أفراد الصحابة وأخبارهم","group_en":"A Collection of the Virtues and Reports of Individual Companions","part_no":49,"group_no":13,"chapter_no":18,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Jābir ibn ʿAbdullāh narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “I was shown Paradise, and I saw the wife of Abū Ṭalḥah. Then I heard the sound of footsteps before me, and it was Bilāl.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"voc":["fazail",313],"full":1,"rep":[10447],"tks":"صحيح: رواه مسلم (2457)."},{"num":10116,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عن جابر بْنِ عَبْدِ اللَّهِ رَضِيَ اللَّهُ عَنْهُمَا قَالَ: كَانَ عُمَرُ يَقُولُ: أَبُو بَكْرٍ سَيِّدُنَا، وَأَعْتَقَ سَيِّدَنَا. يَعْنِي بِلاَلاً."],"takhrij":"صحيح: رواه البخاري في فضائل الصحابة (3754) عن أبي نعيم، ثنا عبدالعزيز بن أبي سلمة، عن محمد بن المنكدر، أنا جابر بن عبد الله قال: فذكره.","grade":"صحيح","chapter_ar":"باب ما جاء في أخبار بلال بن رباح","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب فضائل الصحابة وأخبارهم","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Authentic: Narrated by al-Bukhārī (3754).","chapter_en":"Reports Concerning Bilāl ibn Rabāḥ","part_en":"The Book of the Virtues and Accounts of the Companions","group_ar":"مجموع فضائل أفراد الصحابة وأخبارهم","group_en":"A Collection of the Virtues and Reports of Individual Companions","part_no":49,"group_no":13,"chapter_no":19,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Jābir ibn ʿAbdullāh narrated: ʿUmar used to say: “Abū Bakr is our master, and he set our master free,” meaning Bilāl."]}},"tuhfa":{},"voc":["fazail",314],"full":1,"tks":"صحيح: رواه البخاري (3754)."},{"num":10117,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ قَيْسٍ، أَنَّ بِلاَلاً، قَالَ لأَبِي بَكْرٍ: إِنْ كُنْتَ إِنَّمَا اشْتَرَيْتَنِي لِنَفْسِكَ فَأَمْسِكْنِي، وَإِنْ كُنْتَ إِنَّمَا اشْتَرَيْتَنِي لِلَّهِ فَدَعْنِي وَعَمَلَ اللَّهِ."],"takhrij":"صحيح: رواه البخاري في فضائل الصحابة (3755) عن ابن نمير، عن محمد بن عبيد، ثنا إسماعيل، عن قيس فذكره.","grade":"صحيح","chapter_ar":"باب ما جاء في أخبار بلال بن رباح","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب فضائل الصحابة وأخبارهم","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Authentic: Narrated by al-Bukhārī (3755).","chapter_en":"Reports Concerning Bilāl ibn Rabāḥ","part_en":"The Book of the Virtues and Accounts of the Companions","group_ar":"مجموع فضائل أفراد الصحابة وأخبارهم","group_en":"A Collection of the Virtues and Reports of Individual Companions","part_no":49,"group_no":13,"chapter_no":19,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Qays narrated that Bilāl said to Abū Bakr: “If you purchased me only for yourself, then keep me with you. But if you purchased me for the sake of Allah, then leave me to perform deeds for Allah.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"voc":["fazail",315],"full":1,"tks":"صحيح: رواه البخاري (3755)."},{"num":10118,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ أَنَسِ بْنِ مَالِكٍ رَضِيَ اللَّهُ عَنْهُ أَنَّ النَّبِيَّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ افْتَقَدَ ثَابِتَ بْنَ قَيْسٍ، فَقَالَ رَجُلٌ: يَا رَسُولَ اللَّهِ، أَنَا أَعْلَمُ لَكَ عِلْمَهُ. فَأَتَاهُ فَوَجَدَهُ جَالِسًا فِي بَيْتِهِ، مُنَكِّسًا رَأْسَهُ، فَقَالَ: مَا شَأْنُكَ؟ فَقَالَ: شَرٌّ، كَانَ يَرْفَعُ صَوْتَهُ فَوْقَ صَوْتِ النَّبِيِّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ فَقَدْ حَبِطَ عَمَلُهُ، وَهْوَ مِنْ أَهْلِ النَّارِ. فَأَتَى الرَّجُلُ فَأَخْبَرَهُ أَنَّهُ قَالَ كَذَا وَكَذَا. فَقَالَ مُوسَى بْنُ أَنَسٍ: فَرَجَعَ الْمَرَّةَ الآخِرَةَ بِبِشَارَةٍ عَظِيمَةٍ، فَقَالَ: اذْهَبْ إِلَيْهِ، فَقُلْ لَهُ: إِنَّكَ لَسْتَ مِنْ أَهْلِ النَّارِ، وَلَكِنْ مِنْ أَهْلِ الْجَنَّةِ."],"takhrij":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاري في المناقب (3613) وفي التفسير bukhari(4846) عن علي بن عبد الله، حدثنا أزهر بن سعد، أخبرنا ابن عون، قال: أنبأني موسى بن أنس، عن أنس بن مالك فذكره.","grade":"متفق عليه","chapter_ar":"باب أن ثابت بن قيس من أهل الجنة","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب فضائل الصحابة وأخبارهم","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Agreed upon: Narrated by al-Bukhārī (3613, 4846) and Muslim (119).","chapter_en":"Thābit ibn Qays Is Among the People of Paradise","part_en":"The Book of the Virtues and Accounts of the Companions","group_ar":"مجموع فضائل أفراد الصحابة وأخبارهم","group_en":"A Collection of the Virtues and Reports of Individual Companions","part_no":49,"group_no":13,"chapter_no":20,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Anas ibn Mālik narrated: The Prophet ﷺ noticed that Thābit ibn Qays was absent. A man said: “O Messenger of Allah, I will find out what has happened to him.” He went to Thābit and found him sitting in his house with his head lowered. He asked: “What is the matter with you?” Thābit replied: “It is terrible. I used to raise my voice above the voice of the Prophet ﷺ. My deeds have therefore become worthless, and I am among the people of the Fire.” The man returned and informed the Prophet ﷺ of what Thābit had said. Mūsā ibn Anas said: The man returned to Thābit a second time bearing tremendous good news. The Prophet ﷺ said: “Go to him and tell him: You are not among the people of the Fire. Rather, you are among the people of Paradise.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"voc":["fazail",316],"full":1,"dr":1,"rep":[791],"tks":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (3613، 4846)، ومسلم (119)."},{"num":10119,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ أَنَسِ بْنِ مَالِكٍ، قَالَ: لَمَّا نَزَلَتْ: ﴿يَا أَيُّهَا الَّذِينَ آمَنُوا لَا تَرْفَعُوا أَصْوَاتَكُمْ فَوْقَ صَوْتِ النَّبِيِّ﴾ [الحجرات: ٢]- إِلَى قَوْلِهِ: - ﴿لَا تَشْعُرُونَ﴾ [الحجرات: ٢] قَالَ ثَابِتُ بْنُ قَيْسٍ: أَنَا وَاللَّهِ الَّذِي كُنْتُ أَرْفَعُ صَوْتِي عِنْدَ رَسُولِ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ، ، وَإِنِّي أَخْشَى أَنْ أَكُونَ مِنْ أَهْلِ النَّارِ، إِنِّي كُنْتُ أَرْفَعُ صَوْتِي عِنْدَ النَّبِيِّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ: ، فَقَالَ رَسُولُ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ : بَلْ هُوَ مِنْ أَهْلِ الْجَنَّةِ، أَوْ كَمَا قَالَ."],"takhrij":"صحيح: رواه مسلم في الإيمان (119/188) عن هريم بن عبدالأعلى الأسدي، حدثنا المعتمر بن سليمان، قال: سمعت أبي يذكر عن ثابت، عن أنس فذكره.","grade":"صحيح","chapter_ar":"باب أن ثابت بن قيس من أهل الجنة","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب فضائل الصحابة وأخبارهم","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Authentic: Narrated by Muslim (119, no. 188).","chapter_en":"Thābit ibn Qays Is Among the People of Paradise","part_en":"The Book of the Virtues and Accounts of the Companions","group_ar":"مجموع فضائل أفراد الصحابة وأخبارهم","group_en":"A Collection of the Virtues and Reports of Individual Companions","part_no":49,"group_no":13,"chapter_no":20,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Anas ibn Mālik narrated: When the following verse was revealed: “O you who believe, do not raise your voices above the voice of the Prophet…” continuing to His saying: “…while you are unaware.” (Qur’an 49:2) Thābit ibn Qays said: “By Allah, I am the one who used to raise my voice in the presence of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and I fear that I am among the people of the Fire.” The Prophet ﷺ said: “Rather, he is among the people of Paradise.” Anas said: “We thereafter saw him walking among us as a man from the people of Paradise,” or words to that effect."]}},"tuhfa":{},"full":1,"dr":1,"tks":"صحيح: رواه مسلم (119/188)."},{"num":10120,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ أنس بْنِ مَالِكٍ قَالَ: كُنَّا نَرَاهُ –أي ثابت بن قَيْسِ- يَمْشِي بَيْنَ أَظْهُرِنَا وَنَحْنُ نَعْلَمُ أَنَّهُ مِنْ أَهْلِ الْجَنَّةِ، فَلَمَّا كَانَ يَوْمُ الْيَمَامَةِ كَانَ فِينَا بَعْضُ الِانْكِشَافِ، فَجَاءَ ثَابِتُ بْنُ قَيْسِ بْنِ شَمَّاسٍ، وَقَدْ تحنَّطَ وَلَبِسَ كَفَنَهُ، فَقَالَ: بِئْسَمَا تُعَوِّدُوْنَ أَقْرَانَكُمْ، فَقَاتَلَهُمْ حَتَّى قُتِلَ."],"takhrij":"صحيح: رواه أحمد (12399)، وصحّحه ابن حبان (7168) كلاهما من حديث سليمان، عن ثابت، عن أنس بن مالك فذكره.","grade":"صحيح","chapter_ar":"باب أن ثابت بن قيس من أهل الجنة","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب فضائل الصحابة وأخبارهم","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Authentic: Narrated by Aḥmad (12399) and authenticated by Ibn Ḥibbān (7168).","chapter_en":"Thābit ibn Qays Is Among the People of Paradise","part_en":"The Book of the Virtues and Accounts of the Companions","group_ar":"مجموع فضائل أفراد الصحابة وأخبارهم","group_en":"A Collection of the Virtues and Reports of Individual Companions","part_no":49,"group_no":13,"chapter_no":20,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Anas ibn Mālik narrated: We used to see him—meaning Thābit ibn Qays—walking among us while we knew that he was one of the people of Paradise. On the day of al-Yamāmah, some of our ranks began to fall back. Thābit ibn Qays ibn Shammās came forward after applying embalming perfume to himself and putting on his burial shroud. He said: “What an evil habit you are teaching your opponents!” He then fought them until he was killed."]},"buhuth":{"en":["Al-Bukhārī also recorded it in The Book of Jihād and Military Expeditions (2845), through Mūsā ibn Anas, who said:","He mentioned the day of al-Yamāmah and said:","Anas came to Thābit ibn Qays while Thābit had uncovered his thighs and was applying embalming perfume to himself.","Anas asked:","“O uncle, what is preventing you from coming forward?”","He replied:","“I am coming now, my nephew.”","He continued applying the embalming perfume used for the dead, then came and sat down.","The narration mentioned that some of the people had retreated. Thābit said:","“Move away from before us so that we may fight the enemy. This is not how we used to behave with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. What an evil habit you have taught your opponents!”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"voc":["fazail",318],"full":1,"dr":1,"tks":"صحيح: رواه أحمد (12399)، وصححه ابن حبان (7168)."},{"num":10121,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عن ثَوْبَانَ مَوْلَى رَسُولِ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ قَالَ: قَالَ رَسُولُ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ: مَنْ تَكَفَّلَ لِي أَنْ لاَ يَسْأَلَ النَّاسَ شَيْئًا وَأَتَكَفَّلَ لَهُ بِالْجَنَّةِ. فَقَالَ ثَوْبَانُ أَنَا. فَكَانَ لاَ يَسْأَلُ أَحَدًا شَيْئًا."],"takhrij":"صحيح: رواه أبو داود (1643) عن عبيد الله بن معاذ، حدثنا أبي (هو معاذ بن معاذ العنبري)، حدثنا شعبة، عن عاصم (الأحول)، عن أبي العالية، عن ثوبان فذكره.","grade":"صحيح","chapter_ar":"باب أخبار ثوبان مولى رسول الله ﷺ","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب فضائل الصحابة وأخبارهم","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Authentic: Narrated by Abū Dāwūd (1643), al-Nasā’ī (2590), Ibn Mājah (1837), and Aḥmad (22385).","chapter_en":"Reports Concerning Thawbān, the Freedman of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ","part_en":"The Book of the Virtues and Accounts of the Companions","group_ar":"مجموع فضائل أفراد الصحابة وأخبارهم","group_en":"A Collection of the Virtues and Reports of Individual Companions","part_no":49,"group_no":13,"chapter_no":21,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Thawbān, the freedman of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Who will guarantee for me that he will not ask people for anything, and I will guarantee Paradise for him?” Thawbān replied: “I will.” Thereafter, he would never ask anyone for anything."]},"intro":{"ar":["هو ثوبان مولى النبي ﷺ، صحابي مشهور، اشتراه رسول الله ﷺ وأعتقه، فخدمه إلى أن توفي رسول الله ﷺ، ثم تحول إلى الرملة، ثم حمص، ومات بها سنة أربع وخمسين."],"en":["He was Thawbān, the freedman of the Prophet ﷺ and a well-known Companion.","The Messenger of Allah ﷺ purchased him and set him free. Thawbān continued serving him until the Messenger of Allah ﷺ passed away.","He then moved to al-Ramlah, and afterward to Ḥimṣ, where he died in the year 54 AH."]}},"tuhfa":{},"voc":["fazail",319],"full":1,"dr":1,"tks":"صحيح: رواه أبو داود (1643)، والنسائي (2590)، وابن ماجه (1837)، وأحمد (22385)."},{"num":10122,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عن جابر بْنِ سَمُرَةَ: أَنَّ رَسُولَ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ  كَانَ يَخْطُبُ قَائِمًا. ثُمَّ يَجْلِسُ. ثُمَّ يَقُومُ فَيَخْطُبُ قَائِمًا. فَمَنْ نَبَّأَكَ أَنَّهُ كَانَ يَخْطُبُ جَالِسًا فَقَدْ كَذَبَ. فَقَدْ، وَاللهِ! صَلَّيْتُ مَعَهُ أَكْثَرَ مِنْ أَلْفَيْ صَلَاةٍ."],"takhrij":"صحيح: رواه مسلم في الجمعة (35:862) عن يحيى بن يحيى، أخبرنا أبو خيثمة، عن سماك قال: أنبأني جابر بن سمرة فذكره.","grade":"صحيح","chapter_ar":"باب ما جاء في أخبار جابر بن سمرة","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب فضائل الصحابة وأخبارهم","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Authentic: Narrated by Muslim (862, no. 35).","chapter_en":"Reports Concerning Jābir ibn Samurah","part_en":"The Book of the Virtues and Accounts of the Companions","group_ar":"مجموع فضائل أفراد الصحابة وأخبارهم","group_en":"A Collection of the Virtues and Reports of Individual Companions","part_no":49,"group_no":13,"chapter_no":22,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Jābir ibn Samurah narrated: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ would deliver the sermon while standing, then sit, and then stand again to deliver the sermon. Whoever tells you that he used to deliver the sermon while seated has lied. By Allah, I prayed with him more than two thousand times."]},"intro":{"ar":["هو جابر بن سمرة بن جنادة بن جندب السوائي، نزل الكوفة وابتنى بها دارًا، وتوفي سنة أربع وسبعين، وصلى عليه عمرو بن حريث."],"en":["He was Jābir ibn Samurah ibn Junādah ibn Jundub al-Suwāʾī. He settled in Kūfah and built a house there. He died in the year 74 AH, and ʿAmr ibn Ḥurayth led his funeral prayer."]}},"tuhfa":{},"voc":["fazail",320],"full":1,"rep":[3284],"tks":"صحيح: رواه مسلم (35:862)."},{"num":10123,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ جَابِرِ بْنِ عَبْدِ اللَّهِ قَالَ:  كُنَّا مَعَ النَّبِيِّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ فِي سَفَرٍ، فَتَخَلَّفَ نَاضِحِي، وَسَاقَ الْحَدِيثَ. وَقَالَ فِيهِ: فَنَخَسَهُ رَسُولُ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ، ثُمَّ قَالَ لِي: ارْكَبْ بِاسْمِ اللَّهِ. وَزَادَ أَيْضًا: قَالَ: فَمَا زَالَ يَزِيدُنِي، وَيَقُولُ: وَاللهُ يَغْفِرُ لَكَ."],"takhrij":"صحيح: رواه مسلم في المساقاة (715-112) عن أبي كامل الجحدري، حدثنا عبدالواحد بن زياد، حدثنا الجريري، عن أبي نضرة، عن جابر قال: فذكره.","grade":"صحيح","chapter_ar":"باب فضل جابر بن عبد الله","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب فضائل الصحابة وأخبارهم","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Authentic: Narrated by Muslim (715, no. 112).","chapter_en":"The Virtue of Jābir ibn ʿAbdullāh","part_en":"The Book of the Virtues and Accounts of the Companions","group_ar":"مجموع فضائل أفراد الصحابة وأخبارهم","group_en":"A Collection of the Virtues and Reports of Individual Companions","part_no":49,"group_no":13,"chapter_no":23,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Jābir narrated: We were traveling with the Prophet ﷺ when my riding camel fell behind. He then related the remainder of the narration and said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ prodded it, then said to me: “Mount in the name of Allah.” The narration also adds: He continued increasing the price for me while saying: “May Allah forgive you.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"voc":["fazail",321],"full":1,"tks":"صحيح: رواه مسلم (715/112)."},{"num":10124,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عن جابر بْنِ عَبْدِ اللَّهِ رَضِيَ اللَّهُ عَنْهُمَا يَقُولُ: قَالَ لِي رَسُولُ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ: لَوْ قَدْ جَاءَ مَالُ الْبَحْرَيْنِ لَقَدْ أَعْطَيْتُكَ هَكَذَا وَهَكَذَا ثَلاَثًا. فَلَمْ يَقْدَمْ مَالُ الْبَحْرَيْنِ حَتَّى قُبِضَ رَسُولُ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ، فَلَمَّا قَدِمَ عَلَى أَبِي بَكْرٍ أَمَرَ مُنَادِيًا فَنَادَى: مَنْ كَانَ لَهُ عِنْدَ النَّبِيِّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ دَيْنٌ أَوْ عِدَةٌ فَلْيَأْتِنِي. قَالَ جَابِرٌ: فَجِئْتُ أَبَا بَكْرٍ، فَأَخْبَرْتُهُ أَنَّ النَّبِيَّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ قَالَ: لَوْ جَاءَ مَالُ الْبَحْرَيْنِ أَعْطَيْتُكَ هَكَذَا وَهَكَذَا ثَلاَثًا. قَالَ فَأَعْطَانِي. قَالَ جَابِرٌ: فَلَقِيتُ أَبَا بَكْرٍ بَعْدَ ذَلِكَ، فَسَأَلْتُهُ، فَلَمْ يُعْطِنِي، ثُمَّ أَتَيْتُهُ فَلَمْ يُعْطِنِي، ثُمَّ أَتَيْتُهُ الثَّالِثَةَ فَلَمْ يُعْطِنِي، فَقُلْتُ لَهُ: قَدْ أَتَيْتُكَ فَلَمْ تُعْطِنِي، ثُمَّ أَتَيْتُكَ فَلَمْ تُعْطِنِي، ثُمَّ أَتَيْتُكَ فَلَمْ تُعْطِنِي، فَإِمَّا أَنْ تُعْطِيَنِي، وَإِمَّا أَنْ تَبْخَلَ عَنِّي. فَقَالَ أَقُلْتَ تَبْخَلُ عَنِّي؟ وَأَىُّ دَاءٍ أَدْوَأُ مِنَ الْبُخْلِ، ـ قَالَهَا ثَلاَثًا، ـ مَا مَنَعْتُكَ مِنْ مَرَّةٍ إِلاَّ وَأَنَا أُرِيدُ أَنْ أُعْطِيَكَ. وَعَنْ عَمْرٍو عَنْ مُحَمَّدِ بْنِ عَلِيٍّ سَمِعْتُ جَابِرَ بْنَ عَبْدِ اللَّهِ يَقُولُ جِئْتُهُ، فَقَالَ لِي أَبُو بَكْرٍ عُدَّهَا. فَعَدَدْتُهَا فَوَجَدْتُهَا خَمْسَمِائَةٍ، فَقَالَ خُذْ مِثْلَهَا مَرَّتَيْنِ."],"takhrij":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاري في المغازي (4383) ومسلم في الفضائل (2314-60) كلاهما من طريق سفيان بن عيينة، عن ابن المنكدر، أنه سمع جابر بن عبدالله يقول: فذكره.","grade":"متفق عليه","chapter_ar":"باب فضل جابر بن عبد الله","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب فضائل الصحابة وأخبارهم","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Agreed upon: Narrated by al-Bukhārī (4383) and Muslim (2314, no. 60).","chapter_en":"The Virtue of Jābir ibn ʿAbdullāh","part_en":"The Book of the Virtues and Accounts of the Companions","group_ar":"مجموع فضائل أفراد الصحابة وأخبارهم","group_en":"A Collection of the Virtues and Reports of Individual Companions","part_no":49,"group_no":13,"chapter_no":23,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Jābir ibn ʿAbdullāh narrated: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to me: “If the wealth of Bahrain were to arrive, I would give you this much, this much, and this much,” indicating three handfuls. The wealth of Bahrain did not arrive until after the Messenger of Allah ﷺ had passed away. When it arrived during the caliphate of Abū Bakr, Abū Bakr ordered a caller to announce: “Whoever is owed a debt or has been promised something by the Prophet ﷺ should come to me.” Jābir said: I went to Abū Bakr and informed him that the Prophet ﷺ had said: “If the wealth of Bahrain arrives, I will give you this much, this much, and this much,” three times. So Abū Bakr gave me something. Jābir continued: I met Abū Bakr later and asked him, but he did not give me anything. Then I came to him again, but he did not give me anything. Then I came to him a third time, but he still did not give me anything. I said: “I came to you, but you did not give me anything. Then I came to you again, and you did not give me anything. Then I came to you a third time, and you did not give me anything. Either give me something or admit that you are withholding from me out of miserliness.” Abū Bakr said: “Did you say that I was being miserly toward you? What disease is worse than miserliness?” He repeated this three times. He then said: “Each time I withheld from you, I had intended to give you.” ʿAmr narrated from Muḥammad ibn ʿAlī that he heard Jābir ibn ʿAbdullāh say: I came to Abū Bakr, and he said to me: “Count it.” I counted it and found it to be five hundred. He then said: “Take twice that amount as well.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"voc":["fazail",322],"full":1,"rep":[9487],"tks":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (4383)، ومسلم (2314/60)."},{"num":10125,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ جَابِرِ بْنِ عَبْدِالله قَالَ: خَرَجْتُ مَعَ رَسُولِ الله صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ فِى غَزَاةٍ فَأَبْطَأَ بِي جَمَلِي فَأَتَى عَلَيَّ رَسُولُ الله صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ فَقَالَ لِي: يَا جَابِرُ.قُلْتُ: نَعَمْ.قَالَ: مَا شَأْنُكَ.قُلْتُ أَبْطَأَ بِي جَمَلِي وَأَعْيَا فَتَخَلَّفْتُ.فَنَزَلَ فَحَجَنَهُ بِمِحْجَنِهِ ثُمَّ قَالَ: ارْكَبْ.فَرَكِبْتُ فَلَقَدْ رَأَيْتُنِى أَكُفُّهُ عَنْ رَسُولِ الله صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ فَقَالَ: أَتَزَوَّجْتَ.فَقُلْتُ: نَعَمْ.فَقَالَ: أَبِكْرًا أَمْ ثَيِّبًا؟.فَقُلْتُ: بَلْ ثَيِّبٌ.قَالَ: فَهَلاَّ جَارِيَةً تُلاَعِبُهَا وَتُلاَعِبُكَ.قُلْتُ: إِنَّ لِى أَخَوَاتٍ فَأَحْبَبْتُ أَنْ أَتَزَوَّجَ امْرَأَةً تَجْمَعُهُنَّ وَتَمْشُطُهُنَّ وَتَقُومُ عَلَيْهِنَّ.قَالَ: أَمَا إِنَّكَ قَادِمٌ فَإِذَا قَدِمْتَ فَالْكَيْسَ الْكَيْسَ.ثُمَّ قَالَ: أَتَبِيعُ جَمَلَكَ.قُلْتُ نَعَمْ.فَاشْتَرَاهُ مِنِّى بِأُوقِيَّةٍ ثُمَّ قَدِمَ رَسُولُ الله صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ وَقَدِمْتُ بِالْغَدَاةِ فَجِئْتُ المَسْجِدَ فَوَجَدْتُهُ عَلَى بَابِ المَسْجِدِ فَقَالَ: الآنَ حِينَ قَدِمْتَ.قُلْتُ: نَعَمْ.قَالَ: فَدَعْ جَمَلَكَ، وَادْخُلْ، فَصَلِّ رَكْعَتَيْنِ.قَالَ: فَدَخَلْتُ فَصَلَّيْتُ ثُمَّ رَجَعْتُ فَأَمَرَ بِلاَلاً أَنْ يَزِنَ لِى أُوقِيَّةً فَوَزَنَ لِيْ بِلاَلٌ فَأَرْجَحَ فِى الْمِيزَانِ – قَالَ: - فَانْطَلَقْتُ فَلَمَّا وَلَّيْتُ قَالَ: ادْعُ لِى جَابِرًا.فَدُعِيتُ فَقُلْتُ الآنَ يَرُدُّ عَلَيَّ الجَمَلَ.وَلَمْ يَكُنْ شَيءٌ أَبْغَضَ إِلَيَّ مِنْهُ فَقَالَ: خُذْ جَمَلَكَ، وَلَكَ ثَمَنُهُ."],"takhrij":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاري في البيوع (2097)، ومسلم في الرضاع (715: 57) كلاهما من طريق عبد الوهاب بن عبد المجيد الثقفي، حدثنا عبيد الله، عن وهب بن كيسان، عن جابر بن عبد الله قال: فذكره.","grade":"متفق عليه","chapter_ar":"باب في أخبار جابر بن عبد الله","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب فضائل الصحابة وأخبارهم","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Authentic: Narrated by al-Bukhārī (2097) and Muslim (715, no. 57).","chapter_en":"Reports Concerning Jābir ibn ʿAbdullāh","part_en":"The Book of the Virtues and Accounts of the Companions","group_ar":"مجموع فضائل أفراد الصحابة وأخبارهم","group_en":"A Collection of the Virtues and Reports of Individual Companions","part_no":49,"group_no":13,"chapter_no":24,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Jābir ibn ʿAbdullāh narrated: I went out with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ on a military expedition, but my camel became slow and exhausted, so I fell behind. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ came upon me and said: “O Jābir.” I replied: “Yes.” He asked: “What is the matter with you?” I said: “My camel has become slow and exhausted, so I have fallen behind.” He dismounted, struck it with his crooked staff, and then said: “Mount.” I mounted it, and afterward I found myself holding it back so that it would not overtake the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. He asked: “Have you married?” I replied: “Yes.” He asked: “A virgin or a previously married woman?” I replied: “A previously married woman.” He said: “Why did you not marry a young virgin with whom you could play and who could play with you?” I said: “I have sisters, so I wished to marry a woman who could gather them together, comb their hair, and care for them.” He said: “You are about to arrive home, so when you arrive, act wisely and thoughtfully.” Then he asked: “Will you sell me your camel?” I replied: “Yes.” He purchased it from me for one uqiyyah. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ later arrived in Madinah, and I arrived the following morning. I went to the mosque and found him at the mosque’s entrance. He asked: “Have you only just arrived?” I replied: “Yes.” He said: “Leave your camel and enter the mosque to pray two rakʿahs.” I entered and prayed. When I returned, he instructed Bilāl to weigh one uqiyyah for me. Bilāl weighed it and gave me more than the exact amount. I departed, but when I turned away, the Prophet ﷺ said: “Call Jābir back to me.” I was summoned and thought: “Now he is going to return the camel to me,” although nothing had become more disliked to me than that camel. He then said: “Take your camel, and keep its price as well.”"]},"buhuth":{"en":["Muslim also recorded it in The Book of Breastfeeding (715, no. 58) through another route from Jābir ibn ʿAbdullāh, who said:","We were traveling with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and I was riding a water-carrying camel that remained at the rear of the people.","The Messenger of Allah ﷺ struck it—or he said, prodded it—with something he had with him.","After that, it began overtaking the people and pulling so strongly that I had to restrain it.","The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said:","“Will you sell it to me for such-and-such, and may Allah forgive you?”","I replied:","“It is yours, O Prophet of Allah.”","He again said:","“Will you sell it to me for such-and-such, and may Allah forgive you?”","I replied:","“It is yours, O Prophet of Allah.”","He then asked me:","“Did you marry after your father’s death?”","I replied:","“Yes.”","He asked:","“A previously married woman or a virgin?”","I replied:","“A previously married woman.”","He said:","“Why did you not marry a virgin who would laugh with you and with whom you could laugh, who would play with you and with whom you could play?”","Abū Naḍrah said:","Thereafter, the Muslims used to say:","“Do such-and-such, and may Allah forgive you.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"voc":["fazail",323],"full":1,"dr":1,"tks":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (2097)، ومسلم (715: 57)."},{"num":10126,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ جَابِرِ بْنِ عَبْدِ الله قَالَ خَرَجْتُ مَعَ رَسُولِ الله صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ فِي غَزْوَةِ ذَاتِ الرِّقَاعِ مُرْتَحِلًا عَلَى جَمَلٍ لِي ضَعِيفٍ، فَلَمَّا قَفَلَ رَسُولُ الله صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ جَعَلَتْ الرِّفَاقُ تَمْضِي، وَجَعَلْتُ أَتَخَلَّفُ حَتَّى أَدْرَكَنِي رَسُولُ الله صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ، فَقَالَ: مَا لَكَ يَا جَابِرُ؟ قَالَ: قُلْتُ: يَا رَسُولَ الله أَبْطَأَ بِي جَمَلِي هَذَا، قَالَ: فَأَنِخْهُ وَأَنَاخَ رَسُولُ الله صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ، ثُمَّ قَالَ: أَعْطِنِي هَذِهِ الْعَصَا مِنْ يَدِكَ، -أَوْ قَالَ اقْطَعْ لِي عَصًا مِنْ شَجَرَةٍ- قَالَ: فَفَعَلْتُ، قَالَ: فَأَخَذَ رَسُولُ الله صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ فَنَخَسَهُ بِهَا نَخَسَاتٍ، ثُمَّ قَالَ: ارْكَبْ، فَرَكِبْتُ، فَخَرَجَ وَالَّذِي بَعَثَهُ بِالحَقِّ يُوَاهِقُ نَاقَتَهُ مُوَاهَقَةً، قَالَ: وَتَحَدَّثَ مَعِي رَسُولُ الله صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ فَقَالَ: أَتَبِيعُنِي جَمَلَكَ هَذَا يَا جَابِرُ؟ قَالَ: قُلْتُ: يَا رَسُولَ الله بَلْ أَهَبُهُ لَكَ، قَالَ: لَا، وَلَكِنْ بِعْنِيهِ، قَالَ: قُلْتُ: فَسُمْنِي بِهِ، قَالَ: قَدْ قُلْتُ: أَخَذْتُهُ بِدِرْهَمٍ، قَالَ: قُلْتُ: لَا إِذًا يَغْبِنُنِي رَسُولُ الله صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ، قَالَ: فَبِدِرْهَمَيْنِ قَالَ: قُلْتُ: لَا، قَالَ: فَلَمْ يَزَلْ يَرْفَعُ لِي رَسُولُ الله صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ حَتَّى بَلَغَ الْأُوقِيَّةَ، قَالَ: قُلْتُ: فَقَدْ رَضِيتُ، قَالَ: قَدْ رَضِيتَ؟ قُلْتُ: نَعَمْ.قُلْتُ: هُوَ لَكَ قَالَ: قَدْ أَخَذْتُهُ.","قَالَ: ثُمَّ قَالَ لِي: يَا جَابِرُ هَلْ تَزَوَّجْتَ بَعْدُ؟ قَالَ: قُلْتُ: نَعَمْ يَا رَسُولَ الله، قَالَ: أَثَيِّبًا أَمْ بِكْرًا؟ قَالَ: قُلْتُ: بَلْ ثَيِّبًا، قَالَ: أَفَلَا جَارِيَةً تُلَاعِبُهَا وَتُلَاعِبُكَ؟ قَالَ: قُلْتُ: يَا رَسُولَ الله إِنْ أَبِي أُصِيبَ يَوْمَ أُحُدٍ، وَتَرَكَ بَنَاتٍ لَهُ سَبْعًا، فَنَكَحْتُ امْرَأَةً جَامِعَةً تَجْمَعُ رُؤوسَهُنَّ وَتَقُومُ عَلَيْهِنَّ، قَالَ: أَصَبْتَ إِن شَاءَ الله.","قَالَ: أَمَا إِنَّا لَوْ قَدْ جِئْنَا صِرَارًا أَمَرْنَا بِجَزُورٍ، فَنُحِرَتْ، وَأَقَمْنَا عَلَيْهَا يَوْمَنَا ذَلِكَ، وَسَمِعَتْ بِنَا، فَنَفَضَتْ نَمَارِقَهَا، قَالَ: قُلْتُ: والله يَا رَسُولَ الله مَا لَنَا مِنْ نَمَارِقَ، قَالَ: إِنَّهَا سَتَكُونُ، فَإِذَا أَنْتَ قَدِمْتَ فَاعْمَلْ عَمَلًا كَيِّسًا، قَالَ: فَلَمَّا جِئْنَا صِرَارًا أَمَرَ رَسُولُ الله صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ بِجَزُورٍ، فَنُحِرَتْ، فَأَقَمْنَا عَلَيْهَا ذَلِكَ الْيَوْمَ، فَلَمَّا أَمْسَى رَسُولُ الله صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ دَخَلَ، وَدَخَلْنَا، قَالَ: فَأَخْبَرْتُ المَرْأَةَ الحَدِيثَ وَمَا قَالَ لِي رَسُولُ الله صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ، قَالَتْ: فَدُونَكَ فَسَمْعًا وَطَاعَةً.","قَالَ: فَلَمَّا أَصْبَحْتُ أَخَذْتُ بِرَأْسِ الجَمَلِ، فَأَقْبَلْتُ بِهِ حَتَّى أَنَخْتُهُ عَلَى بَابِ رَسُولِ الله صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ، ثُمَّ جَلَسْتُ فِي المَسْجِدِ قَرِيبًا مِنْهُ، قَالَ: وَخَرَجَ رَسُولُ الله صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ فَرَأَى الجَمَلَ، فَقَالَ: مَا هَذَا؟ قَالُوا: يَا رَسُولَ الله هَذَا جَمَلٌ جَاءَ بِهِ جَابِرٌ، قَالَ: فَأَيْنَ جَابِرٌ؟ فَدُعِيتُ لَهُ، قَالَ: تَعَالَ أَيْ يَا ابْنَ أَخِي، خُذْ بِرَأْسِ جَمَلِكَ فَهُوَ لَكَ، قَالَ: فَدَعَا بِلَالًا، فَقَالَ: اذْهَبْ بِجَابِرٍ فَأَعْطِهِ أُوقِيَّةً، فَذَهَبْتُ مَعَهُ، فَأَعْطَانِي أُوقِيَّةً، وَزَادَنِي شَيْئًا يَسِيرًا، قَالَ: فوالله مَازَالَ يَنْمِي عِنْدَنَا وَنَرَى مَكَانَهُ مِنْ بَيْتِنَا حَتَّى أُصِيبَ أَمْسِ فِيمَا أُصِيبَ النَّاسُ، يَعْنِي: يَوْمَ الحَرَّةِ."],"takhrij":"حسن: رواه الإمام أحمد (15026) عن يعقوب، حدثنا أبي، عن محمد بن إسحاق، حدثني وهب بن كيسان، عن جابر بن عبد الله قال: فذكره.","grade":"حسن","chapter_ar":"باب في أخبار جابر بن عبد الله","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب فضائل الصحابة وأخبارهم","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Hasan: Narrated by Imām Aḥmad (15026).","chapter_en":"Reports Concerning Jābir ibn ʿAbdullāh","part_en":"The Book of the Virtues and Accounts of the Companions","group_ar":"مجموع فضائل أفراد الصحابة وأخبارهم","group_en":"A Collection of the Virtues and Reports of Individual Companions","part_no":49,"group_no":13,"chapter_no":24,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Jābir ibn ʿAbdullāh narrated: I set out with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ during the expedition of Dhāt al-Riqāʿ, riding a weak camel of mine. When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ began the return journey, the rest of the caravan moved ahead while I continued falling behind until the Messenger of Allah ﷺ caught up with me. He asked: “What is the matter with you, O Jābir?” I replied: “O Messenger of Allah, this camel of mine has become slow.” He said: “Make it kneel.” The Messenger of Allah ﷺ then dismounted and said: “Hand me the stick you are carrying.” —or, according to another wording— “Cut a stick for me from a tree.” I did so. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ took the stick and gently prodded the camel several times before saying: “Mount.” I mounted it, and by the One Who sent him with the truth, it began keeping pace with the Prophet’s she-camel. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ then spoke with me and asked: “O Jābir, will you sell me this camel?” I replied: “O Messenger of Allah, I would rather give it to you as a gift.” He said: “No, but sell it to me.” I said: “Then name your price.” He first said: “I will buy it for one dirham.” I replied: “No, then you would be underpaying me, O Messenger of Allah.” He said: “Then two dirhams?” I replied: “No.” The Messenger of Allah ﷺ continued increasing the price until it reached one uqiyyah. I said: “I am satisfied.” He asked: “You are satisfied?” I replied: “Yes.” He said: “Then I have bought it.” He then asked me: “O Jābir, have you married?” I replied: “Yes, O Messenger of Allah.” He asked: “A previously married woman or a virgin?” I replied: “A previously married woman.” He said: “Why did you not marry a young virgin who could play with you and with whom you could play?” I replied: “O Messenger of Allah, my father was martyred on the Day of Uḥud, leaving behind seven daughters. Therefore, I married an experienced woman who could gather them together and take care of them.”","He said: “You made the right choice, if Allah wills.” He then said: “When we arrive at Ṣirār, we shall slaughter a camel, remain there for the day, and your wife will hear of our arrival and prepare her cushions.” I replied: “By Allah, O Messenger of Allah, we have no cushions.” He said: “You will have them in time. So when you arrive home, conduct yourself with wisdom and gentleness.” When we reached Ṣirār, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ ordered that a camel be slaughtered, and we remained there for the rest of the day.","When evening came, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ entered Madinah, and we entered as well. I informed my wife of everything the Messenger of Allah ﷺ had said to me. She replied: “Then do exactly as he instructed. I hear and obey.” The following morning I took hold of the camel and brought it to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, making it kneel at the entrance of his house. I then sat nearby in the mosque. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ came out, saw the camel, and asked: “What is this?”","They replied: “O Messenger of Allah, this is the camel Jābir has brought.” He asked: “Where is Jābir?” I was called, and he said: “Come here, my nephew. Take hold of your camel—it is yours.” He then called Bilāl and said: “Take Jābir and give him one uqiyyah.” Bilāl went with me, gave me one uqiyyah, and added a little extra. Jābir said: “By Allah, that blessing continued to grow among us, and we continued to see its effects until it was lost along with what the people lost on the Day of al-Ḥarrah.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"voc":["fazail",324],"full":1,"dr":1,"tks":"حسن: رواه الإمام أحمد (15026)."},{"num":10127,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عن جابر بن عبد الله قال: اشْتَرَى مِنِّي رَسُولُ الله صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ بَعِيرًا بِوُقِيَّتَيْنِ وَدِرْهَمٍ أَوْ دِرْهَمَيْنِ قَاَلَ: فَلَمَّا قَدِمَ صِرَارًا أَمَرَ بِبَقَرَةٍ فَذُبِحَتْ فَأَكَلُوا مِنْهَا، فَلَمَّا قَدِمَ المَدِينَةَ، أَمَرَنِي أَنْ آتِيَ المَسْجِدَ، فَأُصَلِّيَ رَكْعَتَيْنِ وَوَزَنَ لِي ثَمَنَ الْبَعِيرِ، فَأَرْجَحَ لي."],"takhrij":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاري في الجهاد والسير (3089)، ومسلم في المساقاة (715: 115) كلاهما من طريق شعبة، عن محارب بن دثار، عن جابر بن عبد الله قال: فذكره.","grade":"متفق عليه","chapter_ar":"باب في أخبار جابر بن عبد الله","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب فضائل الصحابة وأخبارهم","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Agreed upon: Narrated by al-Bukhārī (3089) and Muslim (715, no. 115).","chapter_en":"Reports Concerning Jābir ibn ʿAbdullāh","part_en":"The Book of the Virtues and Accounts of the Companions","group_ar":"مجموع فضائل أفراد الصحابة وأخبارهم","group_en":"A Collection of the Virtues and Reports of Individual Companions","part_no":49,"group_no":13,"chapter_no":24,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Jābir narrated: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ purchased a camel from me for two uqiyyahs and one dirham—or, according to another narration, two dirhams. When we reached Ṣirār, he ordered that a cow be slaughtered, and everyone ate from it. When we arrived in Madinah, he instructed me to go to the mosque and pray two rakʿahs. He then weighed out the price of the camel for me and gave me more than the agreed amount."]},"buhuth":{"en":["Ṣirār was an ancient well located about three miles from Madinah on the road leading toward Iraq.","Al-Bukhārī described it simply as a place on the outskirts of Madinah."]}},"tuhfa":{},"voc":["fazail",325],"full":1,"dr":1,"tks":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (3089)، ومسلم (715: 115)."},{"num":10128,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عن جرير بْنِ عَبْدِ اللَّهِ ـ رَضِيَ اللَّهُ عَنْهُ مَا حَجَبَنِي رَسُولُ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ مُنْذُ أَسْلَمْتُ، وَلاَ رَآنِي إِلاَّ ضَحِكَ."],"takhrij":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاري في مناقب الأنصار (3822)، ومسلم في فضائل الصحابة (2475-134) كلاهما من طريق خالد بن عبد الله، عن بيان، عن قيس قال: قال جرير بن عبد الله: فذكره.","grade":"متفق عليه","chapter_ar":"باب فضائل جرير بن عبد الله البجلي","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب فضائل الصحابة وأخبارهم","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Agreed upon: Narrated by al-Bukhārī (3822) and Muslim (2475, no. 134).","chapter_en":"The Virtues of Jarīr ibn ʿAbdullāh al-Bajalī","part_en":"The Book of the Virtues and Accounts of the Companions","group_ar":"مجموع فضائل أفراد الصحابة وأخبارهم","group_en":"A Collection of the Virtues and Reports of Individual Companions","part_no":49,"group_no":13,"chapter_no":25,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Jarīr ibn ʿAbdullāh narrated: From the day I embraced Islam, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ never prevented me from entering to see him, and whenever he saw me, he would smile."]},"buhuth":{"en":["In another narration:","“He never saw me except that he smiled in my face.","I once complained to him that I could not remain firm while riding a horse.","He struck my chest with his hand and supplicated:","‘O Allah, make him firm and make him one who guides others and is rightly guided.’”","Recorded by al-Bukhārī (3035, 3036) and Muslim (2475, no. 135)."]}},"tuhfa":{},"voc":["fazail",326],"full":1,"dr":1,"tks":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (3822)، ومسلم (2475/134)."},{"num":10129,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ جرير بْنِ عَبْدِ اللَّهِ البجلي قَالَ: قَالَ لِي رَسُولُ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ: أَلاَ تُرِيحُنِي مِنْ ذِي الْخَلَصَةِ؟ وَكَانَ بَيْتًا فِي خَثْعَمَ يُسَمَّى كَعْبَةَ الْيَمَانِيَةَ، قَالَ: فَانْطَلَقْتُ فِي خَمْسِينَ وَمِائَةِ فَارِسٍ مِنْ أَحْمَسَ، وَكَانُوا أَصْحَابَ خَيْلٍ، قَالَ: وَكُنْتُ لاَ أَثْبُتُ عَلَى الْخَيْلِ، فَضَرَبَ فِي صَدْرِي حَتَّى رَأَيْتُ أَثَرَ أَصَابِعِهِ فِي صَدْرِي، وَقَالَ: اللَّهُمَّ ثَبِّتْه، وَاجْعَلْهُ هَادِيًا مَهْدِيًّا فَانْطَلَقَ إِلَيْهَا فَكَسَرَهَا وَحَرَّقَهَا، ثُمَّ بَعَثَ إِلَى رَسُولِ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ يُخْبِرُهُ فَقَالَ رَسُولُ جَرِيرٍ: وَالَّذِي بَعَثَكَ بِالْحَقِّ مَا جِئْتُكَ حَتَّى تَرَكْتُهَا كَأَنَّهَا جَمَلٌ أَجْوَفُ أَوْ أَجْرَبُ.قَالَ: فَبَارَكَ فِي خَيْلِ أَحْمَسَ وَرِجَالِهَا خَمْسَ مَرَّاتٍ."],"takhrij":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاري في الجهاد والسير(3020)، ومسلم في فضائل الصحابة (2476-137) كلاهما من طريق إسماعيل بن أبي خالد، عن قيس بن أبي حازم، عن جرير بن عبد الله فذكره.وهذا لفظ البخاري، ولفظ مسلم نحوه.","grade":"متفق عليه","chapter_ar":"باب فضائل جرير بن عبد الله البجلي","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب فضائل الصحابة وأخبارهم","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Agreed upon: Narrated by al-Bukhārī (3020) and Muslim (2476, no. 137).","chapter_en":"The Virtues of Jarīr ibn ʿAbdullāh al-Bajalī","part_en":"The Book of the Virtues and Accounts of the Companions","group_ar":"مجموع فضائل أفراد الصحابة وأخبارهم","group_en":"A Collection of the Virtues and Reports of Individual Companions","part_no":49,"group_no":13,"chapter_no":25,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Jarīr ibn ʿAbdullāh al-Bajalī narrated: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to me: “Will you not relieve me of Dhū al-Khalaṣah?” It was a shrine belonging to the tribe of Khathʿam and was known as the Kaʿbah of Yemen. Jarīr said: I set out with one hundred and fifty horsemen from Aḥmas, who were skilled cavalrymen. I was unable to remain steady upon a horse, so the Prophet ﷺ struck me on the chest until I could see the marks of his fingers upon it, and he said: “O Allah, make him firm, and make him one who guides others and is rightly guided.” I went to Dhū al-Khalaṣah, destroyed it, and burned it. I then sent someone to inform the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. Jarīr’s messenger said: “By the One who sent you with the truth, I did not come to you until I had left it resembling a hollow or diseased camel.” The Prophet ﷺ then invoked Allah’s blessings upon the horses and men of Aḥmas five times."]},"buhuth":{"en":["The narration also states:","“He burned it with fire.”","It further states:","“Jarīr then sent a man from among us, whose kunyah was Abū Arṭāh, to convey the good news to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ.”","In another wording:","“He supplicated for us and for Aḥmas.”","Recorded by al-Bukhārī (3823)."]}},"tuhfa":{},"voc":["fazail",327],"full":1,"dr":1,"tks":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (3020)، ومسلم (2476/137)."},{"num":10130,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنِ الْمُغِيرَةِ بْنِ شِبْلٍ قَالَ: وَقَالَ جَرِيرٌ: لَمَّا دَنَوْتُ مِنَ الْمَدِينَةِ أَنَخْتُ رَاحِلَتِي، ثُمَّ حَلَلْتُ عَيْبَتِي، ثُمَّ لَبِسْتُ حُلَّتِي، ثُمَّ دَخَلْتُ، فَإِذَا رَسُولُ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ يَخْطُبُ، فَرَمَانِي النَّاسُ بِالْحَدَقِ، فَقُلْتُ لِجَلِيسِي: يَا عَبْدَ اللَّهِ، ذَكَرَنِي رَسُولُ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ؟ قَالَ: نَعَمْ، ذَكَرَكَ آنِفًا بِأَحْسَنِ ذِكْرٍ، فَبَيْنَا هُوَ يَخْطُبُ إِذْ عَرَضَ لَهُ فِي خُطْبَتِهِ، وَقَالَ: يَدْخُلُ عَلَيْكُمْ مِنْ هَذَا الْبَابِ، أَوْ مِنْ هَذَا الْفَجِّ، مِنْ خَيْرِ ذِي يَمَنٍ، إِلَّا أَنَّ عَلَى وَجْهِهِ مَسْحَةَ مَلَكٍ قَالَ جَرِيرٌ: فَحَمِدْتُ اللهَ عَزَّ وَجَلَّ عَلَى مَا أَبْلَانِي."],"takhrij":"حسن: رواه أحمد (19179)، والنسائي في فضائل الصحابة (199)، وصحّحه ابن خزيمة (1798)، وابن حبان (7199)، والحاكم (1053) كلهم من طريق يونس بن أبي إسحاق، عن المغيرة بن شُبَيل (وقيل: شِبل)، عن جرير بن عبدالله فذكره.","grade":"حسن","chapter_ar":"باب فضائل جرير بن عبد الله البجلي","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب فضائل الصحابة وأخبارهم","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Hasan: Narrated by Aḥmad (19179) and al-Nasā’ī in Faḍāʾil al-Ṣaḥābah (199), and authenticated by Ibn Khuzaymah (1798).","chapter_en":"The Virtues of Jarīr ibn ʿAbdullāh al-Bajalī","part_en":"The Book of the Virtues and Accounts of the Companions","group_ar":"مجموع فضائل أفراد الصحابة وأخبارهم","group_en":"A Collection of the Virtues and Reports of Individual Companions","part_no":49,"group_no":13,"chapter_no":25,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Jarīr ibn ʿAbdullāh narrated: When I drew near to Madinah, I made my riding animal kneel, opened my travel bag, put on my fine garments, and then entered. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was delivering a sermon, and the people began staring at me. I said to the man sitting beside me: “O servant of Allah, did the Messenger of Allah ﷺ mention me?” He replied: “Yes. He mentioned you a short while ago in the finest manner. While delivering his sermon, he paused and said: ‘A man from among the finest people of Yemen will enter upon you through this door—or through this mountain pass. Indeed, upon his face is the mark of an angel.’” Jarīr said: I praised Allah, Mighty and Majestic, for the favor with which He had blessed me."]}},"tuhfa":{},"voc":["fazail",328],"full":1,"dr":1,"tks":"حسن: رواه أحمد (19179)، والنسائي في فضائل الصحابة (199)، وصححه ابن خزيمة (1798)."},{"num":10131,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ الْبَرَاءِ بْنِ عَازِبٍ قَالَ: اعْتَمَرَ النَّبِيُّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ فِي ذِي الْقَعْدَةِ...الحديث، وَفِيهِ: قصة ابْنَةُ حَمْزَةَ، وأنها تبعتهم حِينَ الخروج مِنْ مَكَّةَ، فَتَنَاوَلَهَا عَلِيٌّ فَأَخَذَ بِيَدِهَا، وَقَالَ لِفَاطِمَةَ: دُونَكِ ابْنَةَ عَمِّكِ، حملتها، فَاخْتَصَمَ فِيهَا عَلِيٌّ وَزَيْدٌ وَجَعْفَرٌ، فَقَالَ عَلِيٌّ: أَنَا أَحَقُّ بِهَا وهي ابْنَةُ عَمِّي.وَقَالَ جَعْفَرٌ: ابْنَةُ عَمِّي وَخَالَتُهَا تَحْتِي.وَقَالَ زَيْدٌ: ابْنَةُ أَخِي فَقَضَى بِهَا النَّبِيُّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ لِخَالَتِهَا، وَقَالَ: الْخَالَةُ بِمَنْزِلَةِ الأُمِّ وَقَالَ لِعَلِيٍّ: أَنْتَ مِنِّي وَأَنَا مِنْكَ وَقَالَ لِجَعْفَرٍ: أَشْبَهْتَ خَلْقِي وَخُلُقِي وَقَالَ لِزَيْدٍ: أَنْتَ أَخُونَا وَمَوْلاَنَا."],"takhrij":"صحيح: رواه البخاري في الصلح (2699) عن عبيد الله بن موسى، عن إسرائيل، عن أبي إسحاق، عن البراء قال: فذكره.","grade":"صحيح","chapter_ar":"باب ما جاء أن جعفر بن أبي طالب أشبه خَلْق النبي ﷺ وخُلُقه","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب فضائل الصحابة وأخبارهم","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Authentic: Narrated by al-Bukhārī (2699).","chapter_en":"Reports That Jaʿfar ibn Abī Ṭālib Most Resembled the Prophet ﷺ in Appearance and Character","part_en":"The Book of the Virtues and Accounts of the Companions","group_ar":"مجموع فضائل أفراد الصحابة وأخبارهم","group_en":"A Collection of the Virtues and Reports of Individual Companions","part_no":49,"group_no":13,"chapter_no":26,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Al-Barāʾ narrated: The Prophet ﷺ performed ʿumrah during the month of Dhū al-Qaʿdah. The narration includes the story of the daughter of Ḥamzah. When the Muslims were leaving Makkah, she followed them. ʿAlī reached out, took her by the hand, and said to Fāṭimah: “Take your cousin’s daughter.” Fāṭimah then carried her. ʿAlī, Zayd, and Jaʿfar disputed over who should care for her. ʿAlī said: “I have the greatest right to her, for she is the daughter of my paternal uncle.” Jaʿfar said: “She is the daughter of my paternal uncle, and her maternal aunt is my wife.” Zayd said: “She is the daughter of my brother.” The Prophet ﷺ awarded her custody to her maternal aunt and said: “The maternal aunt holds the same position as the mother.” He said to ʿAlī: “You are from me, and I am from you.” He said to Jaʿfar: “You resemble me in both my appearance and my character.” He said to Zayd: “You are our brother and our freedman.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"voc":["fazail",329],"full":1,"tks":"صحيح: رواه البخاري (2699)."},{"num":10132,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عن عَبْدِ اللَّهِ بن جَعْفَرٍ قَالَ: لَوْ رَأَيْتَنِي وَقُثَمَ وَعُبَيْدَ اللهِ ابْنَيْ عَبَّاسٍ، وَنَحْنُ صِبْيَانٌ نَلْعَبُ، إِذْ مَرَّ النَّبِيُّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ عَلَى دَابَّةٍ، فَقَالَ: ارْفَعُوا هَذَا إِلَيَّ قَالَ: فَحَمَلَنِي أَمَامَهُ، وَقَالَ لِقُثَمَ: ارْفَعُوا هَذَا إِلَيَّ فَجَعَلَهُ وَرَاءَهُ، وَكَانَ عُبَيْدُ اللَّهِ أَحَبَّ إِلَى عَبَّاسٍ مِنْ قُثَمَ، فَمَا اسْتَحَى مِنْ عَمِّهِ أَنْ حَمَلَ قُثَمَ وَتَرَكَهُ، قَالَ: ثُمَّ مَسَحَ عَلَى رَأْسِي ثَلاثًا، وَقَالَ كُلَّمَا مَسَحَ: اللهُمَّ اخْلُفْ جَعْفَرًا فِي وَلَدِهِ قَالَ: قُلْتُ لِعَبْدِ اللَّهِ: مَا فَعَلَ قُثَمُ؟ قَالَ: اسْتُشْهِدَ، قَالَ: قُلْتُ: اللَّهُ أَعْلَمُ بِالْخَيْرِ وَرَسُولُهُ بِالْخَيْرِ، قَالَ: أَجَلْ."],"takhrij":"حسن: رواه أحمد (1760)، والنسائي في الكبرى (10838، 10845)، وصحّحه الحاكم (1/372) كلهم من طريق ابن جريج، أخبرني جعفر بن خالد بن سارة، أن أباه أخبره أن عبد الله بن جعفر قال: فذكره.","grade":"حسن","chapter_ar":"باب دعاء النبي ﷺ لجعفر بن أبي طالب","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب فضائل الصحابة وأخبارهم","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Hasan: Narrated by Aḥmad (1760) and al-Nasā’ī in al-Sunan al-Kubrā (10838, 10845), and authenticated by al-Ḥākim (1378).","chapter_en":"The Prophet’s ﷺ Supplication for Jaʿfar ibn Abī Ṭālib","part_en":"The Book of the Virtues and Accounts of the Companions","group_ar":"مجموع فضائل أفراد الصحابة وأخبارهم","group_en":"A Collection of the Virtues and Reports of Individual Companions","part_no":49,"group_no":13,"chapter_no":27,"content":{"translation":{"en":["ʿAbdullāh ibn Jaʿfar narrated: You should have seen me, Qutham, and ʿUbaydullāh, the two sons of al-ʿAbbās, when we were young boys playing. The Prophet ﷺ passed by while riding an animal and said: “Lift this boy up to me.” They lifted me up, and he seated me in front of him. He then said regarding Qutham: “Lift this boy up to me.” He placed him behind him. ʿUbaydullāh was more beloved to al-ʿAbbās than Qutham, yet the Prophet ﷺ did not refrain, out of consideration for his uncle, from carrying Qutham and leaving ʿUbaydullāh behind. He then passed his hand over my head three times, saying each time: “O Allah, succeed Jaʿfar in caring for his children.” The narrator said: I asked ʿAbdullāh: “What happened to Qutham?” He replied: “He was martyred.” I said: “Allah knows best where goodness lies, and His Messenger knew best.” He replied: “Yes.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"voc":["fazail",330],"full":1,"dr":1,"tks":"حسن: رواه أحمد (1760)، والنسائي في الكبرى (10838، 10845)، وصححه الحاكم (1378)."},{"num":10133,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ أَبِي هُرَيْرَةَ، قَالَ: قَالَ رَسُولُ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ: رَأَيْتُ جَعْفَرًا يَطِيرُ فِي الْجَنَّةِ مَعَ الْمَلاَئِكَةِ."],"takhrij":"حسن: رواه الترمذي (3763)، وأبو يعلى (6464)، والحاكم (1) كلهم من طرق عن عبد الله بن جعفر المديني، عن العلاء بن عبد الرحمن، عن أبيه، عن أبي هريرة قال: فذكره.وهذا لفظ الترمذي.","grade":"حسن","chapter_ar":"باب أن جعفر بن أبي طالب ذو الجناحين","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب فضائل الصحابة وأخبارهم","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Hasan: Narrated by al-Tirmidhī (3763), Abū Yaʿlā (6464), and al-Ḥākim in al-Mustadrak (3/209).","chapter_en":"Jaʿfar ibn Abī Ṭālib Is the Possessor of Two Wings","part_en":"The Book of the Virtues and Accounts of the Companions","group_ar":"مجموع فضائل أفراد الصحابة وأخبارهم","group_en":"A Collection of the Virtues and Reports of Individual Companions","part_no":49,"group_no":13,"chapter_no":28,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Abū Hurayrah narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “I saw Jaʿfar flying in Paradise with the angels.”"]},"buhuth":{"en":["The wording cited above is that of al-Tirmidhī. The wording of the other narrations is similar:","“I saw Jaʿfar ibn Abī Ṭālib as an angel, flying with the angels in Paradise upon two wings.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"voc":["fazail",331],"full":1,"dr":1,"tks":"حسن: رواه الترمذي (3763)، وأبو يعلى (6464)، والحاكم في المستدرك (1). واللفظ للترمذي، ولفظ الآخرين بنحوه: «رأيت جعفر بن أبي طالب ملكا يطير مع الملائكة بجناحين في الجنة»."},{"num":10134,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنِ الشَّعْبِيِّ، أَنَّ ابْنَ عُمَرَ رَضِيَ اللَّهُ عَنْهُمَا كَانَ إِذَا سَلَّمَ عَلَى ابْنِ جَعْفَرٍ قَالَ: السَّلاَمُ عَلَيْكَ يَا ابْنَ ذِي الْجَنَاحَيْنِ."],"takhrij":"صحيح: رواه البخاري في فضائل الصحابة (3709) عن عمرو بن علي، ثنا يزيد بن هارون، أنا إسماعيل بن أبي خالد، عن الشعبي فذكره.","grade":"صحيح","chapter_ar":"باب أن جعفر بن أبي طالب ذو الجناحين","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب فضائل الصحابة وأخبارهم","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Authentic: Narrated by al-Bukhārī (3709).","chapter_en":"Jaʿfar ibn Abī Ṭālib Is the Possessor of Two Wings","part_en":"The Book of the Virtues and Accounts of the Companions","group_ar":"مجموع فضائل أفراد الصحابة وأخبارهم","group_en":"A Collection of the Virtues and Reports of Individual Companions","part_no":49,"group_no":13,"chapter_no":28,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Al-Shaʿbī narrated: Whenever Ibn ʿUmar greeted the son of Jaʿfar, he would say: “Peace be upon you, O son of the possessor of two wings.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"voc":["fazail",332],"full":1,"tks":"صحيح: رواه البخاري (3709)."},{"num":10135,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ أَبِي هُرَيْرَةَ رَضِيَ اللَّهُ عَنْهُ أَنَّ النَّاسَ، كَانُوا يَقُولُونَ: أَكْثَرَ أَبُو هُرَيْرَةَ. وَإِنِّي كُنْتُ أَلْزَمُ رَسُولَ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ بِشِبَعِ بَطْنِي، حَتَّى لاَ آكُلُ الْخَمِيرَ، وَلاَ أَلْبَسُ الْحَبِيرَ، وَلاَ يَخْدُمُنِي فُلاَنٌ وَلاَ فُلاَنَةُ، وَكُنْتُ أُلْصِقُ بَطْنِي بِالْحَصْبَاءِ مِنَ الْجُوعِ، وَإِنْ كُنْتُ لأَسْتَقْرِئُ الرَّجُلَ الآيَةَ، هِيَ مَعِي، كَىْ يَنْقَلِبَ بِي فَيُطْعِمَنِي، وَكَانَ أَخْيَرَ النَّاسِ لِلْمِسْكِينِ جَعْفَرُ بْنُ أَبِي طَالِبٍ، كَانَ يَنْقَلِبُ بِنَا فَيُطْعِمُنَا مَا كَانَ فِي بَيْتِهِ، حَتَّى إِنْ كَانَ لَيُخْرِجُ إِلَيْنَا الْعُكَّةَ الَّتِي لَيْسَ فِيهَا شَىْءٌ، فَنَشُقُّهَا فَنَلْعَقُ مَا فِيهَا."],"takhrij":"صحيح: رواه البخاري في فضائل الصحابة (3708) عن أحمد بن أبي بكر، ثنا محمد بن إبراهيم بن دينار، عن ابن أبي ذئب، عن سعيد المقبري، عن أبي هريرة فذكره.","grade":"صحيح","chapter_ar":"باب أن جعفر بن أبي طالب من أرحم الناس على المساكين","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب فضائل الصحابة وأخبارهم","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Authentic: Narrated by al-Bukhārī (3708).","chapter_en":"Jaʿfar ibn Abī Ṭālib Was Among the Most Compassionate of People Toward the Poor","part_en":"The Book of the Virtues and Accounts of the Companions","group_ar":"مجموع فضائل أفراد الصحابة وأخبارهم","group_en":"A Collection of the Virtues and Reports of Individual Companions","part_no":49,"group_no":13,"chapter_no":29,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Abū Hurayrah narrated: People used to say: “Abū Hurayrah narrates excessively.” However, I remained constantly in the company of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ merely to satisfy my hunger. At that time, I did not eat leavened bread, wear decorated garments, or have any man or woman serving me. Because of hunger, I would press my stomach against the pebbles. I would sometimes ask a man to recite a verse to me, even though I already knew it, hoping that he would take me home and feed me. The best of all people toward the poor was Jaʿfar ibn Abī Ṭālib. He would take us home and feed us whatever he had in his house. Sometimes he would bring out an empty leather container that had once held clarified butter. We would cut it open and lick whatever traces remained inside it."]}},"tuhfa":{},"voc":["fazail",333],"full":1,"dr":1,"tks":"صحيح: رواه البخاري (3708)."},{"num":10136,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ أَبِي بَرْزَةَ  أَنَّ النَّبِيَّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ كَانَ فِي مَغْزًى لَهُ، فَأَفَاءَ اللهُ عَلَيْهِ، فَقَالَ لِأَصْحَابِهِ: هَلْ تَفْقِدُونَ مِنْ أَحَدٍ؟ قَالُوا: نَعَمْ، فُلَانًا وَفُلَانًا وَفُلَانًا، ثُمَّ قَالَ: هَلْ تَفْقِدُونَ مِنْ أَحَدٍ؟ قَالُوا: نَعَمْ، فُلَانًا وَفُلَانًا وَفُلَانًا، ثُمَّ قَالَ: هَلْ تَفْقِدُونَ مِنْ أَحَدٍ؟ قَالُوا: لَا. قَالَ: لَكِنِّي أَفْقِدُ جُلَيْبِيبًا، فَاطْلُبُوهُ. فَطُلِبَ فِي الْقَتْلَى، فَوَجَدُوهُ إِلَى جَنْبِ سَبْعَةٍ قَدْ قَتَلَهُمْ، ثُمَّ قَتَلُوهُ، فَأَتَى النَّبِيُّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ فَوَقَفَ عَلَيْهِ فَقَالَ: قَتَلَ سَبْعَةً ثُمَّ قَتَلُوهُ، هَذَا مِنِّي وَأَنَا مِنْهُ، هَذَا مِنِّي وَأَنَا مِنْهُ. قَالَ: فَوَضَعَهُ عَلَى سَاعِدَيْهِ، لَيْسَ لَهُ إِلَّا سَاعِدَا النَّبِيِّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ. قَالَ: فَحُفِرَ لَهُ وَوُضِعَ فِي قَبْرِهِ، وَلَمْ يَذْكُرْ غَسْلًا."],"takhrij":"صحيح: رواه مسلم في فضائل الصحابة (2472) عن إسحاق بن عمر بن سليط، ثنا حماد بن سلمة، عن ثابت، عن كنانة بن نعيم، عن أبي برزة فذكره.","grade":"صحيح","chapter_ar":"باب ما جاء في فضائل جليبيب","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب فضائل الصحابة وأخبارهم","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Authentic: Narrated by Muslim (2472).","chapter_en":"Reports Concerning the Virtues of Julaybīb","part_en":"The Book of the Virtues and Accounts of the Companions","group_ar":"مجموع فضائل أفراد الصحابة وأخبارهم","group_en":"A Collection of the Virtues and Reports of Individual Companions","part_no":49,"group_no":13,"chapter_no":30,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Abū Barzah narrated: The Prophet ﷺ was on one of his military expeditions, and Allah granted him victory and spoils. He asked his Companions: “Are you missing anyone?” They replied: “Yes, so-and-so, so-and-so, and so-and-so.” He asked again: “Are you missing anyone?” They replied: “Yes, so-and-so, so-and-so, and so-and-so.” He asked a third time: “Are you missing anyone?” They replied: “No.” He said: “But I am missing Julaybīb. Search for him.” They searched among the slain and found him beside seven enemy soldiers whom he had killed before they killed him. The Prophet ﷺ came and stood over him, saying: “He killed seven, and then they killed him. He is from me, and I am from him. He is from me, and I am from him.” The Prophet ﷺ then carried him upon his forearms, and Julaybīb had no bier other than the forearms of the Prophet ﷺ. A grave was dug for him, and he was placed within it. The narrator did not mention that he was washed."]}},"tuhfa":{},"voc":["fazail",334],"full":1,"rep":[3756],"tks":"صحيح: رواه مسلم (2472)."},{"num":10137,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ أَبِي بَرْزَةَ الْأَسْلَمِيِّ، أَنَّ جُلَيْبِيبًا كَانَ امْرَأً يَدْخُلُ عَلَى النِّسَاءِ، يَمُرُّ بِهِنَّ وَيُلَاعِبُهُنَّ، فَقُلْتُ لِامْرَأَتِي: لَا يَدْخُلَنَّ عَلَيْكُمْ جُلَيْبِيبٌ؛ فَإِنَّهُ إِنْ دَخَلَ عَلَيْكُمْ، لَأَفْعَلَنَّ وَلَأَفْعَلَنَّ. قَالَ: وَكَانَتِ الْأَنْصَارُ إِذَا كَانَ لِأَحَدِهِمْ أَيِّمٌ لَمْ يُزَوِّجْهَا حَتَّى يَعْلَمَ هَلْ لِلنَّبِيِّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ فِيهَا حَاجَةٌ؟ أَمْ لَا. فَقَالَ رَسُولُ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ لِرَجُلٍ مِنَ الْأَنْصَارِ: زَوِّجْنِي ابْنَتَكَ. فَقَالَ: نِعِمَّ وَكَرَامَةٌ يَا رَسُولَ اللَّهِ، وَنُعْمَ عَيْنِي. قَالَ: إِنِّي لَسْتُ أُرِيدُهَا لِنَفْسِي. قَالَ: فَلِمَنْ يَا رَسُولَ اللَّهِ؟ قَالَ: لِجُلَيْبِيبٍ.: قَالَ: فَقَالَ: يَا رَسُولَ اللَّهِ، أُشَاوِرُ أُمَّهَا، فَأَتَى أُمَّهَا، فَقَالَ: رَسُولُ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ يَخْطُبُ ابْنَتَكِ. فَقَالَتْ: نِعِمَّ. وَنُعْمَةُ عَيْنِي. فَقَالَ: إِنَّهُ لَيْسَ يَخْطُبُهَا لِنَفْسِهِ، إِنَّمَا يَخْطُبُهَا لِجُلَيْبِيبٍ. فَقَالَتْ: أَجُلَيْبِيبٌ إنية؟ أَجُلَيْبِيبٌ إنية؟ أَجُلَيْبِيبٌ إنية؟ لَا. لَعَمْرُ اللهِ، لَا نُزَوَّجُهُ. فَلَمَّا أَرَادَ أَنْ يَقُومَ لِيَأْتِيَ رَسُولَ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ فِيُخْبِرَهُ بِمَا قَالَتْ أُمُّهَا: قَالَتِ الْجَارِيَةُ: مَنْ خَطَبَنِي إِلَيْكُمْ؟ فَأَخْبَرَتْهَا أُمُّهَا، فَقَالَتْ: أَتَرُدُّونَ عَلَى رَسُولِ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ أَمْرَهُ؟ ادْفَعُونِي؛ فَإِنَّهُ لَمْ يُضَيِّعْنِي. فَانْطَلَقَ أَبُوهَا إِلَى رَسُولِ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ، فَأَخْبَرَهُ، فَقَالَ: شَأْنَكَ بِهَا، فَزَوَّجَهَا جُلَيْبِيبًا.","قَالَ: فَخَرَجَ رَسُولُ اللهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ فِي غَزْوَةٍ لَهُ، قَالَ: فَلَمَّا أَفَاءَ اللهُ عَلَيْهِ، قَالَ لِأَصْحَابِهِ: هَلْ تَفْقِدُونَ مِنْ أَحَدٍ؟ قَالُوا: نَفْقِدُ فُلَانًا، وَنَفْقِدُ فلانا.قال: انْظُرُوا هَلْ تَفْقِدُونَ مِنْ أَحَدٍ؟ قَالُوا: لا.قال: لَكِنِّي أَفْقِدُ جُلَيْبِيبًا قَالَ: فَاطْلُبُوهُ فِي الْقَتْلَى قَالَ: فَطَلَبُوهُ، فَوَجَدُوهُ إِلَى جَنْبِ سَبْعَةٍ قَدْ قَتَلَهُمْ، ثُمَّ قَتَلُوهُ، فَقَالُوا: يَا رَسُولَ اللهِ، هَا هُوَ ذَا إِلَى جَنْبِ سَبْعَةٍ قَدْ قَتَلَهُمْ، ثُمَّ قَتَلُوهُ، فَأَتَاهُ النَّبِيُّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ، فَقَامَ عَلَيْهِ، فَقَالَ: قَتَلَ سَبْعَةً وَقَتَلُوهُ، هَذَا مِنِّي وَأَنَا مِنْهُ، هَذَا مِنِّي وَأَنَا مِنْهُ مَرَّتَيْنِ أَوْ ثَلَاثًا، ثُمَّ وَضَعَهُ رَسُولُ اللهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ عَلَى سَاعِدَيْهِ، وَحُفِرَ لَهُ، مَا لَهُ سَرِيرٌ إِلَّا سَاعِدَا رَسُولِ اللهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ، ثُمَّ وَضَعَهُ فِي قَبْرِهِ، وَلَمْ يُذْكَرْ أَنَّهُ غَسَّلَهُ.","قَالَ ثَابِتٌ: فَمَا كَانَ فِي الْأَنْصَارِ أَيِّمٌ أَنْفَقَ منها.وحدَّث إِسْحَاقُ بْنُ عَبْدِ اللهِ بْنِ أَبِي طَلْحَةَ ثَابِتًا، قَالَ: هَلْ تَعْلَمْ مَا دَعَا لَهَا رَسُولُ اللهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ؟ قَالَ: اللهُمَّ صُبَّ عَلَيْهَا الْخَيْرَ صَبًّا، وَلَا تَجْعَلْ عَيْشَهَا كَدًّا كَدًّا قَالَ: فَمَا كَانَ فِي الْأَنْصَارِ أَيِّمٌ أَنْفَقَ منها."],"takhrij":"صحيح: رواه أحمد في مسنده (19784) عن عفان، ثنا حماد بن سلمة، عن ثابت، عن كنانة بن نعيم العدوي، عن أبي برزة الأسلمي فذكره.","grade":"صحيح","chapter_ar":"باب ما جاء في فضائل جليبيب","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب فضائل الصحابة وأخبارهم","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Authentic: Narrated by Aḥmad (19784).","chapter_en":"Reports Concerning the Virtues of Julaybīb","part_en":"The Book of the Virtues and Accounts of the Companions","group_ar":"مجموع فضائل أفراد الصحابة وأخبارهم","group_en":"A Collection of the Virtues and Reports of Individual Companions","part_no":49,"group_no":13,"chapter_no":30,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Abū Barzah al-Aslamī narrated: Julaybīb was a man who would pass by women and speak playfully with them. I said to my wife: “Do not allow Julaybīb to enter upon you, for if he enters, I will certainly do such-and-such.” Among the Anṣār, whenever a man had an unmarried daughter, he would not marry her off until he had first learned whether the Prophet ﷺ wished to marry her. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to a man from the Anṣār: “Give me your daughter in marriage.” The man replied: “Yes, with honor and delight, O Messenger of Allah. It would be a joy to me.” The Prophet ﷺ said: “I do not want her for myself.” The man asked: “For whom, then, O Messenger of Allah?” He replied: “For Julaybīb.” The man said: “O Messenger of Allah, I will consult her mother.” He went to her mother and said: “The Messenger of Allah ﷺ is seeking your daughter’s hand in marriage.” She replied: “Yes, with honor and delight.” He said: “He is not seeking her for himself. He is seeking her for Julaybīb.” She exclaimed: “Julaybīb? Julaybīb? Julaybīb? No, by Allah, we will not marry her to him!” When the father was about to leave to inform the Messenger of Allah ﷺ of what her mother had said, the young woman asked: “Who has proposed to you for me?” Her mother informed her. The young woman said: “Will you reject the command of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ? Give me to him in marriage, for he will never cause me to be lost.” Her father went to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and informed him. The Prophet ﷺ said: “Proceed with her.” He then married her to Julaybīb. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ later set out on a military expedition. After Allah granted him victory, he asked his Companions: “Are you missing anyone?” They replied: “We are missing so-and-so and so-and-so.” He asked: “Look again. Are you missing anyone?” They replied: “No.” He said: “But I am missing Julaybīb.” He then said: “Search for him among the slain.” They searched and found him beside seven enemy soldiers whom he had killed before they killed him.","They said: “O Messenger of Allah, here he is beside seven men whom he killed before they killed him.” The Prophet ﷺ came to him, stood over him, and said: “He killed seven, and then they killed him. He is from me, and I am from him. He is from me, and I am from him.” He repeated this two or three times. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ then carried him upon his forearms. Julaybīb had no bier except the forearms of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. A grave was dug for him, and he was placed within it. The narrator did not mention that he was washed. Thābit said: There was no previously unmarried or widowed woman among the Anṣār who possessed greater wealth than she did. Isḥāq ibn ʿAbdullāh ibn Abī Ṭalḥah informed Thābit and asked: “Do you know what the Messenger of Allah ﷺ supplicated for her?” He said: “O Allah, pour goodness upon her in abundance, and do not make her life one of hardship and toil.” There was no woman among the Anṣār who possessed greater wealth than she did."]}},"tuhfa":{},"voc":["fazail",335],"full":1,"dr":1,"rep":[13071],"tks":"صحيح: رواه أحمد (19784)."},{"num":10138,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ أَنَسٍ، قَالَ: كَانَ رَجُلٌ مِنْ أَصْحَابِ رَسُولِ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ يُقَالَ لَهُ: جُلَيْبِيبُ، فِي وَجْهِهِ دَمَامَةٌ، فَعَرَضَ عَلَيْهِ رَسُولُ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ التَّزْوِيجَ فَقَالَ: إِذًا تَجِدُنِي كَاسِدًا، فَقَالَ: غَيْرَ أَنَّكَ عِنْدَ اللَّهِ لَسْتَ بِكَاسِدٍ."],"takhrij":"حسن: رواه أبو يعلى (3343) عن محمد بن أبي بكر المقدمي، حدثنا ديلم بن غزوان، حدثنا ثابت، عن أنس فذكره.","grade":"حسن","chapter_ar":"باب ما جاء في فضائل جليبيب","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب فضائل الصحابة وأخبارهم","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Hasan: Narrated by Abū Yaʿlā (3343).","chapter_en":"Reports Concerning the Virtues of Julaybīb","part_en":"The Book of the Virtues and Accounts of the Companions","group_ar":"مجموع فضائل أفراد الصحابة وأخبارهم","group_en":"A Collection of the Virtues and Reports of Individual Companions","part_no":49,"group_no":13,"chapter_no":30,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Anas narrated: There was a man among the Companions of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ named Julaybīb, whose appearance was considered unattractive. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ proposed marriage to him. Julaybīb said: “Then you will find me unwanted.” The Prophet ﷺ replied: “Yet before Allah, you are not unwanted.”"]},"buhuth":{"en":["The word “كاسدًا” means someone who is unwanted or not sought after."]}},"tuhfa":{},"voc":["fazail",336],"full":1,"dr":1,"tks":"حسن: رواه أبو يعلى (3343)."},{"num":10139,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ أَنَسٍ قَالَ: خَطَبَ النَّبِيُّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ عَلَى جُلَيْبِيبٍ امْرَأَةً مِنَ الْأَنْصَارِ إِلَى أَبِيهَا، فَقَالَ: حَتَّى أَسْتَأْمِرَ أُمَّهَا، فَقَالَ النَّبِيُّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ: فَنَعَمْ إِذًا قَالَ: فَانْطَلَقَ الرَّجُلُ إِلَى امْرَأَتِهِ، فَذَكَرَ ذَلِكَ لَهَا، فَقَالَتْ: لَاهَا اللهُ إِذًا، مَا وَجَدَ رَسُولُ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ إِلَّا جُلَيْبِيبًا، وَقَدْ مَنَعْنَاهَا مِنْ فُلَانٍ وَفُلَانٍ؟ قَالَ: وَالْجَارِيَةُ فِي سِتْرِهَا تَسْتَمِعُ. قَالَ: فَانْطَلَقَ الرَّجُلُ يُرِيدُ أَنْ يُخْبِرَ النَّبِيَّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ بِذَلِكَ، فَقَالَتِ الْجَارِيَةُ: أَتُرِيدُونَ أَنْ تَرُدُّوا عَلَى رَسُولِ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ أَمْرَهُ؟ إِنْ كَانَ قَدْ رَضِيَهُ لَكُمْ، فَأَنْكِحُوهُ، قَالَ: فَكَأَنَّهَا جَلَّتْ عَنْ أَبَوَيْهَا، وَقَالَا: صَدَقْتِ. فَذَهَبَ أَبُوهَا إِلَى النَّبِيِّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ، فَقَالَ: إِنْ كُنْتَ قَدْ رَضِيتَهُ فَقَدْ رَضِينَاهُ. قَالَ: فَإِنِّي قَدْ رَضِيتُهُ. فَزَوَّجَهَا، ثُمَّ فُزِّعَ أَهْلُ الْمَدِينَةِ، فَرَكِبَ جُلَيْبِيبٌ فَوَجَدُوهُ قَدْ قُتِلَ، وَحَوْلَهُ نَاسٌ مِنَ الْمُشْرِكِينَ قَدْ قَتَلَهُمْ، قَالَ أَنَسٌ: فَلَقَدْ رَأَيْتُهَا وَإِنَّهَا لَمِنْ أَنْفَقِ ثَيِّبٍ فِي الْمَدِينَةِ."],"takhrij":"صحيح: رواه أحمد (12393)، عن عبدالرزاق –وهو في مصنفه (10333)- حدثنا معمر، عن ثابت البناني، عن أنس فذكره.وإسناده صحيح.","grade":"صحيح","chapter_ar":"باب ما جاء في فضائل جليبيب","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب فضائل الصحابة وأخبارهم","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Authentic: Narrated by Aḥmad (12393) through ʿAbd al-Razzāq, and it is also found in his Muṣannaf (10333). It was authenticated by Ibn Ḥibbān (4059).","chapter_en":"Reports Concerning the Virtues of Julaybīb","part_en":"The Book of the Virtues and Accounts of the Companions","group_ar":"مجموع فضائل أفراد الصحابة وأخبارهم","group_en":"A Collection of the Virtues and Reports of Individual Companions","part_no":49,"group_no":13,"chapter_no":30,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Anas narrated: The Prophet ﷺ proposed on behalf of Julaybīb to the father of a woman from the Anṣār. Her father said: “I must first seek her mother’s approval.” The Prophet ﷺ said: “That is appropriate.” The man went to his wife and informed her. She said: “No, by Allah! Could the Messenger of Allah ﷺ find no one but Julaybīb, when we have already refused her to so-and-so and so-and-so?” The young woman was listening from behind her curtain. When her father prepared to leave and inform the Prophet ﷺ of their refusal, she said: “Do you intend to reject the decision of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ? Since he has approved him for you, then marry me to him.” It was as though she removed all hesitation from her parents, and they said: “You have spoken the truth.” Her father went to the Prophet ﷺ and said: “Since you have approved him, we too approve him.” The Prophet ﷺ said: “I have indeed approved him.” He then married her to Julaybīb. The people of Madinah were later summoned to battle, and Julaybīb rode out with them. He was found slain, with a number of polytheists around him whom he had killed. Anas said: “I later saw his wife, and she was among the wealthiest previously married women in Madinah.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"voc":["fazail",337],"full":1,"dr":1,"rep":[13070],"tks":"صحيح: رواه أحمد (12393)، عن عبد الرزاق، وهو في مصنفه (10333)، وصححه ابن حبان (4059)."},{"num":10140,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ أَبِي قَتَادَةَ قَالَ:  خَطَبَنَا رَسُولُ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ فَقَالَ: إِنَّكُمْ تَسِيرُونَ عَشِيَّتَكُمْ وَلَيْلَتَكُمْ، وَتَأْتُونَ الْمَاءَ إِنْ شَاءَ اللَّهُ غَدًا، فَانْطَلَقَ النَّاسُ لَا يَلْوِي أَحَدٌ عَلَى أَحَدٍ، قَالَ أَبُو قَتَادَةَ: فَبَيْنَمَا رَسُولُ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ يَسِيرُ حَتَّى ابْهَارَّ اللَّيْلُ وَأَنَا إِلَى جَنْبِهِ، قَالَ: فَنَعَسَ رَسُولُ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ، فَمَالَ عَنْ رَاحِلَتِهِ، فَأَتَيْتُهُ فَدَعَمْتُهُ مِنْ غَيْرِ أَنْ أُوقِظَهُ حَتَّى اعْتَدَلَ عَلَى رَاحِلَتِهِ قَالَ: ثُمَّ سَارَ حَتَّى تَهَوَّرَ اللَّيْلُ مَالَ عَنْ رَاحِلَتِهِ قَالَ: فَدَعَمْتُهُ مِنْ غَيْرِ أَنْ أُوقِظَهُ حَتَّى اعْتَدَلَ عَلَى رَاحِلَتِهِ، قَالَ: ثُمَّ سَارَ حَتَّى إِذَا كَانَ مِنْ آخِرِ السَّحَرِ مَالَ مَيْلَةً هِيَ أَشَدُّ مِنَ الْمَيْلَتَيْنِ الْأُولَيَيْنِ حَتَّى كَادَ يَنْجَفِلُ، فَأَتَيْتُهُ فَدَعَمْتُهُ، فَرَفَعَ رَأْسَهُ، فَقَالَ: مَنْ هَذَا؟ قُلْتُ: أَبُو قَتَادَةَ، قَالَ: مَتَى كَانَ هَذَا مَسِيرَكَ مِنِّي؟ قُلْتُ: مَا زَالَ هَذَا مَسِيرِي مُنْذُ اللَّيْلَةِ، قَالَ: حَفِظَكَ اللهُ بِمَا حَفِظْتَ بِهِ نَبِيَّهُ، ثُمَّ."],"takhrij":"صحيح: رواه مسلم في المساجد (681-311) عن شيبان بن فروخ، حدثنا سليمان (يعني ابن المغيرة)، حدثنا ثابت، عن عبد الله بن رباح، عن أبي قتادة فذكره.والحديث بطوله مذكور في كتاب الأذان.","grade":"صحيح","chapter_ar":"فضل الحارث بن ربعي أبي قتادة الأنصاري","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب فضائل الصحابة وأخبارهم","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Authentic: Narrated by Muslim (681, no. 311).","chapter_en":"The Virtue of al-Ḥārith ibn Ribʿī, Abū Qatādah al-Anṣārī","part_en":"The Book of the Virtues and Accounts of the Companions","group_ar":"مجموع فضائل أفراد الصحابة وأخبارهم","group_en":"A Collection of the Virtues and Reports of Individual Companions","part_no":49,"group_no":13,"chapter_no":31,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Abū Qatādah narrated: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ addressed us and said: “You will travel during this evening and throughout the night, and, if Allah wills, you will reach water tomorrow.” The people set out, and no one turned aside to wait for another. Abū Qatādah said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ continued traveling until the night became very dark, and I was beside him. He became drowsy and leaned to one side of his riding animal. I came close and supported him without waking him until he sat upright again. He then continued traveling until the night became even darker. Again he leaned from his riding animal, so I supported him without waking him until he became upright. He continued onward until the final part of the night, when he leaned much more severely than on the previous two occasions and nearly fell. I came to him and supported him. He raised his head and asked: “Who is this?” I replied: “Abū Qatādah.” He asked: “How long have you been traveling beside me like this?” I replied: “I have remained beside you throughout the night.” He said: “May Allah protect you because of the way you protected His Prophet.” The narration continues."]}},"tuhfa":{},"voc":["fazail",338],"full":1,"tks":"صحيح: رواه مسلم (681/311)."},{"num":10141,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ حُمَيْدٍ، قَالَ: سَمِعْتُ أَنَسًا رَضِيَ اللَّهُ عَنْهُ يَقُولُ: أُصِيبَ حَارِثَةُ يَوْمَ بَدْرٍ وَهْوَ غُلاَمٌ، فَجَاءَتْ أُمُّهُ إِلَى النَّبِيِّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ، فَقَالَتْ: يَا رَسُولَ اللَّهِ، قَدْ عَرَفْتَ مَنْزِلَةَ حَارِثَةَ مِنِّي، فَإِنْ يَكُنْ فِي الْجَنَّةِ أَصْبِرْ وَأَحْتَسِبْ، وَإِنْ تَكُ الأُخْرَى تَرَى مَا أَصْنَعُ، فَقَالَ: وَيْحَكِ، أَوَهَبِلْتِ، أَوَجَنَّةٌ وَاحِدَةٌ هِيَ؟ إِنَّهَا جِنَانٌ كَثِيرَةٌ، وَإِنَّهُ فِي جَنَّةِ الْفِرْدَوْسِ."],"takhrij":"صحيح: رواه البخاري في المغازي (3982) عن عبد الله بن محمد، حدثنا معاوية بن عمرو، حدثنا أبو إسحاق (هو إبراهيم بن محمد الفزاري)، عن حميد (هو الطويل)، عن أنس قال: فذكره.","grade":"صحيح","chapter_ar":"باب أن حارثة بن سراقة بن الحارث الأنصاري في جنة الفردوس","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب فضائل الصحابة وأخبارهم","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Authentic: Narrated by al-Bukhārī (3982).","chapter_en":"Ḥārithah ibn Surāqah ibn al-Ḥārith al-Anṣārī Is in the Garden of al-Firdaws","part_en":"The Book of the Virtues and Accounts of the Companions","group_ar":"مجموع فضائل أفراد الصحابة وأخبارهم","group_en":"A Collection of the Virtues and Reports of Individual Companions","part_no":49,"group_no":13,"chapter_no":32,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Ḥumayd narrated: I heard Anas say: Ḥārithah was killed on the Day of Badr while he was still a young boy. His mother came to the Prophet ﷺ and said: “O Messenger of Allah, you know the place Ḥārithah held in my heart. If he is in Paradise, I will remain patient and seek reward from Allah. But if it is otherwise, then you will see what I will do.” He said: “Woe to you! Have you lost your mind? Is there only one garden? There are many gardens, and he is in the Garden of al-Firdaws.”"]},"buhuth":{"en":["The statement, “Ḥārithah was killed on the Day of Badr,” refers to Ḥārithah ibn Surāqah ibn al-Ḥārith ibn ʿAdī al-Anṣārī.","His father, Surāqah, was a Companion and was martyred on the Day of Ḥunayn.","His mother was al-Rubayyiʿ bint al-Naḍr, the paternal aunt of Anas ibn Mālik."]}},"tuhfa":{},"voc":["fazail",339],"full":1,"dr":1,"tks":"صحيح: رواه البخاري (3982)."},{"num":10142,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ عَائِشَةَ، رَضِيَ اللَّهُ عَنْهَا قَالَتْ: قَالَ رَسُولُ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ: نِمْتُ، فَرَأَيْتُنِي فِي الْجَنَّةِ، فَسَمِعْتُ صَوْتَ قَارِئٍ يَقْرَأُ، فَقُلْتُ: مَنْ هَذَا؟ قَالُوا: حَارِثَةُ بْنُ النُّعْمَانَ فَقَالَ رَسُولُ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ: كَذَلِكَ الْبِرُّ، وَكَانَ أَبَرَّ النَّاسِ بِأُمِّهِ."],"takhrij":"صحيح: رواه أحمد (24080، 25182)،وصحّحه ابن حبان (7014، 7015)، والحاكم (7247) كلهم من طريق معمر وسفيان بن عيينة، عن الزهري، عن عمرة، عن عائشة فذكرته.وإسناده صحيح.","grade":"صحيح","chapter_ar":"باب فضل حارثة بن النعمان","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب فضائل الصحابة وأخبارهم","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Authentic: Narrated by Aḥmad (24080, 25182), authenticated by Ibn Ḥibbān (7014, 7015), and recorded by al-Ḥākim (3/208).","chapter_en":"The Virtue of Ḥārithah ibn al-Nuʿmān","part_en":"The Book of the Virtues and Accounts of the Companions","group_ar":"مجموع فضائل أفراد الصحابة وأخبارهم","group_en":"A Collection of the Virtues and Reports of Individual Companions","part_no":49,"group_no":13,"chapter_no":33,"content":{"translation":{"en":["ʿĀ’ishah narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “I slept and saw myself in Paradise. I heard the voice of a reciter, so I asked: ‘Who is this?’ They replied: ‘This is Ḥārithah ibn al-Nuʿmān.’” The Messenger of Allah ﷺ then said: “Such is the reward of dutifulness. Such is the reward of dutifulness.” He was the most dutiful of people toward his mother."]}},"tuhfa":{},"full":1,"dr":1,"tks":"صحيح: رواه أحمد (24080، 25182)، وصححه ابن حبان (7014، 7015)، والحاكم (7247)."},{"num":10143,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ أَبِي هُرَيْرَةَ قَالَ: قَالَ رَسُولُ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ: بَيْنَا أَنَا فِي الْجَنَّةِ سَمِعْتُ صَوْتَ رَجُلٍ بِالْقُرْآنِ، فَقُلْتُ: مَنْ هَذَا؟ فَقَالُوا: هَذَا حَارِثَةُ بْنُ النُّعْمَانِ. كَذَلِكَ الْبِرُّ. كَذَلِكَ الْبِرُّ. كَذَلِكَ الْبِرُّ. وَكَانَ حَارِثَةُ مِنْ أَبَرِّ النَّاسِ."],"takhrij":"صحيح: رواه البخاري في خلق أفعال العباد (386)، والنسائي في الكبرى (8177)، والطبراني في الأوسط (4602) كلهم من طريق أبي بكر عبد الحميد بن أبي أويس (أخو إسماعيل بن أبي أويس)، عن سليمان بن بلال، عن موسى بن عقبة ومحمد بن أبي عتيق، عن ابن شهاب، عن سعيد بن المسيب، عن أبي هريرة قال: فذكره.","grade":"صحيح","chapter_ar":"باب فضل حارثة بن النعمان","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب فضائل الصحابة وأخبارهم","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Authentic: Narrated by al-Bukhārī in Khalq Afʿāl al-ʿIbād (386) and al-Nasā’ī in al-Sunan al-Kubrā (8177).","chapter_en":"The Virtue of Ḥārithah ibn al-Nuʿmān","part_en":"The Book of the Virtues and Accounts of the Companions","group_ar":"مجموع فضائل أفراد الصحابة وأخبارهم","group_en":"A Collection of the Virtues and Reports of Individual Companions","part_no":49,"group_no":13,"chapter_no":33,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Abū Hurayrah narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “While I was asleep and saw myself in Paradise, I heard the voice of a reciter. I asked: ‘Who is this?’ They replied: ‘This is Ḥārithah ibn al-Nuʿmān.’ Such is the reward of dutifulness. Such is the reward of dutifulness. Such is the reward of dutifulness.” He was among the most dutiful of people."]}},"tuhfa":{},"voc":["fazail",340],"full":1,"dr":1,"tks":"صحيح: رواه البخاري في خلق أفعال العباد (386)، والنسائي في الكبرى (8177)."},{"num":10144,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["حَدَّثَنِي أَبُو سَلَمَةَ، عَنِ الرَّجُلِ الَّذِي مَرَّ بِرَسُولِ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ، وَهُوَ يُنَاجِي جِبْرِيلَ عَلَيْهِ السلام، فَزَعَمَ أَبُو سَلَمَةَ أَنَّهُ تَجَنَّبَ أَنْ يَدْنُوَ مِنْ رَسُولِ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ، ثُمَّ تَخَوُّفًا أَنْ يَسْمَعَ حَدِيثَهُ، فَلَمَّا أَصْبَحَ قَالَ لَهُ رَسُولُ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ: مَا مَنَعَكَ أَنْ تُسَلِّمَ إِذْ مَرَرْتَ بِي الْبَارِحَةَ؟ قَالَ: رَأَيْتُكَ تُنَاجِي رَجُلًا، فَخَشِيتُ أَنْ تَكْرَهَ أَنْ أَدْنُوَ مِنْكُمَا، قَالَ: وَهَلْ تَدْرِي مَنِ الرَّجُلُ؟ قَالَ: لَا، قَالَ: فَذَلِكَ جِبْرِيلُ عَلَيْهِ السلام، وَلَوْ سَلَّمْتَ لَرَدَّ السَّلَامَ، وَقَدْ سَمِعْتُ مِنْ غَيْرِ أَبِي سَلَمَةَ أَنَّهُ حَارِثَةَ بْنَ النُّعْمَانِ."],"takhrij":"صحيح: رواه أحمد (16129) عن عفان، حدثنا وهيب (هو ابن خالد)، حدثنا موسى بن عقبة، حدثني أبو سلمة فذكره.وإسناده صحيح.","grade":"صحيح","chapter_ar":"باب ما جاء في أخبار حارثة بن النعمان","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب فضائل الصحابة وأخبارهم","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Authentic: Narrated by Aḥmad (16129).","chapter_en":"Reports Concerning Ḥārithah ibn al-Nuʿmān","part_en":"The Book of the Virtues and Accounts of the Companions","group_ar":"مجموع فضائل أفراد الصحابة وأخبارهم","group_en":"A Collection of the Virtues and Reports of Individual Companions","part_no":49,"group_no":13,"chapter_no":34,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Abū Salamah ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn ʿAwf narrated from the man who passed by the Messenger of Allah ﷺ while he was speaking privately with Jibrīl (Gabriel), peace be upon him. Abū Salamah said that the man refrained from approaching the Messenger of Allah ﷺ because he feared overhearing their private conversation. The following morning, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ asked him: “What prevented you from greeting me when you passed by me last night?” The man replied: “I saw you conversing privately with another man, and I feared that you might dislike my approaching the two of you.” The Prophet ﷺ asked: “Do you know who that man was?” He replied: “No.” The Prophet ﷺ said: “That was Jibrīl. Had you greeted us, he would have returned your greeting.” The narrator added: I heard from someone other than Abū Salamah that the man was Ḥārithah ibn al-Nuʿmān."]}},"tuhfa":{},"voc":["fazail",341],"full":1,"dr":1,"tks":"صحيح: رواه أحمد (16129)."},{"num":10145,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ عُبَيْدِ اللَّهِ بن أَبِي رَافِعٍ – هُوَ كاتب علي - قَالَ: سَمِعْتُ عَلِيًّا رَضِيَ اللَّهُ عَنْهُ يَقُولُ: بَعَثَنِي رَسُولُ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ أَنَا وَالزُّبَيْرَ وَالْمِقْدَادَ، فَقَالَ: انْطَلِقُوا حَتَّى تَأْتُوا رَوْضَةَ خَاخٍ، فَإِنَّ بِهَا ظَعِينَةً مَعَهَا كِتَابٌ فَخُذُوهُ مِنْهَا.قَالَ: فَانْطَلَقْنَا تَعَادَى بِنَا خَيْلُنَا حَتَّى أَتَيْنَا الرَّوْضَةَ، فَإِذَا نَحْنُ بِالظَّعِينَةِ، قُلْنَا لَهَا: أَخْرِجِي الْكِتَابَ.قَالَتْ: مَا مَعِي كِتَابٌ.فَقُلْنَا: لَتُخْرِجِنَّ الْكِتَابَ أَوْ لَنُلْقِيَنَّ الثِّيَابَ.قَالَ: فَأَخْرَجَتْهُ مِنْ عِقَاصِهَا، فَأَتَيْنَا بِهِ رَسُولَ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ، ، فَإِذَا فِيهِ: مِنْ حَاطِبِ بْنِ أَبِي بَلْتَعَةَ -إِلَى نَاسٍ بِمَكَّةَ مِنَ الْمُشْرِكِينَ- يُخْبِرُهُمْ بِبَعْضِ أَمْرِ رَسُولِ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ .فَقَالَ رَسُولُ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ: يَا حَاطِبُ مَا هَذَا؟.قَالَ: يَا رَسُولَ اللَّهِ، لاَ تَعْجَلْ عليَّ، إِنِّي كُنْتُ امرءا مُلْصَقًا فِي قُرَيْشٍ، يَقُولُ: كُنْتُ حَلِيفًا وَلَمْ أَكُنْ مِنْ أَنْفُسِهَا، وَكَانَ مَنْ مَعَكَ مِنَ الْمُهَاجِرِينَ مَنْ لَهُمْ بِهَا قَرَابَاتٌ يَحْمُونَ أَهْلِيهِمْ وَأَمْوَالَهُمْ، فَأَحْبَبْتُ إِذَا فَاتَنِي ذَلِكَ مِنَ النَّسَبِ فِيهِمْ أَنْ أَتَّخِذَ عِنْدَهُمْ يَدًا يَحْمُونَ قَرَابَتِي، وَلَمْ أَفْعَلْهُ ارْتِدَادًا عَنْ دِينِي، وَلاَ رِضًا بِالْكُفْرِ بَعْدَ الإِسْلاَمِ .فَقَالَ رَسُولُ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ: أَمَا إِنَّهُ قَدْ صَدَقَكُمْ.فَقَالَ عُمَرُ: يَا رَسُولَ اللَّهِ، دَعْنِي أَضْرِبْ عُنُقَ هَذَا الْمُنَافِقِ.فَقَالَ: إِنَّهُ قَدْ شَهِدَ بَدْرًا، وَمَا يُدْرِيكَ لَعَلَّ اللَّهَ قَدْ اطَّلَعَ عَلَى مَنْ شَهِدَ بَدْرًا، فَقَالَ: اعْمَلُوا مَا شِئْتُمْ، فَقَدْ غَفَرْتُ لَكُمْ.فَأَنْزَلَ اللَّهُ سورة الممتحنة: ﴿يَا أَيُّهَا الَّذِينَ آمَنُوا لَا تَتَّخِذُوا عَدُوِّي وَعَدُوَّكُمْ أَوْلِيَاءَ تُلْقُونَ إِلَيْهِمْ بِالْمَوَدَّةِ وَقَدْ كَفَرُوا بِمَا جَاءَكُمْ مِنَ الْحَقِّ يُخْرِجُونَ الرَّسُولَ وَإِيَّاكُمْ أَنْ تُؤْمِنُوا بِاللَّهِ رَبِّكُمْ إِنْ كُنْتُمْ خَرَجْتُمْ جِهَادًا فِي سَبِيلِي وَابْتِغَاءَ مَرْضَاتِي تُسِرُّونَ إِلَيْهِمْ بِالْمَوَدَّةِ وَأَنَا أَعْلَمُ بِمَا أَخْفَيْتُمْ وَمَا أَعْلَنْتُمْ وَمَنْ يَفْعَلْهُ مِنْكُمْ فَقَدْ ضَلَّ سَوَاءَ السَّبِيلِ﴾ [سورة الممتحنة: 1]."],"takhrij":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاري في المغازي (4274)، ومسلم في فضائل الصحابة (2494-161) كلاهما من طريق سفيان بن عيينة، عن عمرو بن دينار قال: أخبرني الحسن بن محمد، أنه سمع عبيد الله بن أبي رافع يقول: سمعت عليا يقول: فذكره.","grade":"متفق عليه","chapter_ar":"باب فضل حاطب بن أبي بلتعة","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب فضائل الصحابة وأخبارهم","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Agreed upon: Narrated by al-Bukhārī (4274) and Muslim (2494, no. 161).","chapter_en":"The Virtue of Ḥāṭib ibn Abī Baltaʿah","part_en":"The Book of the Virtues and Accounts of the Companions","group_ar":"مجموع فضائل أفراد الصحابة وأخبارهم","group_en":"A Collection of the Virtues and Reports of Individual Companions","part_no":49,"group_no":13,"chapter_no":35,"content":{"translation":{"en":["ʿUbaydullāh ibn Abī Rāfiʿ—the scribe of ʿAlī—narrated: I heard ʿAlī (may Allah be pleased with him) say: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ sent me, al-Zubayr, and al-Miqdād, saying: “Proceed until you reach Rawḍat Khākh. There you will find a woman carrying a letter. Take it from her.” We rode swiftly until we reached the place. There we found the woman, and we said: “Bring out the letter.” She replied: “I do not have any letter.” We said: “Either you produce the letter, or we will take off your clothes.” She then removed it from the braids of her hair. We brought it to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. It was a letter from Ḥāṭib ibn Abī Baltaʿah addressed to some of the polytheists in Makkah, informing them of part of the Messenger of Allah’s ﷺ plans. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ asked: “O Ḥāṭib, what is this?” Ḥāṭib replied: “O Messenger of Allah, do not be hasty in judging me. I was a man affiliated with Quraysh as an ally, but I was not one of them by lineage. The Emigrants who are with you have relatives in Makkah who protect their families and property. Since I did not possess such family ties, I wanted to establish a favor with them so they would protect my relatives. I did not do this out of abandoning my religion, nor because I was pleased with disbelief after embracing Islam.” The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “He has spoken the truth.” ʿUmar said: “O Messenger of Allah, allow me to strike the neck of this hypocrite.” The Messenger of Allah ﷺ replied: “He participated in Badr. And what makes you know? Perhaps Allah looked upon those who fought at Badr and said: ‘Do whatever you wish, for I have already forgiven you.’” Allah then revealed the opening verse of Sūrat al-Mumtaḥanah: “O you who believe, do not take My enemies and your enemies as allies, showing them affection while they have disbelieved in the truth that has come to you. They have driven out the Messenger and yourselves because you believe in Allah, your Lord. If you have gone forth striving in My cause and seeking My pleasure, do not secretly show them affection. I know best what you conceal and what you reveal. Whoever among you does that has certainly strayed from the straight path.” (Qur’an 60:1)"]},"buhuth":{"en":["The word “الظعينة” means a woman.","The wording states:","“The Messenger of Allah ﷺ sent me, al-Zubayr, and al-Miqdād.”","In another narration recorded by al-Bukhārī and Muslim, Marthad al-Ghanawī is mentioned instead of al-Miqdād.","Ibn Ḥajar commented:","“It is possible that all three accompanied him, and one narrator mentioned a companion whom the other narrator omitted.”","(Fatḥ al-Bārī, 7/520)."]}},"tuhfa":{},"full":1,"dr":1,"tks":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (4274)، ومسلم (2494/161)."},{"num":10146,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ جَابِرٍ  أَنَّ عَبْدًا لِحَاطِبٍ جَاءَ رَسُولَ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ يَشْكُو حَاطِبًا، فَقَالَ: يَا رَسُولَ اللَّهِ، لَيَدْخُلَنَّ حَاطِبٌ النَّارَ! فَقَالَ رَسُولُ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ: كَذَبْتَ، لَا يَدْخُلُهَا؛ فَإِنَّهُ شَهِدَ بَدْرًا وَالْحُدَيْبِيَةَ."],"takhrij":"صحيح: رواه مسلم في فضائل الصحابة (2195) من طرق عن الليث، عن أبي الزبير، عن جابر فذكره.","grade":"صحيح","chapter_ar":"باب فضل حاطب بن أبي بلتعة","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب فضائل الصحابة وأخبارهم","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Authentic: Narrated by Muslim (2495).","chapter_en":"The Virtue of Ḥāṭib ibn Abī Baltaʿah","part_en":"The Book of the Virtues and Accounts of the Companions","group_ar":"مجموع فضائل أفراد الصحابة وأخبارهم","group_en":"A Collection of the Virtues and Reports of Individual Companions","part_no":49,"group_no":13,"chapter_no":35,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Jābir narrated: A servant belonging to Ḥāṭib came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ complaining about him and said: “O Messenger of Allah, Ḥāṭib will certainly enter the Fire.” The Messenger of Allah ﷺ replied: “You have spoken falsely. He will not enter it, for he participated in the Battle of Badr and the Treaty of al-Ḥudaybiyah.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"voc":["fazail",343],"full":1,"rep":[10077,13326],"tks":"صحيح: رواه مسلم (2195)."},{"num":10147,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ أُمِّ مُبَشِّرٍ، قَالَتْ: جَاءَ غُلَامُ حَاطِبٍ، فَقَالَ: وَاللهِ لَا يَدْخُلُ حَاطِبٌ الْجَنَّةَ، فَقَالَ رَسُولُ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ: كَذَبْتَ، قَدْ شَهِدَ بَدْرًا وَالْحُدَيْبِيَةَ."],"takhrij":"صحيح: رواه أحمد (27045)، وابن أبي عاصم في الآحاد والمثاني (334)، والطبراني في الكبير (25/ح 265) كلهم من طريق معاوية بن عمرو، ثنا زائدة، عن سليمان – هو الأعمش-، عن أبي سفيان، عن جابر، عن أم مبشر قالت: فذكرته.","grade":"صحيح","chapter_ar":"باب فضل حاطب بن أبي بلتعة","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب فضائل الصحابة وأخبارهم","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Authentic: Narrated by Aḥmad (27045) and Ibn Abī ʿĀṣim in al-Āḥād wa al-Mathānī (334).","chapter_en":"The Virtue of Ḥāṭib ibn Abī Baltaʿah","part_en":"The Book of the Virtues and Accounts of the Companions","group_ar":"مجموع فضائل أفراد الصحابة وأخبارهم","group_en":"A Collection of the Virtues and Reports of Individual Companions","part_no":49,"group_no":13,"chapter_no":35,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Umm Mubashshir narrated: A servant of Ḥāṭib said: “By Allah, Ḥāṭib will never enter Paradise.” The Messenger of Allah ﷺ replied: “You have spoken falsely. He participated in the Battle of Badr and the Treaty of al-Ḥudaybiyah.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"voc":["fazail",344],"full":1,"dr":1,"rep":[10075],"tks":"صحيح: رواه أحمد (27045)، وابن أبي عاصم في الآحاد والمثاني (334)."},{"num":10148,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ عَائِشَةَ قَالَتْ: لَمَّا كَانَ يَوْمُ أُحُدٍ هُزِمَ الْمُشْرِكُونَ هَزِيمَةً بيِّنة، فَصَاحَ إِبْلِيسُ: أي عِبَادَ اللَّهِ أُخْرَاكُمْ، فَرَجَعَتْ أُولاَهُمْ عَلَى أُخْرَاهُمْ، فَاجْتَلَدَتْ أُخْرَاهُمْ، فَنَظَرَ حُذَيْفَةُ فَإِذَا هُوَ بِأَبِيهِ، فَنَادَى: أي عِبَادَ اللَّهِ أَبِي أَبِي، فَقَالَتْ: فَوَاللَّهِ مَا احْتَجَزُوا حَتَّى قَتَلُوهُ.فَقَالَ: حُذَيْفَةُ غَفَرَ اللَّهُ لَكُمْ.قَالَ أَبِي (يَعْنِي بِهِ هِشَامِ أَبَاهُ عُرْوَةَ): فَوَاللَّهِ مَا زَالَتْ فِي حُذَيْفَةَ مِنْهَا بَقِيَّةُ خَيْرٍ حَتَّى لَقِيَ اللَّهَ عَزَّ وَجَلَّ."],"takhrij":"صحيح: رواه البخاري في مناقب الأنصار (3824) عن إسماعيل بن خليل، أنا سلمة بن رجاء، عن هشام بن عروة، عن أبيه، عن عائشة قالت: فذكرته.","grade":"صحيح","chapter_ar":"باب ما جاء في فضائل حذيفة بن اليمان","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب فضائل الصحابة وأخبارهم","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Authentic: Narrated by al-Bukhārī (3824).","chapter_en":"Reports Concerning the Virtues of Ḥudhayfah ibn al-Yamān","part_en":"The Book of the Virtues and Accounts of the Companions","group_ar":"مجموع فضائل أفراد الصحابة وأخبارهم","group_en":"A Collection of the Virtues and Reports of Individual Companions","part_no":49,"group_no":13,"chapter_no":36,"content":{"translation":{"en":["ʿĀ’ishah narrated: On the Day of Uḥud, the polytheists suffered a decisive defeat. Then Satan cried out: “O servants of Allah, those behind you!” The Muslims at the front turned back toward those behind them, and the rear ranks began fighting. Ḥudhayfah looked and saw that his own father was among them, so he cried out: “O servants of Allah! My father! My father!” ʿĀ’ishah said: By Allah, they did not stop until they had killed him. Ḥudhayfah then said: “May Allah forgive you.” Hishām narrated from his father, ʿUrwah: By Allah, because of those words, goodness continued to remain with Ḥudhayfah until he met Allah, the Mighty and Majestic."]},"buhuth":{"en":["In another narration recorded by al-Bukhārī (3290):","“Ḥudhayfah said: ‘May Allah forgive you.’”","ʿUrwah said:","“The effect of that remained with Ḥudhayfah…”","The statement:","“By Allah, because of it, goodness remained in Ḥudhayfah…”","means that this lasting goodness was due to his saying:","“May Allah forgive you,”","together with his donating the blood money for his father to the Muslims.","The expression:","“Those behind you!”","may mean:","“Protect those who are behind you and support them,”","making the call appear to be directed at the Muslims.","It may also mean:","“Kill those behind you, for they are the polytheists who have attacked and caught up with you.”","This was all part of Satan’s deception and confusion.","The Muslims fell into that confusion, their swords became mixed in the chaos, and some unintentionally killed others. Among those killed in this confusion was al-Yamān, the father of Ḥudhayfah."]}},"tuhfa":{},"voc":["fazail",345],"full":1,"dr":1,"tks":"صحيح: رواه البخاري (3824)."},{"num":10149,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عن يَزِيدَ بْنِ شَرِيكٍ التميمي قَالَ: كُنَّا عِنْدَ حُذَيْفَةَ، فَقَالَ رَجُلٌ: لَوْ أَدْرَكْتُ رَسُولَ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ قَاتَلْتُ مَعَهُ وَأَبْلَيْتُ. فَقَالَ حُذَيْفَةُ: أَنْتَ كُنْتَ تَفْعَلُ ذَلِكَ! لَقَدْ رَأَيْتُنَا مَعَ رَسُولِ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ لَيْلَةَ الْأَحْزَابِ، وَأَخَذَتْنَا رِيحٌ شَدِيدَةٌ وَقُرٌّ، فَقَالَ رَسُولُ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ: أَلَا رَجُلٌ يَأْتِينِي بِخَبَرِ الْقَوْمِ، جَعَلَهُ اللَّهُ مَعِي يَوْمَ الْقِيَامَةِ. فَسَكَتْنَا، فَلَمْ يُجِبْهُ مِنَّا أَحَدٌ. ثُمَّ قَالَ: أَلَا رَجُلٌ يَأْتِينَا بِخَبَرِ الْقَوْمِ، جَعَلَهُ اللَّهُ مَعِي يَوْمَ الْقِيَامَةِ. فَسَكَتْنَا، فَلَمْ يُجِبْهُ مِنَّا أَحَدٌ. ثُمَّ قَالَ: أَلَا رَجُلٌ يَأْتِينَا بِخَبَرِ الْقَوْمِ، جَعَلَهُ اللَّهُ مَعِي يَوْمَ الْقِيَامَةِ. فَسَكَتْنَا، فَلَمْ يُجِبْهُ مِنَّا أَحَدٌ. فَقَالَ: قُمْ يَا حُذَيْفَةُ، فَأْتِنَا بِخَبَرِ الْقَوْمِ. فَلَمْ أَجِدْ بُدًّا، إِذْ دَعَانِي بِاسْمِي أَنْ أَقُومَ، قَالَ: اذْهَبْ فَأْتِنِي بِخَبَرِ الْقَوْمِ، وَلَا تَذْعَرْهُمْ عَلَيَّ. فَلَمَّا وَلَّيْتُ مِنْ عِنْدِهِ جَعَلْتُ كَأَنَّمَا أَمْشِي فِي حَمَّامٍ، حَتَّى أَتَيْتُهُمْ، فَرَأَيْتُ أَبَا سُفْيَانَ يَصْلِي ظَهْرَهُ بِالنَّارِ، فَوَضَعْتُ سَهْمًا فِي كَبِدِ الْقَوْسِ، فَأَرَدْتُ أَنْ أَرْمِيَهُ، فَذَكَرْتُ قَوْلَ رَسُولِ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ: وَلَا تَذْعَرْهُمْ عَلَيَّ. وَلَوْ رَمَيْتُهُ لَأَصَبْتُهُ، فَرَجَعْتُ وَأَنَا أَمْشِي فِي مِثْلِ الْحَمَّامِ، فَلَمَّا أَتَيْتُهُ فَأَخْبَرْتُهُ بِخَبَرِ الْقَوْمِ، وَفَرَغْتُ قُرِرْتُ، فَأَلْبَسَنِي رَسُولُ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ مِنْ فَضْلِ عَبَاءَةٍ كَانَتْ عَلَيْهِ يُصَلِّي فِيهَا، فَلَمْ أَزَلْ نَائِمًا حَتَّى أَصْبَحْتُ، فَلَمَّا أَصْبَحْتُ قَالَ: قُمْ يَا نَوْمَانُ."],"takhrij":"صحيح: رواه مسلم في الجهاد والسير (99:1788) عن زهير بن حرب وإسحاق بن إبراهيم جميعا عن جرير، عن الأعمش، عن إبراهيم التميمي، عن أبيه (يزيد بن شريك) قال: فذكره.","grade":"صحيح","chapter_ar":"باب ما جاء في فضائل حذيفة بن اليمان","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب فضائل الصحابة وأخبارهم","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Authentic: Narrated by Muslim (1788, no. 99).","chapter_en":"Reports Concerning the Virtues of Ḥudhayfah ibn al-Yamān","part_en":"The Book of the Virtues and Accounts of the Companions","group_ar":"مجموع فضائل أفراد الصحابة وأخبارهم","group_en":"A Collection of the Virtues and Reports of Individual Companions","part_no":49,"group_no":13,"chapter_no":36,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Yazīd ibn Sharīk al-Taymī narrated: We were sitting with Ḥudhayfah when a man said: “Had I lived during the time of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, I would have fought alongside him and distinguished myself.” Ḥudhayfah replied: “Would you really have done that? I was with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ on the night of the Battle of al-Aḥzāb (the Confederates). A fierce wind and bitter cold overtook us. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: ‘Is there anyone who will bring me news of the enemy? Allah will place him with me on the Day of Resurrection.’ We remained silent, and none of us answered him. He asked a second time: ‘Is there anyone who will bring us news of the enemy? Allah will place him with me on the Day of Resurrection.’ Again we remained silent, and no one answered. He asked a third time: ‘Is there anyone who will bring us news of the enemy? Allah will place him with me on the Day of Resurrection.’ Once more we remained silent. Then he said: ‘Stand up, O Ḥudhayfah, and bring us news of the enemy.’” When he called me by name, I had no choice but to stand. He said: “Go and bring me news of the enemy, but do not alarm them against me.” As I departed from him, it was as though I were walking in a warm bath, until I reached the enemy. There I saw Abū Sufyān warming his back by the fire. I placed an arrow in the middle of my bow and was about to shoot him, but I remembered the words of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ: “Do not alarm them against me.” Had I released the arrow, I would certainly have struck him. I returned, still feeling as though I were walking in a warm bath. When I reached the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and informed him of the enemy’s situation, the warmth left me and I began shivering from the cold. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ wrapped me in the extra portion of a cloak that he had been praying in. I remained asleep until morning. When morning came, he said: “Get up, O sleepy one.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"voc":["fazail",346],"full":1,"dr":1,"tks":"صحيح: رواه مسلم (99:1788)."},{"num":10150,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عن حُذَيْفَةَ قَالَ: فَأَتَيْتُ النَّبِيَّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ فَصَلَّيْتُ مَعَهُ الْمَغْرِبَ، فَصَلَّى حَتَّى صَلَّى الْعِشَاءَ ثُمَّ انْفَتَلَ فَتَبِعْتُهُ فَسَمِعَ صَوْتِي فَقَالَ: مَنْ هَذَا؟ حُذَيْفَةُ. قُلْتُ نَعَمْ. قَالَ: مَا حَاجَتُكَ غَفَرَ اللَّهُ لَكَ وَلأُمِّكَ. قَالَ إِنَّ هَذَا مَلَكٌ لَمْ يَنْزِلِ الأَرْضَ قَطُّ قَبْلَ هَذِهِ اللَّيْلَةِ، اسْتَأْذَنَ رَبَّهُ أَنْ يُسَلِّمَ عَلَىَّ وَيُبَشِّرَنِي بِأَنَّ فَاطِمَةَ سَيِّدَةُ نِسَاءِ أَهْلِ الْجَنَّةِ، وَأَنَّ الْحَسَنَ وَالْحُسَيْنَ سَيِّدَا شَبَابِ أَهْلِ الْجَنَّةِ."],"takhrij":"حسن: رواه الترمذيّ (3781) عن عبدالله بن عبدالرحمن، وإسحاق بن منصور، قالا: أخبرنا محمد بن يوسف، عن إسرائيل، عن ميسرة بن حبيب، عن المنهال بن عمرو، عن زرّ بن حبيش، عن حذيفة في حديث أطول منه، وهو مذكور في أبواب النوافل.","grade":"حسن","chapter_ar":"باب ما جاء في فضائل حذيفة بن اليمان","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب فضائل الصحابة وأخبارهم","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Hasan: Narrated by al-Tirmidhī (3781).","chapter_en":"Reports Concerning the Virtues of Ḥudhayfah ibn al-Yamān","part_en":"The Book of the Virtues and Accounts of the Companions","group_ar":"مجموع فضائل أفراد الصحابة وأخبارهم","group_en":"A Collection of the Virtues and Reports of Individual Companions","part_no":49,"group_no":13,"chapter_no":36,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Ḥudhayfah narrated: I came to the Prophet ﷺ and prayed the Maghrib prayer with him. He continued praying until he performed the ʿIshāʾ prayer. Then he left, and I followed him. When he heard my footsteps, he asked: “Who is this? Is it Ḥudhayfah?” I replied: “Yes.” He said: “What brings you here? May Allah forgive you and your mother.” Then he said: “This is an angel who had never descended to the earth before this night. He sought permission from his Lord to greet me and to give me the glad tidings that Fāṭimah is the leader of the women of Paradise, and that al-Ḥasan and al-Ḥusayn are the leaders of the young men of Paradise.”"]},"buhuth":{"en":["Al-Tirmidhī said:","“It is a good, strange narration.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"voc":["fazail",347],"full":1,"dr":1,"tks":"حسن: رواه الترمذي (3781). قال الترمذي: «حسن غريب»."},{"num":10151,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنِ ابْنِ عُمَرَ قَالَ: كُنْتُ عِنْدَ النَّبِيِّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ إِذْ جَاءَ حَرْمَلَةُ بْنُ زَيْدٍ، فَجَلَسَ بَيْنَ يَدَيْ رَسُولِ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ فَقَالَ: يَا رَسُولَ اللَّهِ، الْإِيمَانُ هَهُنَا، وَأَشَارَ إِلَى لِسَانِهِ، وَالنِّفَاقُ هَهُنَا، وَأَشَارَ إِلَى صَدْرِهِ، وَلَا يَذْكُرُ اللَّهَ إِلَّا قَلِيلًا، فَسَكَتَ عَنْهُ النَّبِيُّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ، فَرَدَّدَ ذَلِكَ عَلَيْهِ حَرْمَلَةُ، فَأَخَذَ النَّبِيُّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ بِطَرَفِ لِسَانِ حَرْمَلَةَ، فَقَالَ: اللَّهُمَّ اجْعَلْ لَهُ لِسَانًا صَادِقًا، وَقَلْبًا شَاكِرًا، وَارْزُقْهُ حُبِّي وَحَبَّ مَنْ يُحِبُّنِي، وَصَيِّرْ أَمْرَهُ إِلَى الْخَيْرِ. فَقَالَ حَرْمَلَةُ: يَا رَسُولَ اللَّهِ، إِنْ لِي إِخْوَانًا مُنَافِقِينَ، كُنْتُ فِيهِمْ رَأْسًا، أَلَا أَدُلَّكَ عَلَيْهِمْ؟ فَقَالَ النَّبِيُّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ: مَنْ جَاءَنَا كَمَا جِئْتَنَا اسْتَغْفَرْنَا لَهُ كَمَا اسْتَغْفَرْنَا لَكَ، وَمَنْ أَصَرَّ عَلَى ذَنْبِهِ فَاللَّهُ أَوْلَى بِهِ، وَلَا نَخْرِقُ عَلَى أَحَدٍ سِتْرًا."],"takhrij":"حسن: رواه الطبراني في الكبير (3475)، وابن منده في معرفة الصحابة (1/386)، وأبو نعيم في معرفة الصحابة (2/864) كلهم من طريق الهيثم بن خارجة، ثنا عبد الله بن عبد الرحمن بن يزيد بن جابر، عن أبي ذبحة، عن عطاء بن أبي رباح، عن ابن عمر فذكره.","grade":"حسن","chapter_ar":"باب فضائل حرملة بن زيد","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب فضائل الصحابة وأخبارهم","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Hasan: Narrated by al-Ṭabarānī in al-Muʿjam al-Kabīr (4:5–6) and by Ibn Mandah in Maʿrifat al-Ṣaḥābah (1/386).","chapter_en":"The Virtues of Ḥarmalah ibn Zayd","part_en":"The Book of the Virtues and Accounts of the Companions","group_ar":"مجموع فضائل أفراد الصحابة وأخبارهم","group_en":"A Collection of the Virtues and Reports of Individual Companions","part_no":49,"group_no":13,"chapter_no":37,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Ibn ʿUmar narrated: I was with the Prophet ﷺ when Ḥarmalah ibn Zayd came and sat before the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. He said: “O Messenger of Allah, faith is here,” and he pointed to his tongue. “And hypocrisy is here,” and he pointed to his chest. “And he remembers Allah only a little.” The Prophet ﷺ remained silent. Ḥarmalah repeated what he had said, and the Prophet ﷺ again remained silent. Then the Prophet ﷺ took hold of the tip of Ḥarmalah’s tongue and supplicated: “O Allah, grant him a truthful tongue, a grateful heart, provide him with love for me and love for those who love me, and direct all of his affairs toward goodness.” Ḥarmalah then said: “O Messenger of Allah, I have companions who are hypocrites, and I used to be one of their leaders. Shall I identify them for you?” The Prophet ﷺ replied: “No. Whoever comes to us as you have come, we seek Allah’s forgiveness for him just as we have sought forgiveness for you. Whoever persists in his sin, Allah is more deserving to deal with him. Do not tear away the veil that covers anyone.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"voc":["fazail",348],"full":1,"dr":1,"tks":"حسن: رواه الطبراني في الكبير (3462)، وابن منده في معرفة الصحابة (1/386)."},{"num":10152,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ أَبِي هُرَيْرَةَ،  أَنَّ عُمَرَ مَرَّ بِحَسَّانَ وَهُوَ يُنْشِدُ الشِّعْرَ فِي الْمَسْجِدِ، فَلَحَظَ إِلَيْهِ، فَقَالَ: قَدْ كُنْتُ أُنْشِدُ وَفِيهِ مَنْ هُوَ خَيْرٌ مِنْكَ! ثُمَّ الْتَفَتَ إِلَى أَبِي هُرَيْرَةَ، فَقَالَ: أَنْشُدُكَ اللَّهَ أَسَمِعْتَ رَسُولَ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ يَقُولُ: أَجِبْ عَنِّي، اللَّهُمَّ أَيِّدْهُ بِرُوحِ الْقُدُسِ؟ قَالَ: اللَّهُمَّ نَعَمْ."],"takhrij":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاري في بدء الخلق (3212)، ومسلم في فضائل الصحابة (2485-151) كلاهما من طرق عن سفيان بن عيينة، ثنا الزهري، عن سعيد بن المسيب، عن أبي هريرة قال: فذكره.","grade":"متفق عليه","chapter_ar":"باب ما جاء في فضائل حسان بن ثابت","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب فضائل الصحابة وأخبارهم","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Agreed upon: Narrated by al-Bukhārī (3212) and Muslim (2485, no. 151).","chapter_en":"Reports Concerning the Virtues of Ḥassān ibn Thābit","part_en":"The Book of the Virtues and Accounts of the Companions","group_ar":"مجموع فضائل أفراد الصحابة وأخبارهم","group_en":"A Collection of the Virtues and Reports of Individual Companions","part_no":49,"group_no":13,"chapter_no":38,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Abū Hurayrah narrated: ʿUmar once passed by Ḥassān while he was reciting poetry in the mosque. ʿUmar looked at him disapprovingly. Ḥassān said: “I used to recite poetry here while one who was better than you was present.” He then turned to Abū Hurayrah and said: “I ask you by Allah, did you hear the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: ‘Answer on my behalf. O Allah, support him with the Holy Spirit (Jibrīl).’?” Abū Hurayrah replied: “Yes, by Allah.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"voc":["fazail",349],"full":1,"dr":1,"rep":[3139,14598],"tks":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (3212)، ومسلم (2485/151)."},{"num":10153,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ أَبِي سَلَمَةَ بن عَبْدِ الرَّحْمَنِ بن عَوْفٍ أَنَّهُ سَمِعَ حَسَّانَ بْنَ ثَابِتٍ الأَنْصَارِيَّ يَسْتَشْهِدُ أَبَا هُرَيْرَةَ: أَنْشُدُكَ اللَّهَ، هَلْ سَمِعْتَ النَّبِيَّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ يَقُولُ: يَا حَسَّانُ، أَجِبْ عَنْ رَسُولِ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ، ، اللَّهُمَّ أَيِّدْهُ بِرُوحِ الْقُدُسِ قَالَ أَبُو هُرَيْرَةَ: نَعَمْ."],"takhrij":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاري في الصلاة (453) ومسلم في فضائل الصحابة (2485-152) كلاهما من طريق أبي اليمان الحكم بن نافع قال: أخبرنا شعيب، عن الزهري قال: أخبرني أبو سلمة فذكره.","grade":"متفق عليه","chapter_ar":"باب ما جاء في فضائل حسان بن ثابت","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب فضائل الصحابة وأخبارهم","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Agreed upon: Narrated by al-Bukhārī (453) and Muslim (2485, no. 152).","chapter_en":"Reports Concerning the Virtues of Ḥassān ibn Thābit","part_en":"The Book of the Virtues and Accounts of the Companions","group_ar":"مجموع فضائل أفراد الصحابة وأخبارهم","group_en":"A Collection of the Virtues and Reports of Individual Companions","part_no":49,"group_no":13,"chapter_no":38,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Abū Salamah ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn ʿAwf narrated: I heard Ḥassān ibn Thābit al-Anṣārī asking Abū Hurayrah to testify: “I ask you by Allah, did you hear the Prophet ﷺ say: ‘O Ḥassān, defend the Messenger of Allah. O Allah, support him with the Holy Spirit (Jibrīl).’?” Abū Hurayrah replied: “Yes.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"voc":["fazail",350],"full":1,"tks":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (453)، ومسلم (2485/152)."},{"num":10154,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ عَائِشَةَ رَضِيَ اللَّهُ عَنْهَا قَالَتِ: اسْتَأْذَنَ حَسَّانُ النَّبِيَّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ فِي هِجَاءِ الْمُشْرِكِينَ، قَالَ: كَيْفَ بِنَسَبِي. فَقَالَ حَسَّانُ: لأَسُلَّنَّكَ مِنْهُمْ كَمَا تُسَلُّ الشَّعَرَةُ مِنَ الْعَجِينِ. وَعَنْ أَبِيهِ قَالَ ذَهَبْتُ أَسُبُّ حَسَّانَ عِنْدَ عَائِشَةَ فَقَالَتْ لاَ تَسُبُّهُ فَإِنَّهُ كَانَ يُنَافِحُ عَنِ النَّبِيِّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ."],"takhrij":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاري في المناقب (3531) ومسلم في فضائل الصحابة (2489) كلاهما عن عثمان بن أبي شيبة، ثنا عبدة، عن هشام، عن أبيه، عن عائشة قالت: فذكرته.","grade":"متفق عليه","chapter_ar":"باب ما جاء في فضائل حسان بن ثابت","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب فضائل الصحابة وأخبارهم","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Authentic: Narrated by al-Bukhārī (3531) and Muslim (2489).","chapter_en":"Reports Concerning the Virtues of Ḥassān ibn Thābit","part_en":"The Book of the Virtues and Accounts of the Companions","group_ar":"مجموع فضائل أفراد الصحابة وأخبارهم","group_en":"A Collection of the Virtues and Reports of Individual Companions","part_no":49,"group_no":13,"chapter_no":38,"content":{"translation":{"en":["ʿĀ’ishah reported: Ḥassān sought the Prophet’s ﷺ permission to satirize the polytheists. The Prophet ﷺ asked: “What about my lineage?” Ḥassān replied: “I will separate you from them just as a hair is drawn out of dough.” And from his father, who said: I began speaking against Ḥassān in the presence of ʿĀ’ishah, but she said: “Do not speak against him, for he used to defend the Prophet ﷺ.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"full":1,"dr":1,"tks":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (3531)، ومسلم (2489)."},{"num":10155,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ مَسْرُوقٍ، قَالَ: دَخَلْنَا عَلَى عَائِشَةَ رَضِيَ اللَّهُ عَنْهَا وَعِنْدَهَا حَسَّانُ بْنُ ثَابِتٍ يُنْشِدُهَا شِعْرًا، يُشَبِّبُ بِأَبْيَاتٍ لَهُ، وَقَالَ: حَصَانٌ رَزَانٌ مَا تُزَنُّ بِرِيبَةٍ وَتُصْبِحُ غَرْثَى مِنْ لُحُومِ الْغَوَافِلِ فَقَالَتْ لَهُ عَائِشَةُ لَكِنَّكَ لَسْتَ كَذَلِكَ. قَالَ مَسْرُوقٌ فَقُلْتُ لَهَا لِمَ تَأْذَنِينَ لَهُ أَنْ يَدْخُلَ عَلَيْكِ. وَقَدْ قَالَ اللَّهُ تَعَالَى ﴿وَالَّذِي تَوَلَّى كِبْرَهُ مِنْهُمْ لَهُ عَذَابٌ عَظِيمٌ﴾ [سورة النور: 11]}. فَقَالَتْ وَأَىُّ عَذَابٍ أَشَدُّ مِنَ الْعَمَى. قَالَتْ لَهُ إِنَّهُ كَانَ يُنَافِحُ ـ أَوْ يُهَاجِي ـ عَنْ رَسُولِ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ."],"takhrij":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاري في المغازي (4146) ومسلم في فضائل الصحابة (2488) كلاهما عن بشر بن خالد، أنا محمد بن جعفر، عن شعبة، عن سليمان، عن أبي الضحى، عن مسروق قال: فذكره.وهذا لفظ مسلم ولفظ البخاري نحوه.","grade":"متفق عليه","chapter_ar":"باب ما جاء في فضائل حسان بن ثابت","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب فضائل الصحابة وأخبارهم","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Agreed upon: Narrated by al-Bukhārī (4146) and Muslim (2488).","chapter_en":"Reports Concerning the Virtues of Ḥassān ibn Thābit","part_en":"The Book of the Virtues and Accounts of the Companions","group_ar":"مجموع فضائل أفراد الصحابة وأخبارهم","group_en":"A Collection of the Virtues and Reports of Individual Companions","part_no":49,"group_no":13,"chapter_no":38,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Masrūq narrated: I entered upon ʿĀ’ishah while Ḥassān ibn Thābit was with her, reciting poetry that included the lines: A chaste and dignified woman, never suspected of wrongdoing, Who goes hungry rather than consume the flesh of the heedless. ʿĀ’ishah said to him: “But you are not like that.” Masrūq said: I asked her: “Why do you allow him to enter upon you when Allah has said: ‘And the one who took upon himself the greater share of it—for him is a tremendous punishment.’ (Qur’an 24:11)?” She replied: “What punishment is greater than blindness? Besides, he used to defend—or satirize in defense of—the Messenger of Allah ﷺ.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"full":1,"tks":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (4146)، ومسلم (2488)."},{"num":10156,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنِ الْبَرَاءِ رَضِيَ اللَّهُ عَنْهُ قَالَ: قَالَ النَّبِيُّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ لِحَسَّانَ: اهْجُهُمْ ـ أَوْ هَاجِهِمْ، ـ وَجِبْرِيلُ مَعَكَ."],"takhrij":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاري في بدء الخلق (3213) ومسلم في فضائل الصحابة (2486) كلاهما من طريق شعبة، عن عدي بن ثابت، عن البراء قال: فذكره.","grade":"متفق عليه","chapter_ar":"باب ما جاء في فضائل حسان بن ثابت","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب فضائل الصحابة وأخبارهم","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Agreed upon: Narrated by al-Bukhārī (3213) and Muslim (2486).","chapter_en":"Reports Concerning the Virtues of Ḥassān ibn Thābit","part_en":"The Book of the Virtues and Accounts of the Companions","group_ar":"مجموع فضائل أفراد الصحابة وأخبارهم","group_en":"A Collection of the Virtues and Reports of Individual Companions","part_no":49,"group_no":13,"chapter_no":38,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Al-Barāʾ ibn ʿĀzib narrated: The Prophet ﷺ said to Ḥassān: “Satirize them—or wage verbal battle against them—and Jibrīl (Gabriel) is with you.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"voc":["fazail",353],"full":1,"rep":[8940,12943],"tks":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (3213)، ومسلم (2486)."},{"num":10157,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ عَائِشَةَ أَنَّ رَسُولَ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ قَالَ:  اهْجُوا قُرَيْشًا، فَإِنَّهُ أَشَدُّ عَلَيْهَا مِنْ رَشْقٍ بِالنَّبْلِ! فَأَرْسَلَ إِلَى ابْنِ رَوَاحَةَ فَقَالَ: اهْجُهُمْ - فَهَجَاهُمْ، فَلَمْ يُرْضِ، فَأَرْسَلَ إِلَى كَعْبِ بْنِ مَالِكٍ، ثُمَّ أَرْسَلَ إِلَى حَسَّانَ بْنِ ثَابِتٍ، فَلَمَّا دَخَلَ عَلَيْهِ قَالَ حَسَّانُ: قَدْ آنَ لَكُمْ أَنْ تُرْسِلُوا إِلَى هَذَا الْأَسَدِ الضَّارِبِ بِذَنَبِهِ! ثُمَّ أَدْلَعَ لِسَانَهُ فَجَعَلَ يُحَرِّكُهُ، فَقَالَ: وَالَّذِي بَعَثَكَ بِالْحَقِّ لَأَفْرِيَنَّهُمْ بِلِسَانِي فَرْيَ الْأَدِيمِ. فَقَالَ رَسُولُ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ: لَا تَعْجَلْ، فَإِنَّ أَبَا بَكْرٍ أَعْلَمُ قُرَيْشٍ بِأَنْسَابِهَا، وَإِنَّ لِي فِيهِمْ نَسَبًا، حَتَّى يُلَخِّصَ لَكَ نَسَبِي. فَأَتَاهُ حَسَّانُ، ثُمَّ رَجَعَ فَقَالَ: يَا رَسُولَ اللَّهِ، قَدْ لَخَّصَ لِي نَسَبَكَ، وَالَّذِي بَعَثَكَ بِالْحَقِّ، لَأَسُلَّنَّكَ مِنْهُمْ كَمَا تُسَلُّ الشَّعَْرَةُ مِنَ الْعَجِينِ.","قالت عائشة: فسمعت رسول الله صلى الله عليه وسلم يقول لحسان: إن روح القدس لا يزال يؤيدك ما نافحت عن الله ورسوله.","وَقَالَتْ سَمِعْتُ رَسُولَ اللهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ يَقُولُ: هَجَاهُمْ حَسَّانُ فَشَفَى وَاشْتَفَى.","قال حسان:","هَجَوْتَ مُحَمَّدًا فَأَجَبْتُ عَنْهُ وَعِنْدَ اللهِ فِي ذَاكَ الْجَزَاءُ.","هَجَوْتُ مُحَمَّدًا بَرًّا تَقِيًّا رَسُولُ اللَّهِ شِيمَتَهُ الْوَفَاءَ.","فَإِنَّ أَبِي وَوَالِدَهُ وَعِرْضِي لِعِرْضِ مُحَمَّدٍ مِنْكُمْ وِقَاءُ.","ثَكِلْتُ بُنَيَّتِي إِنْ لَمْ تَرَوْهَا تُثِيرُ النَّقْعَ مِنْ كَنَفَيْ كَدَاءِ.","يُبَارِينَ الْأَعِنَّةَ مُصْعِدَاتٍ عَلَى أَكْتَافِهَا الْأَسَلُ الظِّمَاءُ.","تَظَلُّ جِيَادُنَا مُتَمَطِّرَاتٍ تُلَطِّمُهُنَّ بِالْخُمُرِ النِّسَاءُ.","فَإِنْ أَعْرَضْتُمُو عَنَّا اعْتَمَرْنَا وَكَانَ الْفَتْحُ وَانْكَشَفَ الْغِطَاءُ.","وَإِلَّا فَاصْبِرُوا لِضِرَابِ يَوْمٍ يُعِزُّ اللهُ فِيهِ مَنْ يَشَاءُ.","وَقَالَ اللهُ قَدْ أَرْسَلْتُ عَبْدًا يَقُولُ الْحَقَّ لَيْسَ بِهِ خَفَاءُ.","وَقَالَ اللهُ قَدْ يَسَّرْتُ جُنْدًا هُمُ الْأَنْصَارُ عُرْضَتُهَا اللِّقَاءُ.","لَنَا فِي كُلِّ يَوْمٍ مِنْ مَعَدٍّ سِبَابٌ أَوْ قِتَالٌ أَوْ هِجَاءُ.","فَمَنْ يَهْجُو رَسُولَ اللهِ مِنْكُمْ وَيَمْدَحُهُ وَيَنْصُرُهُ سَوَاءُ.","وَجِبْرِيلٌ رَسُولُ اللهِ فِينَا وَرُوحُ الْقُدْسِ لَيْسَ لَهُ كِفَاءُ."],"takhrij":"صحيح: رواه مسلم في فضائل الصحابة (2490) عن عبد الملك بن شعيب بن الليث، ثني أبي، عن جدي، ثني خالد بن يزيد، ثني سعيد بن أبي هلال، عن عمارة بن غزية، عن محمد بن إبراهيم، عن أبي سلمة بن عبد الرحمن، عن عائشة فذكرته.","grade":"صحيح","chapter_ar":"باب ما جاء في فضائل حسان بن ثابت","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب فضائل الصحابة وأخبارهم","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Authentic: Narrated by Muslim (2490).","chapter_en":"Reports Concerning the Virtues of Ḥassān ibn Thābit","part_en":"The Book of the Virtues and Accounts of the Companions","group_ar":"مجموع فضائل أفراد الصحابة وأخبارهم","group_en":"A Collection of the Virtues and Reports of Individual Companions","part_no":49,"group_no":13,"chapter_no":38,"content":{"translation":{"en":["ʿĀ’ishah reported that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Satirize Quraysh, for it is more severe upon them than being showered with arrows.” He sent for Ibn Rawāḥah and said: “Satirize them.” He satirized them, but it did not satisfy the intended purpose. So he sent for Kaʿb ibn Mālik, and then he sent for Ḥassān ibn Thābit. When Ḥassān entered, he said: “It is time for you to send for this lion striking with his tail.” Then he thrust out his tongue and began moving it, and said: “By the One who sent you with the truth, I shall tear them with my tongue just as leather is torn.” The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Do not be hasty. Abū Bakr is the most knowledgeable of Quraysh concerning their genealogies, and I share lineage with them. Let him distinguish my lineage for you.” Ḥassān went to Abū Bakr, then returned and said: “O Messenger of Allah, he has distinguished your lineage for me. By the One who sent you with the truth, I will separate you from them just as a hair is drawn from dough.” ʿĀ’ishah said: I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say to Ḥassān: “The Holy Spirit will continue to support you so long as you defend Allah and His Messenger.” And she said: I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: “Ḥassān satirized them, thereby bringing relief and satisfying the believers.” Ḥassān said: You satirized Muḥammad, so I answered in his defense,  And with Allah lies the reward for that. You satirized Muḥammad, righteous and upright,  The Messenger of Allah, whose character is faithfulness. Indeed, my father, his father, and my honor  Are a shield protecting Muḥammad’s honor from you. May my daughter lose me if you do not see our horses  Raising clouds of dust from the two sides of Kadāʾ. They race upward, straining against their reins,  While thirsting spears rest upon their shoulders. Our horses continue charging forward,  While women strike their faces with their head-coverings. If you turn away from us, we shall perform ʿUmrah,  And victory will come and the veil will be removed. Otherwise, then endure the blows of a day  On which Allah will grant honor to whomever He wills. Allah has said: “I have sent a servant  Who speaks the truth, in which there is no obscurity.”","And Allah has said: “I have prepared an army—  They are the Anṣār, whose readiness is for battle.” Every day we have with Maʿadd  Either an exchange of insults, fighting, or satire. The one among you who satirizes the Messenger of Allah, and the one who praises him and supports him, are the same. And Jibrīl, the messenger of Allah among us,  Is the Holy Spirit; none can equal him."]}},"tuhfa":{},"full":1,"rep":[9148],"tks":"صحيح: رواه مسلم (2490)."},{"num":10158,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عن الْحَسَنِ يَقُولُ: اسْتَقْبَلَ وَاللَّهِ الْحَسَنُ بْنُ عَلِيٍّ مُعَاوِيَةَ بِكَتَائِبَ أَمْثَالِ الْجِبَالِ، فَقَالَ عَمْرُو بْنُ الْعَاصِ: إِنِّي لأَرَى كَتَائِبَ لاَ تُوَلِّي حَتَّى تَقْتُلَ أَقْرَانَهَا. فَقَالَ لَهُ مُعَاوِيَةُ: ـ وَكَانَ وَاللَّهِ خَيْرَ الرَّجُلَيْنِ ـ أَىْ عَمْرُو، إِنْ قَتَلَ هَؤُلاَءِ هَؤُلاَءِ، وَهَؤُلاَءِ هَؤُلاَءِ، مَنْ لِي بِأُمُورِ النَّاسِ، مَنْ لِي بِنِسَائِهِمْ، مَنْ لِي بِضَيْعَتِهِمْ، فَبَعَثَ إِلَيْهِ رَجُلَيْنِ مِنْ قُرَيْشٍ مِنْ بَنِي عَبْدِ شَمْسٍ: عَبْدَ الرَّحْمَنِ بْنَ سَمُرَةَ، وَعَبْدَ اللَّهِ بْنَ عَامِرِ بْنِ كُرَيْزٍ، فَقَالَ: اذْهَبَا إِلَى هَذَا الرَّجُلِ، فَاعْرِضَا عَلَيْهِ، وَقُولاَ لَهُ، وَاطْلُبَا إِلَيْهِ. فَأَتَيَاهُ، فَدَخَلاَ عَلَيْهِ، فَتَكَلَّمَا، وَقَالاَ لَهُ، فَطَلَبَا إِلَيْهِ، فَقَالَ لَهُمَا الْحَسَنُ بْنُ عَلِيٍّ: إِنَّا بَنُو عَبْدِ الْمُطَّلِبِ، قَدْ أَصَبْنَا مِنْ هَذَا الْمَالِ، وَإِنَّ هَذِهِ الأُمَّةَ قَدْ عَاثَتْ فِي دِمَائِهَا. قَالاَ فَإِنَّهُ يَعْرِضُ عَلَيْكَ كَذَا وَكَذَا، وَيَطْلُبُ إِلَيْكَ وَيَسْأَلُكَ. قَالَ فَمَنْ لِي بِهَذَا؟ قَالاَ: نَحْنُ لَكَ بِهِ. فَمَا سَأَلَهُمَا شَيْئًا إِلاَّ قَالاَ: نَحْنُ لَكَ بِهِ. فَصَالَحَهُ، فَقَالَ الْحَسَنُ: وَلَقَدْ سَمِعْتُ أَبَا بَكْرَةَ يَقُولُ: رَأَيْتُ رَسُولَ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ عَلَى الْمِنْبَرِ، وَالْحَسَنُ بْنُ عَلِيٍّ إِلَى جَنْبِهِ، وَهْوَ يُقْبِلُ عَلَى النَّاسِ مَرَّةً، وَعَلَيْهِ أُخْرَى، وَيَقُولُ: إِنَّ ابْنِي هَذَا سَيِّدٌ، وَلَعَلَّ اللَّهَ أَنْ يُصْلِحَ بِهِ بَيْنَ فِئَتَيْنِ عَظِيمَتَيْنِ مِنَ الْمُسْلِمِينَ. قَالَ لِي عَلِيُّ بْنُ عَبْدِ اللَّهِ: إِنَّمَا ثَبَتَ لَنَا سَمَاعُ الْحَسَنِ مِنْ أَبِي بَكْرَةَ بِهَذَا الْحَدِيثِ."],"takhrij":"صحيح: رواه البخاري في الصلح (2704) عن عبد الله بن محمد، ثنا سفيان، عن أبي موسى قال: سمعت الحسن يقول: فذكره.","grade":"صحيح","chapter_ar":"باب ما جاء في فضل الحسن بن علي، وأنه سيد يصلح الله به بين فئتين من المسلمين","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب فضائل الصحابة وأخبارهم","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Authentic: Narrated by al-Bukhārī (2704).","chapter_en":"Reports Concerning the Virtue of al-Ḥasan ibn ʿAlī and That He Was a Leader Through Whom Allah Would Reconcile Two Groups of Muslims","part_en":"The Book of the Virtues and Accounts of the Companions","group_ar":"مجموع فضائل أفراد الصحابة وأخبارهم","group_en":"A Collection of the Virtues and Reports of Individual Companions","part_no":49,"group_no":13,"chapter_no":39,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Al-Ḥasan (al-Baṣrī) narrated: By Allah, al-Ḥasan ibn ʿAlī advanced toward Muʿāwiyah with armies like mountains. ʿAmr ibn al-ʿĀṣ said: “I see armies that will not retreat until they have destroyed one another.” Muʿāwiyah—who, by Allah, was the better of the two men in this matter—said: “O ʿAmr, if these kill those, and those kill these, who will look after the affairs of the people? Who will care for their women? Who will care for their properties?” He then sent two men from Quraysh, of Banū ʿAbd Shams—ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Samurah and ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿĀmir ibn Kurayz—and instructed them: “Go to this man, present my offer to him, negotiate with him, and seek reconciliation.” They came to al-Ḥasan, entered upon him, spoke with him, and presented Muʿāwiyah’s proposal. Al-Ḥasan ibn ʿAlī said: “We, the family of ʿAbd al-Muṭṭalib, have already received wealth from this treasury, and this nation has shed far too much of its own blood.” They replied: “He is offering you such-and-such and is asking you to accept peace.” Al-Ḥasan asked: “Will you guarantee that for me?” They replied: “We guarantee it.” Whatever he requested from them, they answered: “We guarantee it.” So al-Ḥasan concluded a peace treaty with Muʿāwiyah. Al-Ḥasan then said: I heard Abū Bakrah say: I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ upon the pulpit while al-Ḥasan ibn ʿAlī was beside him. The Prophet ﷺ would look at the people, then at al-Ḥasan, and say: “This son of mine is a leader, and perhaps Allah will bring about reconciliation through him between two great groups of the Muslims.” Abū ʿAbdullāh (al-Bukhārī) said: ʿAlī ibn ʿAbdullāh told me: “The only established narration proving that al-Ḥasan heard directly from Abū Bakrah is this hadith.”"]},"buhuth":{"en":["In another wording recorded by al-Bukhārī (7109):","“When al-Ḥasan ibn ʿAlī marched with the armies toward Muʿāwiyah, ʿAmr ibn al-ʿĀṣ said to Muʿāwiyah: ‘I see an army that will not turn back until its rear ranks are destroyed.’","Muʿāwiyah replied:","‘Who will care for the children of the Muslims?’","ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿĀmir and ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Samurah said:","‘Let us go to him and propose peace.’","The narration then continues with the hadith of Abū Bakrah.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"voc":["fazail",355],"full":1,"dr":1,"tks":"صحيح: رواه البخاري (2704)."},{"num":10159,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنِ أنَسَ قَالَ: رَأيْتُ رَسُولَ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ يَخْطُبُ، وَالْحَسَنُ بْنُ عَلِىٍّ عَلَى فَخِذِهِ وَيَقُولُ: إِنِّي لَأرَجُو أنٌ يَكُونُ ابْنِي هَذَا سَيّدًا، وَإِنِّي لَأرَجُو أنَ يُصْلِحْ اللَّهُ بِهِ بَيْنَ فِئَتَيْنِ مِنْ أمَتِي."],"takhrij":"حسن: رواه النسائي في عمل اليوم والليلة (253)، والبزار في مسنده (6664) كلاهما من طريق عن خالد بن الحارث، حدثنا أشعث، عن الحسن (هو البصري)، عن بعض أصحاب النبي صلى الله عليه وسلم، يعني أنسا قال: فذكره.","grade":"حسن","chapter_ar":"باب ما جاء في فضل الحسن بن علي، وأنه سيد يصلح الله به بين فئتين من المسلمين","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب فضائل الصحابة وأخبارهم","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Hasan: Narrated by al-Nasā’ī in ʿAmal al-Yawm wa al-Laylah (253) and by al-Bazzār in his Musnad (6664).","chapter_en":"Reports Concerning the Virtue of al-Ḥasan ibn ʿAlī and That He Was a Leader Through Whom Allah Would Reconcile Two Groups of Muslims","part_en":"The Book of the Virtues and Accounts of the Companions","group_ar":"مجموع فضائل أفراد الصحابة وأخبارهم","group_en":"A Collection of the Virtues and Reports of Individual Companions","part_no":49,"group_no":13,"chapter_no":39,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Anas narrated: I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ delivering a sermon while al-Ḥasan ibn ʿAlī was sitting upon his thigh. He said: “I truly hope that this son of mine will be a leader, and I hope that Allah will bring about reconciliation through him between two groups from my nation.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"voc":["fazail",356],"full":1,"dr":1,"tks":"حسن: رواه النسائي في عمل اليوم والليلة (253)، والبزار في مسنده (6664)."},{"num":10160,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنِ سَعِيدِ بْنِ أَبِي سَعِيدٍ الْمَقْبُرِيِّ قَالَ: كُنَّا مَعَ أَبِي هُرَيْرَةَ، فَجَاءَ الْحَسَنُ بْنُ عَلِيٍّ فسلَّم عَلَيْهِ، فَرَدَّ عَلَيْهِ الْقَوْمُ وَمَضَى، وَأَبُو هُرَيْرَةَ لَا يَعْلَمُ، فَقِيلَ لَهُ: هَذَا حَسَنُ بْنُ عَلِيٍّ يُسَلِّمُ، فَلَحِقَهُ فَقَالَ: وَعَلَيْكَ يَا سَيِّدِي، فَقِيلَ لَهُ: تَقُولُ: يَا سَيِّدِي؟ فَقَالَ: أَشْهَدُ أَنَّ رَسُولَ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ قَالَ: إِنَّهُ سَيِّدٌ."],"takhrij":"حسن: رواه النسائي في عمل اليوم والليلة (250)، وأبو يعلى (6561)، والطبراني في الكبير (2596) كلهم من طريق زيد بن الحباب، ثنا محمد بن صالح التمار المدني، حدثنا مسلم بن أبي مريم، عن سعيد بن أبي سعيد المقبري فذكره.","grade":"حسن","chapter_ar":"باب ما جاء في فضل الحسن بن علي، وأنه سيد يصلح الله به بين فئتين من المسلمين","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب فضائل الصحابة وأخبارهم","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Hasan: Narrated by al-Nasā’ī in ʿAmal al-Yawm wa al-Laylah (250), Abū Yaʿlā (6561), and al-Ṭabarānī in al-Muʿjam al-Kabīr (24/3).","chapter_en":"Reports Concerning the Virtue of al-Ḥasan ibn ʿAlī and That He Was a Leader Through Whom Allah Would Reconcile Two Groups of Muslims","part_en":"The Book of the Virtues and Accounts of the Companions","group_ar":"مجموع فضائل أفراد الصحابة وأخبارهم","group_en":"A Collection of the Virtues and Reports of Individual Companions","part_no":49,"group_no":13,"chapter_no":39,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Saʿīd ibn Abī Saʿīd al-Maqburī narrated: We were with Abū Hurayrah when al-Ḥasan ibn ʿAlī came and greeted us with salām. The people returned his greeting, and he continued on his way, while Abū Hurayrah had not realized who it was. Someone said to him: “That was al-Ḥasan ibn ʿAlī giving salām.” Abū Hurayrah hurried after him and said: “And peace be upon you, my master.” Someone asked him: “You call him ‘my master’?” He replied: “I bear witness that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: ‘Indeed, he is a leader (sayyid).’”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"voc":["fazail",357],"full":1,"dr":1,"tks":"حسن: رواه النسائي في عمل اليوم والليلة (250)، وأبو يعلى (6561)، والطبراني في الكبير (2596)."},{"num":10161,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عن الْبَرَاءِ بْنِ عَازِبٍ قَالَ: رَأَيْتُ النَّبِيَّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ وَالْحَسَنُ عَلَى عَاتِقِهِ يَقُولُ: اللَّهُمَّ إِنِّي أُحِبُّهُ فَأَحِبَّهُ."],"takhrij":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاري في فضائل الصحابة (3749)، ومسلم في فضائل الصحابة (2422-58) كلاهما من طريق شعبة، عن عدي –هو ابن ثابت-، ثنا البراء بن عازب قال: فذكره.","grade":"متفق عليه","chapter_ar":"باب في محبة النبي ﷺ للحسن بن علي وأخباره","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب فضائل الصحابة وأخبارهم","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Agreed upon: Narrated by al-Bukhārī (3749) and Muslim (2422, no. 58).","chapter_en":"The Prophet’s ﷺ Love for al-Ḥasan ibn ʿAlī and Reports About Him","part_en":"The Book of the Virtues and Accounts of the Companions","group_ar":"مجموع فضائل أفراد الصحابة وأخبارهم","group_en":"A Collection of the Virtues and Reports of Individual Companions","part_no":49,"group_no":13,"chapter_no":40,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Al-Barāʾ ibn ʿĀzib narrated: I saw the Prophet ﷺ carrying al-Ḥasan upon his shoulder, saying: “O Allah, I love him, so love him.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"voc":["fazail",358],"full":1,"tks":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (3749)، ومسلم (2422/58)."},{"num":10162,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ أَبِي هُرَيْرَةَ قَالَ:  خَرَجْتُ مَعَ رَسُولِ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ فِي طَائِفَةٍ مِنَ النَّهَارِ، لَا يُكَلِّمُنِي وَلَا أُكَلِّمُهُ، حَتَّى جَاءَ سُوقَ بَنِي قَيْنُقَاعَ، ثُمَّ انْصَرَفَ، حَتَّى أَتَى خِبَاءَ فَاطِمَةَ، فَقَالَ: أَثَمَّ لُكَعُ؟ أَثَمَّ لُكَعُ؟ يَعْنِي حَسَنًا، فَظَنَنَّا أَنَّهُ إِنَّمَا تَحْبِسُهُ أُمُّهُ لِأَنْ تُغَسِّلَهُ وَتُلْبِسَهُ سِخَابًا، فَلَمْ يَلْبَثْ أَنْ جَاءَ يَسْعَى، حَتَّى اعْتَنَقَ كُلُّ وَاحِدٍ مِنْهُمَا صَاحِبَهُ، فَقَالَ رَسُولُ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ: اللَّهُمَّ إِنِّي أُحِبُّهُ فَأَحِبَّهُ، وَأَحْبِبْ مَنْ يُحِبُّهُ."],"takhrij":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاري في البيوع (2122)، ومسلم في فضائل الصحابة (2421-57) كلاهما من طريق سفيان (هو ابن عيينة)، عن عبيد الله بن أبي يزيد، عن نافع بن جبير بن مطعم، عن أبي هريرة قال: فذكره، والسياق لمسلم.","grade":"متفق عليه","chapter_ar":"باب في محبة النبي ﷺ للحسن بن علي وأخباره","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب فضائل الصحابة وأخبارهم","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Agreed upon: Narrated by al-Bukhārī (2122) and Muslim (2421, no. 57). The wording here is that of Muslim.","chapter_en":"The Prophet’s ﷺ Love for al-Ḥasan ibn ʿAlī and Reports About Him","part_en":"The Book of the Virtues and Accounts of the Companions","group_ar":"مجموع فضائل أفراد الصحابة وأخبارهم","group_en":"A Collection of the Virtues and Reports of Individual Companions","part_no":49,"group_no":13,"chapter_no":40,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Abū Hurayrah narrated: I went out with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ during part of the day. Neither did he speak to me nor did I speak to him, until we reached the marketplace of Banū Qaynuqāʿ. He then returned and came to the tent of Fāṭimah and asked: “Is the little one here? Is the little one here?” He meant al-Ḥasan. We thought that his mother was keeping him briefly in order to wash him and adorn him with a necklace. Before long, al-Ḥasan came running. The Prophet ﷺ and al-Ḥasan embraced one another. Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “O Allah, I love him, so love him, and love whoever loves him.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"voc":["fazail",359],"full":1,"tks":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (2122)، ومسلم (2421/57)، والسياق لمسلم."},{"num":10163,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ أُسَامَةَ بْنِ زَيْدٍ رَضِيَ اللَّهُ عَنْهُمَا حَدَّثَ عَنِ النَّبِيِّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ أَنَّهُ كَانَ يَأْخُذُهُ وَالْحَسَنَ، فَيَقُولُ: اللَّهُمَّ أَحِبَّهُمَا فَإِنِّي أُحِبُّهُمَا."],"takhrij":"صحيح: رواه البخاري في فضائل الصحابة (3735) عن موسى بن إسماعيل، ثنا معتمر، قال: سمعت أبي، ثنا أبو عمثان، عن أسامة بن زيد فذكره.","grade":"صحيح","chapter_ar":"باب في محبة النبي ﷺ للحسن بن علي وأخباره","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب فضائل الصحابة وأخبارهم","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Authentic: Narrated by al-Bukhārī (3735).","chapter_en":"The Prophet’s ﷺ Love for al-Ḥasan ibn ʿAlī and Reports About Him","part_en":"The Book of the Virtues and Accounts of the Companions","group_ar":"مجموع فضائل أفراد الصحابة وأخبارهم","group_en":"A Collection of the Virtues and Reports of Individual Companions","part_no":49,"group_no":13,"chapter_no":40,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Usāmah ibn Zayd narrated that the Prophet ﷺ would take him together with al-Ḥasan and say: “O Allah, love them both, for indeed I love them both.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"voc":["fazail",360],"full":1,"rep":[10050,10095],"tks":"صحيح: رواه البخاري (3735)."},{"num":10164,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ زُهَيْرِ بْنِ الْأَقْمَرِ قَالَ: بَيْنَمَا الْحَسَنُ بْنُ عَلِيٍّ يَخْطُبُ بَعْدَمَا قُتِلَ عَلِيٌّ، رَضِيَ اللَّهُ عَنْهُ إِذْ قَامَ رَجُلٌ مِنَ الْأَزْدِ آدَمُ طُوَالٌ، فَقَالَ: لَقَدْ رَأَيْتُ رَسُولَ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ وَاضِعَهُ فِي حَبْوَتِهِ، يَقُولُ: مَنْ أَحَبَّنِي فَلْيُحِبَّهُ، فَلْيُبَلِّغِ الشَّاهِدُ الْغَائِبَ، وَلَوْلَا عَزْمَةُ رَسُولِ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ مَا حَدَّثْتُكُمْ."],"takhrij":"حسن: رواه أحمد (23106) عن محمد بن جعفر، حدثنا شعبة، عن عمرو بن مرة (هو الجملي)، عن عبد الله بن الحارث (هو الزبيدي)، عن زهير بن الأقمر قال: فذكره.ومن هذا الوجه صحّحه الحاكم (3/173-174).","grade":"حسن","chapter_ar":"باب في محبة النبي ﷺ للحسن بن علي وأخباره","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب فضائل الصحابة وأخبارهم","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Hasan: Narrated by Aḥmad (23106), and authenticated by al-Ḥākim (3/173–174).","chapter_en":"The Prophet’s ﷺ Love for al-Ḥasan ibn ʿAlī and Reports About Him","part_en":"The Book of the Virtues and Accounts of the Companions","group_ar":"مجموع فضائل أفراد الصحابة وأخبارهم","group_en":"A Collection of the Virtues and Reports of Individual Companions","part_no":49,"group_no":13,"chapter_no":40,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Zuhayr ibn al-Aqmar narrated: While al-Ḥasan ibn ʿAlī was delivering a sermon after the martyrdom of ʿAlī, a tall, dark-complexioned man from the tribe of Azd stood up and said: “I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ holding al-Ḥasan in his lap and saying: ‘Whoever loves me should love him. Let those who are present convey this to those who are absent.’” He then added: “Had it not been for the Messenger of Allah ﷺ charging us to convey it, I would not have related it to you.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"voc":["fazail",361],"full":1,"dr":1,"tks":"حسن: رواه أحمد (23106)، وصححه الحاكم (3/173–174)."},{"num":10165,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ مُعَاوِيَةَ، قَالَ: رَأَيْتُ رَسُولَ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ يَمُصُّ لِسَانَهُ - أَوْ قَالَ: شَفَتَهُ، يَعْنِي الْحَسَنَ بْنَ عَلِيٍّ صَلَوَاتُ اللَّهِ عَلَيْهِ - وَإِنَّهُ لَنْ يُعَذَّبَ لِسَانٌ أَوْ شَفَتَانِ مَصَّهُمَا رَسُولُ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ."],"takhrij":"صحيح: رواه أحمد (16848) عن هاشم بن القاسم، حدثنا حريز (هو ابن عثمان الرحبي)، عن عبد الرحمن بن أبي عوف الجرشي، عن معاوية فذكره.وإسناده صحيح.","grade":"صحيح","chapter_ar":"باب في محبة النبي ﷺ للحسن بن علي وأخباره","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب فضائل الصحابة وأخبارهم","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Authentic: Narrated by Aḥmad (16848).","chapter_en":"The Prophet’s ﷺ Love for al-Ḥasan ibn ʿAlī and Reports About Him","part_en":"The Book of the Virtues and Accounts of the Companions","group_ar":"مجموع فضائل أفراد الصحابة وأخبارهم","group_en":"A Collection of the Virtues and Reports of Individual Companions","part_no":49,"group_no":13,"chapter_no":40,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Muʿāwiyah narrated: I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ suck the tongue—or, as he said, the lips—of al-Ḥasan ibn ʿAlī. Muʿāwiyah added: “A tongue or lips that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ has sucked will never be punished.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"voc":["fazail",362],"full":1,"dr":1,"tks":"صحيح: رواه أحمد (16848)."},{"num":10166,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عن أنس قَالَ: لَمْ يَكُنْ أَحَدٌ أَشْبَهَ بِالنَّبِيِّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ مِنَ الْحَسَنِ بْنِ عَلِيٍّ."],"takhrij":"صحيح: رواه البخاري في فضائل الصحابة (3752) عن إبراهيم بن موسى، أنا هشام بن يوسف، عن معمر، عن الزهري، عن أنس، وقال عبد الرزاق: أنا معمر، عن الزهري، أخبرني أنس قال: فذكره.","grade":"صحيح","chapter_ar":"باب في محبة النبي ﷺ للحسن بن علي وأخباره","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب فضائل الصحابة وأخبارهم","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Authentic: Narrated by al-Bukhārī (3752).","chapter_en":"The Prophet’s ﷺ Love for al-Ḥasan ibn ʿAlī and Reports About Him","part_en":"The Book of the Virtues and Accounts of the Companions","group_ar":"مجموع فضائل أفراد الصحابة وأخبارهم","group_en":"A Collection of the Virtues and Reports of Individual Companions","part_no":49,"group_no":13,"chapter_no":40,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Anas narrated: No one resembled the Prophet ﷺ more than al-Ḥasan ibn ʿAlī."]}},"tuhfa":{},"voc":["fazail",363],"full":1,"tks":"صحيح: رواه البخاري (3752)."},{"num":10167,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ أَبِي جُحَيْفَةَ رَضِيَ اللَّهُ عَنْهُ قَالَ: رَأَيْتُ النَّبِيَّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ وَكَانَ الْحَسَنُ يُشْبِهُهُ."],"takhrij":"صحيح: رواه البخاري في المناقب (3543) عن أحمد بن يونس، ثنا زهير، ثنا إسماعيل –هو ابن أبي خالد-، عن أبي جحيفة قال: فذكره.","grade":"صحيح","chapter_ar":"باب في محبة النبي ﷺ للحسن بن علي وأخباره","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب فضائل الصحابة وأخبارهم","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Authentic: Narrated by al-Bukhārī (3543).","chapter_en":"The Prophet’s ﷺ Love for al-Ḥasan ibn ʿAlī and Reports About Him","part_en":"The Book of the Virtues and Accounts of the Companions","group_ar":"مجموع فضائل أفراد الصحابة وأخبارهم","group_en":"A Collection of the Virtues and Reports of Individual Companions","part_no":49,"group_no":13,"chapter_no":40,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Abū Juḥayfah narrated: I saw the Prophet ﷺ, and al-Ḥasan closely resembled him."]}},"tuhfa":{},"voc":["fazail",364],"full":1,"tks":"صحيح: رواه البخاري (3543)."},{"num":10168,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ عُقْبَةَ بْنِ الْحَارِثِ، قَالَ: رَأَيْتُ أَبَا بَكْرٍ رَضِيَ اللَّهُ عَنْهُ وَحَمَلَ الْحَسَنَ وَهْوَ يَقُولُ: بِأَبِي شَبِيهٌ بِالنَّبِيِّ، لَيْسَ شَبِيهٌ بِعَلِيٍّ. وَعَلِيٌّ يَضْحَكُ."],"takhrij":"صحيح: رواه البخاري في فضائل الصحابة (3750) عن عبدان، أنا عبدالله، أني عمر بن سعيد بن أبي حسين، عن ابن أبي مليكة، عن عقبة بن الحارث فذكره.","grade":"صحيح","chapter_ar":"باب في محبة النبي ﷺ للحسن بن علي وأخباره","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب فضائل الصحابة وأخبارهم","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Authentic: Narrated by al-Bukhārī (3750). Another wording appears in al-Bukhārī (3542).","chapter_en":"The Prophet’s ﷺ Love for al-Ḥasan ibn ʿAlī and Reports About Him","part_en":"The Book of the Virtues and Accounts of the Companions","group_ar":"مجموع فضائل أفراد الصحابة وأخبارهم","group_en":"A Collection of the Virtues and Reports of Individual Companions","part_no":49,"group_no":13,"chapter_no":40,"content":{"translation":{"en":["ʿUqbah ibn al-Ḥārith narrated: I saw Abū Bakr carrying al-Ḥasan while saying: “May my father be sacrificed for him! He resembles the Prophet ﷺ and does not resemble ʿAlī.” ʿAlī was present, smiling. In another wording recorded by al-Bukhārī: After leading the ʿAṣr prayer, Abū Bakr went out walking. He saw al-Ḥasan playing with the children, so he lifted him onto his shoulders."]}},"tuhfa":{},"voc":["fazail",365],"full":1,"dr":1,"tks":"صحيح: رواه البخاري (3750)، وفي لفظ له bukhari(3542)."},{"num":10169,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عن علي بن أَبِي طَالِبٍ خَطَبْتُ إِلَى النَّبِيِّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ ابْنَتَهُ فَاطِمَةَ، قَالَ: فَبَاعَ عَلِيٌّ دِرْعًا لَهُ، وَبَعْضَ مَا بَاعَ مِنْ مَتَاعِهِ، فَبَلَغَ أَرْبَعَ مِائَةٍ وَثَمَانِينَ دِرْهَمًا. قَالَ: وَأَمَرَ النَّبِيُّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ أَنْ يَجْعَلَ ثُلُثَيْهِ فِي الطِّيبِ، وَثُلُثًا فِي الثِّيَابِ، وَمَجَّ فِي جَرَّةٍ مِنْ مَاءٍ، فَأَمَرَهُمْ أَنْ يَغْتَسِلُوا بِهِ، قَالَ: وَأَمَرَهَا أَنْ لَا تَسْبِقَهُ بِرِضَاعِ وَلَدِهَا، قَالَ: فَسَبَقَتْهُ بِرَضَاعِ الْحُسَيْنِ وَأَمَّا الْحَسَنُ فَإِنَّ النَّبِيَّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ صَنَعَ فِي فِيهِ شَيْئًا لَا نَدْرِي مَا هُوَ، فَكَانَ أَعْلَمَ الرَّجُلَيْنِ."],"takhrij":"صحيح: رواه أبو يعلى (353) -ومن طريقه الضياء في المختارة (684)- وابن سعد في الطبقات (8/21) كلاهما من طريق المنذر بن ثعلبة، عن علباء بن أحمر، عن علي قال: فذكره.وإسناده صحيح.","grade":"صحيح","chapter_ar":"باب في محبة النبي ﷺ للحسن بن علي وأخباره","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب فضائل الصحابة وأخبارهم","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Authentic: Narrated by Abū Yaʿlā (353), through whom it was also narrated by al-Ḍiyāʾ in al-Mukhtārah (684), and by Ibn Saʿd in al-Ṭabaqāt (8/21).","chapter_en":"The Prophet’s ﷺ Love for al-Ḥasan ibn ʿAlī and Reports About Him","part_en":"The Book of the Virtues and Accounts of the Companions","group_ar":"مجموع فضائل أفراد الصحابة وأخبارهم","group_en":"A Collection of the Virtues and Reports of Individual Companions","part_no":49,"group_no":13,"chapter_no":40,"content":{"translation":{"en":["ʿAlī ibn Abī Ṭālib narrated: I proposed marriage to Fāṭimah, the daughter of the Prophet ﷺ. ʿAlī sold a coat of mail that he owned, along with some of his belongings, and the total came to four hundred and eighty dirhams. The Prophet ﷺ instructed that two-thirds of the money be spent on perfume and one-third on clothing. He then spat into a vessel of water and instructed them to bathe with it. He also instructed Fāṭimah not to nurse her child before bringing him to him. She nursed al-Ḥusayn before bringing him. As for al-Ḥasan, the Prophet ﷺ did something with his mouth that we do not know exactly what it was. As a result, al-Ḥasan became the more knowledgeable of the two brothers."]}},"tuhfa":{},"voc":["fazail",366],"full":1,"dr":1,"tks":"صحيح: رواه أبو يعلى (353)، ومن طريقه الضياء في المختارة (684)، وابن سعد في الطبقات (8/21)."},{"num":10170,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عن عَبْدِ اللَّهِ بن عُمَرَ عَمْرٍو قَالَ: رَأَيْتُ رَسُولَ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ عَلَى الْمِنْبَرِ يَخْطُبُ النَّاسَ، فَخَرَجَ الْحُسَيْنُ بْنُ عَلِيٍّ رَضِيَ اللَّهُ عَنْهُ فِي عُنُقِهِ خِرْقَةٌ يَجُرُّهَا، فَعَثَرَ فِيهَا فَسَقَطَ عَلَى وَجْهِهِ، فَنَزَلَ النَّبِيُّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ عَنِ الْمِنْبَرِ يُرِيدُهُ، فَلَمَّا رَآهُ النَّاسُ أَخَذُوا الصَّبِيَّ فَأَتَوْهُ بِهِ، فَأَخَذَهُ وَحَمَلَهُ فَقَالَ: قَاتَلَ اللَّهُ الشَّيْطَانَ، إِنَّ الْوَلَدَ فِتْنَةٌ، وَاللَّهِ وَاللَّهِ مَا عَلِمْتُ أَنِّي نَزَلْتُ عَنِ الْمِنْبَرِ حَتَّى أَتَيْتُ بِهِ."],"takhrij":"حسن: رواه الطبراني في الكبير (2626) عن عبد الله بن علي الجارودي النيسابوري، ثنا أحمد بن حفص، حدثني أبي، ثنا إبراهيم بن طهمان، عن عباد بن إسحاق، عن زيد بن أبي العتاب، عن عبيد بن جريج، عن عبد الله بن عمر فذكره.","grade":"حسن","chapter_ar":"باب في محبة النبي ﷺ للحسن بن علي وأخباره","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب فضائل الصحابة وأخبارهم","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Hasan: Narrated by al-Ṭabarānī in al-Muʿjam al-Kabīr (3/33–34).","chapter_en":"The Prophet’s ﷺ Love for al-Ḥasan ibn ʿAlī and Reports About Him","part_en":"The Book of the Virtues and Accounts of the Companions","group_ar":"مجموع فضائل أفراد الصحابة وأخبارهم","group_en":"A Collection of the Virtues and Reports of Individual Companions","part_no":49,"group_no":13,"chapter_no":40,"content":{"translation":{"en":["ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿUmar narrated: I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ delivering a sermon from the pulpit. Al-Ḥasan ibn ʿAlī came out wearing a garment around his neck that trailed behind him. He stumbled over it and fell on his face. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ immediately came down from the pulpit to go to him. When the people saw this, they picked up the child and brought him to the Prophet ﷺ. He carried him and said: “May Allah defeat Satan. Indeed, children are a trial. By Allah, I was not even aware that I had come down from the pulpit until he was brought to me.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"voc":["fazail",367],"full":1,"dr":1,"tks":"حسن: رواه الطبراني في الكبير (2613)."},{"num":10171,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ جَابِرٍ قَالَ: مَنْ سَرَّهُ أَنْ يَنْظُرَ إِلَى رَجُلٍ مِنْ أَهْلِ الْجَنَّةِ فَلْيَنْظُرْ إِلَى الْحُسَيْنِ بْنِ عَلِيٍّ، فَإِنِّي سَمِعْتُ رَسُولَ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ يَقُولُهُ."],"takhrij":"حسن: رواه أحمد في فضائل الصحابة (1372)، وأبو يعلى (1874)، وصحّحه ابن حبان (6966) كلهم من طريق الربيع بن سعد الجعفي، عن عبد الرحمن بن سابط، عن جابر بن عبد الله فذكره.","grade":"حسن","chapter_ar":"باب ما جاء في فضل الحسين بن علي","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب فضائل الصحابة وأخبارهم","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Hasan: Narrated by Aḥmad (1372), Abū Yaʿlā (1874), and authenticated by Ibn Ḥibbān (6966).","chapter_en":"Reports Concerning the Virtues of al-Ḥusayn ibn ʿAlī","part_en":"The Book of the Virtues and Accounts of the Companions","group_ar":"مجموع فضائل أفراد الصحابة وأخبارهم","group_en":"A Collection of the Virtues and Reports of Individual Companions","part_no":49,"group_no":13,"chapter_no":41,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Jābir ibn ʿAbdullāh narrated: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Whoever would be pleased to look at a man from the people of Paradise should look at al-Ḥusayn ibn ʿAlī.” Jābir said: “I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say this.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"voc":["fazail",368],"full":1,"dr":1,"tks":"حسن: رواه أحمد (1372)، وأبو يعلى (1874)، وصححه ابن حبان (6966)."},{"num":10172,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ يَعْلَى بْنِ مُرَّة أنهم خَرَجُوا مَعَ النَّبِيِّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ إِلَى طَعَامٍ دُعُوا لَهُ.فَإِذَا حُسَيْنٌ يَلْعَبُ فِي السِّكَّةِ.قَالَ: فَتَقَدَّمَ النَّبِيُّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ أَمَامَ الْقَوْمِ وَبَسَطَ يَدَيْهِ.فَجَعَلَ الْغُلاَمُ يَفِرُّ ههنا وههنا.وَيُضَاحِكُهُ النَّبِيُّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ حَتَّى أَخَذَهُ.فَجَعَلَ إِحْدَى يَدَيْهِ تَحْتَ ذَقَنِهِ، وَالأُخْرَى فِي فَأْسِ رَأْسِهِ فقبَّله.وَقَالَ: حُسَيْنٌ مِنِّي وَأَنَا مِنْ حُسَيْنٍ.أحبَّ اللَّهُ مَنْ أحبَّ حُسَيْنًا.حُسَيْنٌ سِبْطٌ مِنَ الأَسْبَاطِ."],"takhrij":"حسن: رواه الترمذي (3775)، وابن ماجه (144) –والسياق له-، وأحمد (17561)، وصحّحه ابن حبان (6971)، والحاكم (3/177) كلهم من طرق عن عبد الله بن عثمان بن خثيم، عن سعيد بن أبي راشد، عن يعلى بن مرة فذكره.","grade":"حسن","chapter_ar":"باب ما جاء في فضل الحسين بن علي","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب فضائل الصحابة وأخبارهم","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Hasan: Narrated by al-Tirmidhī (3775), Ibn Mājah (144)—whose wording is used here—and al-Bukhārī in al-Adab al-Mufrad (364).","chapter_en":"Reports Concerning the Virtues of al-Ḥusayn ibn ʿAlī","part_en":"The Book of the Virtues and Accounts of the Companions","group_ar":"مجموع فضائل أفراد الصحابة وأخبارهم","group_en":"A Collection of the Virtues and Reports of Individual Companions","part_no":49,"group_no":13,"chapter_no":41,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Yaʿlā ibn Murrah narrated: We went out with the Prophet ﷺ to a meal to which he had been invited. Along the way, al-Ḥusayn was playing in the street. The Prophet ﷺ went ahead of the people and stretched out his arms toward him. The child ran this way and that, playfully, while the Prophet ﷺ smiled and played with him until he caught him. He placed one hand beneath al-Ḥusayn’s chin and the other behind his head, then kissed him and said: “Ḥusayn is from me, and I am from Ḥusayn. May Allah love whoever loves Ḥusayn. Ḥusayn is a branch among the great branches.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"voc":["fazail",369],"full":1,"dr":1,"tks":"حسن: رواه الترمذي (3775)، وابن ماجه (144) – واللفظ له –، والبخاري في الأدب المفرد (364)."},{"num":10173,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ أَنَسِ بْنِ مَالِكٍ رَضِيَ اللَّهُ عَنْهُ أُتِيَ عُبَيْدُ اللَّهِ بْنُ زِيَادٍ بِرَأْسِ الْحُسَيْنِ ـ عَلَيْهِ السَّلاَمُ، ـ فَجُعِلَ فِي طَسْتٍ، فَجَعَلَ يَنْكُتُ، وَقَالَ فِي حُسْنِهِ شَيْئًا. فَقَالَ أَنَسٌ: كَانَ أَشْبَهَهُمْ بِرَسُولِ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ، وَكَانَ مَخْضُوبًا بِالْوَسْمَةِ."],"takhrij":"صحيح: رواه البخاري في فضائل الصحابة (3748) عن محمد بن الحسين بن إبراهيم، حدثني حسين بن محمد، ثنا جرير، عن محمد، عن أنس بن مالك فذكره.","grade":"صحيح","chapter_ar":"باب ما جاء في فضل الحسين بن علي","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب فضائل الصحابة وأخبارهم","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Authentic: Narrated by al-Bukhārī (3748).","chapter_en":"Reports Concerning the Virtues of al-Ḥusayn ibn ʿAlī","part_en":"The Book of the Virtues and Accounts of the Companions","group_ar":"مجموع فضائل أفراد الصحابة وأخبارهم","group_en":"A Collection of the Virtues and Reports of Individual Companions","part_no":49,"group_no":13,"chapter_no":41,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Anas ibn Mālik narrated: The head of al-Ḥusayn, peace be upon him, was brought to ʿUbaydullāh ibn Ziyād and placed in a basin. He began striking it with a stick and made a remark about al-Ḥusayn’s appearance. Anas said: “He was the one who most closely resembled the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and his hair had been dyed with wasmah (a dark herbal dye).”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"voc":["fazail",370],"full":1,"tks":"صحيح: رواه البخاري (3748)."},{"num":10174,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ عَبْدِ اللَّهِ الْبَهِيِّ مَوْلَى الزُّبَيْرِ، قَالَ: كُنْتُ فِي الْمَسْجِدِ، وَمَرْوَانُ يَخْطُبُ، فَقَالَ عَبْدُ الرَّحْمَنِ بْنُ أَبِي بَكْرٍ: وَاللَّهِ مَا اسْتَخْلَفَ أَحَدًا مِنْ أَهْلِهِ، فَقَالَ: مَرْوَانُ: أَنْتَ الَّذِي نَزَلَتْ فِيكَ: ﴿وَالَّذِي قَالَ لِوَالِدَيْهِ أُفٍّ لَكُمَا﴾ [الأحقاف: ١٧]، فَقَالَ عَبْدُ الرَّحْمَنِ: كَذَبْتَ، وَلَكِنَّ رَسُولَ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ لَعَنَ أَبَاكَ."],"takhrij":"حسن: رواه البزار (2273) عن يوسف بن موسى، حدثنا عبد الرحمن بن مغراء، حدثنا إسماعيل بن أبي خالد، عن عبدالله البهي مولى الزبير قال: فذكره.","grade":"حسن","chapter_ar":"باب ما جاء في أخبار الحكم بن أبي العاص","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب فضائل الصحابة وأخبارهم","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Hasan: Narrated by al-Bazzār (2273).","chapter_en":"Reports Concerning al-Ḥakam ibn Abī al-ʿĀṣ","part_en":"The Book of the Virtues and Accounts of the Companions","group_ar":"مجموع فضائل أفراد الصحابة وأخبارهم","group_en":"A Collection of the Virtues and Reports of Individual Companions","part_no":49,"group_no":13,"chapter_no":42,"content":{"translation":{"en":["ʿAbdullāh al-Bahī, the freedman of al-Zubayr, narrated: I was in the mosque while Marwān was delivering a sermon. ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Abī Bakr said: “By Allah, he did not appoint one of his own family as successor.” Marwān replied: “You are the one concerning whom the verse was revealed: ʿBut the one who says to his parents, “Fie upon you both…”’ (Qur’an 46:17).” ʿAbd al-Raḥmān responded: “You have lied. Rather, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ cursed your father.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"full":1,"dr":1,"tks":"حسن: رواه البزار (2273)."},{"num":10175,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنِ الشَّعْبِيِّ قَالَ: سَمِعْتُ عَبْدَ الله بنَ الزُّبَيْرِ وَهُوَ مُسْتَنِدٌ إِلَى الْكَعْبَةِ وَهُوَ يَقُولُ: وَرَبِّ هَذِهِ الْكَعْبَةِ، لَقَدْ لَعَنَ رَسُولُ الله صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ فُلَانًا، وَمَا وُلِدَ مِنْ صُلْبِهِ.","وفي رواية: لقد لعنَ الله الحكمَ وما ولدَ على لسانه نبيه صلى الله عليه وسلم."],"takhrij":"صحيح: رواه أحمد (16128)، والبزار – كشف الأستار (1623) كلاهما من طريق عبدالرزاق، أخبرنا ابنُ عيينة، عن إسماعيل بن أبي خالد، عن الشعبي قال: فذكره.","grade":"صحيح","chapter_ar":"باب ما جاء في أخبار الحكم بن أبي العاص","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب فضائل الصحابة وأخبارهم","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Authentic: Narrated by Aḥmad (16128) and al-Bazzār in Kashf al-Astār (1623).","chapter_en":"Reports Concerning al-Ḥakam ibn Abī al-ʿĀṣ","part_en":"The Book of the Virtues and Accounts of the Companions","group_ar":"مجموع فضائل أفراد الصحابة وأخبارهم","group_en":"A Collection of the Virtues and Reports of Individual Companions","part_no":49,"group_no":13,"chapter_no":42,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Al-Shaʿbī narrated: I heard ʿAbdullāh ibn al-Zubayr, while leaning against the Kaʿbah, say: “By the Lord of this Kaʿbah, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ cursed so-and-so and those born from his lineage.” In another narration: “Allah cursed al-Ḥakam and his offspring upon the tongue of His Prophet ﷺ.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"voc":["fazail",372],"full":1,"dr":1,"tks":"صحيح: رواه أحمد (16128)، والبزار في كشف الأستار (1623)."},{"num":10176,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ عَبْدِ الله بْنِ عَمْرٍو قَالَ: كُنَّا جُلُوسًا عِنْدَ النَّبِيِّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ، وَقَدْ ذَهَبَ عَمْرُو بْنُ الْعَاصِ يَلْبَسُ ثِيَابَهُ لِيَلْحَقَنِي، فَقَالَ وَنَحْنُ عِنْدَهُ :لَيَدْخُلَنَّ عَلَيْكُمْ رَجُلٌ لَعِينٌ فَوَالله مَا زِلْتُ وَجِلًا أَتَشَوَّفُ دَاخِلًا وَخَارِجًا حَتَّى دَخَلَ فُلَانٌ يَعْنِي الحَكَمَ."],"takhrij":"صحيح: رواه أحمد (6520)، والبزار –كشف الأستار (1625)، والطبراني في الأوسط (7155) كلهم من طريق عبدالله بن نمير، حدثنا عثمان بن حكيم، عن أبي أمامة بن سهل بن حنيف، عن عبد الله بن عمرو قال: فذكره.","grade":"صحيح","chapter_ar":"باب ما جاء في أخبار الحكم بن أبي العاص","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب فضائل الصحابة وأخبارهم","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Authentic: Narrated by Aḥmad (6520) and al-Bazzār in Kashf al-Astār (1625).","chapter_en":"Reports Concerning al-Ḥakam ibn Abī al-ʿĀṣ","part_en":"The Book of the Virtues and Accounts of the Companions","group_ar":"مجموع فضائل أفراد الصحابة وأخبارهم","group_en":"A Collection of the Virtues and Reports of Individual Companions","part_no":49,"group_no":13,"chapter_no":42,"content":{"translation":{"en":["ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿAmr narrated: We were sitting with the Prophet ﷺ while ʿAmr ibn al-ʿĀṣ had gone to put on his clothes so that he could join us. While we were sitting there, the Prophet ﷺ said: “A cursed man is about to enter upon you.” I remained anxious, watching everyone who entered and left, until that man entered—the narrator explained that it was al-Ḥakam."]}},"tuhfa":{},"voc":["fazail",373],"full":1,"dr":1,"tks":"صحيح: رواه أحمد (6520)، والبزار في كشف الأستار (1625)."},{"num":10177,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ جَابِرٍ قَالَ: قَالَ رَسُولُ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ: أَفْضَلُ الشُّهَدَاءِ عِنْدَ اللَّهِ حَمْزَةُ بْنُ عَبْدِ الْمُطَّلِبِ."],"takhrij":"حسن: رواه الطبراني في الأوسط (922) عن أحمد (يعني ابن يحيى الحلواني)، حدثنا عمار بن نصر، حدثنا حكيم بن زيد، عن إبراهيم الصائغ، عن عكرمة، عن جابر بن عبد الله فذكره.","grade":"حسن","chapter_ar":"باب ما جاء في فضل حمزة بن عبد المطلب","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب فضائل الصحابة وأخبارهم","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Hasan: Narrated by al-Ṭabarānī in al-Muʿjam al-Awsaṭ (922).","chapter_en":"The Virtues of Ḥamzah ibn ʿAbd al-Muṭṭalib","part_en":"The Book of the Virtues and Accounts of the Companions","group_ar":"مجموع فضائل أفراد الصحابة وأخبارهم","group_en":"A Collection of the Virtues and Reports of Individual Companions","part_no":49,"group_no":13,"chapter_no":43,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Jābir ibn ʿAbdullāh narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “The best of the martyrs in the sight of Allah is Ḥamzah ibn ʿAbd al-Muṭṭalib.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"voc":["fazail",374],"full":1,"dr":1,"tks":"حسن: رواه الطبراني في الأوسط (922)."},{"num":10178,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ أَنَسٍ ـ رَضِيَ اللَّهُ عَنْهُ أَنَّ النَّبِيَّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ نَعَى زَيْدًا وَجَعْفَرًا وَابْنَ رَوَاحَةَ لِلنَّاسِ قَبْلَ أَنْ يَأْتِيَهُمْ خَبَرُهُمْ، فَقَالَ: أَخَذَ الرَّايَةَ زَيْدٌ فَأُصِيبَ، ثُمَّ أَخَذَ جَعْفَرٌ فَأُصِيبَ، ثُمَّ أَخَذَ ابْنُ رَوَاحَةَ فَأُصِيبَ، ـ وَعَيْنَاهُ تَذْرِفَانِ ـ حَتَّى أَخَذَ سَيْفٌ مِنْ سُيُوفِ اللَّهِ، حَتَّى فَتَحَ اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِمْ."],"takhrij":"صحيح: رواه البخاري في فضائل الصحابة (3757) وفي المغازي bukhari(4262) عن أحمد بن واقد، ثنا حماد بن زيد، عن أيوب، عن حميد بن هلال، عن أنس فذكره.","grade":"صحيح","chapter_ar":"باب في فضل خالد بن الوليد وأخباره","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب فضائل الصحابة وأخبارهم","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Authentic: Narrated by al-Bukhārī (3757, 4262).","chapter_en":"The Virtues of Khālid ibn al-Walīd and Reports Concerning Him","part_en":"The Book of the Virtues and Accounts of the Companions","group_ar":"مجموع فضائل أفراد الصحابة وأخبارهم","group_en":"A Collection of the Virtues and Reports of Individual Companions","part_no":49,"group_no":13,"chapter_no":44,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Anas narrated: The Prophet ﷺ informed the people of the deaths of Zayd, Jaʿfar, and Ibn Rawāḥah before news of their martyrdom had reached them. He said: “Zayd took the banner and was martyred. Then Jaʿfar took it and was martyred. Then Ibn Rawāḥah took it and was martyred.” His eyes were shedding tears. Then he said: “Then it was taken up by one of the swords of Allah, and Allah granted victory through him.”"]},"buhuth":{"en":["The statement, “until Allah granted victory through him,” is understood here to refer to Khālid ibn al-Walīd’s wise military withdrawal of the Muslim army from the battlefield. Through his strategic leadership, the enemy did not perceive the Muslims’ weakened position, allowing the army to withdraw safely and return to Madinah. For this reason, the author describes the outcome as a victory (fatḥ). And Allah knows best."]}},"tuhfa":{},"voc":["fazail",375],"full":1,"dr":1,"tks":"صحيح: رواه البخاري (3757، 4262)."},{"num":10179,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عن أبي قتادة فارس رسول الله صلى الله عليه وسلم أن رسول الله صلى الله عليه وسلم قال –في قصة غزوة مؤته -: ثم أخذ اللواء خالد بن الوليد، ولم يكن من الأمراء هو أمَّر نفسه فرفع رسول الله صلى الله عليه وسلم أصبعيه وقال: اللهم هو سيف من سيوفك فانصره."],"takhrij":"حسن: رواه النسائي (8159)، وأحمد (22551)، وصحّحه ابن حبان (7048) كلهم من طرق عن الأسود بن شيبان، عن خالد بن سمير قال: قدم علينا عبد الله بن رباح، فوجدته قد اجتمع إليه ناس من الناس، قال: حدثنا أبو قتادة فذكره.وإسناده حسن من أجل خالد بن سمير، فإنه حسن الحديث.","grade":"حسن","chapter_ar":"باب في فضل خالد بن الوليد وأخباره","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب فضائل الصحابة وأخبارهم","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Hasan: Narrated by al-Nasā’ī (8159), Aḥmad (22551), and authenticated by Ibn Ḥibbān (7048).","chapter_en":"The Virtues of Khālid ibn al-Walīd and Reports Concerning Him","part_en":"The Book of the Virtues and Accounts of the Companions","group_ar":"مجموع فضائل أفراد الصحابة وأخبارهم","group_en":"A Collection of the Virtues and Reports of Individual Companions","part_no":49,"group_no":13,"chapter_no":44,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Abū Qatādah, the cavalryman of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, narrated that during the account of the Battle of Muʾtah, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Then Khālid ibn al-Walīd took up the banner, although he had not been appointed as one of the commanders; he assumed command himself.” The Messenger of Allah ﷺ then raised his two fingers and supplicated: “O Allah, he is one of Your swords, so grant him victory.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"voc":["fazail",376],"full":1,"tks":"حسن: رواه النسائي (8159)، وأحمد (22551)، وصححه ابن حبان (7048)."},{"num":10180,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ عَبْدِ اللَّهِ بْنِ جَعْفَرٍ، قَالَ: بَعَثَ رَسُولُ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ جَيْشًا، اسْتَعْمَلَ عَلَيْهِمْ زَيْدَ بْنَ حَارِثَةَ، فَإِنْ قُتِلَ زَيْدٌ - أَوِ اسْتُشْهِدَ - فَأَمِيرُكُمْ جَعْفَرٌ، فَإِنْ قُتِلَ - أَوِ اسْتُشْهِدَ - فَأَمِيرُكُمْ عَبْدُ اللَّهِ بْنُ رَوَاحَةَ فَلَقُوا الْعَدُوَّ، فَأَخَذَ الرَّايَةَ زَيْدٌ فَقَاتَلَ حَتَّى قُتِلَ، ثُمَّ أَخَذَ الرَّايَةَ جَعْفَرٌ فَقَاتَلَ حَتَّى قُتِلَ، ثُمَّ أَخَذَهَا عَبْدُ اللَّهِ بْنُ رَوَاحَةَ فَقَاتَلَ حَتَّى قُتِلَ، ثُمَّ أَخَذَ الرَّايَةَ خَالِدُ بْنُ الْوَلِيدِ، فَفَتَحَ اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ، وَأَتَى خَبَرُهُمِ النَّبِيَّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ، فَخَرَجَ إِلَى النَّاسِ، فَحَمِدَ اللَّهَ وَأَثْنَى عَلَيْهِ، وَقَالَ: إِنَّ إِخْوَانَكُمْ لَقُوا الْعَدُوَّ، وَإِنَّ زَيْدًا أَخَذَ الرَّايَةَ، فَقَاتَلَ حَتَّى قُتِلَ - أَوِ اسْتُشْهِدَ - ثُمَّ أَخَذَ الرَّايَةَ بَعْدَهُ جَعْفَرُ بْنُ أَبِي طَالِبٍ فَقَاتَلَ حَتَّى قُتِلَ - أَوِ اسْتُشْهِدَ -، ثُمَّ أَخَذَ الرَّايَةَ عَبْدُ اللَّهِ بْنُ رَوَاحَةَ، فَقَاتَلَ حَتَّى قُتِلَ - أَوِ اسْتُشْهِدَ - ثُمَّ أَخَذَ الرَّايَةَ سَيْفٌ مِنْ سُيُوفِ اللَّهِ خَالِدُ بْنُ الْوَلِيدِ، فَفَتَحَ اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ."],"takhrij":"صحيح: رواه أحمد (1750)، والنسائي في الكبرى (8550) كلاهما من طريق وهب بن جرير، حدثنا أبي قال: سمعت محمد بن أبي يعقوب يحدث عن الحسن بن سعد، عن عبد الله بن جعفر فذكره.وإسناده صحيح.","grade":"صحيح","chapter_ar":"باب في فضل خالد بن الوليد وأخباره","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب فضائل الصحابة وأخبارهم","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Authentic: Narrated by Aḥmad (1750) and al-Nasā’ī in al-Sunan al-Kubrā (8550).","chapter_en":"The Virtues of Khālid ibn al-Walīd and Reports Concerning Him","part_en":"The Book of the Virtues and Accounts of the Companions","group_ar":"مجموع فضائل أفراد الصحابة وأخبارهم","group_en":"A Collection of the Virtues and Reports of Individual Companions","part_no":49,"group_no":13,"chapter_no":44,"content":{"translation":{"en":["ʿAbdullāh ibn Jaʿfar narrated: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ dispatched an army and appointed Zayd ibn Ḥārithah as its commander, saying: “If Zayd is killed—or martyred—then your commander will be Jaʿfar. If Jaʿfar is killed—or martyred—then your commander will be ʿAbdullāh ibn Rawāḥah.” When they met the enemy, Zayd carried the banner and fought until he was martyred. Then Jaʿfar took the banner and fought until he was martyred. Then ʿAbdullāh ibn Rawāḥah took it and fought until he was martyred. After that, Khālid ibn al-Walīd took the banner, and Allah granted victory through him. When news reached the Prophet ﷺ, he came out to the people, praised Allah, and said: “Your brothers met the enemy. Zayd took the banner and fought until he was martyred. Then Jaʿfar ibn Abī Ṭālib took it and fought until he was martyred. Then ʿAbdullāh ibn Rawāḥah took it and fought until he was martyred. Then the banner was taken by one of the swords of Allah—Khālid ibn al-Walīd—and Allah granted victory through him.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"voc":["fazail",377],"full":1,"dr":1,"tks":"صحيح: رواه أحمد (1750)، والنسائي في الكبرى (8550)."},{"num":10181,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عن أبي العجفاء قال: قيل لعمر بن الخطاب: لو عهدت يا أمير المؤمنين؟ قال: لو أدركت أبا عبيدة بن الجراح ثم وليته، ثم قدمت على ربي، فقال لي: لِمَ استخلفته على أمة محمد؟ قلت: سمعت عبدك وخليلك يقول: لكل أمة أمين، وإن أمين هذه الأمة أبو عبيدة بن الجراح، ولو أدركت خالد بن الوليد ثم وليته، ثم قدمت على ربي، فقال لي: من استخلفت على أمة محمد؟ لقلت: سمعت عبدك وخليلك يقول لخالد: سيف من سيوف الله سلَّه الله على المشركين."],"takhrij":"حسن: رواه ابن أبي عاصم في الآحاد والمثاني (697) والشاشي في مسنده (617) -والسياق له- كلاهما من طريق ضمرة بن ربيعة، عن يحيى بن أبي عمرو الشيباني، عن أبي العجفاء فذكره.","grade":"حسن","chapter_ar":"باب في فضل خالد بن الوليد وأخباره","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب فضائل الصحابة وأخبارهم","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Hasan: Narrated by Ibn Abī ʿĀṣim in al-Āḥād wa al-Mathānī (697) and by al-Shāshī in his Musnad (617), whose wording is quoted here.","chapter_en":"The Virtues of Khālid ibn al-Walīd and Reports Concerning Him","part_en":"The Book of the Virtues and Accounts of the Companions","group_ar":"مجموع فضائل أفراد الصحابة وأخبارهم","group_en":"A Collection of the Virtues and Reports of Individual Companions","part_no":49,"group_no":13,"chapter_no":44,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Abū al-ʿAjfāʾ narrated: It was said to ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb: “O Commander of the Believers, why do you not appoint a successor?” ʿUmar replied: “Had Abū ʿUbaydah ibn al-Jarrāḥ still been alive, I would have appointed him. Then, when I stood before my Lord and He asked me, ‘Why did you appoint him over the nation of Muḥammad?’ I would have replied: ʿI heard Your servant and beloved say: “Every nation has a trustworthy guardian, and the trustworthy guardian of this nation is Abū ʿUbaydah ibn al-Jarrāḥ.”’ He continued: “And if Khālid ibn al-Walīd had still been alive, I would have appointed him. Then, when I stood before my Lord and He asked me, ‘Whom did you appoint over the nation of Muḥammad?’ I would have replied: ʿI heard Your servant and beloved say to Khālid: “He is one of the swords of Allah, unsheathed by Allah against the polytheists.”’”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"voc":["fazail",378],"full":1,"dr":1,"tks":"حسن: رواه ابن أبي عاصم في الآحاد والمثاني (697)، والشاشي في مسنده (617)، واللفظ له."},{"num":10182,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ أَبِي هُرَيْرَةَ، قَالَ: نَزَلْنَا مَعَ رَسُولِ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ مَنْزِلاً، فَجَعَلَ النَّاسُ يَمُرُّونَ، فَيَقُولُ رَسُولُ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ: مَنْ هَذَا يَا أَبَا هُرَيْرَةَ. فَأَقُولُ: فُلاَنٌ. فَيَقُولُ نِعْمَ عَبْدُ اللَّهِ هَذَا. وَيَقُولُ: مَنْ هَذَا. فَأَقُولُ: فُلاَنٌ. فَيَقُولُ بِئْسَ عَبْدُ اللَّهِ هَذَا. حَتَّى مَرَّ خَالِدُ بْنُ الْوَلِيدِ فَقَالَ: مَنْ هَذَا. فَقُلْتُ: هَذَا خَالِدُ بْنُ الْوَلِيدِ. فَقَالَ: نِعْمَ عَبْدُ اللَّهِ خَالِدُ بْنُ الْوَلِيدِ، سَيْفٌ مِنْ سُيُوفِ اللَّهِ."],"takhrij":"حسن: رواه الترمذي (3846) عن قتيبة، حدثنا الليث، عن هشام بن سعد، عن زيد بن أسلم، عن أبي هريرة فذكره.","grade":"حسن","chapter_ar":"باب في فضل خالد بن الوليد وأخباره","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب فضائل الصحابة وأخبارهم","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Hasan: Narrated by al-Tirmidhī (3846).","chapter_en":"The Virtues of Khālid ibn al-Walīd and Reports Concerning Him","part_en":"The Book of the Virtues and Accounts of the Companions","group_ar":"مجموع فضائل أفراد الصحابة وأخبارهم","group_en":"A Collection of the Virtues and Reports of Individual Companions","part_no":49,"group_no":13,"chapter_no":44,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Abū Hurayrah narrated: We stopped at a campsite with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. As people passed by, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ would ask: “Who is this, O Abū Hurayrah?” I would reply: “So-and-so.” Sometimes he would say: “What an excellent servant of Allah he is.” At other times he would ask about someone else, and after I identified him, he would say: “What an evil servant of Allah he is.” Eventually Khālid ibn al-Walīd passed by. The Prophet ﷺ asked: “Who is this?” I replied: “This is Khālid ibn al-Walīd.” The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “What an excellent servant of Allah Khālid ibn al-Walīd is—a sword from among the swords of Allah.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"voc":["fazail",379],"full":1,"dr":1,"tks":"حسن: رواه الترمذي (3846)."},{"num":10183,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عن أَبِي الدَّرْدَاءِ قَالَ: فَقَالَ: قَالَ رَسُولُ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ: نِعْمَ الرَّجُلُ خُرَيْمٌ الْأَسَدِيُّ لَوْلَا طُولُ جُمَّتِهِ وَإِسْبَالُ إِزَارِهِ فَبَلَغَ ذَلِكَ خُرَيْمًا، فَجَعَلَ يَأْخُذُ شَفْرَةً، فَيَقْطَعُ بِهَا شَعَرَهُ إِلَى أَنْصَافِ أُذُنَيْهِ، وَرَفَعَ إِزَارَهُ إِلَى أَنْصَافِ سَاقَيْهِ.","قال –يعني الراوي-: فأخبرني أبي قال: دخلت بعد ذلك على معاوية، فإذا عنده شيخ جمته فوق أذنيه، ورداؤه إلى ساقيه، فسألت عنه فقالوا: هذا خريم الأسدي.الحديث."],"takhrij":"حسن: رواه أبو داود (4089)، وأحمد (17622) كلاهما من حديث عبدالملك بن عمرو أبي عامر، قال: حدثنا هشام بن سعد، قال: حدثنا قيس بن بشر التغلبي، قال: أخبرني أبي –وكان جليسا لأبي الدرداء- قال أبو الدرداء فذكره في حديث طويل مذكور في كتاب اللباس.","grade":"حسن","chapter_ar":"باب ما جاء في خريم بن فاتك الأسدي","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب فضائل الصحابة وأخبارهم","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Hasan: Narrated by Abū Dāwūd (4089) and Aḥmad (17622).","chapter_en":"Reports Concerning Khuraym ibn Fātik al-Asadī","part_en":"The Book of the Virtues and Accounts of the Companions","group_ar":"مجموع فضائل أفراد الصحابة وأخبارهم","group_en":"A Collection of the Virtues and Reports of Individual Companions","part_no":49,"group_no":13,"chapter_no":45,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Abū al-Dardāʾ narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Khuraym al-Asadī is an excellent man, were it not for the length of his hair and the fact that he lets his garment hang below the proper length.” When this reached Khuraym, he immediately took a razor and cut his hair until it reached the middle of his ears. He also raised his lower garment so that it reached the middle of his shins. The narrator said: My father told me: Later, I entered upon Muʿāwiyah and saw an elderly man with his hair ending above his ears and his garment reaching the middle of his shins.","I asked who he was, and they replied: “This is Khuraym al-Asadī.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"voc":["fazail",380],"full":1,"dr":1,"tks":"حسن: رواه أبو داود (4089)، وأحمد (17622)."},{"num":10184,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عن زَيْدِ بن ثَابِتٍ رَضِيَ اللَّهُ عَنْهُ قَالَ: نَسَخْتُ الصُّحُفَ فِي الْمَصَاحِفِ، فَفَقَدْتُ آيَةً مِنْ سُورَةِ الأَحْزَابِ، كُنْتُ أَسْمَعُ رَسُولَ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ يَقْرَأُ بِهَا، فَلَمْ أَجِدْهَا إِلاَّ مَعَ خُزَيْمَةَ بْنِ ثَابِتٍ الأَنْصَارِيِّ الَّذِي جَعَلَ رَسُولُ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ شَهَادَتَهُ شَهَادَةَ رَجُلَيْنِ، وَهْوَ قَوْلُهُ: ﴿مِنَ الْمُؤْمِنِينَ رِجَالٌ صَدَقُوا مَا عَاهَدُوا اللَّهَ عَلَيْهِ﴾ [سورة الأحزاب: 23]}."],"takhrij":"صحيح: رواه البخاري في الجهاد والسير (2807) من طرق عن الزهري، عن خارجة بن زيد أن زيد بن ثابت قال: فذكره.","grade":"صحيح","chapter_ar":"باب في فضل خزيمة بن ثابت الأنصاري وأخباره","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب فضائل الصحابة وأخبارهم","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Authentic: Narrated by al-Bukhārī (2807).","chapter_en":"The Virtues of Khuzaymah ibn Thābit al-Anṣārī and Reports Concerning Him","part_en":"The Book of the Virtues and Accounts of the Companions","group_ar":"مجموع فضائل أفراد الصحابة وأخبارهم","group_en":"A Collection of the Virtues and Reports of Individual Companions","part_no":49,"group_no":13,"chapter_no":46,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Zayd ibn Thābit narrated: When I was copying the written sheets of the Qur’an into the compiled muṣḥafs, I found that one verse from Sūrat al-Aḥzāb was missing. I had heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ recite it, but I did not find it with anyone except Khuzaymah ibn Thābit al-Anṣārī—the Companion whose testimony the Messenger of Allah ﷺ had declared to be equal to the testimony of two men. The verse was: “Among the believers are men who have been true to what they pledged to Allah.” (Qur’an 33:23)"]},"buhuth":{"en":["The reason why the Messenger of Allah ﷺ regarded Khuzaymah’s testimony as equal to that of two men is explained in the following hadith."]}},"tuhfa":{},"full":1,"dr":1,"tks":"صحيح: رواه البخاري (2807)."},{"num":10185,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ عُمَارَةَ بْنِ خُزَيْمَةَ، أَنَّ عَمَّهُ، حَدَّثَهُ، وَهُوَ، مِنْ أَصْحَابِ النَّبِيِّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ أَنَّ النَّبِيَّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ ابْتَاعَ فَرَسًا مِنْ أَعْرَابِيٍّ، فَاسْتَتْبَعَهُ النَّبِيُّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ لِيَقْضِيَهُ ثَمَنَ فَرَسِهِ، فَأَسْرَعَ رَسُولُ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ الْمَشْىَ، وَأَبْطَأَ الأَعْرَابِيُّ، فَطَفِقَ رِجَالٌ يَعْتَرِضُونَ الأَعْرَابِيَّ فَيُسَاوِمُونَهُ بِالْفَرَسِ، وَلاَ يَشْعُرُونَ أَنَّ النَّبِيَّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ ابْتَاعَهُ، فَنَادَى الأَعْرَابِيُّ رَسُولَ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ فَقَالَ: إِنْ كُنْتَ مُبْتَاعًا هَذَا الْفَرَسَ وَإِلاَّ بِعْتُهُ. فَقَامَ النَّبِيُّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ حِينَ سَمِعَ نِدَاءَ الأَعْرَابِيِّ فَقَالَ: أَوَلَيْسَ قَدِ ابْتَعْتُهُ مِنْكَ. فَقَالَ الأَعْرَابِيُّ: لاَ وَاللَّهِ مَا بِعْتُكَهُ. فَقَالَ النَّبِيُّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ: بَلَى قَدِ ابْتَعْتُهُ مِنْكَ. فَطَفِقَ الأَعْرَابِيُّ يَقُولُ: هَلُمَّ شَهِيدًا. فَقَالَ خُزَيْمَةُ بْنُ ثَابِتٍ: أَنَا أَشْهَدُ أَنَّكَ قَدْ بَايَعْتَهُ. فَأَقْبَلَ النَّبِيُّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ عَلَى خُزَيْمَةَ، فَقَالَ: بِمَ تَشْهَدُ. فَقَالَ بِتَصْدِيقِكَ يَا رَسُولَ اللَّهِ. فَجَعَلَ رَسُولُ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ شَهَادَةَ خُزَيْمَةَ بِشَهَادَةِ رَجُلَيْنِ."],"takhrij":"صحيح: رواه أبو داود (3607)، والنسائي (4648)، وأحمد (21883)، والحاكم (2187) والبيهقي (20515) كلهم من طرق عن الزهري، أخبره عن عمارة بن خزيمة فذكره.","grade":"صحيح","chapter_ar":"باب في فضل خزيمة بن ثابت الأنصاري وأخباره","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب فضائل الصحابة وأخبارهم","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Authentic: Narrated by Abū Dāwūd (3607), al-Nasā’ī (4648), Aḥmad (21883), and al-Ḥākim (2187).","chapter_en":"The Virtues of Khuzaymah ibn Thābit al-Anṣārī and Reports Concerning Him","part_en":"The Book of the Virtues and Accounts of the Companions","group_ar":"مجموع فضائل أفراد الصحابة وأخبارهم","group_en":"A Collection of the Virtues and Reports of Individual Companions","part_no":49,"group_no":13,"chapter_no":46,"content":{"translation":{"en":["ʿUmārah ibn Khuzaymah narrated from his uncle, who was one of the Companions of the Prophet ﷺ: The Prophet ﷺ purchased a horse from a Bedouin and asked him to accompany him so that he could pay its price. The Prophet ﷺ walked ahead at a quicker pace, while the Bedouin lagged behind. Along the way, people approached the Bedouin and began offering to buy the horse, unaware that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ had already purchased it. The Bedouin called out to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and said: “If you are buying this horse, then buy it. Otherwise I will sell it.” When the Prophet ﷺ heard him, he said: “Have you not already sold it to me?” The Bedouin replied: “No, by Allah, I have not sold it to you.” The Prophet ﷺ said: “Rather, you have sold it to me.” The Bedouin then repeatedly demanded: “Bring a witness.” Khuzaymah ibn Thābit stepped forward and said: “I testify that you sold it to him.” The Prophet ﷺ turned to Khuzaymah and asked: “On what basis do you testify, when you were not present?” Khuzaymah replied: “Because I believe you, O Messenger of Allah.” Because of this, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ accepted the testimony of Khuzaymah as being equal to the testimony of two men."]}},"tuhfa":{},"voc":["fazail",382],"full":1,"dr":1,"rep":[6768],"tks":"صحيح: رواه أبو داود (3607)، والنسائي (4648)، وأحمد (21883)، والحاكم (2187)."},{"num":10186,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ خُزَيْمَةَ بْنِ ثَابِتٍ رضي الله عنه قَالَ: إِنَّهُ مَرَّ عَلَى النَّبِيِّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ  وَقَدِ اشْتَرَى فَرَسًا مِنْ أَعْرَابِيٍّ فَجَحَدَهُ الْأَعْرَابِيُّ الْبَيْعَ، فَقَالَ: لَمْ أَبِعْكَ. فَقَالَ النَّبِيُّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ: : قَدْ بِعْتَنِي، فَمَرَّ عَلَيْهِمْ خُزَيْمَةُ بْنُ ثَابِتٍ رضي الله عنه، فَسَمِعَ قَوْلَهُمَا، فَقَالَ: أَنَا أَشْهَدُ أَنَّكَ بِعْتَ. فَقَالَ لَهُ النَّبِيُّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ: : وَمَا عِلْمُكَ بِذَلِكَ ولم تشهدنا؟. فقال: رضي الله عنه: قد شَهِدْنَا عَلَى مَا هُوَ أَعْظَمُ مِنْ ذَلِكَ. فَأَجَازَ النَّبِيُّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ  شَهَادَتَهُ بِشَهَادَةِ رَجُلَيْنِ حَتَّى مَاتَ خُزَيْمَةَ."],"takhrij":"حسن: رواه ابن أبي عمر في مسنده كما في المطالب العالية (4019) عن حسين الجعفي (هو: ابن علي بن الوليد الكوفي)، عن زائدة، ثنا أبو فروة الجهني، عن عبد الرحمن بن أبي ليلى، عن خزيمة بن ثابت قال: فذكره.","grade":"حسن","chapter_ar":"باب في فضل خزيمة بن ثابت الأنصاري وأخباره","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب فضائل الصحابة وأخبارهم","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Hasan: Narrated by Ibn Abī ʿUmar in his Musnad, as cited in al-Maṭālib al-ʿĀliyah (4019).","chapter_en":"The Virtues of Khuzaymah ibn Thābit al-Anṣārī and Reports Concerning Him","part_en":"The Book of the Virtues and Accounts of the Companions","group_ar":"مجموع فضائل أفراد الصحابة وأخبارهم","group_en":"A Collection of the Virtues and Reports of Individual Companions","part_no":49,"group_no":13,"chapter_no":46,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Khuzaymah ibn Thābit narrated: He passed by the Prophet ﷺ after he had purchased a horse from a Bedouin. The Bedouin denied making the sale and said: “I never sold it to you.” The Prophet ﷺ replied: “You did indeed sell it to me.” Khuzaymah ibn Thābit happened to pass by and heard their discussion. He said: “I testify that you sold it to him.” The Prophet ﷺ asked him: “How do you know that, when you were not present with us?” Khuzaymah answered: “Because we have believed and testified to something far greater than this.” Accordingly, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ accepted Khuzaymah’s testimony as equal to the testimony of two men, and this remained his distinction until he passed away."]},"buhuth":{"en":["The Messenger of Allah ﷺ regarded the testimony of Khuzaymah ibn Thābit as equal to that of two men because of the specific incident described above. This ruling was unique to him and is not to be extended by analogy to anyone else."]}},"tuhfa":{},"voc":["fazail",383],"full":1,"dr":1,"tks":"حسن: رواه ابن أبي عمر في مسنده كما في المطالب العالية (4019)."},{"num":10187,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ جَابِرٍ أَنَّ رَسُولَ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ قَالَ:  عُرِضَ عَلَيَّ الْأَنْبِيَاءُ، فَإِذَا مُوسَى ضَرْبٌ مِنَ الرِّجَالِ، كَأَنَّهُ مِنْ رِجَالِ شَنُوءَةَ، وَرَأَيْتُ عِيسَى ابْنَ مَرْيَمَ عَلَيْهِ السلام، فَإِذَا أَقْرَبُ مَنْ رَأَيْتُ بِهِ شَبَهًا عُرْوَةُ بْنُ مَسْعُودٍ، وَرَأَيْتُ إِبْرَاهِيمَ صَلَوَاتُ اللَّهِ عَلَيْهِ، فَإِذَا أَقْرَبُ مَنْ رَأَيْتُ بِهِ شَبَهًا صَاحِبُكُمْ - يَعْنِي: نَفْسَهُ، -، وَرَأَيْتُ جِبْرِيلَ عَلَيْهِ السلام فَإِذَا أَقْرَبُ مَنْ رَأَيْتُ بِهِ شَبَهًا دِحْيَةُ.","وَفِي رِوَايَةِ ابْنِ رُمْحٍ: \"دِحْيَةُ بْنُ خَلِيفَةَ\"."],"takhrij":"صحيح: رواه مسلم في الإيمان (167-271) من طرق عن الليث، عن أبي الزبير، عن جابر فذكره.","grade":"صحيح","chapter_ar":"باب في فضل دحية بن خليفة الكلبي وأخباره","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب فضائل الصحابة وأخبارهم","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Authentic: Narrated by Muslim (167).","chapter_en":"The Virtues of Diḥyah ibn Khalīfah al-Kalbī and Reports Concerning Him","part_en":"The Book of the Virtues and Accounts of the Companions","group_ar":"مجموع فضائل أفراد الصحابة وأخبارهم","group_en":"A Collection of the Virtues and Reports of Individual Companions","part_no":49,"group_no":13,"chapter_no":47,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Jābir narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “The Prophets were shown to me. Mūsā (Moses) was a strongly built man, resembling the men of Shanūʾah. I saw ʿĪsā ibn Maryam (Jesus, son of Mary), peace be upon them both, and the person who most closely resembled him was ʿUrwah ibn Masʿūd. I also saw Ibrāhīm (Abraham), peace be upon him, and the one who most closely resembled him was your companion”—meaning himself ﷺ—“and I saw Jibrīl (Gabriel), peace be upon him, and the one who most closely resembled him was Diḥyah.” In the narration of Ibn Rumḥ, it reads: “Diḥyah ibn Khalīfah.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"voc":["fazail",384],"full":1,"rep":[8384],"tks":"صحيح: رواه مسلم (167)."},{"num":10188,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنِ ابْنِ عُمَرَ، قَالَ: كَانَ جِبْرِيلُ عَلَيْهِ السلام يَأْتِي النَّبِيَّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ فِي صُورَةِ دِحْيَةَ."],"takhrij":"صحيح: رواه أحمد (5857) عن عفَّان، حدثنا حماد بن سلمة، عن إسحاق بن سويد، عن يحيى بن يعمر، عن ابن عمر، فذكر حديث جبريل المشهور، ثم قال قوله المذكور.","grade":"صحيح","chapter_ar":"باب في فضل دحية بن خليفة الكلبي وأخباره","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب فضائل الصحابة وأخبارهم","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Authentic: Narrated by Aḥmad (5857).","chapter_en":"The Virtues of Diḥyah ibn Khalīfah al-Kalbī and Reports Concerning Him","part_en":"The Book of the Virtues and Accounts of the Companions","group_ar":"مجموع فضائل أفراد الصحابة وأخبارهم","group_en":"A Collection of the Virtues and Reports of Individual Companions","part_no":49,"group_no":13,"chapter_no":47,"content":{"translation":{"en":["ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿUmar narrated: Jibrīl (Gabriel), peace be upon him, would come to the Prophet ﷺ in the appearance of Diḥyah."]}},"tuhfa":{},"voc":["fazail",385],"full":1,"dr":1,"tks":"صحيح: رواه أحمد (5857)."},{"num":10189,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنِ امْرَأَةِ رَافِعِ بْنِ خَدِيجٍ أَنَّ رَافِعًا رُمِيَ مَعَ رَسُولِ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ يَوْمَ أُحُدٍ أَوْ يَوْمَ خَيْبَرَ بِسَهْمٍ فِي ثَنْدُوَتِهِ، فَأَتَى النبيَّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ فَقَالَ: يَا رَسُولَ اللَّهِ، انْزِعِ السَّهْمَ، قَالَ: يَا رَافِعُ إِنْ شِئْتَ نَزَعْتُ السَّهْمَ وَالْقُطْبَةَ جَمِيعًا، وَإِنْ شِئْتَ نَزَعْتُ السَّهْمَ، وَتَرَكْتُ الْقُطْبَةَ، وَشَهِدَتُ لَكَ يَوْمَ الْقِيَامَةِ أَنَّكَ شَهِيدٌ قَالَ: يَا رَسُولَ اللَّهِ بَلْ انْزِعِ السَّهْمَ، ودع الْقُطْبَةَ واشهد لِي يَوْمَ الْقِيَامَةِ أني شَهِيدٌ.قَالَ: فَنَزَعَ رَسُولُ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ السَّهْمَ، وَتَرَكَ الْقُطْبَةَ. وَزَادَ فِي رِوَايَةِ: فَعَاشَ بِهَا حَتَّى كَانَ فِي خِلَافَةِ مُعَاوِيَةَ، فَانْتَفَضَ بِهِ الْجُرْحُ فَمَاتَ بَعْدَ الْعَصْرِ."],"takhrij":"حسن: رواه أحمد (27128)، والطبراني في الكبير (4242) كلاهما من طريق عمرو بن مرزوق الواشحي، أخبرني يحيى بن عبد الحميد بن رافع بن خديج، قال: أخبرتي جدتي يعني امرأة رافع بن خديج فذكرته.","grade":"حسن","chapter_ar":"باب فضل رافع بن خديج","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب فضائل الصحابة وأخبارهم","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Hasan: Narrated by Aḥmad (27128) and al-Ṭabarānī in al-Muʿjam al-Kabīr (4/282).","chapter_en":"The Virtues of Rāfiʿ ibn Khadīj","part_en":"The Book of the Virtues and Accounts of the Companions","group_ar":"مجموع فضائل أفراد الصحابة وأخبارهم","group_en":"A Collection of the Virtues and Reports of Individual Companions","part_no":49,"group_no":13,"chapter_no":48,"content":{"translation":{"en":["The wife of Rāfiʿ ibn Khadīj narrated: Rāfiʿ was struck by an arrow while fighting alongside the Messenger of Allah ﷺ on the Day of Uḥud—or the Day of Khaybar. The arrow lodged in the upper part of his chest. He came to the Prophet ﷺ and said: “O Messenger of Allah, remove the arrow.” The Prophet ﷺ replied: “O Rāfiʿ, if you wish, I will remove both the arrow and the embedded arrowhead. Or, if you wish, I will remove only the shaft of the arrow, leave the arrowhead where it is, and testify on your behalf on the Day of Resurrection that you are a martyr.” Rāfiʿ said: “O Messenger of Allah, remove the arrow, leave the arrowhead in place, and testify for me on the Day of Resurrection that I am a martyr.” So the Messenger of Allah ﷺ removed the shaft of the arrow while leaving the arrowhead embedded. Another narration adds: He lived with it until the caliphate of Muʿāwiyah. Then the wound suddenly became inflamed again, and he died after the ʿAṣr prayer."]},"buhuth":{"en":["The wife of Rāfiʿ ibn Khadīj was Umm ʿAbd al-Ḥamīd. Ibn Ḥajar mentioned her in the first section of al-Iṣābah among the Companions.","The statement, “He lived with it until the caliphate of Muʿāwiyah,” indicates that he passed away around 73 AH or 74 AH."]}},"tuhfa":{},"voc":["fazail",386],"full":1,"dr":1,"tks":"حسن: رواه أحمد (27128)، والطبراني في الكبير (4242)."},{"num":10190,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ رَبِيعَةَ الْأَسْلَمِيِّ قَالَ: كُنْتُ أَخْدُمُ رَسُولَ الله صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ، فَقَالَ: يَا رَبِيعَةُ أَلَا تَزَوَّجُ؟ قَالَ: قُلْتُ: والله يَا رَسُولَ الله، مَا أُرِيدُ أَنْ أَتَزَوَّجَ، مَا عِنْدِي مَا يُقِيمُ المَرْأَةَ، وَمَا أُحِبُّ أَنْ يَشْغَلَنِي عَنْكَ شَيْءٌ، فَأَعْرَضَ عَنِّي، فَخَدَمْتُهُ مَا خَدَمْتُهُ، ثُمَّ قَال لِي الثَّانِيَةَ: يَا رَبِيعَةُ أَلَا تَزَوَّجُ؟ فَقُلْتُ: مَا أُرِيدُ أَنْ أَتَزَوَّجَ، مَا عِنْدِي مَا يُقِيمُ المَرْأَةَ، وَمَا أُحِبُّ أَنْ يَشْغَلَنِي عَنْكَ شَيْءٌ، فَأَعْرَضَ عَنِّي، ثُمَّ رَجَعْتُ إِلَى نَفْسِي، فَقُلْتُ: والله لَرَسُولُ الله صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ بِمَا يُصْلِحُنِي فِي الدُّنْيَا وَالْآخِرَةِ أَعْلَمُ مِنِّي، والله لَئِنْ قَالَ: تَزَوَّجْ، لَأَقُولَنَّ: نَعَمْ يَا رَسُولَ الله، مُرْنِي بِمَا شِئْتَ، قَالَ: فَقَالَ: يَا رَبِيعَةُ أَلَا تَزَوَّجُ؟ فَقُلْتُ: بَلَى مُرْنِي بِمَا شِئْتَ، قَالَ: انْطَلِقْ إِلَى آلِ فُلَانٍ، حَيٍّ مِنْ الْأَنْصَارِ، وَكَانَ فِيهِمْ تَرَاخٍ عَن النَّبِيِّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ، فَقُلْ لهُمْ: إِنَّ رَسُولَ الله صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ أَرْسَلَنِي إِلَيْكُمْ يَأْمُرُكُمْ أَنْ تُزَوِّجُونِي فُلَانَةَ لِامْرَأَةٍ مِنْهُمْ، فَذَهَبْتُ، فَقُلْتُ لهُمْ: إِنَّ رَسُولَ الله أَرْسَلَنِي إِلَيْكُمْ، يَأْمُرُكُمْ أَنْ تُزَوِّجُونِي فُلَانَةَ، فَقَالُوا: مَرْحَبًا بِرَسُولِ الله، وَبِرَسُولِ رَسُولِ الله صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ، والله لَا يَرْجِعُ رَسُولُ رَسُولِ الله صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ إِلَّا بِحَاجَتِهِ، فَزَوَّجُونِي، وَأَلْطَفُونِي، وَمَا سَأَلُونِي الْبَيِّنَةَ، فَرَجَعْتُ إِلَى رَسُولِ الله صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ حَزِينًا، فَقَالَ لِي: مَا لَكَ يَا رَبِيعَةُ؟ فَقُلْتُ: يَا رَسُولَ الله، أَتَيْتُ قَوْمًا كِرَامًا، فَزَوَّجُونِي، وَأَكْرَمُونِي، وَأَلْطَفُونِي، وَمَا سَأَلُونِي بَيِّنَةً، وَلَيْسَ عِنْدِي صَدَاقٌ، فَقَالَ رَسُولُ الله صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ: يَا بُرَيْدَةُ الْأَسْلَمِيُّ، اجْمَعُوا لَهُ وَزْنَ نَوَاةٍ مِنْ ذَهَبٍ، قَالَ: فَجَمَعُوا لِي وَزْنَ نَوَاةٍ مِنْ ذَهَبٍ، فَأَخَذْتُ مَا جَمَعُوا لِي، فَأَتَيْتُ بِهِ النَّبِيَّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ، فَقَالَ: اذْهَبْ بِهَذَا إِلَيْهِمْ، فَقُلْ هَذَا صَدَاقُهَا، فَأَتَيْتُهُمْ، فَقُلْتُ: هَذَا صَدَاقُهَا، فَرَضُوه، وَقَبِلُوهُ، وَقَالُوا: كَثِيرٌ طَيِّبٌ، قَالَ: ثُمَّ رَجَعْتُ إِلَى النَّبِيِّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ حَزِينًا، فَقَالَ: يَا رَبِيعَةُ مَا لَكَ حَزِينٌ؟ فَقُلْتُ: يَا رَسُولَ الله، مَا رَأَيْتُ قَوْمًا أَكْرَمَ مِنْهُمْ، رَضُوا بِمَا آتَيْتُهُمْ، وَأَحْسَنُوا، وَقَالُوا: كَثِيرًا طَيِّبًا، وَلَيْسَ عِنْدِي مَا أُولِمُ قَالَ: يَا بُرَيْدَةُ اجْمَعُوا لَهُ شَاةً، قَالَ: فَجَمَعُوا لي كَبْشًا عَظِيمًا سَمِينًا، فَقَالَ لِي رَسُولُ الله صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ: اذْهَبْ إِلَى عَائِشَةَ فَقُلْ لَهَا فَلْتَبْعَثْ بِالْمِكْتَلِ الَّذِي فِيهِ الطَّعَامُ قَالَ: فَأَتَيْتُهَا، فَقُلْتُ لَهَا مَا أَمَرَنِي بِهِ رَسُولُ الله صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ، فَقَالَتْ: هَذَا الْمِكْتَلُ فِيهِ تِسْعُ آصُعِ شَعِيرٍ، لَا، والله إِنْ أَصْبَحَ لَنَا طَعَامٌ غَيْرُهُ، خُذْهُ فَأَخَذْتُهُ، فَأَتَيْتُ بِهِ النَّبِيَّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ، وَأَخْبَرْتُهُ مَا قَالَتْ عَائِشَةُ، فَقَالَ: اذْهَبْ بِهَذَا إِلَيْهِمْ فَقُلْ: لِيُصْبِحْ هَذَا عِنْدَكُمْ خُبْزًا، فَذَهَبْتُ إِلَيْهِمْ، وَذَهَبْتُ بِالْكَبْشِ، وَمَعِي أُنَاسٌ مِنْ أَسْلَمَ، فَقَالَ: لِيُصْبِحْ هَذَا عِنْدَكُمْ خُبْزًا وَهَذَا طَبِيخًا، فَقَالُوا: أَمَّا الخُبْزُ فَسَنَكْفِيكُمُوهُ، وَأَمَّا الْكَبْشُ فَاكْفُونَا أَنْتُمْ، فَأَخَذْنَا الْكَبْشَ أَنَا وَأُنَاسٌ مِنْ أَسْلَمَ، فَذَبَحْنَاهُ، وَسَلَخْنَاهُ، وَطَبَخْنَاهُ، فَأَصْبَحَ عِنْدَنَا خُبْزٌ وَلحْمٌ، فَأَوْلمْتُ، وَدَعَوْتُ رَسُولَ الله صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ.","ثُمَّ قَالَ: إِنَّ رَسُولَ الله صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ أَعْطَانِي أَرْضًا، وَأَعْطَانِي أَبُو بَكْرٍ أَرْضًا، وَجَاءَت الدُّنْيَا، فَاخْتَلَفْنَا فِي عِذْقِ نَخْلَةٍ، فَقُلْتُ أَنَا: هِيَ فِي حَدِّي، وَقَالَ أَبُو بَكْرٍ: هِيَ فِي حَدِّي، فَكَانَ بَيْنِي وَبَيْنَ أَبِي بَكْرٍ كَلَامٌ، فَقَالَ أَبُو بَكْرٍ كَلِمَةً كَرِهَهَا وَنَدِمَ، فَقَالَ لِي: يَا رَبِيعَةُ رُدَّ عَلَيَّ مِثْلَهَا حَتَّى تَكُونَ قِصَاصًا، قَالَ: قُلْتُ لَا أَفْعَلُ، فَقَالَ أَبُو بَكْرٍ: لَتَقُولَنَّ أَوْ لَأَسْتَعْدِيَنَّ عَلَيْكَ رَسُولَ الله صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ، فَقُلْتُ: مَا أَنَا بِفَاعِلٍ، قَالَ: وَرَفَضَ الْأَرْضَ، وَانْطَلَقَ أَبُو بَكْرٍ رَضِيَ اللَّهُ عَنْهُ إِلَى النَّبِيِّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ، وَانْطَلَقْتُ أَتْلُوهُ، فَجَاءَ نَاسٌ مِنْ أَسْلَمَ، فَقَالُوا لِي: رَحِمَ الله أَبَا بَكْرٍ فِي أَيِّ شَيْءٍ يَسْتَعْدِي عَلَيْكَ رَسُولَ الله صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ؟ وَهُوَ قَالَ لَكَ مَا قَال، فَقُلْتُ: أَتَدْرُونَ مَا هَذَا؟ هَذَا أَبُو بَكْرٍ الصِّدِّيقُ، هَذَا ثَانِيَ اثْنَيْنِ، وَهَذَا ذُو شَيْبَةِ المُسْلِمِينَ، إِيَّاكُمْ، لايَلْتَفِتُ فَيَرَاكُمْ تَنْصُرُونِي عَلَيْهِ فَيَغْضَبَ، فَيَأْتِيَ رَسُولَ الله صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ فَيَغْضَبَ لِغَضَبِهِ، فَيَغْضَبَ الله عَزَّ وَجَلَّ لِغَضَبِهِمَا، فَيُهْلِكَ رَبِيعَةَ، قَالُوا: مَا تَأْمُرُنَا؟ قَالَ: ارْجِعُوا قَالَ: فَانْطَلَقَ أَبُو بَكْرٍ رَضِيَ اللَّهُ عَنْهُ إِلَى رَسُولِ الله صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ فَتَبِعْتُهُ وَحْدِي، حَتَّى أَتَى النَّبِيَّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ فَحَدَّثَهُ الحَدِيثَ كَمَا كَانَ، فَرَفَعَ إِلَيَّ رَأْسَهُ، فَقَالَ: يَا رَبِيعَةُ مَا لَكَ وَلِلصِّدِّيقِ؟ قُلْتُ: يَا رَسُولَ الله كَانَ كَذَا، كَانَ كَذَا، قَالَ لِي كَلِمَةً كَرِهَهَا، فَقَالَ لِي: قُلْ كَمَا قُلْتُ حَتَّى يَكُونَ قِصَاصًا، فَأَبَيْتُ، فَقَالَ رَسُولُ الله صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ: أَجَلْ فَلَا تَرُدَّ عَلَيْهِ وَلَكِنْ قُلْ: غَفَرَ الله لَكَ يَا أَبَا بَكْرٍ، فَقُلْتُ: غَفَرَ الله لَكَ يَا أَبَا بَكْرٍ ، قَالَ الحسن: فَوَلَّى أَبُو بَكْرٍ رَضِيَ اللَّهُ عَنْهُ وَهُوَ يَبْكِي."],"takhrij":"حسن: رواه أحمد (16577) –والسياق له-، وأبو داود الطيالسي (1269)، والطبراني في الكبير (5/52-53)، والحاكم (3/521) كلهم من طرق عن مبارك بن فضالة، قال: حدثناأبو عمران الجوني، عن ربيعة بن كعب الأسلمي قال: فذكره.","grade":"حسن","chapter_ar":"باب ما جاء في أخبار ربيعة بن كعب الأسلمي","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب فضائل الصحابة وأخبارهم","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Hasan: Narrated by Aḥmad (16577)—this is his wording—, Abū Dāwūd al-Ṭayālisī (1269), and al-Ṭabarānī in al-Muʿjam al-Kabīr (5/52).","chapter_en":"Reports Concerning Rabīʿah ibn Kaʿb al-Aslamī","part_en":"The Book of the Virtues and Accounts of the Companions","group_ar":"مجموع فضائل أفراد الصحابة وأخبارهم","group_en":"A Collection of the Virtues and Reports of Individual Companions","part_no":49,"group_no":13,"chapter_no":49,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Rabīʿah al-Aslamī narrated: I used to serve the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. One day he said to me, “O Rabīʿah, will you not get married?” I replied, “By Allah, O Messenger of Allah, I do not wish to marry. I have nothing with which I can support a wife, and I do not want anything to distract me from serving you.” The Prophet ﷺ turned away from me. After some time, he asked me again, “O Rabīʿah, will you not get married?” I gave him the same answer: “I do not wish to marry. I have nothing by which I can support a wife, and I do not want anything to distract me from you.” Again, he turned away from me. Then I reflected to myself and said, “By Allah, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ knows better than I do what is best for me in this world and the Hereafter. If he asks me again to marry, I will certainly say, ‘Yes, O Messenger of Allah. Command me as you wish.’” So he asked me a third time, “O Rabīʿah, will you not get married?” I answered, “Yes. Command me, O Messenger of Allah.” He said, “Go to such-and-such a family from among the Anṣār and tell them: ‘The Messenger of Allah ﷺ has sent me to you, commanding you to marry me to such-and-such a woman from among you.’” So I went to them and conveyed the Prophet’s message. They replied, “Welcome to the Messenger of Allah, and welcome to the messenger of the Messenger of Allah. By Allah, the messenger of the Messenger of Allah will not return without having his request fulfilled.” They married her to me, treated me with great kindness and generosity, and did not ask me for any proof. Rabīʿah said: I returned to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ feeling saddened. He asked me, “What is the matter with you, O Rabīʿah?” I replied, “O Messenger of Allah, I went to a people of great generosity. They married me to their daughter, honored me, and treated me kindly. They did not ask me for any proof, but I do not possess anything to give as her bridal gift (mahr).” The Messenger of Allah ﷺ then said, “O Buraydah al-Aslamī, collect for him the weight of a date-stone in gold.” So they gathered for me gold equal in weight to a date-stone. I took what they had collected and brought it to the Prophet ﷺ. He said, “Take this to them and say: ‘This is her bridal gift.’” So I went to them and said, “This is her bridal gift.” They accepted it with pleasure and said, “It is a generous and excellent gift.” Rabīʿah continued: Then I returned to the Prophet ﷺ once again feeling distressed. He asked, “O Rabīʿah, why are you still saddened?” I replied, “O Messenger of Allah, I have never seen a people more generous than them. They accepted what I brought them graciously, treated me with the utmost kindness, and said, ‘It is a generous and excellent gift.’ But I have nothing with which to prepare a wedding feast.” The Prophet ﷺ then said, “O Buraydah, collect a sheep for him.” Rabīʿah said: So they gathered for me a large, fat ram. Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to me, “Go to ʿĀ’ishah and tell her to send the basket that contains the food.” I went to her and conveyed the Prophet’s instruction. She said, “This is the basket. It contains nine sāʿ of barley. By Allah, this is the only food we have left this morning. Take it.” So I took it to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and informed him of what ʿĀ’ishah had said. He replied, “Take this to them and tell them to prepare your wedding meal with it.” So I brought them the ram and the basket. They said, “As for the barley, we will bake it into bread, and as for the ram, we will slaughter it.” Rabīʿah said: We slaughtered it, skinned it, and cooked it. By the next morning we had bread and meat. Then I held the wedding feast (walīmah) and invited the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. Rabīʿah continued: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ granted me a piece of land, and Abū Bakr also granted me a piece of land. As worldly possessions became more plentiful, a dispute arose between us regarding the boundary of a single date-palm tree. I said, “It lies within my boundary,” while Abū Bakr said, “Rather, it lies within my boundary.”","Some words passed between us. During the exchange, Abū Bakr said something that he immediately disliked and regretted. He then said to me, “O Rabīʿah, say the same words back to me so that we will be even.” I replied, “I will not do that.” Abū Bakr said, “Either you will say it back to me, or I will take the matter to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ.” I answered, “I will not do so.” He then left the land and went to the Prophet ﷺ, and I followed after him. Some men from the tribe of Aslam came to me and said, “May Allah have mercy on Abū Bakr! Why is he taking a complaint against you to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ when he was the one who spoke to you as he did?” I replied, “Do you know who this is? This is Abū Bakr al-Ṣiddīq. He is the second of the two in the cave, and he is one of the most honored elders among the Muslims. Beware that he should turn around and see you supporting me against him. If he becomes angry, he may go to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, who would become angry because of his anger. Then Allah, the Mighty and Majestic, would become angry because of their anger, and Rabīʿah would be ruined.” They asked, “Then what do you command us to do?” I said, “Go back.” Abū Bakr went on to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and I followed him alone until he reached the Prophet ﷺ. Abū Bakr related the entire incident exactly as it had happened. The Prophet ﷺ then looked at me and said, “O Rabīʿah, what has happened between you and al-Ṣiddīq?” I replied, “O Messenger of Allah, this and this happened. He spoke a word to me which he regretted, and then asked me to respond with the same words so that we would be even, but I refused.” The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, “Indeed. Do not return the insult to him. Instead, say: ‘May Allah forgive you, O Abū Bakr.’” So I said, “May Allah forgive you, O Abū Bakr.” Al-Ḥasan said: Abū Bakr turned away weeping."]}},"tuhfa":{},"full":1,"dr":1,"tks":"حسن: رواه أحمد (16577) –والسياق له-، وأبو داود الطيالسي (1269)، والطبراني في الكبير (5/52-53)، والحاكم (3/521)."},{"num":10191,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ أَنَسٍ، أَنَّ رَجُلًا مِنْ أَهْلِ الْبَادِيَةِ كَانَ اسْمُهُ زَاهِرًا، وَكَانَ يُهْدِي إِلَى رَسُولِ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ الْهَدِيَّةَ مِنَ الْبَادِيَةِ، فَيُجَهِّزُهُ رَسُولُ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ إِذَا أَرَادَ أَنْ يَخْرُجَ، فَقَالَ النَّبِيُّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ: إِنَّ زَاهِرًا بَادِيَتُنَا، وَنَحْنُ حَاضِرُوهُ. وَكَانَ النَّبِيُّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ يُحِبُّهُ، وَكَانَ رَجُلًا دَمِيمًا، فَأَتَاهُ النَّبِيُّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ يَوْمًا وَهُوَ يَبِيعُ مَتَاعَهُ، فَاحْتَضَنَهُ مِنْ خَلْفِهِ، وَلَا يُبْصِرُهُ الرَّجُلُ، فَقَالَ: أَرْسِلْنِي، مَنْ هَذَا، فَالْتَفَتَ فَعَرَفَ النَّبِيَّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ، فَجَعَلَ لَا يَأْلُو مَا أَلْصَقَ ظَهْرَهُ بِصَدْرِ النَّبِيِّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ، حِينَ عَرَفَهُ، وَجَعَلَ النَّبِيُّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ يَقُولُ: مَنْ يَشْتَرِي الْعَبْدَ؟ فَقَالَ: يَا رَسُولَ اللَّهِ، إِذًا وَاللهِ تَجِدُنِي كَاسِدًا، فَقَالَ النَّبِيُّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ: لَكِنْ عِنْدَ اللَّهِ لَسْتَ بِكَاسِدٍ أَوْ قَالَ: لَكِنْ عِنْدَ اللَّهِ أَنْتَ غَالٍ."],"takhrij":"صحيح: رواه عبد الرزاق (19688)، ومن طريقه أحمد (12648)، والترمذي في الشمائل (239) حدثنا معمر، عن ثابت البناني، عن أنس قال: فذكره.وإسناده صحيح.","grade":"صحيح","chapter_ar":"باب فضل زاهر بن حرام الأشجعي","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب فضائل الصحابة وأخبارهم","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Authentic: Narrated by ʿAbd al-Razzāq (19688); through him by Aḥmad (12648); and by al-Tirmidhī in al-Shamā’il (239).","chapter_en":"The Virtue of Zāhir ibn Ḥarām al-Ashjaʿī","part_en":"The Book of the Virtues and Accounts of the Companions","group_ar":"مجموع فضائل أفراد الصحابة وأخبارهم","group_en":"A Collection of the Virtues and Reports of Individual Companions","part_no":49,"group_no":13,"chapter_no":50,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Narrated from Anas: Anas reported that there was a man from the desert named Zāhir. He used to bring gifts from the desert to the Prophet ﷺ, and whenever he wished to depart, the Prophet ﷺ would provide him with provisions for his journey. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Indeed, Zāhir is our representative from the desert, and we are his people in the town.” The Prophet ﷺ loved him, although he was not physically handsome. One day, while Zāhir was selling his goods in the marketplace, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ came up behind him and embraced him. Zāhir could not see who it was and said, “Let me go! Who is this?” When he turned and recognized the Prophet ﷺ, he began pressing his back against the Prophet’s chest as closely as he could out of love. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ then playfully called out: “Who will buy this servant?” Zāhir replied: “O Messenger of Allah, then by Allah you will find me to be of little value.” The Messenger of Allah ﷺ replied: “But in the sight of Allah you are not of little value.” Or he said: “Rather, in the sight of Allah you are precious.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"voc":["fazail",388],"full":1,"rep":[9519],"tks":"صحيح: رواه عبد الرزاق (19688)، ومن طريقه أحمد (12648)، والترمذي في الشمائل (239)."},{"num":10192,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ زاهر بن حَرَامٍ أَنَّ رَسُولُ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ رَآهُ فِي سُوقِ الْمَدِينَةِ، يَبِيعُ سِلْعَةً لَهُ، وَلَمْ يَكُنْ أَتَاهُ –يَعْنِي فِي ذَلِكَ الْوَقْتِ- فَاحْتَضَنَهُ مِنْ وَرَاءِ كَتِفِهِ، فَالْتَفَتَ فَأَبْصَرَ رَسُولَ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ فقبَّل كفَّه، فَقَالَ: مَنْ يَشْتَرِي الْعَبْدَ؟ فَقَالَ: إِذًا تَجِدُنِي يَا رَسُولَ اللَّهِ كَاسِدًا، قَالَ: لَكِنَّكَ عِنْدَ اللَّهِ رَبِيحٌ فَقَالَ رَسُولُ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ: لِكُلِّ حَاضِرٍ بَادِيَةٌ، وَبَادِيَةُ آلِ مُحَمَّدٍ زَاهِرُ بْنُ حَرَامٍ."],"takhrij":"حسن: رواه البزار –كشف الأستار (2734)، والطبراني في الكبير (5/315) كلاهما من طريق شاذ بن فياض، حدثنا رافع بن سلمة (هو ابن زياد الغطفاني) قال: سمعت أبي يحدث عن سالم (هو ابن أبي الجعد)، عن رجل من أشجع يقال له: زاهر بن حرام الأشجعي قال: وكان رجلا بدويا لا يأتي النبي صلى الله عليه وسلم إذا أتاه إلا بطرفة أو هدية يهديها، فرآه رسول الله صلى الله عليه وسلم فذكر الحديث.","grade":"حسن","chapter_ar":"باب فضل زاهر بن حرام الأشجعي","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب فضائل الصحابة وأخبارهم","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Hasan: Narrated by al-Bazzār in Kashf al-Astār (2734) and al-Ṭabarānī in al-Muʿjam al-Kabīr (5/315).","chapter_en":"The Virtue of Zāhir ibn Ḥarām al-Ashjaʿī","part_en":"The Book of the Virtues and Accounts of the Companions","group_ar":"مجموع فضائل أفراد الصحابة وأخبارهم","group_en":"A Collection of the Virtues and Reports of Individual Companions","part_no":49,"group_no":13,"chapter_no":50,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Narrated from Zāhir ibn Ḥarām: Zāhir ibn Ḥarām narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ saw him in the marketplace of Madinah selling some merchandise. The Prophet ﷺ had not come to him at that time, so he embraced him from behind by his shoulders. Zāhir turned and saw that it was the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, so he kissed his hand. The Prophet ﷺ said: “Who will buy this servant?” Zāhir replied: “O Messenger of Allah, then you will find me to be of little worth.” The Prophet ﷺ said: “Rather, with Allah you are profitable.” Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Every town has its people of the desert, and the people of the desert for the family of Muhammad are Zāhir ibn Ḥarām.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"voc":["fazail",389],"full":1,"dr":1,"tks":"حسن: رواه البزار في كشف الأستار (2734)، والطبراني في الكبير (5/315)."},{"num":10193,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ زَيْدِ بْنِ أَرْقَمَ، قَالَ: كُنْتُ فِي غَزَاةٍ، فَسَمِعْتُ عَبْدَ اللَّهِ بْنَ أُبَىٍّ، يَقُولُ: لاَ تُنْفِقُوا عَلَى مَنْ عِنْدَ رَسُولِ اللَّهِ حَتَّى يَنْفَضُّوا مِنْ حَوْلِهِ، وَلَوْ رَجَعْنَا مِنْ عِنْدِهِ لَيُخْرِجَنَّ الأَعَزُّ مِنْهَا. الأَذَلَّ فَذَكَرْتُ ذَلِكَ لِعَمِّي أَوْ لِعُمَرَ فَذَكَرَهُ لِلنَّبِيِّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ، فَدَعَانِي فَحَدَّثْتُهُ، فَأَرْسَلَ رَسُولُ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ إِلَى عَبْدِ اللَّهِ بْنِ أُبَىٍّ وَأَصْحَابِهِ فَحَلَفُوا مَا قَالُوا، فَكَذَّبَنِي رَسُولُ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ وَصَدَّقَهُ، فَأَصَابَنِي هَمٌّ لَمْ يُصِبْنِي مِثْلُهُ قَطُّ، فَجَلَسْتُ فِي الْبَيْتِ، فَقَالَ لِي عَمِّي: مَا أَرَدْتَ إِلَى أَنْ كَذَّبَكَ رَسُولُ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ وَمَقَتَكَ. فَأَنْزَلَ اللَّهُ تَعَالَى: {إِذَا جَاءَكَ الْمُنَافِقُونَ} فَبَعَثَ إِلَىَّ النَّبِيُّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ فَقَرَأَ فَقَالَ: إِنَّ اللَّهَ قَدْ صَدَّقَكَ يَا زَيْدُ."],"takhrij":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاري في التفسير (4900) عن آدم بن أبي إياس، حدثنا إسرائيل، عن أبي إسحاق، عن زيد بن أرقم فذكره.","grade":"متفق عليه","chapter_ar":"باب فضل زيد بن أرقم وأخباره","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب فضائل الصحابة وأخبارهم","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Agreed upon: Narrated by al-Bukhārī (4900) and Muslim (1/2772).","chapter_en":"The Virtue of Zayd ibn Arqam and His Reports","part_en":"The Book of the Virtues and Accounts of the Companions","group_ar":"مجموع فضائل أفراد الصحابة وأخبارهم","group_en":"A Collection of the Virtues and Reports of Individual Companions","part_no":49,"group_no":13,"chapter_no":51,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Zayd ibn Arqam reported: I was taking part in a military expedition when I heard ʿAbd Allah ibn Ubayy say: “Do not spend anything upon those who are with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ until they disperse from around him. And when we return to Madinah, the more honorable will surely expel the more contemptible from it.” I mentioned this to my uncle—or to ʿUmar—and he reported it to the Prophet ﷺ. The Prophet ﷺ called me, and I related to him what I had heard. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ then summoned ʿAbd Allah ibn Ubayy and his companions. They swore that they had not said it, so the Messenger of Allah ﷺ accepted their statement and regarded my report as untrue. I was overcome by distress unlike anything I had ever experienced before. I remained sitting at home, and my uncle said to me: “What did you gain except that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ regarded your statement as false and became displeased with you?” Then Allah Most High revealed: “When the hypocrites come to you…” [Al-Munāfiqūn 63:1] The Prophet ﷺ sent for me, recited the sūrah, and said: “Indeed, Allah has confirmed that you spoke the truth, O Zayd.”"]}},"tuhfa":{},"voc":["fazail",390],"full":1,"dr":1,"tks":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (4900)، ومسلم (1/2772)."},{"num":10194,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عن أنس بْنِ مَالِكٍ يَقُولُ حَزِنْتُ عَلَى مَنْ أُصِيبَ بِالْحَرَّةِ، فَكَتَبَ إِلَىَّ زَيْدُ بْنُ أَرْقَمَ، وَبَلَغَهُ شِدَّةُ حُزْنِي، يَذْكُرُ أَنَّهُ سَمِعَ رَسُولَ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ يَقُولُ: اللَّهُمَّ اغْفِرْ لِلأَنْصَارِ وَلأَبْنَاءِ الأَنْصَارِ ـ وَشَكَّ ابْنُ الْفَضْلِ فِي: أَبْنَاءِ أَبْنَاءِ الأَنْصَارِ ـ فَسَأَلَ أَنَسًا بَعْضُ مَنْ كَانَ عِنْدَهُ، فَقَالَ: هُوَ الَّذِي يَقُولُ رَسُولُ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ: هَذَا الَّذِي أَوْفَى اللَّهُ لَهُ بِأُذُنِهِ."],"takhrij":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاري في التفسير (4906) عن إسماعيل بن عبد الله قال: حدثني إسماعيل بن إبراهيم بن عقبة، عن موسى بن عقبة، قال: حدثني عبد الله بن الفضل، أنه سمع أنس بن مالك يقول: فذكره.","grade":"متفق عليه","chapter_ar":"باب فضل زيد بن أرقم وأخباره","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب فضائل الصحابة وأخبارهم","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Authentic: Narrated by al-Bukhārī (4906) and Muslim (2506) through another chain.","chapter_en":"The Virtue of Zayd ibn Arqam and His Reports","part_en":"The Book of the Virtues and Accounts of the Companions","group_ar":"مجموع فضائل أفراد الصحابة وأخبارهم","group_en":"A Collection of the Virtues and Reports of Individual Companions","part_no":49,"group_no":13,"chapter_no":51,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Anas ibn Mālik reported: I grieved deeply over those who were killed at al-Ḥarrah. When Zayd ibn Arqam learned of the severity of my grief, he wrote to me, mentioning that he had heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: “O Allah, forgive the Anṣār and the children of the Anṣār.” Ibn al-Faḍl was uncertain whether the narration also included: “And the children of the children of the Anṣār.” One of those who was present with Anas asked him about Zayd ibn Arqam, and Anas said: “He is the one concerning whom the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: ‘This is the one whose hearing Allah vindicated.’”"]},"buhuth":{"en":["In Muslim’s narration (2506), the phrase “the children of the children of the Anṣār” is mentioned without uncertainty."]}},"tuhfa":{},"voc":["fazail",391],"full":1,"dr":1,"tks":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (4906)، ومسلم (2506) من وجه آخر."},{"num":10195,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ زَيْدِ بْنِ أَرْقَمَ، قَالَ: أَصَابَنِي رَمَدٌ، فَعَادَنِي النَّبِيُّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ، قَالَ: فَلَمَّا بَرَأْتُ خَرَجْتُ، قَالَ: فَقَالَ لِي رَسُولُ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ: أَرَأَيْتَ لَوْ كَانَتْ عَيْنَاكَ لِمَا بِهِمَا مَا كُنْتَ صَانِعًا؟ قَالَ: قُلْتُ: لَوْ كَانَتَا عَيْنَايَ لِمَا بِهِمَا صَبَرْتُ وَاحْتَسَبْتُ، قَالَ: لَوْ كَانَتْ عَيْنَاكَ لِمَا بِهِمَا، ثُمَّ صَبَرْتَ وَاحْتَسَبْتَ، لَلَقِيتَ اللهَ عَزَّ وَجَلَّ وَلَا ذَنْبَ لَكَ.","قال إسماعيل: ثم صبرت واحتسبت لأوجب الله تعالى لك الجنة."],"takhrij":"حسن: رواه أحمد (19348) – واللفظ له-، وأبو داود (3102)، وصحّحه الحاكم (1/342) كلهم من طريق حجاج بن محمد، حدثنا يونس بن أبي إسحاق، عن أبيه أبي إسحاق، عن زيد بن أرقم فذكره.","grade":"حسن","chapter_ar":"باب فضل زيد بن أرقم وأخباره","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب فضائل الصحابة وأخبارهم","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Hasan: Narrated by Aḥmad (19348)—and this is his wording—and Abū Dāwūd (3102). Al-Ḥākim declared it authentic (1/343).","chapter_en":"The Virtue of Zayd ibn Arqam and His Reports","part_en":"The Book of the Virtues and Accounts of the Companions","group_ar":"مجموع فضائل أفراد الصحابة وأخبارهم","group_en":"A Collection of the Virtues and Reports of Individual Companions","part_no":49,"group_no":13,"chapter_no":51,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Zayd ibn Arqam reported: I suffered from inflammation of the eyes, so the Prophet ﷺ visited me. When I recovered, I went out. Zayd said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ then asked me: “Tell me, had your eyes remained in the condition they were in, what would you have done?” I replied: “Had my eyes remained as they were, I would have remained patient and sought the reward from Allah.” He said: “Had your eyes remained in that condition, and you then remained patient and sought Allah’s reward, you would have met Allah, the Mighty and Majestic, without any sin upon you.” Ismāʿīl narrated the wording: “Then, had you remained patient and sought Allah’s reward, Allah Most High would have guaranteed Paradise for you.”"]},"buhuth":{"en":["Zayd ibn Arqam died in the year 66 or 68 AH."]}},"tuhfa":{},"voc":["fazail",392],"full":1,"dr":1,"tks":"حسن: رواه أحمد (19348) - واللفظ له -، وأبو داود (3102)، وصححه الحاكم (1/343)."},{"num":10196,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنْ عَبْدِ اللَّهِ بْنِ عُمَرَ رَضِيَ اللَّهُ عَنْهُمَا قَالَ: بَعَثَ النَّبِيُّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ بَعْثًا، وَأَمَّرَ عَلَيْهِمْ أُسَامَةَ بْنَ زَيْدٍ، فَطَعَنَ بَعْضُ النَّاسِ فِي إِمَارَتِهِ، فَقَالَ النَّبِيُّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ: إِنْ تَطْعُنُوا فِي إِمَارَتِهِ فَقَدْ كُنْتُمْ تَطْعُنُونَ فِي إِمَارَةِ أَبِيهِ مِنْ قَبْلُ، وَايْمُ اللَّهِ، إِنْ كَانَ لَخَلِيقًا لِلإِمَارَةِ، وَإِنْ كَانَ لَمِنْ أَحَبِّ النَّاسِ إِلَىَّ، وَإِنَّ هَذَا لَمِنْ أَحَبِّ النَّاسِ إِلَىَّ بَعْدَهُ."],"takhrij":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاري في فضائل الصحابة (3730) ومسلم في فضائل الصحابة (2426-63) كلاهما من طريق عبد الله بن دينار، أنه سمع ابن عمر يقول: فذكره.","grade":"متفق عليه","chapter_ar":"باب ما جاء أن زيد بن حارثة من أحب الناس إلى النبي ﷺ","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب فضائل الصحابة وأخبارهم","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Authentic: Narrated by al-Bukhārī (3730) and Muslim (63–2426).","chapter_en":"What Has Been Related Concerning Zayd ibn Ḥārithah Being Among the People Most Beloved to the Prophet ﷺ","part_en":"The Book of the Virtues and Accounts of the Companions","group_ar":"مجموع فضائل أفراد الصحابة وأخبارهم","group_en":"A Collection of the Virtues and Reports of Individual Companions","part_no":49,"group_no":13,"chapter_no":52,"content":{"translation":{"en":["ʿAbd Allah ibn ʿUmar reported: The Prophet ﷺ dispatched an expedition and appointed Usāmah ibn Zayd as its commander. Some people criticized his appointment, so the Prophet ﷺ said: “If you criticize his leadership, you had previously criticized the leadership of his father. By Allah, his father was certainly worthy of command, and he was among the people most beloved to me. And this man is among the people most beloved to me after him.”"]},"buhuth":{"en":["In another wording, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said while standing upon the pulpit:","“If you criticize his leadership”—meaning Usāmah ibn Zayd—“you had previously criticized the leadership of his father. By Allah, he was certainly worthy of it. By Allah, he was among the people most beloved to me. By Allah, this man is also worthy”—meaning Usāmah ibn Zayd—“and by Allah, he is among the people most beloved to me after his father. Therefore, I instruct you to treat him well, for he is among the righteous among you.”","Narrated by Muslim (64–2426)."]}},"tuhfa":{},"voc":["fazail",393],"full":1,"dr":1,"rep":[10094],"tks":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (3730)، ومسلم (63-2426)."},{"num":10197,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عن عَبْدِ اللَّهِ بن عُمَرَ، عَنْ أَبِيهِ أَنَّهُ كَانَ يَقُولُ:  مَا كُنَّا نَدْعُو زَيْدَ بْنَ حَارِثَةَ إِلَّا زَيْدَ بْنَ مُحَمَّدٍ، حَتَّى نَزَلَ فِي الْقُرْآنِ: ﴿ادْعُوهُمْ لآبَائِهِمْ هُوَ أَقْسَطُ عِنْدَ اللَّهِ ﴾."],"takhrij":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاري في التفسير (4782)، ومسلم في فضائل الصحابة (2425-62) كلاهما من طريق موسى بن عقبة، عن سالم بن عبد الله، عن أبيه فذكره.","grade":"متفق عليه","chapter_ar":"باب ما جاء أن زيد بن حارثة من أحب الناس إلى النبي ﷺ","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب فضائل الصحابة وأخبارهم","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Agreed upon: Narrated by al-Bukhārī (4782) and Muslim (62–2425).","chapter_en":"What Has Been Related Concerning Zayd ibn Ḥārithah Being Among the People Most Beloved to the Prophet ﷺ","part_en":"The Book of the Virtues and Accounts of the Companions","group_ar":"مجموع فضائل أفراد الصحابة وأخبارهم","group_en":"A Collection of the Virtues and Reports of Individual Companions","part_no":49,"group_no":13,"chapter_no":52,"content":{"translation":{"en":["ʿAbd Allah ibn ʿUmar reported that he used to say: We did not call Zayd ibn Ḥārithah by any name other than Zayd ibn Muḥammad until the following was revealed in the Qur’an: “Call them by the names of their fathers; that is more just in the sight of Allah.” [Al-Aḥzāb 33:5]"]}},"tuhfa":{},"full":1,"tks":"متفق عليه: رواه البخاري (4782)، ومسلم (62-2425)."},{"num":10198,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عن جبلة بن حَارِثَةَ أخي زيد أَخُو زَيْدٍ، قَالَ: قَدِمْتُ عَلَى رَسُولِ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ، فَقُلْتُ: يَا رَسُولَ اللَّهِ، ابْعَثْ مَعِي أَخِي زَيْدًا. قَالَ: هُوَ ذَا. قَالَ فَإِنِ انْطَلَقَ مَعَكَ لَمْ أَمْنَعْهُ. قَالَ زَيْدٌ: يَا رَسُولَ اللَّهِ، وَاللَّهِ لاَ أَخْتَارُ عَلَيْكَ أَحَدًا. قَالَ: فَرَأَيْتُ رَأْىَ أَخِي أَفْضَلَ مِنْ رَأْيِي."],"takhrij":"صحيح: رواه الترمذي (3815)، وابن قانع في معجم الصحابة (1/161)، والطبراني في الكبير (2/322)، وصحّحه الحاكم (4948) كلهم من طريق إسماعيل بن أبي خالد، عن أبي عمرو الشيباني (واسمه: سعد بن إياس)، أخبرني جبلة بن حارثة –أخو زيد بن حارثة- قال: فذكره.","grade":"صحيح","chapter_ar":"باب ما جاء أن زيد بن حارثة من أحب الناس إلى النبي ﷺ","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب فضائل الصحابة وأخبارهم","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Authentic: Narrated by al-Tirmidhī (3815) and Ibn Qāniʿ in Muʿjam al-Ṣaḥābah (1/161).","chapter_en":"What Has Been Related Concerning Zayd ibn Ḥārithah Being Among the People Most Beloved to the Prophet ﷺ","part_en":"The Book of the Virtues and Accounts of the Companions","group_ar":"مجموع فضائل أفراد الصحابة وأخبارهم","group_en":"A Collection of the Virtues and Reports of Individual Companions","part_no":49,"group_no":13,"chapter_no":52,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Jabalah ibn Ḥārithah, the brother of Zayd, reported: I came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and said: “O Messenger of Allah, send my brother Zayd with me.” He replied: “He is here. Should he choose to leave with you, I will not prevent him.” Zayd said: “O Messenger of Allah, by Allah, I would never choose anyone over you.” Jabalah said: I then realized that my brother’s judgment was better than my own."]},"buhuth":{"en":["Zayd ibn Ḥārithah was martyred during the lifetime of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ at the Battle of Muʾtah in the year 8 AH, at the age of fifty-five."]}},"tuhfa":{},"voc":["fazail",395],"full":1,"dr":1,"tks":"صحيح: رواه الترمذي (3815)، وابن قانع في معجم الصحابة (1/161)."},{"num":10199,"demo":false,"sanad":"","matn":["عَنِ ابْنِ بُرَيْدَةَ، عَنْ أَبِيهِ، أَنَّ النَّبِيَّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ، قَالَ: دَخَلْتُ الْبَارِحَةَ الْجَنَّةَ، فَإِذَا أَنَا بِجَارِيَةٍ، فَقُلْتُ: لِمَنْ أَنْتِ؟ يَا جَارِيَةُ؟ قَالَتْ: لِزَيْدِ بْنِ حَارِثَةَ رَضِيَ اللَّهُ عَنْهُ، فَبَشَّرَهُ بِهَا حِينَ أَصْبَحَ."],"takhrij":"حسن: رواه ابنُ أبي عاصم في الآحاد والمثاني (256) عن أبي موسى (هو محمد بن المثنى)، حدثنا أحمد بن سعيد الدارمي، حدثنا علي بن حسين بن واقد، أخبرني أبي، عن ابن بريدة (هو عبد الله)، عن أبيه قال: فذكره.","grade":"حسن","chapter_ar":"باب ما جاء أن زيد بن حارثة من أحب الناس إلى النبي ﷺ","chapter_ur":"","part_ar":"كتاب فضائل الصحابة وأخبارهم","part_ur":"","takhrij_en":"Hasan: Narrated by Ibn Abī ʿĀṣim in al-Āḥād wa al-Mathānī (256).","chapter_en":"What Has Been Related Concerning Zayd ibn Ḥārithah Being Among the People Most Beloved to the Prophet ﷺ","part_en":"The Book of the Virtues and Accounts of the Companions","group_ar":"مجموع فضائل أفراد الصحابة وأخبارهم","group_en":"A Collection of the Virtues and Reports of Individual Companions","part_no":49,"group_no":13,"chapter_no":52,"content":{"translation":{"en":["Buraydah ibn al-Ḥuṣayb reported that the Prophet ﷺ said: “Last night I entered Paradise, and there I saw a young woman. I asked her, ‘To whom do you belong?’ She replied, ‘To Zayd ibn Ḥārithah.’” The Prophet ﷺ then gave Zayd the glad tidings of her when morning came."]}},"tuhfa":{},"voc":["fazail",396],"full":1,"dr":1,"tks":"حسن: رواه ابن أبي عاصم في الآحاد والمثاني (256)."}]);